[{"sha":"3b32d861c5ecc1e705812bc21177d0038e3c05ee","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDNiMzJkODYxYzVlY2MxZTcwNTgxMmJjMjExNzdkMDAzOGUzYzA1ZWU","commit":{"author":{"name":"pakrym-oai","email":"pakrym@openai.com","date":"2026-06-22T23:07:27Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T23:07:27Z"},"message":"[codex] migrate environment context to model world state (#29249)\n\n## Why\n\nEnvironment context is model-visible state, but it is currently\nassembled from transient turn values and diffed through\nenvironment-specific paths. That makes initial injection, turn-to-turn\nupdates, and changes that happen within a turn use different baselines.\n\nThis PR introduces the smallest useful model world-state slice:\nenvironments only, with one in-memory baseline and one renderer for full\nstate and diffs.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add a typed `WorldState` container whose sections render fragments\nrelative to an optional previous value. Full rendering uses the same\ndiff path with no previous state.\n- Replace the parallel `EnvironmentContext` representation with an\n`EnvironmentsState` section keyed by environment ID and rendered in\ndeterministic order.\n- Preserve the legacy single-environment output while supporting\nmultiple environments, starting environments, unavailable tombstones,\nand changes to persisted turn-context values.\n- Store the latest complete `WorldState` on `ContextManager` and use it\nfor both turn-boundary and mid-turn environment diffs.\n- Build initial and post-compaction context from the same world-state\nbuilder, then retain the rendered state as the next baseline.\n- Seed the in-memory baseline from the latest `TurnContextItem` when\nresuming an existing rollout; the world state itself is not serialized.\n- Keep non-world settings updates on their existing path and merge\nrendered world-state fragments at the session consumer.\n\n## Known limitation\n\nA legacy `TurnContextItem` only reconstructs the primary environment as\n`local`; it cannot faithfully recover a remote-primary environment ID\nafter resume. Live state uses the exact environment IDs once a complete\nbaseline is established.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just test -p codex-core world_state`\n- `just test -p codex-core record_context_updates`\n- `just test -p codex-core deferred_executor_`\n- `just test -p codex-core build_initial_context`\n- `just test -p codex-core rollout_reconstruction`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nprocess_compacted_history_reinjects_full_initial_context`","tree":{"sha":"6f2099ed2b731ed209c7fbfdceb0a13fdb08ed6a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/6f2099ed2b731ed209c7fbfdceb0a13fdb08ed6a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/3b32d861c5ecc1e705812bc21177d0038e3c05ee","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOcAvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmJIQAF8jUvmjjwsAdY+tUegfLt4D\nFIDfpciWOIhO2s8Xwv8HC3nxPWwjxKC8Rt4ooZAdp0Uy/zC93I8ohcXUNdc3jnpo\ndVWr9lLXtx0k58w45fJUGn2OK8pH76+X4GTeOr7foRpSaaMQDsAJJBl9Kqpl0LWm\nz0g7bgXfPy/l4HQMinUvL+XhZXnGXty4QUzI3VCCX7zw8fVdxqozbmIqRuZ355+B\noZdDq82Oo6xRLPXkMTt59DoouOOxY76n7c4hXCTVIVXss7/aI+iYdxbTcpvDxnq3\ncoumzSSXtZHTpvadKEzYCQGCw9NzHpF1voQgMbMPR5jTVc+q9Rwy1SDmenOFBVgk\nHmD+wYJ/2mES0Pueo81EoLHqAeKnPixDry/Jooq7m5qMGg94WjkK03+EUZiO2Hcr\neegMciOpn+2pTQgHuD7W+9szWavP1aftGyqgcQQVKQdX0xGGB5iKpvRYXalkzBql\nC2EUBK/qgVrBTf6iKVwMv4Xe0TzjL9eNJYX101MQSxiaI/AfiNapVW3Ec38Bq1u/\nmN5CjJBqmzJfp+W9jq1ET6Uy2YpjDfmsq7xOZLr8T699W1FCAGzqN3+TqR6FHHub\n3Dskf6+DyEfNVdq2wejP0jbiS9HcO7aa59NQQe4n4nikwE5HcKAKqvfO67pF2RUv\ni3yBUr5ghZx8/kR1clIH\n=1cBB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6f2099ed2b731ed209c7fbfdceb0a13fdb08ed6a\nparent 2c351cb8646054427e0ea81a484233114b1234f7\nauthor pakrym-oai <pakrym@openai.com> 1782169647 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782169647 -0700\n\n[codex] migrate environment context to model world state (#29249)\n\n## Why\n\nEnvironment context is model-visible state, but it is currently\nassembled from transient turn values and diffed through\nenvironment-specific paths. That makes initial injection, turn-to-turn\nupdates, and changes that happen within a turn use different baselines.\n\nThis PR introduces the smallest useful model world-state slice:\nenvironments only, with one in-memory baseline and one renderer for full\nstate and diffs.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add a typed `WorldState` container whose sections render fragments\nrelative to an optional previous value. Full rendering uses the same\ndiff path with no previous state.\n- Replace the parallel `EnvironmentContext` representation with an\n`EnvironmentsState` section keyed by environment ID and rendered in\ndeterministic order.\n- Preserve the legacy single-environment output while supporting\nmultiple environments, starting environments, unavailable tombstones,\nand changes to persisted turn-context values.\n- Store the latest complete `WorldState` on `ContextManager` and use it\nfor both turn-boundary and mid-turn environment diffs.\n- Build initial and post-compaction context from the same world-state\nbuilder, then retain the rendered state as the next baseline.\n- Seed the in-memory baseline from the latest `TurnContextItem` when\nresuming an existing rollout; the world state itself is not serialized.\n- Keep non-world settings updates on their existing path and merge\nrendered world-state fragments at the session consumer.\n\n## Known limitation\n\nA legacy `TurnContextItem` only reconstructs the primary environment as\n`local`; it cannot faithfully recover a remote-primary environment ID\nafter resume. Live state uses the exact environment IDs once a complete\nbaseline is established.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just test -p codex-core world_state`\n- `just test -p codex-core record_context_updates`\n- `just test -p codex-core deferred_executor_`\n- `just test -p codex-core build_initial_context`\n- `just test -p codex-core rollout_reconstruction`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nprocess_compacted_history_reinjects_full_initial_context`","verified_at":"2026-06-22T23:07:27Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3b32d861c5ecc1e705812bc21177d0038e3c05ee","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3b32d861c5ecc1e705812bc21177d0038e3c05ee","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3b32d861c5ecc1e705812bc21177d0038e3c05ee/comments","author":{"login":"pakrym-oai","id":204937752,"node_id":"U_kgDODDcaGA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204937752?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/pakrym-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2c351cb8646054427e0ea81a484233114b1234f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2c351cb8646054427e0ea81a484233114b1234f7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2c351cb8646054427e0ea81a484233114b1234f7"}]},{"sha":"2c351cb8646054427e0ea81a484233114b1234f7","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDJjMzUxY2I4NjQ2MDU0NDI3ZTBlYTgxYTQ4NDIzMzExNGIxMjM0Zjc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Drew","email":"drewschuster@openai.com","date":"2026-06-22T23:01:27Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T23:01:27Z"},"message":"[plugins] Add dark-mode logo metadata (#29488)\n\nAdds additive dark-mode plugin logo metadata across manifests, remote\ncatalogs, and the app-server protocol while keeping uninstalled Git\nlistings free of synthetic local paths.\n\nSupersedes #28945. This replacement uses an upstream branch so trusted\nCI can use the repository-provided remote Bazel configuration.\n\n## Current state\n\nPlugin interfaces expose only the default logo asset. Clients therefore\ncannot select a dedicated dark-mode logo even when a plugin provides\none.\n\n## What this PR changes\n\n- Adds nullable `logoDark` and `logoUrlDark` fields to\n`PluginInterface`.\n- Resolves local `interface.logoDark` assets and maps remote\n`logo_url_dark` values.\n- Removes path-backed interface assets, including `logoDark`, from\nuninstalled Git fallback listings until the plugin has a real local\nroot.\n- Updates the bundled plugin validator and manifest reference.\n- Regenerates the app-server JSON schemas and TypeScript types.\n\nLocal manifests expose `interface.logoDark` as a package-relative asset\npath. Remote catalog responses expose `logo_url_dark`. These values map\ninto separate app-server fields so clients can preserve local-path and\nremote-URL handling.\n\n## Risk\n\nThe fields are additive and nullable, so existing clients retain their\ncurrent logo behavior. The main risks are an incomplete mapping path or\nexposing a synthetic local path for an uninstalled Git plugin.\nLocal-manifest, remote-catalog, fallback-listing, protocol\nserialization, and app-server integration tests cover those paths.\n\nSpiciness: 2/5\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just write-app-server-schema`\n- `just fmt`\n- Regression test first failed with `logo_dark` resolved to\n`/assets/logo-dark.png`, then passed after the fallback-listing fix.\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins` (267 tests passed)\n- `just test -p codex-app-server 'suite::v2::plugin'` (114 tests passed)\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol -p codex-core-plugins -p\ncodex-plugin -p codex-skills` (517 tests passed before the follow-up)\n- `just test -p codex-tui plugin` (47 tests passed)\n- Validated a local plugin manifest containing `interface.logoDark` with\nthe bundled validator.\n\n## Manual verification\n\nCreate a local plugin with both `interface.logo` and\n`interface.logoDark`, then call `plugin/list` or `plugin/read`. Confirm\nthe response contains separate `logo` and `logoDark` paths. For a remote\ncatalog entry, confirm `logoUrlDark` is populated from `logo_url_dark`.\nFor an uninstalled Git marketplace entry, confirm path-backed interface\nassets remain absent until installation.\n\nIssue: N/A - coordinated maintainer change.","tree":{"sha":"85b7464ca289e06905d2eba325aa0812541f0e1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/85b7464ca289e06905d2eba325aa0812541f0e1c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/2c351cb8646054427e0ea81a484233114b1234f7","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOb7HCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1P8QAKoAHuEaBViNDf8Mu3tj+5kt\nFCIrY6/yudpP2SGkCOqZ+XhbhY9joMqYDmUpu+7G7ZkJbk/sMknIy5CGHxbBUcWc\nfSmvbEM29gNNKwEwmzZvFXLwuW+g25oZUX+05HmjfGb/TUmOPt7UUAdjqY/yA/dZ\nJwQ5jHHakzH/5H77JJxV0tgwN4MwU5oUXOp7jMP5KI/FjQ8zqbjdLao5sFvcBaRR\nHOIIPTx+whkzBrnEyxtQ6zFurtTzF4hzIVcSqebACTxVyLFGAQNfPqqUMBrKW1Dx\n8ctJQx7h4JQL9Gs+UuHGi9rTVhZg0Am2PO0D51Rk1QebF1yt5G1bgInN6qCya1bP\nRD/W+QLsmlNblwCVYRCouvxRSnGsrlX3NRLeorT7d33YSwGMCXD9OnOHGcbbiy/q\nT7UwbfQRnUapn2wF9x/vd59WHdi7eJFfilzmarD8vvF563g5fWeCjXOk3vsOazbh\n3wRz8xvheGS4ovC7Wg/a4x7V6rLdg2SxouNlfaQunPxAxeH3FNyaV9hw1ChEfmUX\nb+gQBoOrVT/0Y759Iq4jWyM7YLluTdyb1dNlWEKvGl/MiO7nqswaGROwX5mE+G6W\nBDKEQMLj/rtrrl4y538H9tt52r4SU6dTp5UpEoXdY2IT3HFM32QWryO69ECaUI6v\nPTI/62Yk2r9GY/Mt8zeO\n=wD1s\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 85b7464ca289e06905d2eba325aa0812541f0e1c\nparent 7ce84e64d892044285e1a5918ddf96d0b8a99c7b\nauthor Drew <drewschuster@openai.com> 1782169287 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782169287 -0700\n\n[plugins] Add dark-mode logo metadata (#29488)\n\nAdds additive dark-mode plugin logo metadata across manifests, remote\ncatalogs, and the app-server protocol while keeping uninstalled Git\nlistings free of synthetic local paths.\n\nSupersedes #28945. This replacement uses an upstream branch so trusted\nCI can use the repository-provided remote Bazel configuration.\n\n## Current state\n\nPlugin interfaces expose only the default logo asset. Clients therefore\ncannot select a dedicated dark-mode logo even when a plugin provides\none.\n\n## What this PR changes\n\n- Adds nullable `logoDark` and `logoUrlDark` fields to\n`PluginInterface`.\n- Resolves local `interface.logoDark` assets and maps remote\n`logo_url_dark` values.\n- Removes path-backed interface assets, including `logoDark`, from\nuninstalled Git fallback listings until the plugin has a real local\nroot.\n- Updates the bundled plugin validator and manifest reference.\n- Regenerates the app-server JSON schemas and TypeScript types.\n\nLocal manifests expose `interface.logoDark` as a package-relative asset\npath. Remote catalog responses expose `logo_url_dark`. These values map\ninto separate app-server fields so clients can preserve local-path and\nremote-URL handling.\n\n## Risk\n\nThe fields are additive and nullable, so existing clients retain their\ncurrent logo behavior. The main risks are an incomplete mapping path or\nexposing a synthetic local path for an uninstalled Git plugin.\nLocal-manifest, remote-catalog, fallback-listing, protocol\nserialization, and app-server integration tests cover those paths.\n\nSpiciness: 2/5\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just write-app-server-schema`\n- `just fmt`\n- Regression test first failed with `logo_dark` resolved to\n`/assets/logo-dark.png`, then passed after the fallback-listing fix.\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins` (267 tests passed)\n- `just test -p codex-app-server 'suite::v2::plugin'` (114 tests passed)\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol -p codex-core-plugins -p\ncodex-plugin -p codex-skills` (517 tests passed before the follow-up)\n- `just test -p codex-tui plugin` (47 tests passed)\n- Validated a local plugin manifest containing `interface.logoDark` with\nthe bundled validator.\n\n## Manual verification\n\nCreate a local plugin with both `interface.logo` and\n`interface.logoDark`, then call `plugin/list` or `plugin/read`. Confirm\nthe response contains separate `logo` and `logoDark` paths. For a remote\ncatalog entry, confirm `logoUrlDark` is populated from `logo_url_dark`.\nFor an uninstalled Git marketplace entry, confirm path-backed interface\nassets remain absent until installation.\n\nIssue: N/A - coordinated maintainer change.","verified_at":"2026-06-22T23:01:27Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2c351cb8646054427e0ea81a484233114b1234f7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2c351cb8646054427e0ea81a484233114b1234f7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2c351cb8646054427e0ea81a484233114b1234f7/comments","author":{"login":"drewschuster-openai","id":181145906,"node_id":"U_kgDOCswRMg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/181145906?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/drewschuster-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/drewschuster-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drewschuster-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drewschuster-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drewschuster-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drewschuster-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drewschuster-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drewschuster-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drewschuster-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drewschuster-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drewschuster-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7ce84e64d892044285e1a5918ddf96d0b8a99c7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7ce84e64d892044285e1a5918ddf96d0b8a99c7b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/7ce84e64d892044285e1a5918ddf96d0b8a99c7b"}]},{"sha":"7ce84e64d892044285e1a5918ddf96d0b8a99c7b","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDdjZTg0ZTY0ZDg5MjA0NDI4NWUxYTU5MThkZGY5NmQwYjhhOTljN2I","commit":{"author":{"name":"pakrym-oai","email":"pakrym@openai.com","date":"2026-06-22T23:00:56Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T23:00:56Z"},"message":"[codex] Update esbuild to 0.28.1 (#29489)\n\n## Why\n\nThe TypeScript workspace resolved `esbuild` 0.25.10 transitively through\nthe SDK toolchain. `esbuild` 0.28.1 adds integrity verification to the\nDeno binary download path addressed by\n[GHSA-gv7w-rqvm-qjhr](https://github.com/evanw/esbuild/security/advisories/GHSA-gv7w-rqvm-qjhr),\npreventing an attacker-controlled npm registry from supplying an\nexecutable without a content check.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add a root workspace resolution for `esbuild` 0.28.1.\n- Regenerate `pnpm-lock.yaml` so `tsup`, `bundle-require`, and `ts-jest`\nall resolve the patched version.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Frozen pnpm install, including the SDK's `tsup` build\n- `pnpm --filter @openai/codex-sdk exec jest tests/exec.test.ts\n--runInBand`\n- Confirmed the installed dependency graph contains only `esbuild`\n0.28.1","tree":{"sha":"4f4d6810eae831ba5fc4d6ce9f41215558ac0e14","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/4f4d6810eae831ba5fc4d6ce9f41215558ac0e14"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/7ce84e64d892044285e1a5918ddf96d0b8a99c7b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOb6oCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAz80QAFuyqZQB6btkQuai/AgAGpos\nAv2oQO9u5Z302amsjmZtsWs+hxivzXE9PdDS6kIprwkn2zgqHBlerxFhY3xVYXim\nmOEvIUKqCKf5rM0GrHA+0uDIcDsKDH+inl1N4u7CuvieU5VEW175l/bFG8lOP+Pq\n1Iy6PKJwXaf2q8p0Ed2r2aQHCUA1HxEU2urZsEaZOqch7ikUg0+5ajWspVD/Rnwn\n3TnKxe0KlKQdFyhvEmC3YpakRoHMZX76DgtDsw+bK0Ra72bMqTAOAHFfW7xpPz4T\nR+mP6N/Zt0aZC4/Nunls6UVXSv/OhNUKkKVcW2L/nH+VwBZzL/2XE/cQ93iryEEe\nQuNg8x1ICRRlzuBTl+pT+Tbz1tyfbaf+peg9Tg2kjH54l3cAn0zYqX1ks428LZGd\noYRuk7zqF4+TTRVV6FkjCdiwvdQkY0iGx9g7/9DnOG06qX2uLeV6PwnqGkLW83Am\nssllv4KSQvUV8yeEYZ0fvs8//AtszhmgxU4ari6i78KTDogGsG0DZwKaFtZflL1K\nCY9yHkCW7N3Pr05p+YopAX3SlBup8FIh1IGUIgJVHLy4bRH0v2hEU7fZfktRtR3V\nNAqKv2QBr25pztSpxu7qlHgEQQ2OtvAOmcj5ujF3YyBJvhGu3g7VLvttnbn/3pnk\nQV206wwAOrJGv9aL7ifk\n=q1Su\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4f4d6810eae831ba5fc4d6ce9f41215558ac0e14\nparent 372b5ac7c2876ace31b736a35a19e09a45c6f798\nauthor pakrym-oai <pakrym@openai.com> 1782169256 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782169256 -0700\n\n[codex] Update esbuild to 0.28.1 (#29489)\n\n## Why\n\nThe TypeScript workspace resolved `esbuild` 0.25.10 transitively through\nthe SDK toolchain. `esbuild` 0.28.1 adds integrity verification to the\nDeno binary download path addressed by\n[GHSA-gv7w-rqvm-qjhr](https://github.com/evanw/esbuild/security/advisories/GHSA-gv7w-rqvm-qjhr),\npreventing an attacker-controlled npm registry from supplying an\nexecutable without a content check.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add a root workspace resolution for `esbuild` 0.28.1.\n- Regenerate `pnpm-lock.yaml` so `tsup`, `bundle-require`, and `ts-jest`\nall resolve the patched version.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Frozen pnpm install, including the SDK's `tsup` build\n- `pnpm --filter @openai/codex-sdk exec jest tests/exec.test.ts\n--runInBand`\n- Confirmed the installed dependency graph contains only `esbuild`\n0.28.1","verified_at":"2026-06-22T23:00:57Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7ce84e64d892044285e1a5918ddf96d0b8a99c7b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/7ce84e64d892044285e1a5918ddf96d0b8a99c7b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7ce84e64d892044285e1a5918ddf96d0b8a99c7b/comments","author":{"login":"pakrym-oai","id":204937752,"node_id":"U_kgDODDcaGA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204937752?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/pakrym-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"372b5ac7c2876ace31b736a35a19e09a45c6f798","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/372b5ac7c2876ace31b736a35a19e09a45c6f798","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/372b5ac7c2876ace31b736a35a19e09a45c6f798"}]},{"sha":"372b5ac7c2876ace31b736a35a19e09a45c6f798","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDM3MmI1YWM3YzI4NzZhY2UzMWI3MzZhMzVhMTllMDlhNDVjNmY3OTg","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-22T22:19:54Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T22:19:54Z"},"message":"Upgrade bundled OpenSSL to 3.6.3 (#29487)\n\n## Summary\n\n- upgrade the bundled OpenSSL source from 3.5.5 to 3.6.3\n- update the Bazel `openssl-sys` build dependency to use the upgraded\nsource crate\n- refresh the Bazel module lockfile\n\n## Why\n\nOpenSSL 3.5.5 is within the affected ranges for security issues fixed in\nlater releases. The Rust `openssl-src` wrapper does not currently\npublish OpenSSL 3.5.7, so this moves the vendored Linux musl build to\nthe available patched 3.6.3 release.","tree":{"sha":"a0e1e35ec3b993a670c364889ff1e3b6cd1e551c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/a0e1e35ec3b993a670c364889ff1e3b6cd1e551c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/372b5ac7c2876ace31b736a35a19e09a45c6f798","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqObUKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKf4QAI34N8COOFdoqX0BbTAQJ5UU\nj7igRuCNuD8aam78kqYqHHkfSZNu2uWu6pmziUdMppm4HJhNrwn2Fz4Aas93e5Hb\n9SRw1EPar+InxqoWVoQJnPLxiuVj7TtEqHg5OZl7TK3rneC8V1HAOpcXInfrpGGJ\nLFmiYDAik53eBZVRwNwBYQ6uaWnr6Bjmjign5c0Vb0Muj9/FnBJHHYnI3FeuEzRP\nMt1MypcXdOQPgIdT6nFwXvpezZAp4wisIRmrpyoUxcJAFilMA7H9nGwPCxLvK/Dx\nuVeatylUzahZ5ViZ621czDyHkxVw0j5SuZe0ZvkmNT1XmbHy/lqWLV+Kplr0M7yr\nxK8TdFcv35kbh8VwAJ0Kyu2NpMQJy+sicDa/Sn0/IIdFMMQ3rXHQxuldGMcqdmiS\nskj7DYDsECPdvSIEn1VY/RF6JYCQUeT2370Oi3xls7CqU+HPfPRxIbdze8YUD4td\n3CJ4oryC5dibNeLIKYGkGuALYITwdscL+0BRxVQuwHEm4rNYrV3LjcStxxckBwSl\n7/1HEM4OfdZpIzycMPjtLUliehlN5FGKOkOvifmUcCtWauNQWwQsNdmPuW5CRm3M\nCXyyhqSHe9tITBi8uZVWnC+E5hO33y9nmw5GJvfeMkQU/1TW4dLX+nDeCC7V0ii6\nH5dIJI1nHqZ0jcXB+fi0\n=bzCl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a0e1e35ec3b993a670c364889ff1e3b6cd1e551c\nparent bf7148626b36e278e8473a09996f21ec6a0c7482\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782166794 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782166794 +0200\n\nUpgrade bundled OpenSSL to 3.6.3 (#29487)\n\n## Summary\n\n- upgrade the bundled OpenSSL source from 3.5.5 to 3.6.3\n- update the Bazel `openssl-sys` build dependency to use the upgraded\nsource crate\n- refresh the Bazel module lockfile\n\n## Why\n\nOpenSSL 3.5.5 is within the affected ranges for security issues fixed in\nlater releases. The Rust `openssl-src` wrapper does not currently\npublish OpenSSL 3.5.7, so this moves the vendored Linux musl build to\nthe available patched 3.6.3 release.","verified_at":"2026-06-22T22:19:56Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/372b5ac7c2876ace31b736a35a19e09a45c6f798","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/372b5ac7c2876ace31b736a35a19e09a45c6f798","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/372b5ac7c2876ace31b736a35a19e09a45c6f798/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"bf7148626b36e278e8473a09996f21ec6a0c7482","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bf7148626b36e278e8473a09996f21ec6a0c7482","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/bf7148626b36e278e8473a09996f21ec6a0c7482"}]},{"sha":"bf7148626b36e278e8473a09996f21ec6a0c7482","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGJmNzE0ODYyNmIzNmUyNzhlODQ3M2EwOTk5NmYyMWVjNmEwYzc0ODI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Ning","email":"ericning@openai.com","date":"2026-06-22T22:08:59Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T22:08:59Z"},"message":"[codex] fetch featured IDs for remote plugins (#29485)\n\n## Summary\n\n- fetch featured plugin IDs when the loaded catalog includes\n`openai-curated-remote`\n- extend the existing remote marketplace regression test to cover the\nfeatured IDs response\n\n## Why\n\nWhen the remote plugin catalog was enabled, app-server loaded\n`openai-curated-remote` but skipped `/plugins/featured` because the\nrequest processor only fetched featured IDs for the local\n`openai-curated` marketplace. As a result, the desktop app could not\nrender the backend-curated remote featured set.\n\nThis keeps the existing local behavior and also returns the curated\nranking for remote plugins.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nplugin_list_includes_remote_marketplaces_when_remote_plugin_enabled`","tree":{"sha":"23220da1f925732dbff7d74864b1a89393ab4eaa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/23220da1f925732dbff7d74864b1a89393ab4eaa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/bf7148626b36e278e8473a09996f21ec6a0c7482","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqObJ7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASHgQAD/edoyf9adDZjNqhYyDRlLi\n1DF1SIg6SJEEBE80tTx//Jkq1ll1WrwENM9jynA0Sgdmz8V1QOxeyHkDY1ZlmrEA\n6H2GNm2Ebbwi9dkRQO8SwfvR1Li6GU4AxWw9zTHgEhkVW5+wHTHB/mv9cnOSVUJx\n5Czd3uSOfcrr0W9o737yNTVaMi7NKM8+hxFhL6dUstXYWoij9PrBRUsjy0jBz7xh\nWLf4btR/7j/k2YZhQPc8LfGJsZKHOHYrdLUY1QIGBu+WtLHE/W5CClkTTgHuJxKI\n/Ya/YXL38SrOs1M2CsL1EDold6olDGoJH/IJJ64OYOhEQtVXviKCKav/KHLskwkC\nNcvOumeWgEI56kM9O9MATs1aWWYTInlwLuuvq3GBYPbv3QvwDEnJinU70xg20UOX\n0oYrc0E2Q/XESyVDSvyLePWGsPjoLkdBCsKyyt+ncaEpysElNeTibHF2JdVtYhj1\n1Tcc+SZgsMKMoi23nSBZC0mHGrmNrGoNMAZwTarthFfCt6hCWTBx0grWwMnnAf3W\nHq2ihAwzkYs6q5Jb57Ji4rAUIN3csUSWIHfBj75aMUSE+M1ONn2VitA+1EzDKOUz\nCh8QEmlXNqnPgvBl+yNTN8ubwIaXNH8HbmnbS64VrL1aIVf5oJz912jai5eqw3HH\nSVK3iaJlyB+kOLp6uLI2\n=4xJS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 23220da1f925732dbff7d74864b1a89393ab4eaa\nparent ff37f4a6efc98c205809c2ae20e2c01e7b49040d\nauthor Eric Ning <ericning@openai.com> 1782166139 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782166139 -0700\n\n[codex] fetch featured IDs for remote plugins (#29485)\n\n## Summary\n\n- fetch featured plugin IDs when the loaded catalog includes\n`openai-curated-remote`\n- extend the existing remote marketplace regression test to cover the\nfeatured IDs response\n\n## Why\n\nWhen the remote plugin catalog was enabled, app-server loaded\n`openai-curated-remote` but skipped `/plugins/featured` because the\nrequest processor only fetched featured IDs for the local\n`openai-curated` marketplace. As a result, the desktop app could not\nrender the backend-curated remote featured set.\n\nThis keeps the existing local behavior and also returns the curated\nranking for remote plugins.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nplugin_list_includes_remote_marketplaces_when_remote_plugin_enabled`","verified_at":"2026-06-22T22:09:00Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bf7148626b36e278e8473a09996f21ec6a0c7482","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/bf7148626b36e278e8473a09996f21ec6a0c7482","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bf7148626b36e278e8473a09996f21ec6a0c7482/comments","author":{"login":"ericning-o","id":182030612,"node_id":"U_kgDOCtmRFA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/182030612?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o","html_url":"https://github.com/ericning-o","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/events{/privacy}","received