0e2c01e7b49040d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqObJPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcKwQACNzCnw2nXY5sJmOgfT7QJMI\n9WRh1V2LfoX4e6S/WE8ifw5FFviw8/cGYmQtJff/b6B9c2iYywd1J55EKD3hnyDS\nfsiN/qz2d94GUgk2uNeltmn+/m9TrEvpPgEYvoRBxTCJV4Aqqpa2X4aAne6rQO/y\nfqtHWzo+g3rhkufIPvSiHEGBc3x5wH5F7HykQCLlwv0jVuaszkPRNRw3+7fh2ulh\noh/76pC/yRO9D94zGqFYLeaTEcsSCF26i56ETx1QlScUgXS4tZAPS8ovnPkk/AbS\nl5byCYcrzN26nSUb05ryUFEEbN7ErzdpRhpRe1g66C85BYxrRzoh7E4o6LJvLpYo\nPPh0dUwDGKBIumQwg5V8I2J3B9ax7PFDaG6aKxCm/Di1INPLyFhFa/ZI30H8qpSs\nVHRTOX0NnGZCGJPWJOHH3QH4oGLcFY0D7kMli67moMGmd1B5HYPpiMbnthG0URjM\n+QLxjrMSKMiKwubT0vXQH7nYOX/dNU1b7OpmjCI1UKEN675emwo3hVZ6u/Nbz3Qd\nizABaYWsfT6+VPR3asdiz+E672uI8r04EyjsGonAmdLQdHX+PqPnTqSfur/Bn8l8\nIlOPvWcqHT+76eUSUzFOwvsD6SAg9LMOw8J+15iLu7Aj3dnJdqpJBPRH0ARCv9Hs\nIjXRZWfgT9rxusrIC05V\n=bCSv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3ca71697a58ce7f9a6853dc06a23e36d205fa2b9\nparent 5f129a4703ceaf843e1cb6996bbf4a4f21225198\nauthor Samuel Yuan <syuan@openai.com> 1782166095 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782166095 +0000\n\nRegister full CDP requirements feature (#28769)\n\nregister cdp requirements feature flag","verified_at":"2026-06-22T22:08:16Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ff37f4a6efc98c205809c2ae20e2c01e7b49040d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ff37f4a6efc98c205809c2ae20e2c01e7b49040d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ff37f4a6efc98c205809c2ae20e2c01e7b49040d/comments","author":{"login":"syuan-oai","id":226170383,"node_id":"U_kgDODXsWDw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/226170383?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syuan-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/syuan-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syuan-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syuan-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syuan-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syuan-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syuan-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syuan-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syuan-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syuan-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syuan-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5f129a4703ceaf843e1cb6996bbf4a4f21225198","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5f129a4703ceaf843e1cb6996bbf4a4f21225198","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/5f129a4703ceaf843e1cb6996bbf4a4f21225198"}]},{"sha":"5f129a4703ceaf843e1cb6996bbf4a4f21225198","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDVmMTI5YTQ3MDNjZWFmODQzZTFjYjY5OTZiYmY0YTRmMjEyMjUxOTg","commit":{"author":{"name":"canvrno-oai","email":"kbond@openai.com","date":"2026-06-22T21:38:33Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T21:38:33Z"},"message":"PAC 3 - Add Windows system proxy resolver (#26708)\n\n## Summary\n\nStacked on #26707.\n\nAdds the Windows implementation of the shared system-proxy contract.\nThis allows Codex-owned auth clients to use the route Windows selects\nfor each auth URL, including explicit PAC configuration, WPAD\nauto-detection, static proxies, and bypass rules.\n\nThe `respect_system_proxy` feature is disabled by default, so existing\nclient behavior remains unchanged unless explicitly enabled.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Adds Windows-only `codex-client` dependencies:\n- `windows-sys` with `Win32_Foundation` and `Win32_Networking_WinHttp`;\n  - `sha2` for redacted cache keys.\n- Dispatches system-proxy resolution to `outbound_proxy/windows.rs` on\nWindows.\n- Reads the current-user WinHTTP/IE proxy configuration via\n`WinHttpGetIEProxyConfigForCurrentUser`.\n- Resolves explicit PAC URLs first, then OS-enabled WPAD auto-detection,\nthen static proxy and bypass settings.\n- Uses `WinHttpGetProxyForUrl` for PAC/WPAD and maps results into the\nshared `SystemProxyDecision::{Direct, Proxy, Unavailable}` contract.\n- Parses `DIRECT`, `PROXY`, `HTTPS`, and keyed static proxy entries.\n- Treats unsupported schemes such as SOCKS as unavailable so the shared\nresolver can apply its environment-proxy fallback.\n- Handles Windows bypass entries, including `<local>` and host, suffix,\nwildcard, and port matching.\n- Releases WinHTTP-owned strings with `GlobalFree` and closes sessions\nwith `WinHttpCloseHandle`.\n- Hashes URL-specific cache keys with SHA-256 so PAC decisions remain\nURL-specific without retaining raw request URLs or query strings.\n\n## End-user behavior\n\n- Disabled/default: existing client behavior is unchanged.\n- Enabled with `[features.respect_system_proxy]`:\n- Windows auth clients honor explicit PAC configuration, OS-enabled\nWPAD, static proxies, and bypass rules;\n  - valid OS/PAC `DIRECT` decisions use a direct connection;\n- unavailable system resolution falls back to explicit environment proxy\nvariables, then `DIRECT`, through the shared contract from #26707.\n- Unsupported proxy schemes are not silently translated into a different\nroute.\n- Custom CA handling remains separate from proxy selection.\n\n## Tests\n\nAdds coverage for:\n\n- PAC-style proxy tokens such as `PROXY proxy.internal:8080` and `HTTPS\nproxy.internal:8443`;\n- static WinHTTP proxy entries keyed by target scheme;\n- `DIRECT` and unsupported proxy-token behavior;\n- Windows bypass matching, including `<local>`, wildcard, suffix, and\nport-qualified entries;\n- preserving URL-specific PAC cache decisions without retaining the raw\nURL on Windows.","tree":{"sha":"4851191f91f46a082859b7acbd55b34a6c66861e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/4851191f91f46a082859b7acbd55b34a6c66861e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/5f129a4703ceaf843e1cb6996bbf4a4f21225198","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOatZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXocQABPIY2DqZkE1GWXVrJu3fJqV\nderRnq/HrF4ZVYxPkkt7gyi2SDYBr0AlYh2GDF07FfLUZrG5jyMrC/0uoei/kmfd\nl42G26PUDN9fg0nphFoYSoqvykP6X8geL1QTevAgZBQborhGVY6g2lrWB4Qm64sH\nZAYa3RT/KeUwkoBYDnTRLUTVf5PNOYANbrOSFsaa8WKPEz3mU3clJD84X6BV/KLC\nNMNR+KGDL+81gliAJ8/AT/Oh8FZnTEb/9sYKceehslRyBqb2jCCPrOBddfP0xO2c\n033Xh+J0yEdWiEB4ZAJqU0BjvXkutNy7TC43OMwRhXUMtqAsz3AAQA8J8w4DBVU5\nUAU8aVxBMQZXQc2W6/EiIJHrQyVyQvdgUCBm2ntX9bDJoyswGLP08wQc78pIFqMh\nXSnaSSgiB+qytarsgsC/1Yl0lzyuEJCa8rada0kB7h0GE11LK955a+5pvvu+Mzde\nfbIyX2lwxrSwLXJqcYpqpWHNwyyXN35B6apBOFy5M/CgyAK+Db87Sea2YUKX3ZBh\nXvMghlTQaR8SUVcuI4x0rp68bqHJmCY4VFlHPmMb7/ECeT97hikgTYV6KDAe2YYw\nYr6BfVV9d2JELcmKxRw+eEXOlj6CoaQi0/UWDk0ADh1YmQPiC7rzR69g+vInAPhs\n6UnuwumrXvujkQAy3Qu1\n=o+qJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4851191f91f46a082859b7acbd55b34a6c66861e\nparent a72433d5606984e71dc37a83a65a6f91af5c84b4\nauthor canvrno-oai <kbond@openai.com> 1782164313 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782164313 -0700\n\nPAC 3 - Add Windows system proxy resolver (#26708)\n\n## Summary\n\nStacked on #26707.\n\nAdds the Windows implementation of the shared system-proxy contract.\nThis allows Codex-owned auth clients to use the route Windows selects\nfor each auth URL, including explicit PAC configuration, WPAD\nauto-detection, static proxies, and bypass rules.\n\nThe `respect_system_proxy` feature is disabled by default, so existing\nclient behavior remains unchanged unless explicitly enabled.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Adds Windows-only `codex-client` dependencies:\n- `windows-sys` with `Win32_Foundation` and `Win32_Networking_WinHttp`;\n  - `sha2` for redacted cache keys.\n- Dispatches system-proxy resolution to `outbound_proxy/windows.rs` on\nWindows.\n- Reads the current-user WinHTTP/IE proxy configuration via\n`WinHttpGetIEProxyConfigForCurrentUser`.\n- Resolves explicit PAC URLs first, then OS-enabled WPAD auto-detection,\nthen static proxy and bypass settings.\n- Uses `WinHttpGetProxyForUrl` for PAC/WPAD and maps results into the\nshared `SystemProxyDecision::{Direct, Proxy, Unavailable}` contract.\n- Parses `DIRECT`, `PROXY`, `HTTPS`, and keyed static proxy entries.\n- Treats unsupported schemes such as SOCKS as unavailable so the shared\nresolver can apply its environment-proxy fallback.\n- Handles Windows bypass entries, including `<local>` and host, suffix,\nwildcard, and port matching.\n- Releases WinHTTP-owned strings with `GlobalFree` and closes sessions\nwith `WinHttpCloseHandle`.\n- Hashes URL-specific cache keys with SHA-256 so PAC decisions remain\nURL-specific without retaining raw request URLs or query strings.\n\n## End-user behavior\n\n- Disabled/default: existing client behavior is unchanged.\n- Enabled with `[features.respect_system_proxy]`:\n- Windows auth clients honor explicit PAC configuration, OS-enabled\nWPAD, static proxies, and bypass rules;\n  - valid OS/PAC `DIRECT` decisions use a direct connection;\n- unavailable system resolution falls back to explicit environment proxy\nvariables, then `DIRECT`, through the shared contract from #26707.\n- Unsupported proxy schemes are not silently translated into a different\nroute.\n- Custom CA handling remains separate from proxy selection.\n\n## Tests\n\nAdds coverage for:\n\n- PAC-style proxy tokens such as `PROXY proxy.internal:8080` and `HTTPS\nproxy.internal:8443`;\n- static WinHTTP proxy entries keyed by target scheme;\n- `DIRECT` and unsupported proxy-token behavior;\n- Windows bypass matching, including `<local>`, wildcard, suffix, and\nport-qualified entries;\n- preserving URL-specific PAC cache decisions without retaining the raw\nURL on Windows.","verified_at":"2026-06-22T21:38:34Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5f129a4703ceaf843e1cb6996bbf4a4f21225198","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/5f129a4703ceaf843e1cb6996bbf4a4f21225198","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5f129a4703ceaf843e1cb6996bbf4a4f21225198/comments","author":{"login":"canvrno-oai","id":257630656,"node_id":"U_kgDOD1shwA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257630656?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/canvrno-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a72433d5606984e71dc37a83a65a6f91af5c84b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a72433d5606984e71dc37a83a65a6f91af5c84b4","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a72433d5606984e71dc37a83a65a6f91af5c84b4"}]},{"sha":"a72433d5606984e71dc37a83a65a6f91af5c84b4","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGE3MjQzM2Q1NjA2OTg0ZTcxZGMzN2E4M2E2NWE2ZjkxYWY1Yzg0YjQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"jameswt-oai","email":"jameswt@openai.com","date":"2026-06-22T21:28:39Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T21:28:39Z"},"message":"[codex-core-plugins] Remote Plugin ID Persisted to File (#27669)\n\n## This PR\n\nRemote plugin analytics cannot rely only on the in-memory\ninstalled-plugin snapshot because that snapshot is refreshed\nasynchronously after startup. This PR persists the authoritative backend\nidentity alongside each cached remote plugin bundle so later consumers\ncan resolve it without a network request.\n\n### Behavior\n\n- Store Codex-owned remote installation metadata in an atomic\n`.codex-remote-plugin-install.json` sidecar under the plugin cache root.\n- Use a versioned, snake_case schema:\n\n  ```json\n  {\n    \"schema_version\": 1,\n    \"remote_plugin_id\": \"plugins~Plugin_...\"\n  }\n  ```\n\n- Write the metadata during remote bundle installation.\n- Backfill it when bundle sync finds an already-current cached bundle.\n- Clear it when a generic/local install replaces the cache.\n- Let existing uninstall and stale-cache removal delete it with the\nplugin cache root.\n- Reject unsupported schema versions rather than silently misreading\nfuture formats.\n\nThis PR does not change analytics serialization or event behavior.\n\n### Review surface\n\nThe implementation is limited to four `codex-core-plugins` files:\n\n- `store.rs`: owns the versioned sidecar read/write/remove lifecycle.\n- `remote_bundle.rs`: persists the backend ID after a remote bundle\ninstall.\n- `remote/remote_installed_plugin_sync.rs`: backfills metadata for an\nalready-current cached bundle.\n- Tests cover the storage lifecycle and both remote write paths.\n\n## Testing / Validation\n\n### Automated\n\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins` (268 tests passed)\n- `just fix -p codex-core-plugins` passes with one pre-existing\n`large_enum_variant` warning in `manifest.rs`.\n- Coverage verifies the exact filename and JSON schema, identity\nreplacement, local reinstall clearing, uninstall cleanup, remote bundle\ninstallation, unsupported schema rejection, and installed-plugin sync\nbackfill.\n\n### Live manual validation\n\nValidated the production app-server RPC path with an isolated temporary\n`CODEX_HOME` and the PR-built Codex binary. The app-server communicated\nover stdio and did not bind a port.\n\nTest plugin: `plugins~Plugin_b80dd84519148191a409cde181c9b3d6`\n(`build-macos-apps@openai-curated-remote`).\n\n1. Confirmed `plugin/read` initially reported the plugin uninstalled.\n2. Installed it through `plugin/install` and confirmed version `0.1.4`\nwas cached.\n3. Verified\n`$CODEX_HOME/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/build-macos-apps/.codex-remote-plugin-install.json`\nwas created beside the `0.1.4/` bundle directory with mode `0600` and\nthe expected contents:\n\n   ```json\n   {\n     \"schema_version\": 1,\n\"remote_plugin_id\": \"plugins~Plugin_b80dd84519148191a409cde181c9b3d6\"\n   }\n   ```\n\n4. Deleted only the sidecar, restarted the app-server, and confirmed\ninstalled-plugin startup sync recreated it with the same contents.\n5. Uninstalled through `plugin/uninstall`, confirmed `plugin/read`\nreturned `installed: false`, and verified the local plugin cache root\nwas removed.\n6. Restored the account's original uninstalled state and removed the\nisolated home and copied credentials.\n\n## Split Overview\n\n```text\nmain\n├── #27093  Debug analytics capture                     merged\n│   └── #27099  Non-mutating plugin smoke               merged\n│       └── #27100  Remote install/uninstall smoke      merged\n└── #27102  Plugin telemetry metadata refactor          merged\n    └── #27669  Persist remote plugin identity           ← this PR\n\nNext:\n└── Final PR: add explicit local and remote IDs to plugin analytics\n```\n\nThis PR is based directly on `main`; prerequisite\n[#27102](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27102) has merged. The\noriginal combined [#26281](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/26281)\nremains the aggregate reference until the final replacement PR is\npublished.","tree":{"sha":"69a796bd13ed4ce51977530759f672bd88888951","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/69a796bd13ed4ce51977530759f672bd88888951"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/a72433d5606984e71dc37a83a65a6f91af5c84b4","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOakHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAT54QAAvIDk5FmB5bbT9fUSszWVXs\nVuD7EigDbdkCWXucLnsUf2hFDCL+s01zCcFd2FI7vO0eXN/FSjyLDRzWqWpwaLzm\n1Gnp/Sw44DhpRsYSEchzGfl9++lGo+BhzN2y9vbU91QoM0TkYB8Puq8UY9Dn1U+H\nXP6gIDs4EHR5D5OolN9dUnJq03sRxV4SaFAnzeJ6kb+ZaClnbE97MOxOopWL6gSW\nOZyDvawC38YNaiyvKqFSaZb725iIyulzMgAr7lgYM3YhsnmDK5QM3TVyzFX8Wm56\nmFgnvY38/eYMxXKHY3kruI6c6fZ5HbXJM5KNgaS9s5o7I6PxjFgHJ2NBp5zNbNjW\n/1QDZZBIPa00MEgTVYiUOJ7tiHuGZ3RqwJVSmWv7tlzt4hCryfehTXVbZu+KHFqo\nl+uWuAjPtTvWvdGngGpM4plzU1+fsHv/ERJe41UwNNizUQEeDLQ85CHURYl41qHU\nd0A9k/K3xTkWr6JKkAfdqI7jSudOL3Owokrs8VJwx9xoH/9QEKCMLhaDSsGRaVMf\n2Uj4smxvYQI1c6ZTEbcsYIGRZIwCKHkNrIufE8GAyV2H1c8XroH1FuO0TESqtUSW\nhuipgqPbbivorjA5n9fh5Smei1fKIYjWmlwC5H54+AhTlJp7yQLWKPGvzysOZQsz\n4UCLWT0G7ekWmvfHgPLW\n=HkfK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 69a796bd13ed4ce51977530759f672bd88888951\nparent 0a9b7d2c36937420135efdcfe7b960d34b763d8f\nauthor jameswt-oai <jameswt@openai.com> 1782163719 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782163719 -0700\n\n[codex-core-plugins] Remote Plugin ID Persisted to File (#27669)\n\n## This PR\n\nRemote plugin analytics cannot rely only on the in-memory\ninstalled-plugin snapshot because that snapshot is refreshed\nasynchronously after startup. This PR persists the authoritative backend\nidentity alongside each cached remote plugin bundle so later consumers\ncan resolve it without a network request.\n\n### Behavior\n\n- Store Codex-owned remote installation metadata in an atomic\n`.codex-remote-plugin-install.json` sidecar under the plugin cache root.\n- Use a versioned, snake_case schema:\n\n  ```json\n  {\n    \"schema_version\": 1,\n    \"remote_plugin_id\": \"plugins~Plugin_...\"\n  }\n  ```\n\n- Write the metadata during remote bundle installation.\n- Backfill it when bundle sync finds an already-current cached bundle.\n- Clear it when a generic/local install replaces the cache.\n- Let existing uninstall and stale-cache removal delete it with the\nplugin cache root.\n- Reject unsupported schema versions rather than silently misreading\nfuture formats.\n\nThis PR does not change analytics serialization or event behavior.\n\n### Review surface\n\nThe implementation is limited to four `codex-core-plugins` files:\n\n- `store.rs`: owns the versioned sidecar read/write/remove lifecycle.\n- `remote_bundle.rs`: persists the backend ID after a remote bundle\ninstall.\n- `remote/remote_installed_plugin_sync.rs`: backfills metadata for an\nalready-current cached bundle.\n- Tests cover the storage lifecycle and both remote write paths.\n\n## Testing / Validation\n\n### Automated\n\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins` (268 tests passed)\n- `just fix -p codex-core-plugins` passes with one pre-existing\n`large_enum_variant` warning in `manifest.rs`.\n- Coverage verifies the exact filename and JSON schema, identity\nreplacement, local reinstall clearing, uninstall cleanup, remote bundle\ninstallation, unsupported schema rejection, and installed-plugin sync\nbackfill.\n\n### Live manual validation\n\nValidated the production app-server RPC path with an isolated temporary\n`CODEX_HOME` and the PR-built Codex binary. The app-server communicated\nover stdio and did not bind a port.\n\nTest plugin: `plugins~Plugin_b80dd84519148191a409cde181c9b3d6`\n(`build-macos-apps@openai-curated-remote`).\n\n1. Confirmed `plugin/read` initially reported the plugin uninstalled.\n2. Installed it through `plugin/install` and confirmed version `0.1.4`\nwas cached.\n3. Verified\n`$CODEX_HOME/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/build-macos-apps/.codex-remote-plugin-install.json`\nwas created beside the `0.1.4/` bundle directory with mode `0600` and\nthe expected contents:\n\n   ```json\n   {\n     \"schema_version\": 1,\n\"remote_plugin_id\": \"plugins~Plugin_b80dd84519148191a409cde181c9b3d6\"\n   }\n   ```\n\n4. Deleted only the sidecar, restarted the app-server, and confirmed\ninstalled-plugin startup sync recreated it with the same contents.\n5. Uninstalled through `plugin/uninstall`, confirmed `plugin/read`\nreturned `installed: false`, and verified the local plugin cache root\nwas removed.\n6. Restored the account's original uninstalled state and removed the\nisolated home and copied credentials.\n\n## Split Overview\n\n```text\nmain\n├── #27093  Debug analytics capture                     merged\n│   └── #27099  Non-mutating plugin smoke               merged\n│       └── #27100  Remote install/uninstall smoke      merged\n└── #27102  Plugin telemetry metadata refactor          merged\n    └── #27669  Persist remote plugin identity           ← this PR\n\nNext:\n└── Final PR: add explicit local and remote IDs to plugin analytics\n```\n\nThis PR is based directly on `main`; prerequisite\n[#27102](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27102) has merged. The\noriginal combined [#26281](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/26281)\nremains the aggregate reference until the final replacement PR is\npublished.","verified_at":"2026-06-22T21:28:40Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a72433d5606984e71dc37a83a65a6f91af5c84b4","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a72433d5606984e71dc37a83a65a6f91af5c84b4","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a72433d5606984e71dc37a83a65a6f91af5c84b4/comments","author":{"login":"jameswt-oai","id":247462917,"node_id":"U_kgDODr_8BQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247462917?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jameswt-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0a9b7d2c36937420135efdcfe7b960d34b763d8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0a9b7d2c36937420135efdcfe7b960d34b763d8f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/0a9b7d2c36937420135efdcfe7b960d34b763d8f"}]},{"sha":"0a9b7d2c36937420135efdcfe7b960d34b763d8f","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDBhOWI3ZDJjMzY5Mzc0MjAxMzVlZmRjZmU3Yjk2MGQzNGI3NjNkOGY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Anton Panasenko","email":"apanasenko@openai.com","date":"2026-06-22T21:24:02Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T21:24:02Z"},"message":"chore: advance tungstenite fork pins (#29480)\n\n## Why\n\n`openai-oss-forks/tokio-tungstenite` now includes the updated\n`tungstenite` fork revision from\n[openai-oss-forks/tokio-tungstenite#3](https://github.com/openai-oss-forks/tokio-tungstenite/pull/3).\nCodex should consume the merged fork commit and resolve its direct and\ntransitive `tungstenite` dependencies to the same revision instead of\nretaining the older pins.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Advanced the `tokio-tungstenite` git pin to\n`0e5b2d73aa18dd9f0a50ee9ff199d5aef7594186`.\n- Advanced the `tungstenite` fork pin to\n`4fffad30fe373adbdcffab9545e9e9bf4f2fc19f` and adjusted the patch source\nso the transitive dependency resolves to that revision.\n- Updated `Cargo.lock` and `MODULE.bazel.lock` to match the dependency\ngraph.","tree":{"sha":"7aaa0dd02240c3a16622b84e5e027ff9d1a52114","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/7aaa0dd02240c3a16622b84e5e027ff9d1a52114"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/0a9b7d2c36937420135efdcfe7b960d34b763d8f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOafyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACQ4QAHnCDgLTKbE+4Uv3DBa9oe7I\nAeqMZY66CfvBLoaGAnErnrtd6Xexxfu/P/DlQvQxqux7cmZaLCyrKkEy15XQDabw\nDNhdStWQmRpoTu6XWDWJZ8Ac2agF8rvDI1RrgAXqlqdCR7MhUSyfAagD4YcsueaT\ng550zDJzqBeLh8RykmG2SRTiY/3Og7HEea+qKe9trP9j2L08QnCGlmMUx04Nmqfi\nip9rCYXbPc+vmL5wMFWvHfvmg6qpVGGulOetc4zDnZhNX14sjqy5akUr5tbIMBmy\nhiWu1kDRQJ7hrNbrNoAJxrEfqpvEgX0R9ZbMGC5pIHX1tOG12rw5IBicXR1NNAy4\nWXWtUDQapLNAKABY0vOBlBS66qJZaK90zEFVjrP3Kb9wt32BZ+Fs+yRDCELT2D4I\nR62MV1knLZF/DyPioKncbr/NFm9Khh9foCkicRjsqmJPBgO39eDqdtxeIVxRudjd\nAt9+fxKbbslO6hferVwlf6akTV70y0l0NVPySXcOJGJzqr7oSTirPIINBetxfqUM\nIIhWtWvPE5yp3FPwXvkUx9ZiM1qMrVC4mTI1CZt+nDNWzEWdizR4GWCroBq5SWCL\n3uZDHq6/1KE20jAXUibqgZvShA8p6AuU/+axGwg5iBKineDYF96Qqk98dDffZOBD\nY1XnpsCtxrDsDHk8B8Zz\n=gtvx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7aaa0dd02240c3a16622b84e5e027ff9d1a52114\nparent 527ccb4a5df8a75d6aeb4c6ae4341f99a1205a1e\nauthor Anton Panasenko <apanasenko@openai.com> 1782163442 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782163442 -0700\n\nchore: advance tungstenite fork pins (#29480)\n\n## Why\n\n`openai-oss-forks/tokio-tungstenite` now includes the updated\n`tungstenite` fork revision from\n[openai-oss-forks/tokio-tungstenite#3](https://github.com/openai-oss-forks/tokio-tungstenite/pull/3).\nCodex should consume the merged fork commit and resolve its direct and\ntransitive `tungstenite` dependencies to the same revision instead of\nretaining the older pins.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Advanced the `tokio-tungstenite` git pin to\n`0e5b2d73aa18dd9f0a50ee9ff199d5aef7594186`.\n- Advanced the `tungstenite` fork pin to\n`4fffad30fe373adbdcffab9545e9e9bf4f2fc19f` and adjusted the patch source\nso the transitive dependency resolves to that revision.\n- Updated `Cargo.lock` and `MODULE.bazel.lock` to match the dependency\ngraph.","verified_at":"2026-06-22T21:24:02Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0a9b7d2c36937420135efdcfe7b960d34b763d8f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/0a9b7d2c36937420135efdcfe7b960d34b763d8f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0a9b7d2c36937420135efdcfe7b960d34b763d8f/comments","author":{"login":"apanasenko-oai","id":228802911,"node_id":"U_kgDODaNBXw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228802911?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/apanasenko-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"527ccb4a5df8a75d6aeb4c6ae4341f99a1205a1e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/527ccb4a5df8a75d6aeb4c6ae4341f99a1205a1e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/527ccb4a5df8a75d6aeb4c6ae4341f99a1205a1e"}]},{"sha":"527ccb4a5df8a75d6aeb4c6ae4341f99a1205a1e","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDUyN2NjYjRhNWRmOGE3NWQ2YWViNGM2YWU0MzQxZjk5YTEyMDVhMWU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Winston Howes","email":"winston@openai.com","date":"2026-06-22T21:16:48Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T21:16:48Z"},"message":"Honor startup custom CA bundles with managed MITM (#29014)\n\n## Why\n\nWhen Codex starts with a custom CA override such as\n`SSL_CERT_FILE=/path/to/corp-ca.pem codex`, `rustls-native-certs` treats\nthat override as a replacement for the platform trust store. The managed\nproxy then rewrites child CA variables to its generated bundle, so the\ncustom root or the ordinary platform roots can be lost. The proxy's\nupstream TLS connector must trust the same roots or private and\ncorporate upstream certificates still fail after interception.\n\n## What\n\n- load platform-native roots without consulting inherited CA override\nvariables\n- append certificates from the existing curated startup CA file\nvariables and `SSL_CERT_DIR`\n- share those platform and startup roots with the MITM upstream rustls\nconnector\n- exclude the Codex managed MITM CA from upstream trust\n- normalize OpenSSL `TRUSTED CERTIFICATE` blocks while dropping trailing\ntrust metadata\n- skip an inherited current Codex-managed bundle so nested launches do\nnot duplicate it\n- append the Codex managed MITM CA to the child-facing bundle\n- copy certificate material only, so a private key or unrelated text\ncolocated in a startup file is never exposed through the public bundle\n\nThis is intentionally limited to CA paths present when Codex starts. It\ndoes not parse inline shell assignments or add per-command bundle\nmaterialization.\n\nThis changes only `codex-network-proxy` and dependency metadata; it does\nnot touch `codex-core` or sandbox orchestration.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-network-proxy`\n- includes an end-to-end upstream TLS test using a server trusted only\nby the startup custom CA\n- `just fix -p codex-network-proxy`\n- `just bazel-lock-check`","tree":{"sha":"385386c29d8eddad137da859bbcf115c13c0392e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/385386c29d8eddad137da859bbcf115c13c0392e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/527ccb4a5df8a75d6aeb4c6ae4341f99a1205a1e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOaZACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAg74QAGqtew1DayLdFUaTU9IKjNyZ\ncu/WLK3Z3488WSVbsvLuQoQGRBS+8tnwNJqdbLXjHnM5PP4a/rpohY9nxyjlLA9y\nRX2u7rbph3OyuQhTzSX1vwn1eCIPBKx/uFAv4ANJkxF1ckBK3FssrG3S2bmrToOH\nuw4ELB9EVQ9L/9QjthPEPmg0nayxdAsn+fMxDC8TPqV6/j5QzaHxiFIgBXpHPHhC\nZwGvzrzk3sVL/ll8Ou+3B4/ohT1sfrhJRL23IKB6ueMwo54Idvj3qmYK0MueLnKC\nLFHbjNfBEbqMIiJK5AOo1W2AQjogd7oxEI1lf993eG2IOw32mWGd8iyehjXbSs9u\nu6Qp/rP319apsdOhZ9vb9GNwRbioeXAJh7+YOf2lN5iFnNpqKN3QiMF7OMMBdAmz\nhxobtxHLnlL+YSS4ufzDGUZT3CqecwyeS3U1zHDwV4fcnXWyMutYpHdDG8SF74aV\nfcZ2Cj1qjfZpTJZ1LnWd+QXWLi5WSr8MJ7IluU0y6bTCOCqwn4I4+HjWCqZP28gB\nZePFg9+mpxmEcXcIPzk1gBNFXHniCdAv9pCoyXsGF3kIRKDYVz6YMxO4XjQcO53r\nAEGWmujTgQCxDciLT/w+hlU8mooHkqCf3RIlftWYoCmnLo7gfXCyETIHYH9mIIrp\nfGrjLJfEzZ0Q7ViBCS5D\n=n9vw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 385386c29d8eddad137da859bbcf115c13c0392e\nparent 6db576895a808608d65578f9d704971601c23c9b\nauthor Winston Howes <winston@openai.com> 1782163008 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782163008 -0700\n\nHonor startup custom CA bundles with managed MITM (#29014)\n\n## Why\n\nWhen Codex starts with a custom CA override such as\n`SSL_CERT_FILE=/path/to/corp-ca.pem codex`, `rustls-native-certs` treats\nthat override as a replacement for the platform trust store. The managed\nproxy then rewrites child CA variables to its generated bundle, so the\ncustom root or the ordinary platform roots can be lost. The proxy's\nupstream TLS connector must trust the same roots or private and\ncorporate upstream certificates still fail after interception.\n\n## What\n\n- load platform-native roots without consulting inherited CA override\nvariables\n- append certificates from the existing curated startup CA file\nvariables and `SSL_CERT_DIR`\n- share those platform and startup roots with the MITM upstream rustls\nconnector\n- exclude the Codex managed MITM CA from upstream trust\n- normalize OpenSSL `TRUSTED CERTIFICATE` blocks while dropping trailing\ntrust metadata\n- skip an inherited current Codex-managed bundle so nested launches do\nnot duplicate it\n- append the Codex managed MITM CA to the child-facing bundle\n- copy certificate material only, so a private key or unrelated text\ncolocated in a startup file is never exposed through the public bundle\n\nThis is intentionally limited to CA paths present when Codex starts. It\ndoes not parse inline shell assignments or add per-command bundle\nmaterialization.\n\nThis changes only `codex-network-proxy` and dependency metadata; it does\nnot touch `codex-core` or sandbox orchestration.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-network-proxy`\n- includes an end-to-end upstream TLS test using a server trusted only\nby the startup custom CA\n- `just fix -p codex-network-proxy`\n- `just bazel-lock-check`","verified_at":"2026-06-22T21:16:49Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/527ccb4a5df8a75d6aeb4c6ae4341f99a1205a1e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/527ccb4a5df8a75d6aeb4c6ae4341f99a1205a1e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/527ccb4a5df8a75d6aeb4c6ae4341f99a1205a1e/comments","author":{"login":"winston-openai","id":177672674,"node_id":"U_kgDOCpcR4g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177672674?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/winston-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6db576895a808608d65578f9d704971601c23c9b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6db576895a808608d65578f9d704971601c23c9b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6db576895a808608d65578f9d704971601c23c9b"}]},{"sha":"6db576895a808608d65578f9d704971601c23c9b","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDZkYjU3Njg5NWE4MDg2MDhkNjU1NzhmOWQ3MDQ5NzE2MDFjMjNjOWI","commit":{"author":{"name":"viyatb-oai","email":"viyatb@openai.com","date":"2026-06-22T21:05:50Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T21:05:50Z"},"message":"fix(config): address permission profile review follow-ups (#29479)\n\n## Summary\n\n- rename `Config::permission_profile_allowed` to\n`is_permission_profile_allowed`\n- use `BUILT_IN_PERMISSION_PROFILE_DANGER_FULL_ACCESS` in the TUI and\nits assertion\n- follow up on the late review comments from #26678\n\nThe previous `:danger-no-sandbox` value was an invalid built-in profile\nID. #26678 corrected it to `:danger-full-access`; this PR centralizes\nthe value to prevent future drift.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Not run per request; `cargo fmt` only\n\nCo-authored-by: Codex <noreply@openai.com>","tree":{"sha":"72179079dddf5c4c76813877c956ab3a56daa630","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/72179079dddf5c4c76813877c956ab3a56daa630"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/6db576895a808608d65578f9d704971601c23c9b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOaOuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqVMQAFGlJUNykLI1XXtfKFf90zLL\n8Re6JQkYxikguHDNEPLWJgLNR28SibAm4Sm3/L7e8PNU09O80agVagRHR3Hz9QQn\nYnpwBIzZCmEqFFUDt4LZ/Dt7D6luTKFLxDuTtgerXV53DTLzmI9ESr96UihB8Kaz\nk8CeBYrCItWXKxjedgULBcA04KMBOEJqpIJLhQbXRyilAlvylbEVdd/B0VOsjLlS\n4N0irzgS6VNezcs50ntXUEsT5yTS60DVMGRO9IfWybphg8ZysHjya7jNsXRMtvT8\nGw5ysEuY1b0/o/6LkNpgn7H0CzJmmSYa/EVeN8+A+ScCs/MeqaptFXrdD9jCzCn/\n7bazKO3MUI0oMHeCnLzgrIJgrhUzmF0E2+EZbjAhjNzfghBCJrduf8UrPungGc0h\nt/PRzkpN6R3GoZ3LWTkVSs9oQ2Wwt9LnkemFrFZMvd7aDKKnTg1Jc+e/yg7h9knC\nE9rg2+vu71T2g6Q4/4PenHCach6Xv7je1Ql8Mcj1MiH0PM2k/HnuMuE6UoSDFPib\nVzc6p/P993Bsz413jV0f/4j7FGGrGI85+4Qg4wViVzSCbN3NR00nxirgZGrMqnlN\ntmN6ApskUJqQHA8w3sv74mH//9p4fYWZPW0gOi5F6QHPN05+ZTxtWYCsUOx2e9u6\nxeQF0uLV8ivM7KX17uwn\n=wsXt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 72179079dddf5c4c76813877c956ab3a56daa630\nparent cb255c52e93bab74d35be7a093d0770a8dd66772\nauthor viyatb-oai <viyatb@openai.com> 1782162350 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782162350 +0000\n\nfix(config): address permission profile review follow-ups (#29479)\n\n## Summary\n\n- rename `Config::permission_profile_allowed` to\n`is_permission_profile_allowed`\n- use `BUILT_IN_PERMISSION_PROFILE_DANGER_FULL_ACCESS` in the TUI and\nits assertion\n- follow up on the late review comments from #26678\n\nThe previous `:danger-no-sandbox` value was an invalid built-in profile\nID. #26678 corrected it to `:danger-full-access`; this PR centralizes\nthe value to prevent future drift.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Not run per request; `cargo fmt` only\n\nCo-authored-by: Codex <noreply@openai.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-22T21:05:51Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6db576895a808608d65578f9d704971601c23c9b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6db576895a808608d65578f9d704971601c23c9b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6db576895a808608d65578f9d704971601c23c9b/comments","author":{"login":"viyatb-oai","id":234056686,"node_id":"U_kgDODfNr7g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234056686?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/viyatb-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"cb255c52e93bab74d35be7a093d0770a8dd66772","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/cb255c52e93bab74d35be7a093d0770a8dd66772","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/cb255c52e93bab74d35be7a093d0770a8dd66772"}]},{"sha":"cb255c52e93bab74d35be7a093d0770a8dd66772","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGNiMjU1YzUyZTkzYmFiNzRkMzViZTdhMDkzZDA3NzBhOGRkNjY3NzI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Celia Chen","email":"celia@openai.com","date":"2026-06-22T20:55:32Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T20:55:32Z"},"message":"[codex] handle request_user_input in app-server test client (#29476)\n\n## Why\n\n`codex-app-server-test-client` previously treated\n`item/tool/requestUserInput` as an unsupported server request and\nterminated the connection. That made it impossible to use the client for\nend-to-end testing of interactive turns: an operator could observe the\nrequest, but could not answer it and confirm that the same turn resumed.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Handle `ToolRequestUserInput` server requests in the test client's\ncentral request dispatcher.\n- Render numbered terminal choices, accept exact option labels, support\nfree-form `Other` and text-only questions, and collect multiple answers.\n- Send a protocol-native `ToolRequestUserInputResponse` and continue\nstreaming the active turn.\n- Fail clearly when interactive input is requested without a terminal.\n- Document the interactive behavior and add focused tests for option\nselection, free-form answers, multiple questions, and invalid-selection\nretries.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-test-client`\n- `just bazel-lock-check`\n- Manually exercised the app-server flow, selected `TUI`, observed\n`serverRequest/resolved`, and verified that the same turn completed with\nthe selected answer.","tree":{"sha":"d5cec17b381a53f427baa2b26df487d42a53aca9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/d5cec17b381a53f427baa2b26df487d42a53aca9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/cb255c52e93bab74d35be7a093d0770a8dd66772","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOaFECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcS4QAJF/H8Cnuch7hOan7OCOtUUB\nEmPS2jjSd24zIMG5qGQ4n/qYrg4Vkxb9tJjZSAqgguROXUGw6ZcXr5Zus9lhXN0k\naChMOus4B+/JSYWXxS/8xNCtmq2IAM59PvW2d0yUvDikhhokhoIKv4YrSP0CAC3K\nicQwXf2GTuIwMZ2r/WUCDdhIalUWA0M1PmE8TVuMSgA4YMfEfIOh6447ltvMytbJ\nBTTdG+sspEhBgdX4i4XfNmB9o0sNlpYImKmNHUivDCAEYY9Fi5agQbZrwtHlEhaD\na5V4/PzQ+Wn7KZcbVFt9hbNYJ0OzPhJTWc9cECZ8PEAaVj5+PR7gd7WkY8w87Ty5\nEaK0mK3gGH3cluXmywHIX4sGP2tYOfGO7MYke5G8pMcB4IEDMqdmpGAfIxktkpr6\nZpk7vLW3O/FzmMTOS/6uI4tJapYEMtTxDdpOeH6bhbN/TqDIIN6EPBP/yBlkbnhx\n9z7zAceGog7NRFvOxV1iVxNFxO5QFoFPD9kO7YOuL8Cjtf8RyX3+vMAOyqkkZQBJ\nwHC0dOTdT2uTZl2ppJPXCXTqhBCcz5mtG7M2GuIsR6ZGbOHae3izkl/xlN/x4Pz2\nKWXitn+FYK8P1C/XSF+7eqFLzVZPfM9knPO4FDITnszc7yHwB7yGPpyp3LvqoWeo\nRpbr5IiVQb7NcUQT8i0x\n=chuc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d5cec17b381a53f427baa2b26df487d42a53aca9\nparent ced3e4b9a7576fe08950965f2584d4d0c0d96937\nauthor Celia Chen <celia@openai.com> 1782161732 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782161732 -0700\n\n[codex] handle request_user_input in app-server test client (#29476)\n\n## Why\n\n`codex-app-server-test-client` previously treated\n`item/tool/requestUserInput` as an unsupported server request and\nterminated the connection. That made it impossible to use the client for\nend-to-end testing of interactive turns: an operator could observe the\nrequest, but could not answer it and confirm that the same turn resumed.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Handle `ToolRequestUserInput` server requests in the test client's\ncentral request dispatcher.\n- Render numbered terminal choices, accept exact option labels, support\nfree-form `Other` and text-only questions, and collect multiple answers.\n- Send a protocol-native `ToolRequestUserInputResponse` and continue\nstreaming the active turn.\n- Fail clearly when interactive input is requested without a terminal.\n- Document the interactive behavior and add focused tests for option\nselection, free-form answers, multiple questions, and invalid-selection\nretries.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-test-client`\n- `just bazel-lock-check`\n- Manually exercised the app-server flow, selected `TUI`, observed\n`serverRequest/resolved`, and verified that the same turn completed with\nthe selected answer.","verified_at":"2026-06-22T20:55:33Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/cb255c52e93bab74d35be7a093d0770a8dd66772","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/cb255c52e93bab74d35be7a093d0770a8dd66772","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/cb255c52e93bab74d35be7a093d0770a8dd66772/comments","author":{"login":"celia-oai","id":209693228,"node_id":"U_kgDODH-qLA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/209693228?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/celia-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ced3e4b9a7576fe08950965f2584d4d0c0d96937","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ced3e4b9a7576fe08950965f2584d4d0c0d96937","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ced3e4b9a7576fe08950965f2584d4d0c0d96937"}]},{"sha":"ced3e4b9a7576fe08950965f2584d4d0c0d96937","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGNlZDNlNGI5YTc1NzZmZTA4OTUwOTY1ZjI1ODRkNGQwYzBkOTY5Mzc","commit":{"author":{"name":"viyatb-oai","email":"viyatb@openai.com","date":"2026-06-22T20:48:09Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T20:48:09Z"},"message":"permission profiles: expose availability to clients (#26678)\n\n## Why\n\n`permissionProfile/list` currently advertises every built-in and\nconfigured profile even when effective enterprise requirements prevent\nselecting it. That forces each client to reconstruct policy from\nlower-level requirement fields, which is easy to miss and difficult to\nkeep consistent.\n\nThe catalog should remain complete so clients can explain that an option\nwas disabled by an administrator, while also reporting whether each\nprofile is selectable.\n\n## What\n\n- Add an `allowed` field to each permission profile summary.\n- Build a shared catalog from the effective config and current\nrequirements, including `allowed_sandbox_modes`, `allowed_permissions`,\nand filesystem restrictions.\n- Use the shared catalog in app-server and the TUI so disallowed\nprofiles remain visible but cannot be selected.\n- Use the canonical `:danger-full-access` profile ID in the TUI.\n- Update the app-server schemas, API documentation, behavioral tests,\nand TUI snapshots.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis PR targets `main` directly and is independent of #24852. It\npreserves the current behavior where built-in profiles are constrained\nby sandbox-mode requirements and `allowed_permissions` applies to\nconfigured profiles.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core\npermission_profile_catalog_marks_profiles_disallowed_by_requirements`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server permission_profile_list`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `just test -p codex-tui profile_permissions`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n- `just fix -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `just fix -p codex-app-server`\n- `just fix -p codex-tui`\n- `just fmt`\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Codex <noreply@openai.com>\nCo-authored-by: Joey Trasatti <joey.trasatti@openai.com>","tree":{"sha":"a450eb525b29396c225ec106caff1c6bf2b217ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/a450eb525b29396c225ec106caff1c6bf2b217ec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/ced3e4b9a7576fe08950965f2584d4d0c0d96937","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOZ+JCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAR5YQABN6C2pCpp6aJor83wkH0TC2\n5MtFywVBdwqnplpqZjZYUQO/0aEPfDbQbGRo6aOWp8srRTeUvjmloW8jOl12ncqG\nLKWsBo/UOL4Tk8gZeI4n/7c4jAIoBxtf0S/8OxF6NKdwrpK8i5SWmETxke+qhxmb\n57WA6RAtNVV3gNCbrUmgp39G7UzrrVtgkqNU7jUSjQxEqUqZJ1IAOypUR4u26wls\njkSC15nrrgOUVQMGTeLPu0eNa6wEhMV900bkbx0DxPp7Nsz4vOc6NmWIok/N2Q2t\nHgsjj1/SCGrOvY9MNSHaTiXeLshMUoof+Itq97ZZXDJtm1VzwUy5DYzKpT5vQgpp\n92I34W3VRL0xWXsiDPc/UQ35tuLbqy0mel5rXtGIs1UFdvfJplm2/URlmU1u8934\n+RU56KGl4IQlVL7Ry3XrxvhkyIpEYJbIFFglaPMnaLSrDfAk4VCI8W4v2Z8DyGXT\nKXQyg3nOsPTuvPzt3S+q/iMKPekVKF6szypqs+xeHn9fAzj0z2tZDwbUznF8sPY3\nPtteM2KvBbeh6NQqtA2hMuCYkGSNqzZ3gLmWy5omOHgEMrOYRpVSgrv04ggxCLBR\nds6Ai0b9yLteEswG7xtuQo+BX+DDE4c7uY0+AMWge4DOWiUITl+9TXFXVyOaBEMy\nut0jBuOA/hO4zfeVTqSp\n=3Mnf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a450eb525b29396c225ec106caff1c6bf2b217ec\nparent bd5bd953fb2a5d610a30d112eafe20b644924085\nauthor viyatb-oai <viyatb@openai.com> 1782161289 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782161289 -0700\n\npermission profiles: expose availability to clients (#26678)\n\n## Why\n\n`permissionProfile/list` currently advertises every built-in and\nconfigured profile even when effective enterprise requirements prevent\nselecting it. That forces each client to reconstruct policy from\nlower-level requirement fields, which is easy to miss and difficult to\nkeep consistent.\n\nThe catalog should remain complete so clients can explain that an option\nwas disabled by an administrator, while also reporting whether each\nprofile is selectable.\n\n## What\n\n- Add an `allowed` field to each permission profile summary.\n- Build a shared catalog from the effective config and current\nrequirements, including `allowed_sandbox_modes`, `allowed_permissions`,\nand filesystem restrictions.\n- Use the shared catalog in app-server and the TUI so disallowed\nprofiles remain visible but cannot be selected.\n- Use the canonical `:danger-full-access` profile ID in the TUI.\n- Update the app-server schemas, API documentation, behavioral tests,\nand TUI snapshots.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis PR targets `main` directly and is independent of #24852. It\npreserves the current behavior where built-in profiles are constrained\nby sandbox-mode requirements and `allowed_permissions` applies to\nconfigured profiles.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core\npermission_profile_catalog_marks_profiles_disallowed_by_requirements`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server permission_profile_list`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `just test -p codex-tui profile_permissions`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n- `just fix -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `just fix -p codex-app-server`\n- `just fix -p codex-tui`\n- `just fmt`\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Codex <noreply@openai.com>\nCo-authored-by: Joey Trasatti <joey.trasatti@openai.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-22T20:48:10Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ced3e4b9a7576fe08950965f2584d4d0c0d96937","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ced3e4b9a7576fe08950965f2584d4d0c0d96937","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ced3e4b9a7576fe08950965f2584d4d0c0d96937/comments","author":{"login":"viyatb-oai","id":234056686,"node_id":"U_kgDODfNr7g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234056686?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/viyatb-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"bd5bd953fb2a5d610a30d112eafe20b644924085","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bd5bd953fb2a5d610a30d112eafe20b644924085","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/bd5bd953fb2a5d610a30d112eafe20b644924085"}]},{"sha":"bd5bd953fb2a5d610a30d112eafe20b644924085","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGJkNWJkOTUzZmIyYTVkNjEwYTMwZDExMmVhZmUyMGI2NDQ5MjQwODU","commit":{"author":{"name":"rka-oai","email":"rka@openai.com","date":"2026-06-22T20:25:48Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T20:25:48Z"},"message":"[codex] configure rollout budget reminder thresholds (#29423)\n\n## Summary\n\nInstead of:\n\n    reminder_interval_tokens = 65_536\n\nallow users to configure explicit remaining-token reminder thresholds:\n\nreminder_at_remaining_tokens = [65_536, 32_768, 16_384, 8_192, 4_096,\n2_048, 1_024, 512]\n\n## Validation\n\n- CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 just test -p codex-core rollout_budget: 9 passed\n- just fix -p codex-core\n- just fmt","tree":{"sha":"335653ba010d9e203c62b828cf1e69cc85dc83b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/335653ba010d9e203c62b828cf1e69cc85dc83b4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/bd5bd953fb2a5d610a30d112eafe20b644924085","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOZpMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAa+IQAIK1mswJBoWWPJ2TVjID+3IP\nxKlfcNZrGFgNzOV36Vtq9V6RoD2Gmtw53frWyNkIcLbH6YdR8n3IuX48csOaai4y\nr5457//LpAR08Q/o7ROpe5v4s/Ol1AWj/i2Mcw5gG2Dtk+qGqyWzisjLfItFGKT/\nt04VPm5WuNBdCZ8bZ/RYvC49EQUM0oa15n8aGFZZNudMm7Tf3hdMVphS/SuY2nNc\nefXrOBmQHSJmOF3uPwjIV7ebNAUxDYy4St2BjV+GhUjzBlRtL+8+fVbZUX5YBM8K\njfet0nb5Eon/0jvRWaktdGnOQiimh0VP5vOq2sN4xBrFYV5TGE6h0c9BZQFP91z1\nnHFnXGqRLK06GTTfoP74AEQtRTrkPe4Urbs0y7Qjv4mEiinP+iEksmHtPBXvjphd\nnf3knqPw7w27kETfDA0pqFDb2biIfSE+tQRkrLx2bEtl9sCAEh/tOOD/+6q5TLEP\npjWniA9ldINj2+Qhfs1bhuIwMAr+Rt7RDvZMmdRSN2XzpvDkUPI97hBsgrwuhz08\nWekw753Tm19xF4mBU9zgM0KC1yarqVYsT+1ssBHYiqzzr5D/t1QnGUrjwgW971GN\n+L0QNf4XKJaYebLgxS1YOz9cfYet2eDnwIK1j7PbepoC1Zopi4umx8PtKDglL0tY\nciJFipl6FRI75hvepvFI\n=Et5z\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 335653ba010d9e203c62b828cf1e69cc85dc83b4\nparent 5a67d898a58cebc075ffea2643009217ed3e76f1\nauthor rka-oai <rka@openai.com> 1782159948 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782159948 -0700\n\n[codex] configure rollout budget reminder thresholds (#29423)\n\n## Summary\n\nInstead of:\n\n    reminder_interval_tokens = 65_536\n\nallow users to configure explicit remaining-token reminder thresholds:\n\nreminder_at_remaining_tokens = [65_536, 32_768, 16_384, 8_192, 4_096,\n2_048, 1_024, 512]\n\n## Validation\n\n- CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 just test -p codex-core rollout_budget: 9 passed\n- just fix -p codex-core\n- just fmt","verified_at":"2026-06-22T20:25:49Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bd5bd953fb2a5d610a30d112eafe20b644924085","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/bd5bd953fb2a5d610a30d112eafe20b644924085","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bd5bd953fb2a5d610a30d112eafe20b644924085/comments","author":{"login":"rka-oai","id":240799229,"node_id":"U_kgDODlpN_Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/240799229?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/rka-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5a67d898a58cebc075ffea2643009217ed3e76f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5a67d898a58cebc075ffea2643009217ed3e76f1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/5a67d898a58cebc075ffea2643009217ed3e76f1"}]},{"sha":"5a67d898a58cebc075ffea2643009217ed3e76f1","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDVhNjdkODk4YTU4Y2ViYzA3NWZmZWEyNjQzMDA5MjE3ZWQzZTc2ZjE","commit":{"author":{"name":"efrazer-oai","email":"efrazer@openai.com","date":"2026-06-22T20:19:40Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T20:19:40Z"},"message":"Allow ChatGPT accounts without email (#28991)\n\n# Summary\n\nCodex required every ChatGPT account to have an email address. A\nservice-account personal access token can return valid account metadata\nwithout one, so PAT login failed while decoding the metadata response.\n\nThis change makes email optional in the account metadata type that owns\nit and preserves that absence through authentication, provider account\nstate, the app-server API, generated clients, and TUI bootstrap.\nExisting accounts with email addresses keep the same behavior.\n\n## Behavior-changing call sites\n\n| Call site | Behavior after this change |\n| --- | --- |\n| `login/src/auth/personal_access_token.rs` | PAT metadata accepts a\nmissing or null email and retains `None`. |\n| `agent-identity/src/lib.rs` | Agent Identity JWT claims accept an\nomitted email. |\n| `login/src/auth/storage.rs` and `login/src/auth/agent_identity.rs` |\nStored and managed Agent Identity records carry `Option<String>`.\nDeserialization maps the legacy empty-string sentinel to `None`. |\n| `login/src/auth/manager.rs` | `get_account_email` returns the stored\noption, and managed identity bootstrap no longer converts `None` to an\nempty string. |\n| `model-provider/src/provider.rs` and `protocol/src/account.rs` | A\nChatGPT provider account requires a plan type but may carry no email. |\n| `app-server-protocol/src/protocol/v2/account.rs` | `account/read`\nkeeps the `email` field on the wire and returns `null` when the account\nhas no email. Generated TypeScript and JSON schemas describe a required,\nnullable field. |\n| `sdk/python/src/openai_codex/generated/v2_all.py` | The generated\nPython `ChatgptAccount` model accepts `None` for email. |\n| `tui/src/app_server_session.rs` | Email-less ChatGPT accounts\nbootstrap normally, keep external feedback routing, omit account-email\ntelemetry, and display the plan in account status. |\n\n## Design decisions\n\n- Missing email remains `None` at every layer. The code never uses an\nempty string as a substitute.\n- The app-server response includes `\"email\": null` instead of omitting\nthe field. Clients retain a stable response shape.\n- Plan type remains required for provider account state. This change\nrelaxes only the email assumption.\n\n## Testing\n\nTests: affected test targets compile, scoped Clippy and formatting pass,\na focused TUI snapshot covers plan-only account status, real\nbefore/after PAT login smoke covers metadata without email, app-server\nsmoke covers `account/read` with `email: null`, and a regression smoke\ncovers an existing email-bearing PAT. Unit tests run in CI.\n\n## Evidence\n\nVisual smoke evidence will be attached here.","tree":{"sha":"90c9c3105e7ef26f3a1220461321382206e2143d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/90c9c3105e7ef26f3a1220461321382206e2143d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/5a67d898a58cebc075ffea2643009217ed3e76f1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOZjcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8K0QAITaEZngeMAvjSnUIF6m4kAw\n+FI/RKSgb9D3kk6BbdkDAv7zTcFFHFAFUYbvKNuF/2xKgKt/+SxOmNZalvHGZFRw\nrdq9hkDJbFKtZkIwpN7gXmkRvSfRZxW0qa5KlrmHUF8kaQyy8V/GJBAj1swq8JpU\nCHoZ1zdzt5JIjD45bd+zJ43TFe7iav3V28Nj8PVNUW9j/Q+vGZbEufg/PJ+0gPJa\nCjRrm5073IK+8/3I8+vq1w8ZgtouHo6J+9CO/qoS4yD2makYz76mDjA5914FrieE\niKEr9mMUUWi8NWE4/nLJCJypSL4rKh2uHjASMdifASeV5YDbzrogP6tSR4AGXsUh\n7jka+ixWdCN1H+LPGPCjBcUkpI2RXqy5Y9VZiPTpA+GuMVjQbo8CB2KNnivBYLSX\nwx4bVOZhTE8JRMHPfpMP3Rucr2hnX7eMz/Tk8pGxlrney1wmlrJzAatppxjkjKAl\nPgb4hZ3oaUxJoQd5choBppmLfw206/XbY4v39oCrwDFGjEL9kFZapsQYSTXmYZz8\nuAzwoRVFS7Z7srVO3Yh0wDU5MinYlULLVJ8m6CEBx962V24CvdK6r2gescY4STDK\noxML9HbhK8s5sFmGMWC5pN3B5oJlHjYL3KLzBmkdWnmE9NW/StfYsCLdy7WfiCJK\nx8XtsW9V9I+VMiQncFaE\n=QEUC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 90c9c3105e7ef26f3a1220461321382206e2143d\nparent 1659c4a6291ae956f020c9c7354ff3cc3d050c48\nauthor efrazer-oai <efrazer@openai.com> 1782159580 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782159580 -0700\n\nAllow ChatGPT accounts without email (#28991)\n\n# Summary\n\nCodex required every ChatGPT account to have an email address. A\nservice-account personal access token can return valid account metadata\nwithout one, so PAT login failed while decoding the metadata response.\n\nThis change makes email optional in the account metadata type that owns\nit and preserves that absence through authentication, provider account\nstate, the app-server API, generated clients, and TUI bootstrap.\nExisting accounts with email addresses keep the same behavior.\n\n## Behavior-changing call sites\n\n| Call site | Behavior after this change |\n| --- | --- |\n| `login/src/auth/personal_access_token.rs` | PAT metadata accepts a\nmissing or null email and retains `None`. |\n| `agent-identity/src/lib.rs` | Agent Identity JWT claims accept an\nomitted email. |\n| `login/src/auth/storage.rs` and `login/src/auth/agent_identity.rs` |\nStored and managed Agent Identity records carry `Option<String>`.\nDeserialization maps the legacy empty-string sentinel to `None`. |\n| `login/src/auth/manager.rs` | `get_account_email` returns the stored\noption, and managed identity bootstrap no longer converts `None` to an\nempty string. |\n| `model-provider/src/provider.rs` and `protocol/src/account.rs` | A\nChatGPT provider account requires a plan type but may carry no email. |\n| `app-server-protocol/src/protocol/v2/account.rs` | `account/read`\nkeeps the `email` field on the wire and returns `null` when the account\nhas no email. Generated TypeScript and JSON schemas describe a required,\nnullable field. |\n| `sdk/python/src/openai_codex/generated/v2_all.py` | The generated\nPython `ChatgptAccount` model accepts `None` for email. |\n| `tui/src/app_server_session.rs` | Email-less ChatGPT accounts\nbootstrap normally, keep external feedback routing, omit account-email\ntelemetry, and display the plan in account status. |\n\n## Design decisions\n\n- Missing email remains `None` at every layer. The code never uses an\nempty string as a substitute.\n- The app-server response includes `\"email\": null` instead of omitting\nthe field. Clients retain a stable response shape.\n- Plan type remains required for provider account state. This change\nrelaxes only the email assumption.\n\n## Testing\n\nTests: affected test targets compile, scoped Clippy and formatting pass,\na focused TUI snapshot covers plan-only account status, real\nbefore/after PAT login smoke covers metadata without email, app-server\nsmoke covers `account/read` with `email: null`, and a regression smoke\ncovers an existing email-bearing PAT. Unit tests run in CI.\n\n## Evidence\n\nVisual smoke evidence will be attached here.","verified_at":"2026-06-22T20:19:41Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5a67d898a58cebc075ffea2643009217ed3e76f1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/5a67d898a58cebc075ffea2643009217ed3e76f1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5a67d898a58cebc075ffea2643009217ed3e76f1/comments","author":{"login":"efrazer-oai","id":263771262,"node_id":"U_kgDOD7jUfg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/263771262?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/efrazer-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/efrazer-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/efrazer-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/efrazer-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/efrazer-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/efrazer-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/efrazer-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/efrazer-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/efrazer-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/efrazer-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/efrazer-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1659c4a6291ae956f020c9c7354ff3cc3d050c48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1659c4a6291ae956f020c9c7354ff3cc3d050c48","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1659c4a6291ae956f020c9c7354ff3cc3d050c48"}]},{"sha":"1659c4a6291ae956f020c9c7354ff3cc3d050c48","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDE2NTljNGE2MjkxYWU5NTZmMDIwYzljNzM1NGZmM2NjM2QwNTBjNDg","commit":{"author":{"name":"canvrno-oai","email":"kbond@openai.com","date":"2026-06-22T20:03:11Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T20:03:11Z"},"message":"PAC 2 - Add shared auth system proxy contract (#26707)\n\n## Summary\n\nStacked on #26706.\n\nAdds the shared auth/system-proxy contract that later platform resolver\nPRs plug into. This PR moves Codex-owned auth and startup HTTP clients\nthrough a common route-aware boundary, but does not yet add Windows or\nmacOS system proxy resolution.\n\nThe default path remains unchanged when `respect_system_proxy` is absent\nor disabled.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Adds `codex-client/src/outbound_proxy.rs` with the shared\nroute-selection model:\n  - `OutboundProxyConfig`;\n  - `ClientRouteClass`;\n  - `RouteFailureClass`;\n  - `build_reqwest_client_for_route`.\n- Preserves the existing reqwest/default-client behavior when no route\nconfig is supplied.\n- Uses the fixed MVP routing policy when route config is supplied:\nplatform system/PAC/WPAD discovery, then explicit env proxy variables,\nthen direct connection.\n- Keeps platform-specific system discovery behind the shared client\nboundary. This PR provides the contract and fallback behavior; later\nresolver PRs plug in Windows and macOS discovery.\n- Adds `login::AuthRouteConfig` so auth call sites depend on a small\npolicy type instead of platform resolver details.\n- Maps the resolved `Config.respect_system_proxy` boolean into\n`AuthRouteConfig` for auth-owned clients.\n- Wires the route config through browser login, device-code login,\naccess-token login, login status, logout/revoke, token refresh, API-key\nexchange, app-server account login, TUI/app startup, cloud-config\nbootstrap, cloud tasks, plugin auth, and exec startup config loading.\n\n## End-user behavior\n\n- No behavior changes by default.\n- When `respect_system_proxy = true`, auth-owned clients opt into the\nshared route-aware client path.\n- On platforms without a resolver implementation in this PR, system\ndiscovery is unavailable and the route-aware path falls back to explicit\nenv proxy handling, then direct connection.\n- Custom CA handling remains separate from proxy route selection and\nstill runs through the shared client builder.\n- No proxy URLs, PAC contents, or resolved platform details are exposed\nthrough the public config surface introduced here.\n\n## Tests\n\nAdds or updates coverage for:\n\n- preserving default auth-client fallback behavior when no route config\nis provided;\n- injected environment-proxy fallback without mutating process\nenvironment;\n- existing login-server E2E flows using explicit `auth_route_config:\nNone` to guard unchanged default behavior;\n- updated auth manager, login, logout, cloud-config, startup, and\nplugin-auth call sites passing route config explicitly.","tree":{"sha":"f8249452bce7049ce892af8f3eba193db4745ce2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/f8249452bce7049ce892af8f3eba193db4745ce2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/1659c4a6291ae956f020c9c7354ff3cc3d050c48","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOZT/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAm4gQAGvMvTrymu1yQEOTA9EXsP/R\nmunEvxwwOkYEZq21EdrtVM4cJF330fZHEJKPnpmLhGuVt/YeQZETwP1xUyEi4pKv\nlnLEwrsZL/tZw9MKAWMGppegRQmxjb99aVRoIsQW0Kqtx+6jHI/7vdR9hxYPTVLJ\npPeM27ZLSt0LOMhHj+x6k3QdFZRQieUuqS48xiJjtv0eRBNbRdSWipBCzf2Hoha4\n3IR46N3JkNgxe2PONE7hhh/BPUC08IfHRc/KcGFH1Ql42nJ5Y2I40rF/R6ZXkRmS\nr3VnCutR1Q2O4WaRJ7wkumfGwCQAaDpJg+CQbsCY0Qhlh4eZ116MenCByJwGA9vj\nci8bgVKkk/WQiAHYpw8nDDjy2wsFiKaj4MrjiNg1BRS7QyTF3ULKict3ZPtROCZb\n9uM4m4zMCsbOAUu+Rh8sIR8Epx+GaJZzAGQoC6/WQ+O+p3+yC+WSnRkZ0cjkfLgg\nFLqiitx9f19I2mK6VQXYXrFx84aaLYy0FO8gLZ4Ia4MnGNNMgB8hvy10EvuV2S4J\nrabJfG3a+D7mEtUVQYCHTeH81nXz84nf63XeiBn2K1VkAvDcL9uxRgerAaEjWwkS\nfijfOSsph8X/E+1T6W/fxgntevZgTjMiZva2kHNbq0eQPrK/WilsXY5UZvpO8yIw\n92QMQ3H0ZRs+7LtwViYn\n=7LFv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f8249452bce7049ce892af8f3eba193db4745ce2\nparent e48ab86693c56ae500ff1e3ca08ec71272628170\nauthor canvrno-oai <kbond@openai.com> 1782158591 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782158591 -0700\n\nPAC 2 - Add shared auth system proxy contract (#26707)\n\n## Summary\n\nStacked on #26706.\n\nAdds the shared auth/system-proxy contract that later platform resolver\nPRs plug into. This PR moves Codex-owned auth and startup HTTP clients\nthrough a common route-aware boundary, but does not yet add Windows or\nmacOS system proxy resolution.\n\nThe default path remains unchanged when `respect_system_proxy` is absent\nor disabled.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Adds `codex-client/src/outbound_proxy.rs` with the shared\nroute-selection model:\n  - `OutboundProxyConfig`;\n  - `ClientRouteClass`;\n  - `RouteFailureClass`;\n  - `build_reqwest_client_for_route`.\n- Preserves the existing reqwest/default-client behavior when no route\nconfig is supplied.\n- Uses the fixed MVP routing policy when route config is supplied:\nplatform system/PAC/WPAD discovery, then explicit env proxy variables,\nthen direct connection.\n- Keeps platform-specific system discovery behind the shared client\nboundary. This PR provides the contract and fallback behavior; later\nresolver PRs plug in Windows and macOS discovery.\n- Adds `login::AuthRouteConfig` so auth call sites depend on a small\npolicy type instead of platform resolver details.\n- Maps the resolved `Config.respect_system_proxy` boolean into\n`AuthRouteConfig` for auth-owned clients.\n- Wires the route config through browser login, device-code login,\naccess-token login, login status, logout/revoke, token refresh, API-key\nexchange, app-server account login, TUI/app startup, cloud-config\nbootstrap, cloud tasks, plugin auth, and exec startup config loading.\n\n## End-user behavior\n\n- No behavior changes by default.\n- When `respect_system_proxy = true`, auth-owned clients opt into the\nshared route-aware client path.\n- On platforms without a resolver implementation in this PR, system\ndiscovery is unavailable and the route-aware path falls back to explicit\nenv proxy handling, then direct connection.\n- Custom CA handling remains separate from proxy route selection and\nstill runs through the shared client builder.\n- No proxy URLs, PAC contents, or resolved platform details are exposed\nthrough the public config surface introduced here.\n\n## Tests\n\nAdds or updates coverage for:\n\n- preserving default auth-client fallback behavior when no route config\nis provided;\n- injected environment-proxy fallback without mutating process\nenvironment;\n- existing login-server E2E flows using explicit `auth_route_config:\nNone` to guard unchanged default behavior;\n- updated auth manager, login, logout, cloud-config, startup, and\nplugin-auth call sites passing route config explicitly.","verified_at":"2026-06-22T20:03:12Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1659c4a6291ae956f020c9c7354ff3cc3d050c48","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1659c4a6291ae956f020c9c7354ff3cc3d050c48","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1659c4a6291ae956f020c9c7354ff3cc3d050c48/comments","author":{"login":"canvrno-oai","id":257630656,"node_id":"U_kgDOD1shwA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257630656?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/canvrno-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e48ab86693c56ae500ff1e3ca08ec71272628170","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e48ab86693c56ae500ff1e3ca08ec71272628170","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e48ab86693c56ae500ff1e3ca08ec71272628170"}]},{"sha":"e48ab86693c56ae500ff1e3ca08ec71272628170","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGU0OGFiODY2OTNjNTZhZTUwMGZmMWUzY2EwOGVjNzEyNzI2MjgxNzA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Michael Bolin","email":"mbolin@openai.com","date":"2026-06-22T19:31:52Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T19:31:52Z"},"message":"core: remove unused permissions cwd plumbing (#29468)\n\n## Why\n\n`compile_scoped_filesystem_pattern()` accepted a `_policy_cwd` parameter\neven though scoped glob compilation no longer uses the policy working\ndirectory. Keeping that unused argument forced the surrounding\npermissions compilation path to keep forwarding `policy_cwd` through\ncall sites that did not need it, making the API look more dependent on\ncwd resolution than it is.\n\n## What changed\n\nRemoved the unused cwd parameter from\n`compile_scoped_filesystem_pattern()` and the callers that only\nforwarded it: `compile_filesystem_permission()`,\n`compile_permission_profile()`, and\n`compile_permission_profile_selection()`. Workspace root resolution\nstill keeps `policy_cwd`, because that path still resolves relative\nroots against the active policy cwd.\n\nRelevant code:\n[`codex-rs/core/src/config/permissions.rs`](https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/b8b9816102e064dae4488ec130cf560f63c1ab78/codex-rs/core/src/config/permissions.rs#L346).\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-core config::permissions`\n- `just test -p codex-core` was also run after building\n`test_stdio_server`; it passed the touched permissions coverage but\nstill reported unrelated existing failures in `cli_stream` and shell\nsnapshot tests.","tree":{"sha":"70af8370219262084aaa2be5f3a8fd2a249910e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/70af8370219262084aaa2be5f3a8fd2a249910e7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/e48ab86693c56ae500ff1e3ca08ec71272628170","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOY2oCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA94AQAEd99sAK+eRMfvCgUEk3OsNP\nvT9v6adLEjhOBH4MierqHnzy/qmBYSabjwJbhvlgoflp9UxMjY8pCyMX63XwKF8Q\nTGa2vzxmh/Ovr3kxFB23BdSxgcJXIqgeKrZzBgJaOxOLnk0Ts7U2jMf/lQNpF27N\niwbRXi0MjIDwjfDTQT8jRMLYWqBqMmEGuGfv/rLgzJBnHXjhUhItDjcu/cgiKvO1\n2fngEeVpMI1z2glfubmVaQ8IzbFAAykqZVb4PivkxWSoMAIZgmy4/0GkUGqllsuM\nGj80Eiuej51e5SBSzvkKWHgz1KrNSDQ63tImYwD7nbvnJ/osnsJ3EU9vSSzzn1GM\nUDnjKcvNhlQnbs7CpfTRGu5C7ICfidpeXWtJfqslCspFHEvi4hpEEGxUtmKvt1cK\n2fvypfVCmDe3lJ2orqNJJsfVOTB6qL2OCIL7fx4RwbTZEAyC5Xxq8zx+V0pqvyft\nKmQXtjXfY1n94OhxHdntbvZxYjnzOxt4q6nf6DmTCRAD3kzw/MJ2Vg8pIfYuEDpb\nSjlzCXjLUpq5TBPa7oZWX8oADfX6JSYKYSGcVDrHj88vKoJlifFwaHnuGA+tHGgK\n9ggyj5v+VbBfWcEhVptRZj+LQ0T6xVc7GgVzuC+XG561MY2wF9cmGz6ZaDdbJduq\nkE8vcKMunOm1bV6d7YRU\n=exSd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 70af8370219262084aaa2be5f3a8fd2a249910e7\nparent 15f448d8b06c25c9ad04b2abeb3e4e2f07e4c327\nauthor Michael Bolin <mbolin@openai.com> 1782156712 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782156712 -0700\n\ncore: remove unused permissions cwd plumbing (#29468)\n\n## Why\n\n`compile_scoped_filesystem_pattern()` accepted a `_policy_cwd` parameter\neven though scoped glob compilation no longer uses the policy working\ndirectory. Keeping that unused argument forced the surrounding\npermissions compilation path to keep forwarding `policy_cwd` through\ncall sites that did not need it, making the API look more dependent on\ncwd resolution than it is.\n\n## What changed\n\nRemoved the unused cwd parameter from\n`compile_scoped_filesystem_pattern()` and the callers that only\nforwarded it: `compile_filesystem_permission()`,\n`compile_permission_profile()`, and\n`compile_permission_profile_selection()`. Workspace root resolution\nstill keeps `policy_cwd`, because that path still resolves relative\nroots against the active policy cwd.\n\nRelevant code:\n[`codex-rs/core/src/config/permissions.rs`](https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/b8b9816102e064dae4488ec130cf560f63c1ab78/codex-rs/core/src/config/permissions.rs#L346).\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-core config::permissions`\n- `just test -p codex-core` was also run after building\n`test_stdio_server`; it passed the touched permissions coverage but\nstill reported unrelated existing failures in `cli_stream` and shell\nsnapshot tests.","verified_at":"2026-06-22T19:31:53Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e48ab86693c56ae500ff1e3ca08ec71272628170","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e48ab86693c56ae500ff1e3ca08ec71272628170","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e48ab86693c56ae500ff1e3ca08ec71272628170/comments","author":{"login":"bolinfest","id":655869,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTg2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/655869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest","html_url":"https://github.com/bolinfest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"15f448d8b06c25c9ad04b2abeb3e4e2f07e4c327","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/15f448d8b06c25c9ad04b2abeb3e4e2f07e4c327","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/15f448d8b06c25c9ad04b2abeb3e4e2f07e4c327"}]},{"sha":"15f448d8b06c25c9ad04b2abeb3e4e2f07e4c327","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDE1ZjQ0OGQ4YjA2YzI1YzlhZDA0YjJhYmViM2U0ZTJmMDdlNGMzMjc","commit":{"author":{"name":"jgershen-oai","email":"jgershen@openai.com","date":"2026-06-22T18:54:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T18:54:44Z"},"message":"[codex] Start the guardian child session when parent session is started (#27982)\n\n## Why\n\nThe first auto-review currently creates its Guardian child session on\ndemand, adding avoidable latency before the review can begin. Creating\nthe ordinary Guardian child during parent-session initialization lets\nthat child use the existing session startup WebSocket prewarm before the\nfirst escalation. This does not introduce a Guardian-specific prewarm\nmechanism.\n\n## What changed\n\n- initialize the existing Guardian review-session manager owned by\n`Session` when a thread starts with auto-review enabled and an approval\npolicy that routes to Guardian\n- use the standard Guardian child-session construction and the existing\nsession startup WebSocket prewarm\n- preserve the existing reuse-key invalidation and lazy creation\nfallback when startup initialization fails or the effective review\nconfiguration changes\n- add an integration test that verifies normal root-session startup\nemits a Guardian `generate=false` prewarm request\n\n## Benchmark\n\nI compared release builds against main. Each prompt first ran a\nnon-escalated `sleep 3`, then requested an escalated marker command.\n\n| binary | count | avg Guardian duration | median Guardian duration |\navg Guardian TTFT |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| origin-main | 10 | 4008.7 ms | 3949.5 ms | 3746.5 ms |\n| session-fix | 10 | 2865.0 ms | 2594.0 ms | 2492.7 ms |\n\nGuardian duration fell by 28.5% and Guardian TTFT fell by 33.5%. These\nmeasurements cover Guardian review latency; they do not measure parent\nthread-start latency.","tree":{"sha":"b71f33d4157bb8007a42bf20ba928645b802bc8b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/b71f33d4157bb8007a42bf20ba928645b802bc8b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/15f448d8b06c25c9ad04b2abeb3e4e2f07e4c327","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOYT0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJioQAJXtUs6fiv460BaWOz5Ubsbn\nuRN/n3k/JETUUyd+RfQ795+mL8LsdNYWjAHC3jygWWgd4PdNrccFXe8jw//QDUKZ\nKm2p4sNhluBzuSRVyZjOJJEC0d/vqCOLS3SaWZSktDPw1eS5uVjVRbN/ylgqKnex\n5cJT+SsEdmQzbd1bw1/ZpGh5ojryePGk/FM96lwU6gQNqx107N4NfoOfjsh1saGB\n2nDzQKGpNsIVrOOg5UmjlaezQ7NViuholX0xunWekLXtKf5w2RjxW7JvINCwSw1a\nBrBCfgnunEISZnhYcRTYzA+XMNtzhGDyOFpfCZ1Kjkm7wjTgARid7K6EHS22ARnD\n4dAhmJ6oHnWRTTzB+IeJBIBhmXHNgl1IvgwXKUZ3MU06q1hgHf53KHphiSJ64326\n0eg+2G1HUbP7tDOBqHTqghWxoQQNPC7Oc6BF9b43r+lolNvSXRxgs1/c1sqh1QHc\nEoqbFb6jX7zveVLAuKfAurR68Tn3kuvirlDCHGxuSXQ0FLTb2T96ehhb2/qdOEEy\nFW8qk0dCWTNEHzze7UOMIpa+NtmrUDhfVt/FD71D4ABt7sohL7AR51IUiuBVZUJr\n7om12fQpm49XELpqn/rUj9SrLZMojYFSTKsc/KWz8IDzPvzsYxHel5g5CDC7kOOr\nA8j4pnDpocqKqak/WjVC\n=hQCi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b71f33d4157bb8007a42bf20ba928645b802bc8b\nparent 5c0fbf34925041ac94a267aa17237e4e07b0ce42\nauthor jgershen-oai <jgershen@openai.com> 1782154484 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782154484 -0700\n\n[codex] Start the guardian child session when parent session is started (#27982)\n\n## Why\n\nThe first auto-review currently creates its Guardian child session on\ndemand, adding avoidable latency before the review can begin. Creating\nthe ordinary Guardian child during parent-session initialization lets\nthat child use the existing session startup WebSocket prewarm before the\nfirst escalation. This does not introduce a Guardian-specific prewarm\nmechanism.\n\n## What changed\n\n- initialize the existing Guardian review-session manager owned by\n`Session` when a thread starts with auto-review enabled and an approval\npolicy that routes to Guardian\n- use the standard Guardian child-session construction and the existing\nsession startup WebSocket prewarm\n- preserve the existing reuse-key invalidation and lazy creation\nfallback when startup initialization fails or the effective review\nconfiguration changes\n- add an integration test that verifies normal root-session startup\nemits a Guardian `generate=false` prewarm request\n\n## Benchmark\n\nI compared release builds against main. Each prompt first ran a\nnon-escalated `sleep 3`, then requested an escalated marker command.\n\n| binary | count | avg Guardian duration | median Guardian duration |\navg Guardian TTFT |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| origin-main | 10 | 4008.7 ms | 3949.5 ms | 3746.5 ms |\n| session-fix | 10 | 2865.0 ms | 2594.0 ms | 2492.7 ms |\n\nGuardian duration fell by 28.5% and Guardian TTFT fell by 33.5%. These\nmeasurements cover Guardian review latency; they do not measure parent\nthread-start latency.","verified_at":"2026-06-22T18:54:45Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/15f448d8b06c25c9ad04b2abeb3e4e2f07e4c327","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/15f448d8b06c25c9ad04b2abeb3e4e2f07e4c327","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/15f448d8b06c25c9ad04b2abeb3e4e2f07e4c327/comments","author":{"login":"jgershen-oai","id":263770668,"node_id":"U_kgDOD7jSLA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/263770668?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jgershen-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jgershen-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jgershen-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jgershen-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jgershen-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jgershen-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jgershen-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jgershen-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jgershen-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jgershen-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jgershen-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5c0fbf34925041ac94a267aa17237e4e07b0ce42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5c0fbf34925041ac94a267aa17237e4e07b0ce42","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/5c0fbf34925041ac94a267aa17237e4e07b0ce42"}]},{"sha":"5c0fbf34925041ac94a267aa17237e4e07b0ce42","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDVjMGZiZjM0OTI1MDQxYWM5NGEyNjdhYTE3MjM3ZTRlMDdiMGNlNDI","commit":{"author":{"name":"jay","email":"jayp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-22T18:45:41Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T18:45:41Z"},"message":"[codex] Fix usage-limit reset copy and state (#28793)\n\n## Why\n\nThe reset flow introduced in #28154 still describes earned reset credits\nas \"rate-limit resets\" and uses generic reset-scope copy. It can also\nretain a stale available-credit count after redemption or an account\nchange, leaving the reset action enabled after the last credit is used.\n\nThis follow-up updates terminology only within that reset feature.\nExisting rate-limit wording elsewhere in the CLI and TUI is unchanged.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Rename reset-specific `/usage` menu items, startup hints, and reset\ndialogs to \"usage limit reset.\"\n- Describe monthly resets for Free, Go, and accounts that report a\nmonthly usage window; otherwise describe the current 5-hour and weekly\nlimits.\n- Recheck a cached zero balance when `/usage` is reopened, and refresh\nthe balance after redemption so the final reset immediately disables the\naction.\n- Correlate async refresh results before updating snapshots and clear\naccount-derived reset state, warnings, prompts, and status surfaces when\nthe account changes.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-tui chatwidget::tests::usage` — 29 passed.\n- `just test -p codex-tui chatwidget::tests::status_command_tests` — 7\npassed.\n- Account-boundary prompt and plan-mode prompt regression tests passed.\n- `cargo insta pending-snapshots` from `codex-rs/tui` — no pending\nsnapshots.\\\n\n<img width=\"814\" height=\"318\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2a460e96-458b-4805-8d9f-c759382d21a4\"\n/>\nview for monthly\n<img width=\"905\" height=\"243\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/179f88e3-08fb-4af5-8dc6-ce6a944ed681\"\n/>","tree":{"sha":"7ea7359ceb43a8c7f46a24a0c4757877657a4bbc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/7ea7359ceb43a8c7f46a24a0c4757877657a4bbc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/5c0fbf34925041ac94a267aa17237e4e07b0ce42","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOYLVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+X8QAFHJEQcM3yx2K6VhEyMFmWnj\nczLI4bErXgX2ihzzwb7zPeOG2E4+EHEQTk+NOVU9kMqCXsDXW5WH6wRYpPHJsF+m\nyE6FNspyfuohWpA7hTaMKi+RzZo7xg3Psh+FL/g1kqKcwXkK88TR2Xxbv/ol5ySA\ngZLNn3wqX3hI/cuw8z1zTNagTZRx3MWzcIVyMRr22PJZs/1cdJI9XIdP5bbCnkNx\nHmdW6yQ9VMiowcug3WeV1ZRGkWShb8QZftosfAYtpDpXVsxVCbeSzCXnKE8WoUyd\nvMo52rHo2BeSnEIR6lJqJM1O3LGrnPeZZr/IR4pck+ZQYNf/7lOZOtn5Akyu3Uil\nPAKGGokk+r2sPM3ZLVHztVinC26Yzvx7fBgp8p6IeskAT9foKCcobUxcOs3tQLW0\nFBAr142MKB4wof6sfyv1EaHwysLBn/fUueaL9otoAoYWDWM1wYOx/aZ32T6U6ToL\nfArTU9pin6RfJWdph9/w1eBjc3lJZqCr/QsDLF2G1RhTJu3ThYn9CSjSt4aTlZBw\nUSiXb1aWWmT3g8RdEpQ3JfyUa9xud0thfA6OhPoAnE7rIjWJ6dPsVGkZm4O11I+v\nSe4RUzq88mMAq/gPxznblXFPs3++i22yDdjvK44btzrAgwcghT45d3djAsOEpD+3\nn9scugM0b+03Uqpgqj57\n=BMFE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7ea7359ceb43a8c7f46a24a0c4757877657a4bbc\nparent 20431d49a07d7cb6f3271a1e03929b444f3b50bb\nauthor jay <jayp@openai.com> 1782153941 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782153941 +0000\n\n[codex] Fix usage-limit reset copy and state (#28793)\n\n## Why\n\nThe reset flow introduced in #28154 still describes earned reset credits\nas \"rate-limit resets\" and uses generic reset-scope copy. It can also\nretain a stale available-credit count after redemption or an account\nchange, leaving the reset action enabled after the last credit is used.\n\nThis follow-up updates terminology only within that reset feature.\nExisting rate-limit wording elsewhere in the CLI and TUI is unchanged.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Rename reset-specific `/usage` menu items, startup hints, and reset\ndialogs to \"usage limit reset.\"\n- Describe monthly resets for Free, Go, and accounts that report a\nmonthly usage window; otherwise describe the current 5-hour and weekly\nlimits.\n- Recheck a cached zero balance when `/usage` is reopened, and refresh\nthe balance after redemption so the final reset immediately disables the\naction.\n- Correlate async refresh results before updating snapshots and clear\naccount-derived reset state, warnings, prompts, and status surfaces when\nthe account changes.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-tui chatwidget::tests::usage` — 29 passed.\n- `just test -p codex-tui chatwidget::tests::status_command_tests` — 7\npassed.\n- Account-boundary prompt and plan-mode prompt regression tests passed.\n- `cargo insta pending-snapshots` from `codex-rs/tui` — no pending\nsnapshots.\\\n\n<img width=\"814\" height=\"318\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2a460e96-458b-4805-8d9f-c759382d21a4\"\n/>\nview for monthly\n<img width=\"905\" height=\"243\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/179f88e3-08fb-4af5-8dc6-ce6a944ed681\"\n/>","verified_at":"2026-06-22T18:45:42Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5c0fbf34925041ac94a267aa17237e4e07b0ce42","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/5c0fbf34925041ac94a267aa17237e4e07b0ce42","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5c0fbf34925041ac94a267aa17237e4e07b0ce42/comments","author":{"login":"jayp-oai","id":286152634,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5Xug","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286152634?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jayp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jayp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jayp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jayp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jayp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jayp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jayp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jayp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jayp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jayp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jayp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"20431d49a07d7cb6f3271a1e03929b444f3b50bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/20431d49a07d7cb6f3271a1e03929b444f3b50bb","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/20431d49a07d7cb6f3271a1e03929b444f3b50bb"}]},{"sha":"20431d49a07d7cb6f3271a1e03929b444f3b50bb","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDIwNDMxZDQ5YTA3ZDdjYjZmMzI3MWExZTAzOTI5YjQ0NGYzYjUwYmI","commit":{"author":{"name":"rka-oai","email":"rka@openai.com","date":"2026-06-22T18:34:14Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T18:34:14Z"},"message":"[sdk/python] Stop advertising HTTP image URLs (#29464)\n\n## Summary\n\n- use generated image data URLs in the Python SDK examples and notebook\n- document HTTP and HTTPS image URLs as deprecated and recommend\n`LocalImageInput`\n- replace the remote-URL integration test with data-URL coverage\n\n`ImageInput` remains available for data URLs. The SDK does not duplicate\napp-server URL validation.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `uv run --frozen --no-sync ruff check --output-format=full .`\n- `uv run --frozen --no-sync ruff format --check .`\n- full Python SDK test suite with an isolated writable\n`CODEX_SQLITE_HOME` (119 passed, 38 skipped)","tree":{"sha":"2819cecc345e0ca5032a0137d167bb1fa41871b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/2819cecc345e0ca5032a0137d167bb1fa41871b4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/20431d49a07d7cb6f3271a1e03929b444f3b50bb","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOYAmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANBsQAFSJHSJCsiANpJb63ObFMrbR\nZZJPsMXcT2IJs6PYSf6RjdzuBZeAku+1hHvru3+RfCBS+mwG+Oj12NDXdS0QMnJD\n0dWYoAnfMUgfCWvVkYbQYllBEsGKcD4r434l+kQIxBMi8ZKV2873h4F++lIIwV5G\nSJRPjFXHPbf4dJmMZxjX5bwVRHlUSau2hGHLXKVFcOI/jWfaV66Hv7ZSvnsXg/be\nT9jk1Bt5nixn5Y/bVKvCl7Qi9Y7hEpXntc83nSk/8Mlu4yEtojjOzwc6xMSDWDTG\nfH+ImPj4oQFi8u0fxfBWbLRSW9pjktrfz8ZFh8r2DkYB3V3656zVhuPYjO2M7Ud+\nGkZgNB0eWkccajvtc4D8y6kQB6ehR3RCSVrRNbHwAYuDcgDmYbi7fudy7XX+vtYD\nn2xwUuH/cRRbLl7EdmWyG2TY77nKZzdyRge4OBFLAYRVhbjKk3UeZoxvKwTNJoAf\nl68E1rVINAtyvJyz6UtgRTe1OqUARRyTonsneM8u0SmaAFY88/JaWJ0WNfR42gA9\nm8ub/UHeZIgVPq1u3dFOaap0gTQFYqp2HnIMzO0796vvhUrCXAbjiIPGMPpoFFIw\nDeSzFJ01iOb3ASEmIdiutYnMPm+a6M0mLA/H9nqN+d6rspd714h7WNPcQ5bXbbRU\ncI99HFxIAkHymAj0R/Ys\n=K8j0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2819cecc345e0ca5032a0137d167bb1fa41871b4\nparent 5b95745eae1b13be75d6c395a6baec8e7b7ad99b\nauthor rka-oai <rka@openai.com> 1782153254 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782153254 -0700\n\n[sdk/python] Stop advertising HTTP image URLs (#29464)\n\n## Summary\n\n- use generated image data URLs in the Python SDK examples and notebook\n- document HTTP and HTTPS image URLs as deprecated and recommend\n`LocalImageInput`\n- replace the remote-URL integration test with data-URL coverage\n\n`ImageInput` remains available for data URLs. The SDK does not duplicate\napp-server URL validation.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `uv run --frozen --no-sync ruff check --output-format=full .`\n- `uv run --frozen --no-sync ruff format --check .`\n- full Python SDK test suite with an isolated writable\n`CODEX_SQLITE_HOME` (119 passed, 38 skipped)","verified_at":"2026-06-22T18:34:14Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/20431d49a07d7cb6f3271a1e03929b444f3b50bb","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/20431d49a07d7cb6f3271a1e03929b444f3b50bb","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/20431d49a07d7cb6f3271a1e03929b444f3b50bb/comments","author":{"login":"rka-oai","id":240799229,"node_id":"U_kgDODlpN_Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/240799229?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/rka-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5b95745eae1b13be75d6c395a6baec8e7b7ad99b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5b95745eae1b13be75d6c395a6baec8e7b7ad99b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/5b95745eae1b13be75d6c395a6baec8e7b7ad99b"}]},{"sha":"5b95745eae1b13be75d6c395a6baec8e7b7ad99b","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDViOTU3NDVlYWUxYjEzYmU3NWQ2YzM5NWE2YmFlYzhlN2I3YWQ5OWI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Owen Lin","email":"owenlin0@gmail.com","date":"2026-06-22T18:11:25Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T18:11:25Z"},"message":"core: rename metadata -> internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough (#28968)\n\n## Description\nThis PR cuts Codex over from generic `ResponseItem.metadata` (introduced\nhere: https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/28355) to\n`ResponseItem.internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough`, which is the\nblessed path and has strongly-typed keys.\n\nFor now we have to drop this MAv2 usage of `metadata`:\nhttps://github.com/openai/codex/pull/28561 until we figure out where\nthat should live.","tree":{"sha":"e45e2da6a0af8a56921c0d60fdf428daf02ec918","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/e45e2da6a0af8a56921c0d60fdf428daf02ec918"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/5b95745eae1b13be75d6c395a6baec8e7b7ad99b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOXrNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAam4QAEVdNIZ86mwLBwAM0xJERiAG\namGlKPd2v5L1WuwwkPvkb8p74HInlyctHQS2/iSfaki4o7CfPGNlL2E2GDHJzOht\nJfS/Exobx1LcYaQrdi8eGbFhXhCr5TGM8txwL0FLg84GO6ig8HPC41v+3nDDiBUg\nRRhh/oAFFaWnP/Puk209dGe34GHpq3sFAGOli+/0dRBevGLINZV7kPxF59F6gTRp\nWzkdP7ZACEYN1doTcW2F6I3JqdL6mlRtWYzk3jjPN71wU0jS28h0olgd3SyKoLgX\nXIHUYyD+BjjlxhIJYagY62EEYsCblG702xlMBQ7U7OhrbfhBGyXEZeRkk3lCbD5F\nBuqTOo84NoqD6DRqyZvtUBey1H6oYurh2+/i+eCf3PXrTmeYlKLPk8kSOK0a7r3V\n59jSYx1K+x0yzAksgIPAbR2VMVW1GRw4GSltsEYuatmgmHmgfuLU7wAN+t9vbxGy\nPbUd+z627u0bzv2LteKuPzzMLPK7AX/ClGVLD72QC+brUwZb16gz3wdqawMz4qbx\n5nrqgtgU0BaVr2tcCoQaGvHoPCzoWr3N+AZwyiFR+j6wV7nKomta1g/Bl+LAlruN\nxAA5jXDPXgyeASS5q6wk53VUfuBfnicnDi7IMkmp7BbciCqjsobH8Omk5SfOiA5G\nKEmBfVJM5bj4KU7y45j2\n=JmDX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e45e2da6a0af8a56921c0d60fdf428daf02ec918\nparent 9f06cf1a0907f650887ca26af5cee13b4f9a13ea\nauthor Owen Lin <owenlin0@gmail.com> 1782151885 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782151885 -0700\n\ncore: rename metadata -> internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough (#28968)\n\n## Description\nThis PR cuts Codex over from generic `ResponseItem.metadata` (introduced\nhere: https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/28355) to\n`ResponseItem.internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough`, which is the\nblessed path and has strongly-typed keys.\n\nFor now we have to drop this MAv2 usage of `metadata`:\nhttps://github.com/openai/codex/pull/28561 until we figure out where\nthat should live.","verified_at":"2026-06-22T18:11:26Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5b95745eae1b13be75d6c395a6baec8e7b7ad99b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/5b95745eae1b13be75d6c395a6baec8e7b7ad99b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5b95745eae1b13be75d6c395a6baec8e7b7ad99b/comments","author":{"login":"owenlin0","id":947871,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk0Nzg3MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/947871?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0","html_url":"https://github.com/owenlin0","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9f06cf1a0907f650887ca26af5cee13b4f9a13ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9f06cf1a0907f650887ca26af5cee13b4f9a13ea","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9f06cf1a0907f650887ca26af5cee13b4f9a13ea"}]},{"sha":"9f06cf1a0907f650887ca26af5cee13b4f9a13ea","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDlmMDZjZjFhMDkwN2Y2NTA4ODdjYTI2YWY1Y2VlMTNiNGY5YTEzZWE","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-22T17:33:28Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T17:33:28Z"},"message":"Report remote sandbox denials semantically (#29424)\n\n## Why\n\n#29113 moved remote sandbox setup and enforcement to the exec server.\nThat gives the executor ownership of the platform-specific work: a Linux\nexecutor chooses and runs a Linux sandbox even when the Codex\norchestrator is running on macOS or Windows.\n\nIt also means the orchestrator no longer knows which concrete sandbox\nthe executor selected. When that sandbox blocks a remote command, the\norchestrator currently sees only a failed process and can treat the\ndenial as an ordinary command failure. The existing sandbox approval and\nretry path is then skipped.\n\nThis PR lets the executor report one portable fact:\n\n> This command probably failed because the executor sandbox blocked it.\n\nThe executor keeps its concrete sandbox type private. The protocol sends\nonly the semantic result.\n\n## Example\n\nSuppose a local macOS Codex session asks a Linux devbox to write outside\nthe allowed workspace.\n\nBefore this PR:\n\n```text\nLinux sandbox blocks the write\n    -> remote process exits with \"Permission denied\"\n    -> local orchestrator sees an ordinary command failure\n    -> the normal sandbox approval and retry path can be skipped\n```\n\nWith this PR:\n\n```text\nLinux sandbox blocks the write\n    -> executor reports sandboxDenied: true\n    -> unified exec returns UnifiedExecError::SandboxDenied\n    -> the existing approval prompt is shown\n    -> an approved retry runs through the existing unsandboxed retry path\n```\n\n## What changes\n\n### The executor remembers its selected sandbox\n\nThe prepared remote process now retains the executor-selected\n`SandboxType`. This value never crosses the executor boundary.\n\nCommands started without a sandbox retain `SandboxType::None` and are\nnever reported as sandbox denials.\n\n### The executor uses the existing denial heuristic\n\nThe existing local denial heuristic moves from `codex-core` into the\nshared `codex-sandboxing` crate.\n\nWhen a sandboxed remote process exits, the executor:\n\n1. waits the same short output grace period used by local unified exec;\n2. reads the output currently available in the existing retained output\nbuffer;\n3. runs the existing heuristic using the exit code and common denial\nmessages;\n4. stores the yes/no result before publishing the process exit.\n\nThis deliberately matches the old local unified-exec behavior. It does\nnot add a new streaming classifier, another output buffer, or stronger\noutput-retention guarantees.\n\n### The protocol reports a portable boolean\n\n`process/read` gains `sandboxDenied`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"exited\": true,\n  \"exitCode\": 1,\n  \"closed\": false,\n  \"sandboxDenied\": true\n}\n```\n\nThe field defaults to `false` when an older executor omits it. The\nresponse does not expose the executor sandbox implementation or\nexecutor-native paths.\n\n### Unified exec uses the existing error path\n\nThe exec-server client carries `sandboxDenied` into the unified process\nstate. If it is true, unified exec returns the existing `SandboxDenied`\nerror instead of trying to classify remote output using an\norchestrator-side sandbox type.\n\nRemote process exit remains visible as soon as the process exits. This\nPR does not wait for stdout or stderr to close and does not change the\nexisting process lifecycle.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis PR is intentionally limited to matching the existing local\nunified-exec behavior for the initial command execution path.\n\nIt does not add:\n\n- incremental denial tracking across the full output stream;\n- new denial handling for commands completed later through\n`write_stdin`;\n- new guarantees for preserving the semantic flag during the narrow\nreconnect-recovery race.\n\nThose can be considered separately if the same behavior is added for\nlocal execution.\n\n## Test coverage\n\nOne remote end-to-end integration test covers the complete intended\nflow:\n\n```text\nremote read-only sandbox\n    -> denied write\n    -> executor reports the denial\n    -> Codex requests approval\n    -> user approves\n    -> retry succeeds on the remote executor\n```\n\nExisting lifecycle coverage continues to verify that remote process exit\nis reported before late output streams close.","tree":{"sha":"21e82fbebd039716b895b8be80b514d60ae78071","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/21e82fbebd039716b895b8be80b514d60ae78071"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/9f06cf1a0907f650887ca26af5cee13b4f9a13ea","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOXHoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhJ8QAIp6f8/dbg9y596X0/v/Xo/e\nWP5XXmAK7Mb4SKfc9EJlCjY0oei7h0wWmm4sSvjBza9J3frW8xX1xVBXAKWRaHOZ\n4kAR4R6NA9XK9a6snp3/NyiWJJM4/i5oXFfGbVVm0O870QcwtxkpFEZcW+84ZmnX\nFSLOzGv6elj9z34LdQ/y/Ey+R5xy2OL28h+KhpEf8rPSwYqXv6l4XpqyWGSQ7Vxq\n6tO24DoQJ0XYTuYX+4qyyJeBoz7cuOP+sxGgn1g3GP/MrLCTlUzEUQUPslL2NrWl\nh1+ddHdoZOx9zgmV1jC6Xy31XZZx3oeCZbsyAELZ8n95Vt6A0IZ4JdMit7xHRGgY\n8Z64ay0/usli0oiPklxby8sGNONcEwT3/t+mB6/BcoioeDsUBLKAGvCg50aCp3CW\nlTcFYymjiAf8t3HP8E3i4k9jNQgSSDDJNkOwBBvqy13obfm8/y/5KAjO+3u5SOIW\nHgzHhbTLSXM0/XVdUqszThYWTml0npfW7n74kBExQLGV1+R4QEnxN+f1Is6Tud6g\nHGJWUxqucQshUor6q3b4HpHzdwDb3cCsW3/Cv8JhdFgfX5CIa1tZNGCXc79dksQX\nyWtbkdoTq61Se5ECxF4ENSakpP5xZwZDCef9P7QoyEwM4JIJqRW1VFRppQQCc9un\nFman9cdQy5SajKmA54mx\n=+aik\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 21e82fbebd039716b895b8be80b514d60ae78071\nparent f6fa2593126d726fed67920e24eadc5c5c12bf0d\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782149608 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782149608 +0200\n\nReport remote sandbox denials semantically (#29424)\n\n## Why\n\n#29113 moved remote sandbox setup and enforcement to the exec server.\nThat gives the executor ownership of the platform-specific work: a Linux\nexecutor chooses and runs a Linux sandbox even when the Codex\norchestrator is running on macOS or Windows.\n\nIt also means the orchestrator no longer knows which concrete sandbox\nthe executor selected. When that sandbox blocks a remote command, the\norchestrator currently sees only a failed process and can treat the\ndenial as an ordinary command failure. The existing sandbox approval and\nretry path is then skipped.\n\nThis PR lets the executor report one portable fact:\n\n> This command probably failed because the executor sandbox blocked it.\n\nThe executor keeps its concrete sandbox type private. The protocol sends\nonly the semantic result.\n\n## Example\n\nSuppose a local macOS Codex session asks a Linux devbox to write outside\nthe allowed workspace.\n\nBefore this PR:\n\n```text\nLinux sandbox blocks the write\n    -> remote process exits with \"Permission denied\"\n    -> local orchestrator sees an ordinary command failure\n    -> the normal sandbox approval and retry path can be skipped\n```\n\nWith this PR:\n\n```text\nLinux sandbox blocks the write\n    -> executor reports sandboxDenied: true\n    -> unified exec returns UnifiedExecError::SandboxDenied\n    -> the existing approval prompt is shown\n    -> an approved retry runs through the existing unsandboxed retry path\n```\n\n## What changes\n\n### The executor remembers its selected sandbox\n\nThe prepared remote process now retains the executor-selected\n`SandboxType`. This value never crosses the executor boundary.\n\nCommands started without a sandbox retain `SandboxType::None` and are\nnever reported as sandbox denials.\n\n### The executor uses the existing denial heuristic\n\nThe existing local denial heuristic moves from `codex-core` into the\nshared `codex-sandboxing` crate.\n\nWhen a sandboxed remote process exits, the executor:\n\n1. waits the same short output grace period used by local unified exec;\n2. reads the output currently available in the existing retained output\nbuffer;\n3. runs the existing heuristic using the exit code and common denial\nmessages;\n4. stores the yes/no result before publishing the process exit.\n\nThis deliberately matches the old local unified-exec behavior. It does\nnot add a new streaming classifier, another output buffer, or stronger\noutput-retention guarantees.\n\n### The protocol reports a portable boolean\n\n`process/read` gains `sandboxDenied`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"exited\": true,\n  \"exitCode\": 1,\n  \"closed\": false,\n  \"sandboxDenied\": true\n}\n```\n\nThe field defaults to `false` when an older executor omits it. The\nresponse does not expose the executor sandbox implementation or\nexecutor-native paths.\n\n### Unified exec uses the existing error path\n\nThe exec-server client carries `sandboxDenied` into the unified process\nstate. If it is true, unified exec returns the existing `SandboxDenied`\nerror instead of trying to classify remote output using an\norchestrator-side sandbox type.\n\nRemote process exit remains visible as soon as the process exits. This\nPR does not wait for stdout or stderr to close and does not change the\nexisting process lifecycle.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis PR is intentionally limited to matching the existing local\nunified-exec behavior for the initial command execution path.\n\nIt does not add:\n\n- incremental denial tracking across the full output stream;\n- new denial handling for commands completed later through\n`write_stdin`;\n- new guarantees for preserving the semantic flag during the narrow\nreconnect-recovery race.\n\nThose can be considered separately if the same behavior is added for\nlocal execution.\n\n## Test coverage\n\nOne remote end-to-end integration test covers the complete intended\nflow:\n\n```text\nremote read-only sandbox\n    -> denied write\n    -> executor reports the denial\n    -> Codex requests approval\n    -> user approves\n    -> retry succeeds on the remote executor\n```\n\nExisting lifecycle coverage continues to verify that remote process exit\nis reported before late output streams close.","verified_at":"2026-06-22T17:33:29Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9f06cf1a0907f650887ca26af5cee13b4f9a13ea","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9f06cf1a0907f650887ca26af5cee13b4f9a13ea","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9f06cf1a0907f650887ca26af5cee13b4f9a13ea/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f6fa2593126d726fed67920e24eadc5c5c12bf0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f6fa2593126d726fed67920e24eadc5c5c12bf0d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f6fa2593126d726fed67920e24eadc5c5c12bf0d"}]},{"sha":"f6fa2593126d726fed67920e24eadc5c5c12bf0d","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGY2ZmEyNTkzMTI2ZDcyNmZlZDY3OTIwZTI0ZWFkYzVjNWMxMmJmMGQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"canvrno-oai","email":"kbond@openai.com","date":"2026-06-22T17:30:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T17:30:16Z"},"message":"TUI Plugin Sharing 3 - render remote plugin catalog sections (#26703)\n\n## Summary\n\n[#26701](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/26701) added remote plugin\nidentity support, [#26702](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/26702)\nadded remote-section fetching and state, and\n[#28768](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/28768) extracted the\ncatalog rendering module. This PR builds the product-facing `/plugins`\ncatalog on that foundation so remote records appear as OpenAI Curated,\nWorkspace, and Shared with me sections rather than backend marketplace\nimplementation details.\n\nPlugin details remain read-only for sharing metadata. This PR does not\nadd share-authoring actions or change the app-server protocol.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Renders OpenAI Curated, Workspace, and Shared with me sections with\nloading, empty, and error states.\n- Preserves section selection and stable tab ordering as remote sections\ntransition between fallback and populated states.\n- Shows OpenAI Curated loading only when the explicit vertical fallback\nrequest was issued.\n- Centralizes remote marketplace identity matching around the existing\nmarketplace constants.\n- Uses product labels for remote marketplaces and identifies the\npersonal marketplace as Local by its path.\n- Shows read-only source, authentication, version, and sharing metadata\nin plugin detail views.\n- Applies narrow display deduplication for local and remote records\nsharing a remote plugin ID:\n  - installed records take precedence;\n- local mapped sources are preferred for details only when their\ninstalled state matches the selected record.\n- Returns from detail and confirmation views through the current plugin\ncache so newly loaded remote sections are not overwritten by an older\ncaptured response.\n- Keeps admin-disabled plugins view-only and labels default-installed\nplugins as Available by default.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew tests:\n\n- `plugins_popup_admin_disabled_available_plugin_has_view_only_hint`\n- `plugins_popup_remote_section_fallback_states_snapshot`\n-\n`plugins_popup_installed_remote_row_keeps_remote_detail_when_local_share_is_uninstalled`\n\nUpdated existing plugin catalog tests and snapshots for product labels,\ndetail metadata, personal-marketplace labeling, and stable tab ordering.\n\nVerification:\n\n- `cargo clippy -p codex-tui --all-targets -- -D warnings`\n\n## Follow-ups\n\n- Local/remote duplicate normalization should eventually move into\napp-server. This PR intentionally keeps the compatibility behavior\nnarrow and display-only.\n- PR5 will sanitize sensitive components before displaying Git source\nURLs.","tree":{"sha":"79f0009b651f2c2a98a20690a9efdfbb10595c81","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/79f0009b651f2c2a98a20690a9efdfbb10595c81"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/f6fa2593126d726fed67920e24eadc5c5c12bf0d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOXEoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAevgQABciVMhG64QDxdzdd2I2Eyau\n/7+07PnvirviOacmMJu+cFksCjcsJiUllBNMNYh6lc1EfdvwHFpcCabMfPntsbIr\n1ogyW6ag9cGNqlb2XfPJQhkn2GKtKu8HYJIPasPOzaxqemaLdZyiQ+QBp8Vf+RsK\nFNE1VwSzkJYenD3AD1K/NfnSThpISLrNf3qvY6peDwDalqqyLXuqj2bq3/Eq/Wy4\n/k0ZlQsQUP0+YCBqtcjIQ65TCyTYI435/yj90Vz7vnW6pfU4yEPe/lz+sl9MWqyE\n3CQv/E7f4FoS00U+0H57KYQPjh19SMwnG3mcie2tOyjtWpjo6og88/VlyarWueWI\n9+xt0RgwjxtB/oqrdZ7iWU6rgItcXLOlYUvZ//q8afsCxTYNFIejAgXPbnlyhtFq\ncH7P1U5850yTb3uzSPbYuiOyA4q+QnTLPU/BKUfYk2/xs2C02alWkJGGBxtw3zxn\nC5PSnzRxaDHqmGadF2dW/p+QPB0+tsXxsbkRXTOoyXR/++8HK5G8LjmXf8jtD1r2\n9k5pDVFzAb+odAHGEMAInc4fu5H0Ya6NzRO+SfbK0Ky4M8t6jqUV8ojAxH91shpI\nFnVT/kEl9Cr+GR+WhbW8tI18xD8pwl0MD+DtqyT/YvOHPkDfxK9q6o2FuftFDLxS\n+NzCIibykl0KaoTljIlM\n=uO/9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 79f0009b651f2c2a98a20690a9efdfbb10595c81\nparent 44dbae90eb5a2e3e047d9636bf2463f3beb00fa8\nauthor canvrno-oai <kbond@openai.com> 1782149416 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782149416 -0700\n\nTUI Plugin Sharing 3 - render remote plugin catalog sections (#26703)\n\n## Summary\n\n[#26701](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/26701) added remote plugin\nidentity support, [#26702](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/26702)\nadded remote-section fetching and state, and\n[#28768](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/28768) extracted the\ncatalog rendering module. This PR builds the product-facing `/plugins`\ncatalog on that foundation so remote records appear as OpenAI Curated,\nWorkspace, and Shared with me sections rather than backend marketplace\nimplementation details.\n\nPlugin details remain read-only for sharing metadata. This PR does not\nadd share-authoring actions or change the app-server protocol.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Renders OpenAI Curated, Workspace, and Shared with me sections with\nloading, empty, and error states.\n- Preserves section selection and stable tab ordering as remote sections\ntransition between fallback and populated states.\n- Shows OpenAI Curated loading only when the explicit vertical fallback\nrequest was issued.\n- Centralizes remote marketplace identity matching around the existing\nmarketplace constants.\n- Uses product labels for remote marketplaces and identifies the\npersonal marketplace as Local by its path.\n- Shows read-only source, authentication, version, and sharing metadata\nin plugin detail views.\n- Applies narrow display deduplication for local and remote records\nsharing a remote plugin ID:\n  - installed records take precedence;\n- local mapped sources are preferred for details only when their\ninstalled state matches the selected record.\n- Returns from detail and confirmation views through the current plugin\ncache so newly loaded remote sections are not overwritten by an older\ncaptured response.\n- Keeps admin-disabled plugins view-only and labels default-installed\nplugins as Available by default.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew tests:\n\n- `plugins_popup_admin_disabled_available_plugin_has_view_only_hint`\n- `plugins_popup_remote_section_fallback_states_snapshot`\n-\n`plugins_popup_installed_remote_row_keeps_remote_detail_when_local_share_is_uninstalled`\n\nUpdated existing plugin catalog tests and snapshots for product labels,\ndetail metadata, personal-marketplace labeling, and stable tab ordering.\n\nVerification:\n\n- `cargo clippy -p codex-tui --all-targets -- -D warnings`\n\n## Follow-ups\n\n- Local/remote duplicate normalization should eventually move into\napp-server. This PR intentionally keeps the compatibility behavior\nnarrow and display-only.\n- PR5 will sanitize sensitive components before displaying Git source\nURLs.","verified_at":"2026-06-22T17:30:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f6fa2593126d726fed67920e24eadc5c5c12bf0d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f6fa2593126d726fed67920e24eadc5c5c12bf0d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f6fa2593126d726fed67920e24eadc5c5c12bf0d/comments","author":{"login":"canvrno-oai","id":257630656,"node_id":"U_kgDOD1shwA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257630656?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/canvrno-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"44dbae90eb5a2e3e047d9636bf2463f3beb00fa8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/44dbae90eb5a2e3e047d9636bf2463f3beb00fa8","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/44dbae90eb5a2e3e047d9636bf2463f3beb00fa8"}]},{"sha":"44dbae90eb5a2e3e047d9636bf2463f3beb00fa8","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDQ0ZGJhZTkwZWI1YTJlM2UwNDdkOTYzNmJmMjQ2M2YzYmViMDBmYTg","commit":{"author":{"name":"jameswt-oai","email":"jameswt@openai.com","date":"2026-06-22T17:27:23Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T17:27:23Z"},"message":"[codex] Centralize Plugin Analytics Metadata (#27102)\n\nThis PR moves construction of `PluginTelemetryMetadata` from loader and\nmodel helpers into `PluginsManager`, which already owns installed plugin\nstate and will eventually perform remote identity enrichment. The\nmetadata type remains in `codex-plugin`, and serialized analytics events\nremain unchanged.\n\n## Before\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    subgraph Events[\"Analytics event paths\"]\n        direction TB\n        Lifecycle[\"Local install / uninstall\"]\n        Config[\"Enable / disable\"]\n        Remote[\"Remote install\"]\n        Used[\"Plugin used\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Construction[\"Metadata construction\"]\n        direction TB\n        Loader[\"Loader telemetry helpers\"]\n        Summary[\"PluginCapabilitySummary::telemetry_metadata\"]\n        Override[\"Caller adds remote_plugin_id\"]\n    end\n\n    Metadata[\"PluginTelemetryMetadata\"]\n\n    Lifecycle --> Loader\n    Config --> Loader\n    Remote --> Loader\n    Loader -->|\"local events\"| Metadata\n    Loader -->|\"remote install\"| Override\n    Override --> Metadata\n    Used --> Summary\n    Summary --> Metadata\n```\n\nTelemetry metadata was constructed through loader helpers, a\ncapability-summary method, and a remote-install call-site override.\n\n## After\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    subgraph Events[\"Analytics event paths\"]\n        direction TB\n        Lifecycle[\"Local install / uninstall\"]\n        Config[\"Enable / disable\"]\n        Remote[\"Remote install\"]\n        Used[\"Plugin used\"]\n    end\n\n    Manager[\"PluginsManager — single construction owner\"]\n    Metadata[\"PluginTelemetryMetadata\"]\n\n    Lifecycle --> Manager\n    Config --> Manager\n    Remote -->|\"authoritative remote ID\"| Manager\n    Used -->|\"capability summary\"| Manager\n    Manager --> Metadata\n```\n\nEvery analytics path delegates metadata construction to\n`PluginsManager`. Remote install still supplies its authoritative\nbackend ID explicitly.\n\n## What Changes\n\n- Make loader code return a focused plugin capability summary instead of\nconstructing analytics metadata.\n- Centralize immutable plugin telemetry metadata construction in\n`PluginsManager`.\n- Route local install/uninstall, remote install, enable/disable, and\nplugin-used emitters through the manager.\n- Preserve the current serialized analytics contract exactly.\n\nNormal metadata still has no remote override. Remote install continues\nto provide its authoritative backend ID explicitly, so the existing\nserializer continues reporting that ID through `plugin_id`.\nSnapshot-based enrichment is intentionally deferred to the final PR.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins` (238 tests passed)\n- `just test -p codex-plugin` (3 tests passed)\n- Scoped Clippy/compile checks passed for `codex-plugin`,\n`codex-core-plugins`, `codex-app-server`, and `codex-core`.\n\n## Split Overview\n\n```text\nmain\n├── #27093  Debug analytics capture                 (merged)\n├── #27099  Non-mutating plugin smoke               (merged)\n├── #27100  Remote install/uninstall smoke          (merged)\n└── #27102  Plugin telemetry metadata refactor      ← you are here\n    └── #27669  Persist remote plugin identity\n\nAfter #27102 and #27669 merge:\n└── Final PR: add explicit local and remote IDs to plugin analytics\n```\n\nReview order and dependencies:\n\n1. [#27093 Add debug-only analytics event\ncapture](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27093) (merged)\n2. [#27099 Add a plugin analytics smoke\nworkflow](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27099) (merged)\n3. [#27100 Add a remote plugin analytics mutation smoke\nworkflow](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27100) (merged)\n4. This metadata refactor, independent and based on `main`\n5. [#27669 Persist remote plugin\nidentity](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27669), stacked on this\nPR\n6. Final remote-ID behavior PR, created after the prerequisites merge\n\nThe original [#26281](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/26281)\nremains open as the aggregate reference until the final replacement PR\nis published.","tree":{"sha":"059760f476852cb71f21bbb6d207e973734e30db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/059760f476852cb71f21bbb6d207e973734e30db"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/44dbae90eb5a2e3e047d9636bf2463f3beb00fa8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOXB7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVf0QAFR8tEObnGZQ15dRg4mKVtTq\nYC/7AUcGvqxA983suAHKIOqVI5gPgk2YhblcvvLuEXvw29uinOism065bJ1thVGE\nUK4UG32ft9lK61RO557mJqsYGVsxF0r2JgKixrPD0UeTQfJoQRF2L/X7En0Xfq7L\ndJT/gGE2LErltk2aWjYT7+Cmac8lVKzOyuPBlyjUL6JO0lir9k/oOwKl0uEDAzzd\nOCh4LfeMV3fIvpTdGNY2ZAkDta7y4XyoQrvsw9B3N+zgE5AYh5Fq3pXKdXREE6ut\ny3/ULyLugi0bZeF+eg2ywDJjGFZR86miYpNu+0XWOYwAMY8Jp5Gjo2YQpbcXLtgi\nx+RmXnmsaP56I1V+eclo/lgVQ1CNtwGvS+4EVAm2kVrzOUZf2QRh/fEBM7+aIIx4\nG7Zf40+sp42iy7uxxX1S+pB0KemgreaqSiQofv4h87G0zlmQig6VP8pYqCfTA/R3\nBLibwMj8PEWjR7HZkUksMHz0exybBLlnedTLv2gSXP/Yim47gUOho/5qhliN8i/9\nZT1l0ofB2iVETD/uU+Ct+LaRUBlEDi1LduNXRGMVpI1UPd5jhSQeKHkvJOEs4X4m\naRii2BnRMyq3LjuziVjzNtRoce4aSIBiYlfeSzPhxRQLk8ZYRbxEivj3SY/rflcY\nf6nQh9w7ajKjLLssc25X\n=rcO3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 059760f476852cb71f21bbb6d207e973734e30db\nparent c1f8b280b5cfc280c75682cab1b5be4a4dc58709\nauthor jameswt-oai <jameswt@openai.com> 1782149243 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782149243 -0700\n\n[codex] Centralize Plugin Analytics Metadata (#27102)\n\nThis PR moves construction of `PluginTelemetryMetadata` from loader and\nmodel helpers into `PluginsManager`, which already owns installed plugin\nstate and will eventually perform remote identity enrichment. The\nmetadata type remains in `codex-plugin`, and serialized analytics events\nremain unchanged.\n\n## Before\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    subgraph Events[\"Analytics event paths\"]\n        direction TB\n        Lifecycle[\"Local install / uninstall\"]\n        Config[\"Enable / disable\"]\n        Remote[\"Remote install\"]\n        Used[\"Plugin used\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Construction[\"Metadata construction\"]\n        direction TB\n        Loader[\"Loader telemetry helpers\"]\n        Summary[\"PluginCapabilitySummary::telemetry_metadata\"]\n        Override[\"Caller adds remote_plugin_id\"]\n    end\n\n    Metadata[\"PluginTelemetryMetadata\"]\n\n    Lifecycle --> Loader\n    Config --> Loader\n    Remote --> Loader\n    Loader -->|\"local events\"| Metadata\n    Loader -->|\"remote install\"| Override\n    Override --> Metadata\n    Used --> Summary\n    Summary --> Metadata\n```\n\nTelemetry metadata was constructed through loader helpers, a\ncapability-summary method, and a remote-install call-site override.\n\n## After\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    subgraph Events[\"Analytics event paths\"]\n        direction TB\n        Lifecycle[\"Local install / uninstall\"]\n        Config[\"Enable / disable\"]\n        Remote[\"Remote install\"]\n        Used[\"Plugin used\"]\n    end\n\n    Manager[\"PluginsManager — single construction owner\"]\n    Metadata[\"PluginTelemetryMetadata\"]\n\n    Lifecycle --> Manager\n    Config --> Manager\n    Remote -->|\"authoritative remote ID\"| Manager\n    Used -->|\"capability summary\"| Manager\n    Manager --> Metadata\n```\n\nEvery analytics path delegates metadata construction to\n`PluginsManager`. Remote install still supplies its authoritative\nbackend ID explicitly.\n\n## What Changes\n\n- Make loader code return a focused plugin capability summary instead of\nconstructing analytics metadata.\n- Centralize immutable plugin telemetry metadata construction in\n`PluginsManager`.\n- Route local install/uninstall, remote install, enable/disable, and\nplugin-used emitters through the manager.\n- Preserve the current serialized analytics contract exactly.\n\nNormal metadata still has no remote override. Remote install continues\nto provide its authoritative backend ID explicitly, so the existing\nserializer continues reporting that ID through `plugin_id`.\nSnapshot-based enrichment is intentionally deferred to the final PR.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins` (238 tests passed)\n- `just test -p codex-plugin` (3 tests passed)\n- Scoped Clippy/compile checks passed for `codex-plugin`,\n`codex-core-plugins`, `codex-app-server`, and `codex-core`.\n\n## Split Overview\n\n```text\nmain\n├── #27093  Debug analytics capture                 (merged)\n├── #27099  Non-mutating plugin smoke               (merged)\n├── #27100  Remote install/uninstall smoke          (merged)\n└── #27102  Plugin telemetry metadata refactor      ← you are here\n    └── #27669  Persist remote plugin identity\n\nAfter #27102 and #27669 merge:\n└── Final PR: add explicit local and remote IDs to plugin analytics\n```\n\nReview order and dependencies:\n\n1. [#27093 Add debug-only analytics event\ncapture](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27093) (merged)\n2. [#27099 Add a plugin analytics smoke\nworkflow](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27099) (merged)\n3. [#27100 Add a remote plugin analytics mutation smoke\nworkflow](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27100) (merged)\n4. This metadata refactor, independent and based on `main`\n5. [#27669 Persist remote plugin\nidentity](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27669), stacked on this\nPR\n6. Final remote-ID behavior PR, created after the prerequisites merge\n\nThe original [#26281](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/26281)\nremains open as the aggregate reference until the final replacement PR\nis published.","verified_at":"2026-06-22T17:27:24Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/44dbae90eb5a2e3e047d9636bf2463f3beb00fa8","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/44dbae90eb5a2e3e047d9636bf2463f3beb00fa8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/44dbae90eb5a2e3e047d9636bf2463f3beb00fa8/comments","author":{"login":"jameswt-oai","id":247462917,"node_id":"U_kgDODr_8BQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247462917?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jameswt-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c1f8b280b5cfc280c75682cab1b5be4a4dc58709","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c1f8b280b5cfc280c75682cab1b5be4a4dc58709","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c1f8b280b5cfc280c75682cab1b5be4a4dc58709"}]},{"sha":"c1f8b280b5cfc280c75682cab1b5be4a4dc58709","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGMxZjhiMjgwYjVjZmMyODBjNzU2ODJjYWIxYjViZTRhNGRjNTg3MDk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-22T17:26:30Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T17:26:30Z"},"message":"ci: restore custom Windows runner with hermetic LLVM 0.7.9 (#29143)\n\nThe custom Windows argument-comment-lint job was temporarily moved to\n`windows-2022` in #28940 after hermetic LLVM source extraction failed on\nthe newer runner. This takes the upstream extraction fix so the job can\nreturn to the intended custom runner.\n\nThis upgrades `llvm` to `0.7.9` and `rules_cc` to `0.2.18`, refreshes\nthe module lock, rebases the remaining Windows and custom libc++\npatches, drops the obsolete symlink-extraction workaround, and restores\nthe `windows-x64` runner configuration.\n\nValidation:\n\n- Verified all LLVM patches apply cleanly against the `0.7.9` source.\n- Built `@llvm-project//compiler-rt:clang_rt.builtins.static`.","tree":{"sha":"f44ac2b6e40d7a27e98e256f1aea5cbfbe1de4f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/f44ac2b6e40d7a27e98e256f1aea5cbfbe1de4f0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/c1f8b280b5cfc280c75682cab1b5be4a4dc58709","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOXBGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIC4QAEU+ivgN2jHeLgzbNy/s9GAl\nbZJ4ZSGEMAaSVpeN8m9GAdc0VHkVl9g1eosnNH+N3Bwbp+4BoO+/w+0BrpB24ROM\nobPdOU1Z9k5Yu8D87PcytEw1SmZGw5/i1jVxoNXCQcG9673gzKU/aqumOAo4TZsn\nRS4s4SYFCeJcYIhPqHzfJZMfQLvrmFuIWgHfGHkFhKPUmG0NpX45hzy/Snhg666/\nxkhp4yi8rry9QZdIg2aaTr9XMGW0YbO7tybZn7nd5mXFOk356NhXUFL9Xyvf/MWC\nSFk8k14qIKTPCS5vfamyq6mXFZOMWHHhZPSKiJMmpqfeghcN4kgz1oTR67u2OyqM\nAgtfX6bjN9oUvLso4ODAuPHgyQGX6rRo1pACIApm/kSxVF1LDtLC6gKEjFYG99ro\nnvwuup2H44dqYP6R1P7p5uPfe6XtTvzjALj9G0uQ4sTkrNDrMKWZARJ9NSu/tZwh\nG6wbzzPUfrJOBVCRLHD2GXHUxPhyZ7PkbiH/Hsok62enIyIceIh8ihBKY1GXP9iO\nB5pN0U6iSnSTnReeszexI7m1z6QjDzKtdDckNZOaK5x/iafHgVhqCVowNI+GnEBr\n85iQpZxr0q6Ul7vb7F/WyDjxS43qZNdaea5OJvbkSFHthEXtzW/0z70IOS029B0W\naWYo8K3lenOOvAbTApU2\n=cZL5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f44ac2b6e40d7a27e98e256f1aea5cbfbe1de4f0\nparent e79d72d75d479c1aceaf6a5853833e7ddad33c29\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1782149190 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782149190 +0000\n\nci: restore custom Windows runner with hermetic LLVM 0.7.9 (#29143)\n\nThe custom Windows argument-comment-lint job was temporarily moved to\n`windows-2022` in #28940 after hermetic LLVM source extraction failed on\nthe newer runner. This takes the upstream extraction fix so the job can\nreturn to the intended custom runner.\n\nThis upgrades `llvm` to `0.7.9` and `rules_cc` to `0.2.18`, refreshes\nthe module lock, rebases the remaining Windows and custom libc++\npatches, drops the obsolete symlink-extraction workaround, and restores\nthe `windows-x64` runner configuration.\n\nValidation:\n\n- Verified all LLVM patches apply cleanly against the `0.7.9` source.\n- Built `@llvm-project//compiler-rt:clang_rt.builtins.static`.","verified_at":"2026-06-22T17:26:31Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c1f8b280b5cfc280c75682cab1b5be4a4dc58709","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c1f8b280b5cfc280c75682cab1b5be4a4dc58709","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c1f8b280b5cfc280c75682cab1b5be4a4dc58709/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e79d72d75d479c1aceaf6a5853833e7ddad33c29","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e79d72d75d479c1aceaf6a5853833e7ddad33c29","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e79d72d75d479c1aceaf6a5853833e7ddad33c29"}]},{"sha":"e79d72d75d479c1aceaf6a5853833e7ddad33c29","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGU3OWQ3MmQ3NWQ0NzljMWFjZWFmNmE1ODUzODMzZTdkZGFkMzNjMjk","commit":{"author":{"name":"rka-oai","email":"rka@openai.com","date":"2026-06-22T17:05:11Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T17:05:11Z"},"message":"remove flag for image preparation (#29429)\n\n## What\n\n- make Fjord's centralized response-item image preparation unconditional\nfor new and resumed history\n- have local user images and `view_image` outputs always defer decoding\nand resizing to that path\n- retain `resize_all_images` as an ignored, removed compatibility key\nfor released clients\n- delete the flag-off producer paths and obsolete policy-specific tests\n\n## Why\n\nCentralized preparation is now the intended image path. Keeping the\nruntime feature checks also kept two image-processing implementations\nalive and allowed client config to select the legacy behavior.\n\nThis is a clean replacement for #28975, rebuilt from the latest `main`.\n\n## How\n\n`prepare_response_items` now runs whenever items enter history and\nwhenever persisted history is reconstructed. Producers emit deferred\nimage data, so malformed images become the existing model-visible\nplaceholder instead of failing the session at the producer.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just fix -p codex-core -p codex-features`\n- `just test -p codex-features` — 52 passed\n- focused affected `codex-core` set — 20 passed\n- `just test -p codex-core handle_accepts_explicit_high_detail` — 1\npassed\n- full `just test -p codex-core` attempt — 2,723 passed; 88 unrelated\nenvironment failures from read-only `~/.codex` SQLite state and\nunavailable integration helper binaries","tree":{"sha":"ed9ed6befa9dd9290fff114cb94a9eb38696cea2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/ed9ed6befa9dd9290fff114cb94a9eb38696cea2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/e79d72d75d479c1aceaf6a5853833e7ddad33c29","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOWtHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdqoQAC9c0Zv7S7JwTnIakeB/iQ6m\n4A0ehWw6La5JRhsOBKXz3v3+dKc0SR/KGFKHyNP+1IhIiZkr2Ro4Z93sEpaEszCb\n3svC+02Bm3TiiAZUmrzU74yFlscaV6JoGd+7FCV1sBcef23iqeLxKzDB8hHZrrGu\nZAvurKbihSSEpSG6DrMK6yx6pUeS4C6TChhUUFdZ5sBT/4B28HbtKu3ELPkuYuNw\nwWpJiZMY8IElSUDZg4RNiqoCEOZyuw2AldvikcnuDHdIees7gPmF82925FW0YRNO\nx9U5E4vQTGThLJEox111WVZD1PmmhWoJtJRUvfWNiPltWztsT8V59iP8FgnlHKx4\noWRqCKXwI/mK4TxdS0lgg+7Wo6hzqcP46zbFmSVhG3kyZ+aNpw4sX5kvPTRIrJ4n\nT1bzu8/ABlADK4BEROrhXhMWUkq9xfYqcycKC6YjLcvHxA50hEX9V+0g1xvT1eYb\np9uiQ7fmT4m6cbwhmfIAjk1y5SILeRgX4oH+Ak18aRe1CNN2ej3xdRnxcGgAom9A\nQ7C9NW8xhHAQ41wLKO2eJleSi/lAuQoHLRBLrbMBI98Ry4/OZpIHIQvdiXHTvycL\nSSWebB3QmjdFtZWwUCyt3Rv7rTGvNhiuHL6AQw1fq99meFiPFozZvRA/dPPtRoCD\nSrshafe0duC0kcZOIABh\n=UBY+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ed9ed6befa9dd9290fff114cb94a9eb38696cea2\nparent e98d43ac372ddf7f513c0e30c56dd8dc35ea5404\nauthor rka-oai <rka@openai.com> 1782147911 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782147911 -0700\n\nremove flag for image preparation (#29429)\n\n## What\n\n- make Fjord's centralized response-item image preparation unconditional\nfor new and resumed history\n- have local user images and `view_image` outputs always defer decoding\nand resizing to that path\n- retain `resize_all_images` as an ignored, removed compatibility key\nfor released clients\n- delete the flag-off producer paths and obsolete policy-specific tests\n\n## Why\n\nCentralized preparation is now the intended image path. Keeping the\nruntime feature checks also kept two image-processing implementations\nalive and allowed client config to select the legacy behavior.\n\nThis is a clean replacement for #28975, rebuilt from the latest `main`.\n\n## How\n\n`prepare_response_items` now runs whenever items enter history and\nwhenever persisted history is reconstructed. Producers emit deferred\nimage data, so malformed images become the existing model-visible\nplaceholder instead of failing the session at the producer.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just fix -p codex-core -p codex-features`\n- `just test -p codex-features` — 52 passed\n- focused affected `codex-core` set — 20 passed\n- `just test -p codex-core handle_accepts_explicit_high_detail` — 1\npassed\n- full `just test -p codex-core` attempt — 2,723 passed; 88 unrelated\nenvironment failures from read-only `~/.codex` SQLite state and\nunavailable integration helper binaries","verified_at":"2026-06-22T17:05:12Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e79d72d75d479c1aceaf6a5853833e7ddad33c29","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e79d72d75d479c1aceaf6a5853833e7ddad33c29","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e79d72d75d479c1aceaf6a5853833e7ddad33c29/comments","author":{"login":"rka-oai","id":240799229,"node_id":"U_kgDODlpN_Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/240799229?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/rka-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e98d43ac372ddf7f513c0e30c56dd8dc35ea5404","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e98d43ac372ddf7f513c0e30c56dd8dc35ea5404","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e98d43ac372ddf7f513c0e30c56dd8dc35ea5404"}]},{"sha":"e98d43ac372ddf7f513c0e30c56dd8dc35ea5404","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGU5OGQ0M2FjMzcyZGRmN2Y1MTNjMGUzMGM1NmRkOGRjMzVlYTU0MDQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-22T16:17:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T16:17:04Z"},"message":"Filter noisy targets from persistent logs (#29457)\n\n## Why\n\nThe local SQLite log sink currently enables TRACE for every target. This\npersists high-volume dependency logs bridged through `target=log` and\nduplicates OpenTelemetry mirror events in `codex_otel.log_only` and\n`codex_otel.trace_safe`.\n\nThese records rapidly consume the per-partition log budget and cause\nunnecessary SQLite insert-and-prune churn.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Keep TRACE persistence for other targets.\n- Exclude bridged `target=log` events from the SQLite sink.\n- Exclude the two `codex_otel` mirror targets from the SQLite sink.\n- Share the same filter between app-server and TUI.\n\nRemote OpenTelemetry export and metrics are unchanged.","tree":{"sha":"e71db0eaadf0d14a393f93b93b31a3618549c27a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/e71db0eaadf0d14a393f93b93b31a3618549c27a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/e98d43ac372ddf7f513c0e30c56dd8dc35ea5404","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOWAACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbyIQAGM8X6GMR5ZtPyBxgBi9xdJI\nxFHN+VOg8kVJ2FBaQp5BkHFc/8mT67waIWvgT3Xhi6UKhv5pF9Cy0ougiJQJVMg0\nNtMQWXezRi7RR85kmKBQloUQ1q2GAnZgeSzlPRdVwas+BCtQxf3oqnSmN0LMmV9/\nt9DRwt70MOiPu7dHp2u22Zh//fkV3RhRqOeuR2hFsSlHWA0nDgurneyb8MmMZzGs\n8C316K3qggG0DXrke28e56J5wuMypBOxWZCsxdqE0yYQ+lM9MwsA1pG8x5MIDEGW\n90dpuhqa6KDXKuz3/KIj3Vt9Kvv+NNx9Xuxnq585JsJCWkTr5oOpPAywI0i6Hwlx\nDScdaWWbxfRnIkldaXcm+DZKIWoa2K1/ISsPsCOorhfzfS//P4+vQjaZk6Jlx+JS\nXIk2bK4+BvtMfTUIWF6Sredq9qfSogdoS6KHnA3UNDtFK51h2jlmFdOuW1Jc2TsZ\nN6k8Nm7Jk/+gNknMc94kmZ8k2QMJ0qWmQQYQvYLHt9OM2XV7IY1/sx6pDM+pwEWL\nOcVcM3arnz+VgWE9vxJc43i6P9wpnalnQDmtlWMgx3lJygqcE1WVc1Jp71OVkZyJ\nQS7+gLqRIOWT9b3ID2dNIm+wroLf/vxtm18gBhPIt4eunvDZoLxbIxlREWqEc91e\ndScCz3awkIvlxM2aEJSK\n=dUyw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e71db0eaadf0d14a393f93b93b31a3618549c27a\nparent 8f8de7844f9a95ba0f07b9ae584b5c08b3173dd6\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782145024 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782145024 +0200\n\nFilter noisy targets from persistent logs (#29457)\n\n## Why\n\nThe local SQLite log sink currently enables TRACE for every target. This\npersists high-volume dependency logs bridged through `target=log` and\nduplicates OpenTelemetry mirror events in `codex_otel.log_only` and\n`codex_otel.trace_safe`.\n\nThese records rapidly consume the per-partition log budget and cause\nunnecessary SQLite insert-and-prune churn.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Keep TRACE persistence for other targets.\n- Exclude bridged `target=log` events from the SQLite sink.\n- Exclude the two `codex_otel` mirror targets from the SQLite sink.\n- Share the same filter between app-server and TUI.\n\nRemote OpenTelemetry export and metrics are unchanged.","verified_at":"2026-06-22T16:17:05Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e98d43ac372ddf7f513c0e30c56dd8dc35ea5404","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e98d43ac372ddf7f513c0e30c56dd8dc35ea5404","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e98d43ac372ddf7f513c0e30c56dd8dc35ea5404/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8f8de7844f9a95ba0f07b9ae584b5c08b3173dd6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8f8de7844f9a95ba0f07b9ae584b5c08b3173dd6","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8f8de7844f9a95ba0f07b9ae584b5c08b3173dd6"}]},{"sha":"8f8de7844f9a95ba0f07b9ae584b5c08b3173dd6","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDhmOGRlNzg0NGY5YTk1YmEwZjA3YjlhZTU4NGI1YzA4YjMxNzNkZDY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Owen Lin","email":"owenlin0@gmail.com","date":"2026-06-22T16:05:27Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T16:05:27Z"},"message":"fix(core): restore thread_source in x-codex-turn-metadata (#29455)\n\n## Description\n\nRestore `thread_source` in `x-codex-turn-metadata`.\n\nInadvertently removed `thread_source` from `x-codex-turn-metadata` in\nhttps://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27122 - didn't realize it was a\ntop-level thread app-server API field, not passed in\n`responsesapi_client_metadata`.\n\nThis also reserves the key so `responsesapi_client_metadata` cannot\noverride it.","tree":{"sha":"db9965d26a87c663c8d33b3aa89896f8e7b2187f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/db9965d26a87c663c8d33b3aa89896f8e7b2187f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/8f8de7844f9a95ba0f07b9ae584b5c08b3173dd6","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOV1HCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1IEQADv/cc7VBaAL9l2TWe13EYms\n6UhHfSEl2lk07gHxVh7F32U4lNjS+6JOOo0GyHc0JKLD3xWJHoaErysAMPn34kl8\nPr+OpEOoQEb4R0Ybvsn76Y+C6bmg2a8yyGWf+FLvSz3vM6CEVs3aa/O06sjCwFEn\nRZ7HaN4p7fH7DIbBKqxnO1y5MgTt0fjpfM/r2m7YK4IsCYeZDL+mpA4aA69rd73y\ncC22DqUNA5aX/K4k3A+t+4zMWeR/ubej1bypiFLS/JYfYjDoIFtzdwZvTIv28HJJ\ngUrj+pN9eZWlYNu7msiVzxajBt5RcKbU74lfWO0fBp5Kh0TN9dgIwseXC7yoeV1O\nlTGyqfWXhku7wH0WKnSTToOMyd4RELhzjUajA6HjcteA5ESBHj8CnR47OmT8dnVE\nS8huzGjeDTsWaJmMYGaebx6jGQ2Oha2QDnp3AtGZb6IL91j0ok673q0MEvJCzwwN\nAOcUQmA5rGerV3yENS7H20D7U+WpGbLejkveRgzRPX+T5rWsmDch1AF+/SQ+lDb5\nBcuV083YgTkkKfHrAaKWFPTj8wxedE8nUxKcMa33W4gLz5rL1KrMWdiyFjTecfe1\nRsyRDKkufoh9s1dQhaCkQd9ht2br8FRfhHmWN/NXRWQHFcSE5vy2ukB6+PIv1Vsu\nwOCCN5AoDIUNdahXhXUi\n=5VYy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree db9965d26a87c663c8d33b3aa89896f8e7b2187f\nparent 22886f21dee225bc54dcb3fd81771be810c61175\nauthor Owen Lin <owenlin0@gmail.com> 1782144327 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782144327 -0700\n\nfix(core): restore thread_source in x-codex-turn-metadata (#29455)\n\n## Description\n\nRestore `thread_source` in `x-codex-turn-metadata`.\n\nInadvertently removed `thread_source` from `x-codex-turn-metadata` in\nhttps://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27122 - didn't realize it was a\ntop-level thread app-server API field, not passed in\n`responsesapi_client_metadata`.\n\nThis also reserves the key so `responsesapi_client_metadata` cannot\noverride it.","verified_at":"2026-06-22T16:05:28Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8f8de7844f9a95ba0f07b9ae584b5c08b3173dd6","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8f8de7844f9a95ba0f07b9ae584b5c08b3173dd6","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8f8de7844f9a95ba0f07b9ae584b5c08b3173dd6/comments","author":{"login":"owenlin0","id":947871,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk0Nzg3MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/947871?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0","html_url":"https://github.com/owenlin0","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"22886f21dee225bc54dcb3fd81771be810c61175","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/22886f21dee225bc54dcb3fd81771be810c61175","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/22886f21dee225bc54dcb3fd81771be810c61175"}]},{"sha":"22886f21dee225bc54dcb3fd81771be810c61175","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDIyODg2ZjIxZGVlMjI1YmM1NGRjYjNmZDgxNzcxYmU4MTBjNjExNzU","commit":{"author":{"name":"sayan-oai","email":"sayan@openai.com","date":"2026-06-22T15:47:43Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T15:47:43Z"},"message":"core: refresh environment context before sampling (#29073)\n\n## Why\n\nNonblocking environment snapshots allow a turn to reach the model while\na remote environment is still starting. The initial context can describe\nthat environment as still loading, but nothing currently refreshes the\nmodel-visible environment context when startup finishes during the same\nturn.\n\nThis adds the first request-scoped reconciliation slice on top of\n#28683. It is gated by `DeferredExecutor` and intentionally updates only\nmodel-visible environment context; tools and other environment-derived\nstate will migrate separately.\n\n## What\n\n- Add a minimal `StepContext` containing the environment snapshot\ncaptured before each sampling request.\n- Render attached environments with their resolved shell and starting\nenvironments with `still loading`.\n- Track the latest environment state recorded in model history and\nappend a bounded update only when it changes.\n- Seed that baseline from full initial context so ready-at-start\nenvironments are not duplicated.\n- Clear the in-memory baseline when history is rewritten so replacement\nhistory can be refreshed safely.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core deferred_executor`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nenvironment_context_baseline_deduplicates_until_history_is_replaced`\n\nThe integration coverage verifies that a pending environment reaches the\nfirst request, the ready state reaches the next request, later requests\ndo not duplicate it, and ready-at-start environments remain\nsingle-injected.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Live verification</summary>\n\n- Connected to a real remote executor with startup deliberately delayed\nand forced three sampling requests in one turn.\n- Inspected the raw model inputs: request 1 showed the remote\nenvironment as `still loading`, request 2 appended its ready shell and\ncwd, and request 3 contained no duplicate ready update.\n- With the feature disabled, startup waited for the delayed executor and\nthe first request contained only the ready environment.\n- With a synchronously ready environment and the feature enabled, the\nfirst request contained one environment context with no duplicate.\n- Executed `pwd` and read a marker file through the remote process\nrunner; the command exited successfully and returned the remote cwd and\nmarker contents.\n\n</details>","tree":{"sha":"86a7cf83e27792f082d7e06ddea008107ed187e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/86a7cf83e27792f082d7e06ddea008107ed187e0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/22886f21dee225bc54dcb3fd81771be810c61175","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOVkfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPBgQAImd+HW37ZXKlW4+ObFRCihg\nTnMDKbk5X0W/vMQFjxyY3LyMHkLwoI+Vbp+KVceIcErZY7HqOoCUGp1lmBw76AwF\n/NHt814IQ17Dl3SLVn9RMN0nTOho1l5izXYU8GTnRyxYDtxUOSJry1Cvs+iqHtpp\nhuwTe+xUFcs2B/Rtp1pN5Dt69Dsf67UOqDToArJQVtT00CsahCAziKiEvQZ2KSY2\nIonVrDVIeEz41PZtJ16J9MiagTbuZawK4oF/92UVNayD01/pwewfXQWJsIUZ2s5f\n9SQ58wOD0yUE8h6oS+7HU/nxzjCs062EbS7fuOQIPLr5NOc768Z93V6+cThh4O4u\nR7XnS7LMGnYk1j+FGMDW19fGRP2/3ar55Whwa1I3RD94aYtMnzoV4nmAB3ppOpjT\nbQr2ZAC5VfL+3wq2vR3jyreMSizpF5cIT67Otsq/aknkx6/H3nVx/zp50b/zpv3G\ndzvFTllyoetm9O4ERR4vVI9261KAE6TrrHBj2Ak9gS216ZzCOc1G+P5Kv5CcCd5b\nvNZcudaAMLhL1pAEP6+RMcuDePNsNGdUocCPw4rdhsc7d2Nfqw4Wl3SGCIYUhfY7\nZHGc5T7XcdrJ5jrtLT0DrlZzhaQ8Ec+0LKnHpAyB1ttjN7sx5eoubRN7vnOmhQZn\ntAdoeA3+VAGt4EcihCdP\n=RX6Q\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 86a7cf83e27792f082d7e06ddea008107ed187e0\nparent 91e6da943b08677cf1c9346fb438488471fc03a5\nauthor sayan-oai <sayan@openai.com> 1782143263 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782143263 -0700\n\ncore: refresh environment context before sampling (#29073)\n\n## Why\n\nNonblocking environment snapshots allow a turn to reach the model while\na remote environment is still starting. The initial context can describe\nthat environment as still loading, but nothing currently refreshes the\nmodel-visible environment context when startup finishes during the same\nturn.\n\nThis adds the first request-scoped reconciliation slice on top of\n#28683. It is gated by `DeferredExecutor` and intentionally updates only\nmodel-visible environment context; tools and other environment-derived\nstate will migrate separately.\n\n## What\n\n- Add a minimal `StepContext` containing the environment snapshot\ncaptured before each sampling request.\n- Render attached environments with their resolved shell and starting\nenvironments with `still loading`.\n- Track the latest environment state recorded in model history and\nappend a bounded update only when it changes.\n- Seed that baseline from full initial context so ready-at-start\nenvironments are not duplicated.\n- Clear the in-memory baseline when history is rewritten so replacement\nhistory can be refreshed safely.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core deferred_executor`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nenvironment_context_baseline_deduplicates_until_history_is_replaced`\n\nThe integration coverage verifies that a pending environment reaches the\nfirst request, the ready state reaches the next request, later requests\ndo not duplicate it, and ready-at-start environments remain\nsingle-injected.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Live verification</summary>\n\n- Connected to a real remote executor with startup deliberately delayed\nand forced three sampling requests in one turn.\n- Inspected the raw model inputs: request 1 showed the remote\nenvironment as `still loading`, request 2 appended its ready shell and\ncwd, and request 3 contained no duplicate ready update.\n- With the feature disabled, startup waited for the delayed executor and\nthe first request contained only the ready environment.\n- With a synchronously ready environment and the feature enabled, the\nfirst request contained one environment context with no duplicate.\n- Executed `pwd` and read a marker file through the remote process\nrunner; the command exited successfully and returned the remote cwd and\nmarker contents.\n\n</details>","verified_at":"2026-06-22T15:47:44Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/22886f21dee225bc54dcb3fd81771be810c61175","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/22886f21dee225bc54dcb3fd81771be810c61175","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/22886f21dee225bc54dcb3fd81771be810c61175/comments","author":{"login":"sayan-oai","id":244841968,"node_id":"U_kgDODpf98A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/244841968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/sayan-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"91e6da943b08677cf1c9346fb438488471fc03a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/91e6da943b08677cf1c9346fb438488471fc03a5","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/91e6da943b08677cf1c9346fb438488471fc03a5"}]},{"sha":"91e6da943b08677cf1c9346fb438488471fc03a5","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDkxZTZkYTk0M2IwODY3N2NmMWM5MzQ2ZmI0Mzg0ODg0NzFmYzAzYTU","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-22T15:43:08Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T15:43:08Z"},"message":"Stop logging every Responses WebSocket event (#29432)\n\n## Why\n\nEvery successful Responses WebSocket event currently produces three\nlocal log records: the full payload at TRACE, an OpenTelemetry log\nevent, and an OpenTelemetry trace event.\n\nOn busy threads these records fill the 1,000-row log partition in\nseconds and cause continuous SQLite insert-and-prune churn.\n\nRelated to\nhttps://openai.slack.com/archives/C095U48JNL9/p1782128972644209\n\n## What changed\n\n- Stop logging each successful Responses WebSocket payload at TRACE.\n- Stop emitting `codex.websocket_event` as OpenTelemetry log and trace\nevents.\n- Keep WebSocket event counters, duration metrics, response timing\nmetrics, parsing, and error handling.","tree":{"sha":"bda9c6b00e2be2d3596fbd40fb0465306900dbd7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/bda9c6b00e2be2d3596fbd40fb0465306900dbd7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/91e6da943b08677cf1c9346fb438488471fc03a5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOVgMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/SUQAKQr97KWZMYKnHISjQ9RnamR\nCwcrgEYN1Zg2iZgdmvSgJetSj8YAuSRb2M2TWMT4UpGy4XIyzSJI7OWedJjEx+ov\n8dxiMMDVU7V3PsIx8B1t4TxACmqtQOVUToyx0s+YV90OWSCo3U4f/SGqRI4xHO9J\nQCmw0IFg9hbPhGYGumb4KKE/kSLolTQMaYN91tXMm/7RC72IFPwkf2tgJF5cH1E3\nBD80MzOPERXyncyk8TkPET2mwfuTo2cbTsHvWqn3I8eiRVW6jVE9yKZtA9N3nWsn\na5QGUDGPSlQOz2nOE5X6jDcRNFABO3BnBCERhDiyplOBVAHTkdODUZu6GQB8ZaI0\nxFbfs9g7lh9v1PwysnGR6j8DFYWR8wcvkb4mzogawR7L/OqeCmitLJaQgX0A4q1t\nv9nSF/dqWNjlOPRca4SNqdFDrS0J3uF2ybUoNEi6riOQAByFMS/0Y+pi5jm9JrCw\nXTLtnMeqrbQhOqj1/lMohuV4F7SbBbddwE6heSx1ptaZFNfzqrwAXwOfAPs4E2HY\nsgpSeMGgbBWPm/GeMPHqKfo3ZWUjY6vC69rcJdEDRHbLKz9aiRk5EkZY5uvt3lYn\niJmpw0aUobAumDzCGVDsKkqpsKIzP0T1wH4rALW0quS0y5RXiaN9OALG5pasK8zC\nveB9IaCKZrDKBX77lh60\n=qLT9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree bda9c6b00e2be2d3596fbd40fb0465306900dbd7\nparent 21d36296f137c0954df24ea86abe9619318915e6\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782142988 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782142988 +0200\n\nStop logging every Responses WebSocket event (#29432)\n\n## Why\n\nEvery successful Responses WebSocket event currently produces three\nlocal log records: the full payload at TRACE, an OpenTelemetry log\nevent, and an OpenTelemetry trace event.\n\nOn busy threads these records fill the 1,000-row log partition in\nseconds and cause continuous SQLite insert-and-prune churn.\n\nRelated to\nhttps://openai.slack.com/archives/C095U48JNL9/p1782128972644209\n\n## What changed\n\n- Stop logging each successful Responses WebSocket payload at TRACE.\n- Stop emitting `codex.websocket_event` as OpenTelemetry log and trace\nevents.\n- Keep WebSocket event counters, duration metrics, response timing\nmetrics, parsing, and error handling.","verified_at":"2026-06-22T15:43:08Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/91e6da943b08677cf1c9346fb438488471fc03a5","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/91e6da943b08677cf1c9346fb438488471fc03a5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/91e6da943b08677cf1c9346fb438488471fc03a5/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"21d36296f137c0954df24ea86abe9619318915e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/21d36296f137c0954df24ea86abe9619318915e6","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/21d36296f137c0954df24ea86abe9619318915e6"}]},{"sha":"21d36296f137c0954df24ea86abe9619318915e6","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDIxZDM2Mjk2ZjEzN2MwOTU0ZGYyNGVhODZhYmU5NjE5MzE4OTE1ZTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"xli-oai","email":"xli@openai.com","date":"2026-06-22T11:25:07Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T11:25:07Z"},"message":"Add workspace messages app-server API (#29001)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Add backend-client types and fetch support for active workspace\nmessages.\n- Add the app-server v2 `account/workspaceMessages/read` method,\ngenerated schemas, and README documentation.\n- Delegate workspace-message eligibility to the Codex backend feature\ngate; map a backend 404 to `featureEnabled: false`.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just write-app-server-schema`\n- `just test -p codex-backend-client`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server workspace_messages`\n- `just fix -p codex-backend-client -p codex-app-server-protocol -p\ncodex-app-server`\n- `just fmt`\n\n## Stack\n\n- Base PR for #28232, which adds the TUI status-line integration.","tree":{"sha":"70a8a10a390539ef879c01c4bd6474ea60112e1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/70a8a10a390539ef879c01c4bd6474ea60112e1f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/21d36296f137c0954df24ea86abe9619318915e6","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqORuTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACjUQAAboMIorW4t6vTkwMeF1whS3\n+yGnSxdRLRfK+GhuRjB19gane99O0h0shDlAAabHXAJ48EYtVzt10qtH98JQOH1g\n5UzvsAkmRkfBGbWAjpYkm2uFiIcc+HUkOMC6GE5rQ50FAkhEYwjnmzNDshHjrtZG\neDSsSiMg+rcT1UfrwTJyoCLyAGc/g+EkTbIJeiTZXuW0C/XU2aZanqTKdWglKKs5\n7ZYjtQAtjmfdpR4oJH66c2WHaR0SpBmL2q727q1TJhoLIf+74efrfFzPovzmKJ50\nKLZZ2oGHjDtC6MMWwye2kjefl2u9+U0soqYAVbO8J9a54GXYkKnTnEYboqVvYJWM\nJsOhrIhCqAm4KtcHqV/9mLq95uuptdd+Z11fJCoHU6pmRyDyG5BZACx2IumqYJ/O\n6M0LISJOLNqvaEMx9QLgwp8c9QQ2l4zJFTCl3qULxaG3rKp+KSK+F9Y59ZwWd/nU\nvpsa1ynfBBqdrLmtyfk46Dx3AdYzhr7HPrmUThItEMy0qjSx5Jz3ct07XKnKu1e9\nWGgHoXtBN51fk0e2SDAMI391oeZDvXNFCkL0WtKrmH4QC17R475evBBS/eVOFpkW\nYyBnDeLrWBY1YUM/CRlKJTd2R4r0NtOKwCY2NTLLTyYFlC41nLhjDqV0RPL+CB/4\nrPaxGCYGhJ2PeTv1OQMz\n=y6b0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 70a8a10a390539ef879c01c4bd6474ea60112e1f\nparent 9c3b10e5d4fcd1881c191b26467a6b0aa5b50682\nauthor xli-oai <xli@openai.com> 1782127507 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782127507 -0700\n\nAdd workspace messages app-server API (#29001)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Add backend-client types and fetch support for active workspace\nmessages.\n- Add the app-server v2 `account/workspaceMessages/read` method,\ngenerated schemas, and README documentation.\n- Delegate workspace-message eligibility to the Codex backend feature\ngate; map a backend 404 to `featureEnabled: false`.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just write-app-server-schema`\n- `just test -p codex-backend-client`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server workspace_messages`\n- `just fix -p codex-backend-client -p codex-app-server-protocol -p\ncodex-app-server`\n- `just fmt`\n\n## Stack\n\n- Base PR for #28232, which adds the TUI status-line integration.","verified_at":"2026-06-22T11:25:08Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/21d36296f137c0954df24ea86abe9619318915e6","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/21d36296f137c0954df24ea86abe9619318915e6","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/21d36296f137c0954df24ea86abe9619318915e6/comments","author":{"login":"xli-oai","id":270779301,"node_id":"U_kgDOECPDpQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270779301?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xli-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/xli-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xli-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xli-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xli-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xli-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xli-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xli-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xli-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xli-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xli-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9c3b10e5d4fcd1881c191b26467a6b0aa5b50682","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9c3b10e5d4fcd1881c191b26467a6b0aa5b50682","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9c3b10e5d4fcd1881c191b26467a6b0aa5b50682"}]},{"sha":"9c3b10e5d4fcd1881c191b26467a6b0aa5b50682","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDljM2IxMGU1ZDRmY2QxODgxYzE5MWIyNjQ2N2E2YjBhYTViNTA2ODI","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-22T10:45:37Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T10:45:37Z"},"message":"Apply sandbox intent inside remote exec servers (#29113)\n\n## Why\n\nPR #29108 lets the orchestrator send sandbox intent with `process/start`\nwithout wrapping the command for its own operating system.\n\nThis PR completes that boundary by making the executor interpret and\nenforce the intent using its own filesystem paths and sandbox\nimplementation.\n\nFor example, a macOS TUI targeting a Linux devbox sends `/bin/bash -lc\npwd`. The Linux executor turns that into its own `codex-linux-sandbox\n... /bin/bash -lc pwd` launch.\n\n## What changes\n\n- Keep `process/start` unchanged when no sandbox intent is present.\n- Convert sandbox `PathUri` values into native paths on the executor.\n- Bind symbolic `:workspace_roots` permissions to the executor's native\nsandbox cwd.\n- Select the sandbox implementation on the executor and wrap the\noriginal command immediately before spawning it.\n- Reject sandbox-required execution before spawning when the executor\ncannot enforce the intent.\n- Pass exec-server runtime paths into process creation so Linux can\nlocate `codex-linux-sandbox`.\n\nThe boundary is therefore:\n\n```text\norchestrator                         executor\noriginal argv + sandbox intent  ->  select and enforce local sandbox\n```\n\nThis PR intentionally treats a denied remote command as an ordinary\ncommand failure. Draft follow-up #29424 carries a semantic\n`sandboxDenied` result back to unified exec for the existing approval\nand retry flow.\n\n## Platform scope\n\nLinux and macOS use their existing direct-spawn sandbox transforms.\n\nWindows sandboxed remote process launch is intentionally unsupported in\nthis PR. The current Windows direct-spawn wrapper does not correctly\npreserve arbitrary argv, TTY behavior, or pass the full child\nenvironment out of band. The executor rejects the request instead of\nrunning it incorrectly or unsandboxed.\n\n## Known follow-ups\n\n- The transported permission profile can still contain\norchestrator-materialized helper or explicit paths. A `TODO(jif)` marks\nwhere the executor boundary should receive pre-host-materialization\npermission intent.\n- The sandbox wrapper currently replaces a requested custom inner\n`arg0`. A `TODO(jif)` marks where this must be preserved or rejected\nexplicitly.\n- Draft PR #29424 contains the deferred sandbox-denial classification\nand approval/retry behavior.\n\n## Rollout assumption\n\nThis executor-sandbox stack is unreleased and its client and executor\nare expected to move together. This PR does not add mixed-version\nnegotiation with older exec servers.","tree":{"sha":"ca31a34ba63c471c557490101abc60062e3146bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/ca31a34ba63c471c557490101abc60062e3146bd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/9c3b10e5d4fcd1881c191b26467a6b0aa5b50682","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqORJRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAffsQAFGG0NH0wBZ8snplLqCOiOFP\n2y8qTl2wBwvCM7SxHjGYrvcdHCfOZnOcRQQEtvQpry1/CqV+575ukJdNsZEFc1Yc\nwPiGdnpoUVDIZVpg93lQpLtKbOVeLXr1sROcHdOEiqLyMd7rpqQSIY7faWOPtxDp\nypBueb+Q2dag/gPGxkmcoiisPcoAGDp47r6/RL31Q9XrP0xU3UJ9vwoCiKxssNTE\nseTlBNxUCkvB+K/uqRbrOdG2a8obarMQsmVXAxS5X7eR5PuHFCyOwdF12fHs1yRa\n++COnsjnirMVD9Fu5w61s6qw1Dh6bBshTpihUML+CLkfJrmNvFG0ADfcLjpzongI\nNO7VJuGM1kV3DXPDaUY/4tz2rmbXVzKsMt4ofdp6VwCSnvGCbM7KtjiAyQdfxbpJ\n7a6oy5HBHwk6Py7akbYeCpMGDFxYC2bTdHoWS5XzQMqcuj5SLBwYPjbFeqgUaZTM\nTdMK3u2uufMCJmb0vpD9DA6vLFZ7QWN5B0FeA3wN0WjsbvjZEkk7quX4kGyTaGxf\nQacrwPcj31+WhIRzJqi9nmPZZJfFBpVK4exNblzoFVrFa+nXpiTappw/X74Aj46Q\neamwHQqqgWRTRnfCB7M+bWpCKRS1R+ln7NyzoBpOzjagSWgJl/HZa1UxTOzayg5K\ngOseyZLGY3qj+qNyr2Nt\n=itX/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ca31a34ba63c471c557490101abc60062e3146bd\nparent c03742ca0a78a8e54cd881032a2327363678b5aa\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782125137 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782125137 +0200\n\nApply sandbox intent inside remote exec servers (#29113)\n\n## Why\n\nPR #29108 lets the orchestrator send sandbox intent with `process/start`\nwithout wrapping the command for its own operating system.\n\nThis PR completes that boundary by making the executor interpret and\nenforce the intent using its own filesystem paths and sandbox\nimplementation.\n\nFor example, a macOS TUI targeting a Linux devbox sends `/bin/bash -lc\npwd`. The Linux executor turns that into its own `codex-linux-sandbox\n... /bin/bash -lc pwd` launch.\n\n## What changes\n\n- Keep `process/start` unchanged when no sandbox intent is present.\n- Convert sandbox `PathUri` values into native paths on the executor.\n- Bind symbolic `:workspace_roots` permissions to the executor's native\nsandbox cwd.\n- Select the sandbox implementation on the executor and wrap the\noriginal command immediately before spawning it.\n- Reject sandbox-required execution before spawning when the executor\ncannot enforce the intent.\n- Pass exec-server runtime paths into process creation so Linux can\nlocate `codex-linux-sandbox`.\n\nThe boundary is therefore:\n\n```text\norchestrator                         executor\noriginal argv + sandbox intent  ->  select and enforce local sandbox\n```\n\nThis PR intentionally treats a denied remote command as an ordinary\ncommand failure. Draft follow-up #29424 carries a semantic\n`sandboxDenied` result back to unified exec for the existing approval\nand retry flow.\n\n## Platform scope\n\nLinux and macOS use their existing direct-spawn sandbox transforms.\n\nWindows sandboxed remote process launch is intentionally unsupported in\nthis PR. The current Windows direct-spawn wrapper does not correctly\npreserve arbitrary argv, TTY behavior, or pass the full child\nenvironment out of band. The executor rejects the request instead of\nrunning it incorrectly or unsandboxed.\n\n## Known follow-ups\n\n- The transported permission profile can still contain\norchestrator-materialized helper or explicit paths. A `TODO(jif)` marks\nwhere the executor boundary should receive pre-host-materialization\npermission intent.\n- The sandbox wrapper currently replaces a requested custom inner\n`arg0`. A `TODO(jif)` marks where this must be preserved or rejected\nexplicitly.\n- Draft PR #29424 contains the deferred sandbox-denial classification\nand approval/retry behavior.\n\n## Rollout assumption\n\nThis executor-sandbox stack is unreleased and its client and executor\nare expected to move together. This PR does not add mixed-version\nnegotiation with older exec servers.","verified_at":"2026-06-22T10:45:37Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9c3b10e5d4fcd1881c191b26467a6b0aa5b50682","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9c3b10e5d4fcd1881c191b26467a6b0aa5b50682","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9c3b10e5d4fcd1881c191b26467a6b0aa5b50682/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c03742ca0a78a8e54cd881032a2327363678b5aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c03742ca0a78a8e54cd881032a2327363678b5aa","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c03742ca0a78a8e54cd881032a2327363678b5aa"}]},{"sha":"c03742ca0a78a8e54cd881032a2327363678b5aa","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGMwMzc0MmNhMGE3OGE4ZTU0Y2Q4ODEwMzJhMjMyNzM2MzY3OGI1YWE","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-22T08:05:36Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T08:05:36Z"},"message":"Simplify multi-agent mode controls (#29324)\n\n## Why\n\nMulti-agent delegation policy was split across `multiAgentMode`,\n`features.multi_agent_mode`, and `usage_hint_enabled`. These controls\ncould disagree: a requested mode could be downgraded by the feature\nflag, and disabling usage hints also disabled mode instructions.\n\nSome clients also need multi-agent tools without adding\ndelegation-policy text to model context. The previous two-mode API could\nnot express that directly.\n\n## What changed\n\n`multiAgentMode` is now the only live delegation-policy control:\n\n| Mode | Behavior |\n| --- | --- |\n| `none` | Keep multi-agent tools available without adding mode\ninstructions. |\n| `explicitRequestOnly` | Only delegate after an explicit user request.\n|\n| `proactive` | Delegate when parallel work materially improves speed or\nquality. |\n\n- new threads default to `explicitRequestOnly`; omitting the mode on\nlater turns keeps the current value\n- thread start, resume, fork, and settings responses always report the\nconcrete current mode instead of `null`\n- mode selection remains sticky across turns and resume\n- usage-hint text no longer controls whether mode instructions apply\n- `features.multi_agent_mode` and `usage_hint_enabled` remain accepted\nas ignored compatibility settings so existing configs continue to load\n- app-server documentation and generated schemas describe the three-mode\nAPI\n\n## Tests\n\n- `just test -p codex-core multi_agent_mode`\n- `just test -p codex-core multi_agent_v2_config_from_feature_table`\n- `just test -p codex-core spawn_agent_description`\n- `just test -p codex-features`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server multi_agent_mode`","tree":{"sha":"1e68e880788873561d372cd4398a087b518a6251","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/1e68e880788873561d372cd4398a087b518a6251"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/c03742ca0a78a8e54cd881032a2327363678b5aa","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOOzQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtCEQADsPEjs30kxOpxBFwDxlhOXF\nt+SW05ZDuiMdJuCCPM5L7jReNegdIXRmOk7KVqES4dB4tSY07kovDpGimiWEPPdI\nTW8U3gvWUJnK9i/mU+cAA/ZNy7InYND4qh3UJVyc662uBcLvQQTB3X8TDdqxt3lV\n5mI2P6Yw+6ljCb8QcTR0eVSl7LtInf4UrNYsB0xXDBa4BlZ7tmtapIbo4VOD3sOh\nTDB/1Hmf0X8FZil75CF9IAi7Ks8Qv0BftbneHp3+KKkyL/BZCLBkuYd++B9pIxde\nREsoCkafyMvuh9GLREtCPPjJgJyPWP2U1sKdwPGBAiKf/sXN7oJe5uqDKWM7ZaSB\nQnbcC3e1aW+cFycygd/cKVvHOYXP2jqrH7MH+fSEWNlwetQc5mwBwJ+nCbaS//CX\nOgSSFdVrBI4f8pSLNsHtF52QAQkrGazPyrDCuUfd+Lp9pN37tfAGP+NETB7rpfVD\n3b/npP+h5dGihM/eC70tZMXxXplhUrxk000N80c/jVz6Ss3ajdxa4OPYNG8yin03\nMkWL2uws08alkOhdmNMX6TGoW9mESbxOMv3Xxi6M2BK0A5WK4wSj6kUgBjSLOiKw\nYV/SuVSr5t57kVefILGGHtIOLtpMTJZZc7L2MLELF3Ftdf0WdUzhNv4EeZ+2cr1P\nYVL9Gt0Rd0Ylg1xcVTbg\n=TFiE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1e68e880788873561d372cd4398a087b518a6251\nparent 6d15bb3d17f2b2a7d2a11ddd0689dc9244bf744c\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782115536 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782115536 +0200\n\nSimplify multi-agent mode controls (#29324)\n\n## Why\n\nMulti-agent delegation policy was split across `multiAgentMode`,\n`features.multi_agent_mode`, and `usage_hint_enabled`. These controls\ncould disagree: a requested mode could be downgraded by the feature\nflag, and disabling usage hints also disabled mode instructions.\n\nSome clients also need multi-agent tools without adding\ndelegation-policy text to model context. The previous two-mode API could\nnot express that directly.\n\n## What changed\n\n`multiAgentMode` is now the only live delegation-policy control:\n\n| Mode | Behavior |\n| --- | --- |\n| `none` | Keep multi-agent tools available without adding mode\ninstructions. |\n| `explicitRequestOnly` | Only delegate after an explicit user request.\n|\n| `proactive` | Delegate when parallel work materially improves speed or\nquality. |\n\n- new threads default to `explicitRequestOnly`; omitting the mode on\nlater turns keeps the current value\n- thread start, resume, fork, and settings responses always report the\nconcrete current mode instead of `null`\n- mode selection remains sticky across turns and resume\n- usage-hint text no longer controls whether mode instructions apply\n- `features.multi_agent_mode` and `usage_hint_enabled` remain accepted\nas ignored compatibility settings so existing configs continue to load\n- app-server documentation and generated schemas describe the three-mode\nAPI\n\n## Tests\n\n- `just test -p codex-core multi_agent_mode`\n- `just test -p codex-core multi_agent_v2_config_from_feature_table`\n- `just test -p codex-core spawn_agent_description`\n- `just test -p codex-features`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server multi_agent_mode`","verified_at":"2026-06-22T08:05:36Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c03742ca0a78a8e54cd881032a2327363678b5aa","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c03742ca0a78a8e54cd881032a2327363678b5aa","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c03742ca0a78a8e54cd881032a2327363678b5aa/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6d15bb3d17f2b2a7d2a11ddd0689dc9244bf744c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6d15bb3d17f2b2a7d2a11ddd0689dc9244bf744c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6d15bb3d17f2b2a7d2a11ddd0689dc9244bf744c"}]},{"sha":"6d15bb3d17f2b2a7d2a11ddd0689dc9244bf744c","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDZkMTViYjNkMTdmMmIyYTdkMmExMWRkZDA2ODlkYzkyNDRiZjc0NGM","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-22T07:36:08Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T07:36:08Z"},"message":"Persist session IDs across thread resume (#29327)\n\n## Summary\n\nA cold-resumed subagent kept its durable thread ID but could receive a\nnew session ID, splitting one agent tree across multiple sessions after\na restart.\n\nPersist the root session ID in every rollout `SessionMeta`, carry it\nthrough thread creation, and restore it before initializing the resumed\n`Session` and `AgentControl`.\n\n## Behavior\n\nFor a nested agent tree:\n\n```text\nroot session R\n  parent thread P\n    child thread C\n```\n\nThe child rollout stores:\n\n```text\nsession_id:       R\nparent_thread_id: P\nid:               C\n```\n\nAfter a cold resume, the child still belongs to root session `R` while\nits immediate parent remains `P`. The integration coverage uses distinct\nvalues for all three IDs so it catches restoring the session from\n`parent_thread_id`.\n\n## Legacy rollouts\n\nPrevious rollouts have `id` but no `session_id`. `SessionMetaLine`\ndeserialization treats a missing `session_id` as `id`, keeping those\nfiles readable, listable, and resumable. When a legacy subagent is\nresumed through its root, that synthesized child ID no longer overrides\nthe inherited root-scoped `AgentControl`. New rollouts always persist\nthe explicit root session ID.","tree":{"sha":"a56a29a467ef6128f723e44141c5eee36e27ca62","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/a56a29a467ef6128f723e44141c5eee36e27ca62"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/6d15bb3d17f2b2a7d2a11ddd0689dc9244bf744c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOOXoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATfwQAEPEfT8do2mayswid/EtR4zH\n5FAt3hty1cRzp4qLtZ7izzDTUFJDVxF2DiVMlN/db96ZnAarIaLqAPcfMwv3TQWV\nNTl2WNXVs2/CEENeOvgurXa8AdkQsymlbcjmEtgHqUlNa+tkOmWLfo9ZJXXOi5qD\nLsfRLVju4z8UN1JIqsArBA8aqBo8sLg7D+yoMLYSLh0kpZJU+RHAN0q0bSC/lGc3\nE4ABe+kx2/8V6Fgo2fzpj3lvsVRxGj+/xo0KTqwr2YhHwSEnmYdy7Jntqytb0bN3\nHMTcZYE3wmFxoSDota87pURZ33SCkvunmf0kdmyfBX74crpxcNlpLoTzO1KZe7Kn\nVxEFaGlv6TbfMuCdbPy3yPjpSreNEqxJD7TswJUo2TMiY7bV81zFvzdH12CGLRCk\nhyaM0r9pNf2ZkIO2LHHEpLqHcVgAWe+3KXthBWZkEU7GHzndNEgDg+t3QvJlL0fz\nK7J+2HgfuqUuRNk5YDmW2ptfW0gDxJL0Na+ixPCaTlMiVxgey9G4HPFC0m1nP7Lf\nKwLpoG5QQGNlOgMRKhBQAQjdh/NrVhGhF5SsIfJ3LC1vejE/f1euQSpALS0lnIIP\nbFcYw/102I74uf8Dpn4g0Hy0ndyNZrJj8xFyYEvoqtHzXW2tDhRfQ0B7OzuKDKIm\nuw/LV/TAK6wGEMsAtemR\n=dZDN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a56a29a467ef6128f723e44141c5eee36e27ca62\nparent 98845e484070a1f93fa24842db0e429c7cec9f81\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782113768 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782113768 +0200\n\nPersist session IDs across thread resume (#29327)\n\n## Summary\n\nA cold-resumed subagent kept its durable thread ID but could receive a\nnew session ID, splitting one agent tree across multiple sessions after\na restart.\n\nPersist the root session ID in every rollout `SessionMeta`, carry it\nthrough thread creation, and restore it before initializing the resumed\n`Session` and `AgentControl`.\n\n## Behavior\n\nFor a nested agent tree:\n\n```text\nroot session R\n  parent thread P\n    child thread C\n```\n\nThe child rollout stores:\n\n```text\nsession_id:       R\nparent_thread_id: P\nid:               C\n```\n\nAfter a cold resume, the child still belongs to root session `R` while\nits immediate parent remains `P`. The integration coverage uses distinct\nvalues for all three IDs so it catches restoring the session from\n`parent_thread_id`.\n\n## Legacy rollouts\n\nPrevious rollouts have `id` but no `session_id`. `SessionMetaLine`\ndeserialization treats a missing `session_id` as `id`, keeping those\nfiles readable, listable, and resumable. When a legacy subagent is\nresumed through its root, that synthesized child ID no longer overrides\nthe inherited root-scoped `AgentControl`. New rollouts always persist\nthe explicit root session ID.","verified_at":"2026-06-22T07:36:09Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6d15bb3d17f2b2a7d2a11ddd0689dc9244bf744c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6d15bb3d17f2b2a7d2a11ddd0689dc9244bf744c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6d15bb3d17f2b2a7d2a11ddd0689dc9244bf744c/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"98845e484070a1f93fa24842db0e429c7cec9f81","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/98845e484070a1f93fa24842db0e429c7cec9f81","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/98845e484070a1f93fa24842db0e429c7cec9f81"}]},{"sha":"98845e484070a1f93fa24842db0e429c7cec9f81","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDk4ODQ1ZTQ4NDA3MGExZjkzZmEyNDg0MmRiMGU0MjljN2NlYzlmODE","commit":{"author":{"name":"sayan-oai","email":"sayan@openai.com","date":"2026-06-22T05:11:42Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T05:11:42Z"},"message":"chore: fix merge race (auto-compaction feature access) (#29393)\n\n## Summary\n\n- read the `AutoCompaction` feature flag through `TurnContext::config`\n- fix both the mid-turn and pre-sampling compaction checks\n\n## Why\n\n#28260 was validated against an older base where `TurnContext` exposed a\ndirect `features` field. It was then merged after that field had moved\nunder `config`, leaving the merge result unable to compile with `E0609`\non `turn_context.features`.\n\nThis restores compilation for Bazel, SDK, and argument-comment-lint jobs\nthat build `codex-core`. Behavior is unchanged: disabling\n`auto_compaction` still skips automatic compaction.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `CODEX_HOME=/private/tmp/codex-fix-auto-compaction-test-home just test\n-p codex-core auto_compaction_feature_disabled` — 4 passed\n- `just test -p codex-core` — `codex-core` compiled; 2,722 passed and 89\nunrelated local-environment failures remained because the sandbox could\nnot write the default Codex SQLite/proxy paths and some first-party test\nbinaries were unavailable","tree":{"sha":"bf3e33205533621130321f4e78f48489cca35588","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/bf3e33205533621130321f4e78f48489cca35588"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/98845e484070a1f93fa24842db0e429c7cec9f81","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOMQOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdIUQAG3TwOxPb+Gl+kKwfx/Vasif\nD0HZfLRigyvb43u0VRHx7Q9rfoM34uvJEqcBSx+VfIKaG5NtcE/EW0GGr4J+dv8A\noXRRsMAeNN8maZWrD5ng+LfBcTzqG58MoeUyh7ohx+sqFqRIN6b9qmxzQgNHphB5\nAt1Khsk/NZHFWIsuxB3d4BnSCL5aBR1SUdq7pKsQxiQNKVPA7IAfs0nTYP2RZs9a\nNM/9ejf+uVdduZ6qSajnLkbB9Mk2xctgrB1xaLgaTaGB0eChmq57XGa0/7dH0TYS\nm09NcQr4PoUArKBSlsPEZiw8wDhwzehaTCJC+FgRW9NVXzgDys7TFiCwn/gut5CZ\nxFfcNk9OX6S45jRuIiIhOQ3pR/yNE0cINDoYVOx2D2LLn5lnnQOvQAuxO4AASUP0\nezz6LIlqdu+FQ4wuzPCWFA3mZVpuoD7VxhVX0aqcjeCcGxasAX1BkCpTk89SxX+0\n24WtAW56DAUj4oPoIs+EBpRG5w8re8SiBVwkdPkgT8P49YoyGGsQ1lj8brSJdTZF\n8Mox6yYZ8NstmPGeIlbwZixj+TkMO26L2GEe06HmH9OpYe7FdvtcJ+nEIo1Fz6fT\n+OUTZBy3UaIKdz4Mvk0nL2w2zaKhbQTDGXsO3+YUhbVoFXwHW1ZXK+UeUuSf/sra\nJZov5B/drKZoha0aB/+e\n=HCjT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree bf3e33205533621130321f4e78f48489cca35588\nparent 566f7bf6314cbf213de523a0268d8df89f93ef62\nauthor sayan-oai <sayan@openai.com> 1782105102 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782105102 +0000\n\nchore: fix merge race (auto-compaction feature access) (#29393)\n\n## Summary\n\n- read the `AutoCompaction` feature flag through `TurnContext::config`\n- fix both the mid-turn and pre-sampling compaction checks\n\n## Why\n\n#28260 was validated against an older base where `TurnContext` exposed a\ndirect `features` field. It was then merged after that field had moved\nunder `config`, leaving the merge result unable to compile with `E0609`\non `turn_context.features`.\n\nThis restores compilation for Bazel, SDK, and argument-comment-lint jobs\nthat build `codex-core`. Behavior is unchanged: disabling\n`auto_compaction` still skips automatic compaction.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `CODEX_HOME=/private/tmp/codex-fix-auto-compaction-test-home just test\n-p codex-core auto_compaction_feature_disabled` — 4 passed\n- `just test -p codex-core` — `codex-core` compiled; 2,722 passed and 89\nunrelated local-environment failures remained because the sandbox could\nnot write the default Codex SQLite/proxy paths and some first-party test\nbinaries were unavailable","verified_at":"2026-06-22T05:11:42Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/98845e484070a1f93fa24842db0e429c7cec9f81","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/98845e484070a1f93fa24842db0e429c7cec9f81","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/98845e484070a1f93fa24842db0e429c7cec9f81/comments","author":{"login":"sayan-oai","id":244841968,"node_id":"U_kgDODpf98A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/244841968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/sayan-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"566f7bf6314cbf213de523a0268d8df89f93ef62","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/566f7bf6314cbf213de523a0268d8df89f93ef62","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/566f7bf6314cbf213de523a0268d8df89f93ef62"}]},{"sha":"566f7bf6314cbf213de523a0268d8df89f93ef62","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDU2NmY3YmY2MzE0Y2JmMjEzZGU1MjNhMDI2OGQ4ZGY4OWY5M2VmNjI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Francis Chalissery","email":"fc@openai.com","date":"2026-06-22T03:39:14Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T03:39:14Z"},"message":"Propagate safety buffering events to app-server clients (#29371)\n\nResponses API safety buffering metadata currently stops at the transport\nboundary, so app-server clients cannot render the in-progress safety\nreview state.\n\nThis change:\n- decodes and deduplicates `safety_buffering` metadata from Responses\nAPI SSE and WebSocket events without suppressing the original response\nevent\n- emits a typed core event containing the requested model plus backend\nuse cases and reasons\n- forwards that event as `turn/safetyBuffering/updated` through\napp-server v2 and updates generated protocol schemas\n- keeps the side-channel event out of persisted rollouts and turn timing\n\nThis supports the Codex Apps buffering UX and depends on the Responses\nAPI backend work in https://github.com/openai/openai/pull/1044569 and\nhttps://github.com/openai/openai/pull/1044571.\n\nValidation:\n- focused `codex-core` safety-buffering integration test passes\n- `cargo check -p codex-core -p codex-app-server -p\ncodex-app-server-protocol`\n- `just fix -p codex-api -p codex-protocol -p codex-core -p\ncodex-app-server-protocol -p codex-app-server -p codex-rollout -p\ncodex-rollout-trace -p codex-otel`\n- `just fmt`\n- broad package test run: 4,430/4,492 passed; 62 unrelated\nlocal-environment/concurrency failures involved unavailable test\nbinaries, MCP subprocess setup, and app-server timeouts","tree":{"sha":"05327750e4d0c9dba4a7444f24404ddd273ddb1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/05327750e4d0c9dba4a7444f24404ddd273ddb1f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/566f7bf6314cbf213de523a0268d8df89f93ef62","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOK5iCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+iAQAEQ+/gqN6xTgsFnxdwyayBs8\n/oQ5SDZw0KMxkvPridKlUV77N7pvDKgAl2V3KPk9CCQvY8+ggGxvDrAVNR644Bze\nx475EazsoFZu+W1pAkSt5ChppdfPf5LqCv2mFTNJr/DMpq2v5zRH/Z3a9jvxLnle\nM36dha8MzQnDahXTGS4zAQ6CWKI6RIXDSoXdaENIjv6LLu2KHL9VDtUvKT3RCAv7\ni01v6MQrPKWhniCSKLzG3WBae0Pk6JI/LMQjD4I1UoKcsTdqEGv9j6mOUbbU/AQn\naYgUz6/4r/Kh9O/S1cULcMrfYU07d8cFhm/t+PetPQJi1bc8fNjS4UZiMJs2DFw6\n7dmxTG5ycEWAbnilXoiZp5MnbwAk7V3wKylDacP5mtvARsa37/tqZuv7tbMFhCK8\nc0wNth8NJbp8xhwAZRURDiizVaSvvdNx2IQ8apEkMm8cicKkX+2khRd2jWiX3kXW\nsSyFn3shaQxO4OQFtTzkOYjEYdAl9nLHJxFryME0Fp1WpGb9KO4DSASNbPHJbFZR\nFnE1hZEGBhQktjCRdtkpKH4gxd2KUJenkMw/tOwoHsBpTy9rDkoDlJLreM5A5bEV\nY8yu2HPrGJFuxsJXoI267PUoG6zcp7XvdyEr2+K1mFWJ4w3z1hwmjM20AyTTDOVC\nh7BaYLZJ27NuSSS+N7g6\n=2H3/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 05327750e4d0c9dba4a7444f24404ddd273ddb1f\nparent b21f0e7a98c05a570cc227e2ec62a2e29c3a7225\nauthor Francis Chalissery <fc@openai.com> 1782099554 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782099554 +0000\n\nPropagate safety buffering events to app-server clients (#29371)\n\nResponses API safety buffering metadata currently stops at the transport\nboundary, so app-server clients cannot render the in-progress safety\nreview state.\n\nThis change:\n- decodes and deduplicates `safety_buffering` metadata from Responses\nAPI SSE and WebSocket events without suppressing the original response\nevent\n- emits a typed core event containing the requested model plus backend\nuse cases and reasons\n- forwards that event as `turn/safetyBuffering/updated` through\napp-server v2 and updates generated protocol schemas\n- keeps the side-channel event out of persisted rollouts and turn timing\n\nThis supports the Codex Apps buffering UX and depends on the Responses\nAPI backend work in https://github.com/openai/openai/pull/1044569 and\nhttps://github.com/openai/openai/pull/1044571.\n\nValidation:\n- focused `codex-core` safety-buffering integration test passes\n- `cargo check -p codex-core -p codex-app-server -p\ncodex-app-server-protocol`\n- `just fix -p codex-api -p codex-protocol -p codex-core -p\ncodex-app-server-protocol -p codex-app-server -p codex-rollout -p\ncodex-rollout-trace -p codex-otel`\n- `just fmt`\n- broad package test run: 4,430/4,492 passed; 62 unrelated\nlocal-environment/concurrency failures involved unavailable test\nbinaries, MCP subprocess setup, and app-server timeouts","verified_at":"2026-06-22T03:39:15Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/566f7bf6314cbf213de523a0268d8df89f93ef62","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/566f7bf6314cbf213de523a0268d8df89f93ef62","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/566f7bf6314cbf213de523a0268d8df89f93ef62/comments","author":{"login":"fc-oai","id":269039706,"node_id":"U_kgDOEAk4Wg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/269039706?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fc-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/fc-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fc-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fc-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fc-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fc-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fc-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fc-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fc-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fc-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fc-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b21f0e7a98c05a570cc227e2ec62a2e29c3a7225","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b21f0e7a98c05a570cc227e2ec62a2e29c3a7225","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b21f0e7a98c05a570cc227e2ec62a2e29c3a7225"}]},{"sha":"b21f0e7a98c05a570cc227e2ec62a2e29c3a7225","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGIyMWYwZTdhOThjMDVhNTcwY2MyMjdlMmVjNjJhMmUyOWMzYTcyMjU","commit":{"author":{"name":"rhan-oai","email":"rhan@openai.com","date":"2026-06-22T03:11:50Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T03:11:50Z"},"message":"[codex] Add internal auto-compaction opt-out (#28260)\n\n## Summary\n\n- add a default-on `auto_compaction` feature flag as an internal escape\nhatch\n- skip pre-turn, model-switch/hash, and mid-turn automatic compaction\nwhen the flag is disabled\n- preserve manual `/compact` behavior and surface the existing\ncontext-window error when the provider runs out of room\n- add integration coverage for disabled pre-turn and mid-turn compaction\n\n## Motivation\n\nLong-running SPO optimization rollouts need the option to preserve their\nfull context and fail on context exhaustion instead of entering another\ncompaction window. This deliberately uses the existing feature-flag\nmechanism rather than adding a dedicated public config or app-server\nAPI.\n\nDisable it with:\n\n```sh\ncodex --disable auto_compaction\n```\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-features` — 51 passed\n- `just test -p codex-core auto_compaction_feature_disabled` — 2 passed\n- `just fix -p codex-core -p codex-features`\n- `just write-config-schema`\n- `just test -p codex-core` — the new compaction tests passed; the\noverall local run had 54 unrelated environment failures, primarily\nmissing first-party test binaries and shell-snapshot timeouts","tree":{"sha":"3d39b83515c55b1cccf9d48435c311a6f6b9a825","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/3d39b83515c55b1cccf9d48435c311a6f6b9a825"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/b21f0e7a98c05a570cc227e2ec62a2e29c3a7225","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOKf2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwmwQAKA+PnBfo4pcOqXYxTjDFG0K\nA69KirxxC6PcW78gOOj0OMoAZCT6mwCr7kgqjsXzkaKhKXdSsR06lSef4VerBC0e\nAVM9eZ4DoKJTNz55IjhkAbXdJLo38Rzfy2cG5lTEoUtmuaqxycs/y6Qn1aotpTOD\nrl+HlL1rndV1SltMmrTDPfoSAVViMeQjSDn6Su1Dzfk7va4Gn8tJhw6Qv+653cAa\nY4H/jMZMDVXRCpteHYnxeKEFz37+iAJcG7XBXLzf0GszHDDIgKsvVmR4E+OjcnJx\nbInzLrDLLHlV1Jy3NTcoQc5iqjyus/WCFcw9yX+42XhVk+/rymOWKGCFsDzUM3KP\no0mvKgXs7AZ2p+QijJg1QokPVZZZXCLc76aKwtYWTOdrSlj2JtdmFBjYbGTM3kV7\nsX1dNs3gfLyWmqdkSnMjFr9lYZtDsEXU+iH0Dd9U1V+lwpecTHvsl9VzgZw5qigD\nlYLJUpbHl18GbOtB2aAvGah3PWOIFIKbISly+ei9meN1fS76mu3n1BB83ukGddJu\ng76DAtjqUDFFNVSpisrqnoqMNeRrAlf65S0HOwVquJCsnUoQ29P0+Yngo+5Rk4cP\n2dYKNrEI4DT8LZnNyJN0fofreCjvFzPhJBjFBtJyTrErTmStuKSoFXSQrURSuKzY\n5hDHmEUqfw0cCH1saLLS\n=Kg3X\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3d39b83515c55b1cccf9d48435c311a6f6b9a825\nparent eb8c1ee85f18d055d00b3a0912dd0e55e62a82e8\nauthor rhan-oai <rhan@openai.com> 1782097910 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782097910 -0700\n\n[codex] Add internal auto-compaction opt-out (#28260)\n\n## Summary\n\n- add a default-on `auto_compaction` feature flag as an internal escape\nhatch\n- skip pre-turn, model-switch/hash, and mid-turn automatic compaction\nwhen the flag is disabled\n- preserve manual `/compact` behavior and surface the existing\ncontext-window error when the provider runs out of room\n- add integration coverage for disabled pre-turn and mid-turn compaction\n\n## Motivation\n\nLong-running SPO optimization rollouts need the option to preserve their\nfull context and fail on context exhaustion instead of entering another\ncompaction window. This deliberately uses the existing feature-flag\nmechanism rather than adding a dedicated public config or app-server\nAPI.\n\nDisable it with:\n\n```sh\ncodex --disable auto_compaction\n```\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-features` — 51 passed\n- `just test -p codex-core auto_compaction_feature_disabled` — 2 passed\n- `just fix -p codex-core -p codex-features`\n- `just write-config-schema`\n- `just test -p codex-core` — the new compaction tests passed; the\noverall local run had 54 unrelated environment failures, primarily\nmissing first-party test binaries and shell-snapshot timeouts","verified_at":"2026-06-22T03:11:51Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b21f0e7a98c05a570cc227e2ec62a2e29c3a7225","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b21f0e7a98c05a570cc227e2ec62a2e29c3a7225","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b21f0e7a98c05a570cc227e2ec62a2e29c3a7225/comments","author":{"login":"rhan-oai","id":214716640,"node_id":"U_kgDODMxQ4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/214716640?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/rhan-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"eb8c1ee85f18d055d00b3a0912dd0e55e62a82e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/eb8c1ee85f18d055d00b3a0912dd0e55e62a82e8","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/eb8c1ee85f18d055d00b3a0912dd0e55e62a82e8"}]},{"sha":"eb8c1ee85f18d055d00b3a0912dd0e55e62a82e8","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGViOGMxZWU4NWYxOGQwNTVkMDBiM2EwOTEyZGQwZTU1ZTYyYTgyZTg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Channing Conger","email":"cconger@openai.com","date":"2026-06-21T22:35:01Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-21T22:35:01Z"},"message":"code-mode: preserve initial yield at completion (#29289)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Retain the first pre-observation `yield_control()` boundary when a\ncell completes before observation.\n- Deliver the preserved yield before the buffered completion.\n- Keep later unattached yields as no-ops.\n\n## Why\n\nCreate followed by the initial wait must preserve the former execute\nresponse boundary even when the script runs to completion first.\n\n## Impact\n\nThe first wait observes the same initial yield boundary as before create\nand observe were decoupled.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Focused initial-yield signature regression passed.\n- Stack-tip validation: `just test -p codex-code-mode -p\ncodex-code-mode-protocol` (70 passed).\n- Parent branch:\n`cconger/code-mode-runtime-compact-03e2-observation-delivery`.","tree":{"sha":"274d25b0bae796c9468fe11b751191c21f66565d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/274d25b0bae796c9468fe11b751191c21f66565d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/eb8c1ee85f18d055d00b3a0912dd0e55e62a82e8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOGcVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFiAQAFh+D0FRTOsPN4xGL0rXZMON\nvPRPiQzNmJGhrAUVCuYTNCgrfC09mpr+f5rLaOPRJrXtlTqWVtDmAiRoH8AAviIs\nNQ0Z2W8C1BZ5Vx9V3ZXs8+9D6EuA3+sZWX1xY1SSsF7IKA+kBl9s4kfEdtrHKogz\nKnJAVWgy9Ly4j5O/OxJ1tFRT2yyvWBJuEUecY7gMXdplsjKUh1KpxILCMqdwpmtI\nwc7QFP7YNwSMaJRuFgxY5v6ed/0WI/6UubSml51co7tMffuT0R4uYFMFw2tzWUud\ne7ZfNhvt4iW4MjZkp1joiEQVQHlwro75GNdAgnRP2N37B4GO4OiOeMpaagJo3uJ4\neesYVM4D0+3IkBOUlg390g4V6XVaiRKs4nIwie8yvAS5m4j0TNg+2HunyVIQGQi+\nN0J8iBvh+E0URFoQhjoFfd4K+/jMrPrGzorn4fuQHwApP4oB9GgAOpAbbrCRMH0h\npL5Z/lSJs5x+y9INoN24z2/DTAer0AlZSWEfu3l2pea5izyglFMPOp/AlY4N05h0\nwijxi3Sg3lLwPDYhbPbH5R8LXCNES2+y7omWZY2KmNzyTluLhDNm6oBKnVo5T8dW\ntnthTxBpvm9jnZLHen9OUbZEze9Ezq3yW2Y46CxQMqe6EV0XA0TSXGSq6qSgHRRD\nQsfndK0yx/jBiiCTkR7a\n=GAuF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 274d25b0bae796c9468fe11b751191c21f66565d\nparent 3b605b9c63f9123b39493b24d95d9a8428813e9f\nauthor Channing Conger <cconger@openai.com> 1782081301 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782081301 -0700\n\ncode-mode: preserve initial yield at completion (#29289)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Retain the first pre-observation `yield_control()` boundary when a\ncell completes before observation.\n- Deliver the preserved yield before the buffered completion.\n- Keep later unattached yields as no-ops.\n\n## Why\n\nCreate followed by the initial wait must preserve the former execute\nresponse boundary even when the script runs to completion first.\n\n## Impact\n\nThe first wait observes the same initial yield boundary as before create\nand observe were decoupled.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Focused initial-yield signature regression passed.\n- Stack-tip validation: `just test -p codex-code-mode -p\ncodex-code-mode-protocol` (70 passed).\n- Parent branch:\n`cconger/code-mode-runtime-compact-03e2-observation-delivery`.","verified_at":"2026-06-21T22:35:02Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/eb8c1ee85f18d055d00b3a0912dd0e55e62a82e8","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/eb8c1ee85f18d055d00b3a0912dd0e55e62a82e8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/eb8c1ee85f18d055d00b3a0912dd0e55e62a82e8/comments","author":{"login":"cconger","id":200563,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMDU2Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/200563?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger","html_url":"https://github.com/cconger","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3b605b9c63f9123b39493b24d95d9a8428813e9f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3b605b9c63f9123b39493b24d95d9a8428813e9f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3b605b9c63f9123b39493b24d95d9a8428813e9f"}]},{"sha":"3b605b9c63f9123b39493b24d95d9a8428813e9f","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDNiNjA1YjljNjNmOTEyM2IzOTQ5M2IyNGQ5NWQ5YTg0Mjg4MTNlOWY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Channing Conger","email":"cconger@openai.com","date":"2026-06-21T20:53:37Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-21T20:53:37Z"},"message":"code-mode: preserve dropped observation output (#29288)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Restore yielded output when an observation receiver disappears before\ndelivery.\n- Preserve pending-frontier output and tool IDs across failed delivery.\n- Add dropped-observer coverage for yield and pending observations.\n\n## Why\n\nCanceling a wait must not consume output or a pending frontier that the\ncaller never received.\n\n## Impact\n\nA later observation can recover undelivered incremental output without\nduplication.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Stack-tip validation: `just test -p codex-code-mode -p\ncodex-code-mode-protocol` (70 passed).\n- Parent branch:\n`cconger/code-mode-runtime-compact-03e-shutdown-hierarchy`.","tree":{"sha":"9c0f7d35e4a3341aefe4d7397c20cc9a4951cc2e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/9c0f7d35e4a3341aefe4d7397c20cc9a4951cc2e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/3b605b9c63f9123b39493b24d95d9a8428813e9f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOE9RCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6OYQAFrf5K7dU2UiGpjzwONqytcB\noWY1zptHlOVgS3bYBD6JYQdobdKIR+luSzD/A3gFdpOdthbEYjRmdp5QXsAvDYcv\nah0UMZ/X0W8AGqyJUz+OG4oCrSJWE/5du12rd+roF6ScozBsY52MW9pfk4POaFFN\naJ0MvFzjxUf4kLXm4KbZBMUJO7vGZ1JiqkDazasDlrgQjLoj1mmsxkuTmEtZ7h0j\n0f80LyIx+DGk6vj0t6ekDcYY6hEzi1LAY4H97TcoYb2TQtwr4ymOEc6V3pBEKGVc\neJmRPYozOLqSf1s3LxO9/BVoBqixjElHrvRZyXQPD9fJuy8grmUzoJLRiZbVBnFx\nlHsgZMJUAZYKRAfaJiOLVhUXRx/A0jQr+Wgqx7947Kyyg6+ziSu3lnDlCTikZWUa\nTGzEYzo9ppZOONkOla2Wc15bRG9ujD62b70zSbv1cN9ygPLIFyw7gisybAKmtYgO\n+J0FR33pbyG0Gfok4+Jdr9kiZNLhqPaEnkYG9ATcKDVL9oU0Bv1tod3qpr+/qEPj\no3elpEs8+2Qkb1ZmIncEafh3YMz8Ag390E6psNmsl+HpCgGU1Kc0x6WxRlxMIa+d\nRfsT9IKskk753INvMIe8PMIRMCKJt/7uxBm755NgoGdxqQNakSBRfwc+Is3pxTmI\nAubVWYHLXPIuqJg5d2FP\n=7knl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9c0f7d35e4a3341aefe4d7397c20cc9a4951cc2e\nparent 6bfc58a688a73c287da51797d99c3345caecbae8\nauthor Channing Conger <cconger@openai.com> 1782075217 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782075217 -0700\n\ncode-mode: preserve dropped observation output (#29288)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Restore yielded output when an observation receiver disappears before\ndelivery.\n- Preserve pending-frontier output and tool IDs across failed delivery.\n- Add dropped-observer coverage for yield and pending observations.\n\n## Why\n\nCanceling a wait must not consume output or a pending frontier that the\ncaller never received.\n\n## Impact\n\nA later observation can recover undelivered incremental output without\nduplication.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Stack-tip validation: `just test -p codex-code-mode -p\ncodex-code-mode-protocol` (70 passed).\n- Parent branch:\n`cconger/code-mode-runtime-compact-03e-shutdown-hierarchy`.","verified_at":"2026-06-21T20:53:38Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3b605b9c63f9123b39493b24d95d9a8428813e9f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3b605b9c63f9123b39493b24d95d9a8428813e9f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3b605b9c63f9123b39493b24d95d9a8428813e9f/comments","author":{"login":"cconger","id":200563,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMDU2Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/200563?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger","html_url":"https://github.com/cconger","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/