https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/rhan-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9c79d87d0606f1076eb309a609be2bac22cec968","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9c79d87d0606f1076eb309a609be2bac22cec968","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9c79d87d0606f1076eb309a609be2bac22cec968"}]},{"sha":"9c79d87d0606f1076eb309a609be2bac22cec968","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDljNzlkODdkMDYwNmYxMDc2ZWIzMDlhNjA5YmUyYmFjMjJjZWM5Njg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Channing Conger","email":"cconger@openai.com","date":"2026-06-21T20:15:38Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-21T20:15:38Z"},"message":"code-mode: make session shutdown authoritative (#29287)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Give each session and cell a hierarchical cancellation token.\n- Track cell tasks so shutdown waits for admitted actors without polling\nthe registry.\n- Make shutdown authoritative across concurrent admission and\nnon-cooperative callbacks.\n\n## Why\n\nA best-effort registry scan can miss cells admitted concurrently or\nblocked behind the registry lock.\n\n## Impact\n\nSession shutdown reliably stops every admitted cell and rejects new work\nonce shutdown begins.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Stack-tip validation: `just test -p codex-code-mode -p\ncodex-code-mode-protocol` (70 passed).\n- Parent branch: `cconger/code-mode-runtime-compact-03c-terminal-state`.","tree":{"sha":"41c6a1c7599af805715d9315b4ee19cd5b5aa65d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/41c6a1c7599af805715d9315b4ee19cd5b5aa65d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/9c79d87d0606f1076eb309a609be2bac22cec968","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOEZqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAn30QAG9EwXdz42kHEHQ3SGErHiu7\nTvV+Fmf/x0Ij+LGsptMZ91nJFwSLBSs9z55Y1TZ/nyeMNOQuqIZO7ZVragJp4v4o\nmXDAcTLP56zr6zKcyvNZBgFY9tozY4j1MZveUmSSSr9wxBUz81Pj3rpvSeHRjC2G\nk41Q+uqP0YLh1zQw/41oo+WblkNzvnGTYMLEPPCa6Zumpo+wWmZtEf6hjbn+n58D\nYgCdUldPmZ3QT2bFfo2Lv5Wjg6lagkLgUKGFbWW5uXKznwPKVFanRBu3Kb+ILtBm\nIiMcd9SiaGHCYXMisefqZQ8m6Z6pUSIDE6L9FRNb1zxhCytQMqTEGWWx80/iBUbV\nLKNNnX5gHXoQcNgLITdFhJl2sKmC+byAzo04K39kWneWTw8JrB/BnPCiZDV4e5fk\nZHz3d8pmMfAZqkGip4KXK1PiONWULn9TDxesKR0LLuRMAbOCSp+JQ2pecKh/2a0E\nVIeUHJKT2xCmU8UqTt+EENkMDS8j5rmlyMG+9+WxBvX7NmVrwNcDkjYmH5wOcgWf\n3nrS9b3G27gUVfLsLFiP0Z/cF3AgUuKq8kVf7GnqQ7tibrtxAil5C/V7XI2C4tM9\nJ38Ds29Y52HBhMlazD9RJna9kADExzbmbQGzsTKeMIpr199YMlezUgYmP57vc4cw\n2EOl7hGBn1ZAyMIJ6Dis\n=B6lq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 41c6a1c7599af805715d9315b4ee19cd5b5aa65d\nparent f774455c3a831dfab2c6f37a1f624b8097f6f2c2\nauthor Channing Conger <cconger@openai.com> 1782072938 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782072938 -0700\n\ncode-mode: make session shutdown authoritative (#29287)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Give each session and cell a hierarchical cancellation token.\n- Track cell tasks so shutdown waits for admitted actors without polling\nthe registry.\n- Make shutdown authoritative across concurrent admission and\nnon-cooperative callbacks.\n\n## Why\n\nA best-effort registry scan can miss cells admitted concurrently or\nblocked behind the registry lock.\n\n## Impact\n\nSession shutdown reliably stops every admitted cell and rejects new work\nonce shutdown begins.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Stack-tip validation: `just test -p codex-code-mode -p\ncodex-code-mode-protocol` (70 passed).\n- Parent branch: `cconger/code-mode-runtime-compact-03c-terminal-state`.","verified_at":"2026-06-21T20:15:38Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9c79d87d0606f1076eb309a609be2bac22cec968","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9c79d87d0606f1076eb309a609be2bac22cec968","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9c79d87d0606f1076eb309a609be2bac22cec968/comments","author":{"login":"cconger","id":200563,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMDU2Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/200563?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger","html_url":"https://github.com/cconger","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f774455c3a831dfab2c6f37a1f624b8097f6f2c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f774455c3a831dfab2c6f37a1f624b8097f6f2c2","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f774455c3a831dfab2c6f37a1f624b8097f6f2c2"}]},{"sha":"f774455c3a831dfab2c6f37a1f624b8097f6f2c2","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGY3NzQ0NTVjM2E4MzFkZmFiMmM2ZjM3YTFmNjI0YjgwOTdmNmYyYzI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Channing Conger","email":"cconger@openai.com","date":"2026-06-21T19:05:24Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-21T19:05:24Z"},"message":"code-mode: linearize cell terminal state (#29286)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Introduce a single cell terminal-state machine for completion and\ntermination.\n- Make stored-value commits atomic with the winning terminal outcome.\n- Buffer terminal results for later observation and cover\ntermination-before-commit behavior.\n\n## Why\n\nCompletion, termination, observation, and stored-value updates must\nagree on one linearized outcome under cancellation races.\n\n## Impact\n\nTerminal delivery becomes deterministic and terminated cells cannot\ncommit state after termination wins.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Focused terminal-state regression passed.\n- Stack-tip validation: `just test -p codex-code-mode -p\ncodex-code-mode-protocol` (70 passed).\n- Parent branch:\n`cconger/code-mode-runtime-compact-03b-session-runtime`.","tree":{"sha":"fcf860499d25c486c131d4cf268920e77ba27eec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/fcf860499d25c486c131d4cf268920e77ba27eec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/f774455c3a831dfab2c6f37a1f624b8097f6f2c2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqODX0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApS8QAGmXJKLdjrfIvVVfBKHOVtuG\nGp2OiENi5YYvmZ9C5mdUgutoFpfSxz2jXW9DKm2PqAgiPxOin8iQ89Fj+RUA0O04\ngfBcQthTWgBSUKqu3IxnilboXHFsqYg4VKyZgABP9+yg9vQKulMWOAxu/vcO86Xn\nMzVYsMwgb9yfkwM7CZY14Xliov8NtoGEtxSgib9ejvjpjq5nZsAPr3pzsDTv/3cs\nRgYM2ThPgOrKv5GbhBgNZQ6DanWo59mS5mPGh8iAwT4FskHxsVlW7GazqXBnyuvH\nbWv9L0QPOPVHzTl9NjfCW1eKy2wb2Eol7HvwSRXKYX/kTERQ724LM6LEAvfmisl9\nWmc1aXvJ3EmyqqLhhqJgniZ0Uj73uS7YIbG/filkWkRm+P/mRjtxUBPu7wlV0aeo\nQyM4z00cDwOZ20vsHL/r/slVD0NL1uThGTBJiC26sEDGAtuVcBTFQO+Y1mG0ZPbb\nUN+M5yHK594Eb4QjlIQ5FgSO/ZqypVU7/o0QyOgI+T9R6GnmXl9zJvVyPCA2p3j0\nLRmRw9unSc+7q3a16bUB9aF1xugFozaICgKfhXvfGZuDuCx2y2Z9gYenpygDHTda\nZax3KQ2hgl4ifOySSIVGQuTvj2fh/CB/sxJRyq1o684QOF7iXWBSNJVvomaOhhAY\n0kJNPV33/XHrv+dZ4o5X\n=HlxC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree fcf860499d25c486c131d4cf268920e77ba27eec\nparent 63f009e9dad2e70454b7ed6434d8aa28dfb52b51\nauthor Channing Conger <cconger@openai.com> 1782068724 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782068724 -0700\n\ncode-mode: linearize cell terminal state (#29286)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Introduce a single cell terminal-state machine for completion and\ntermination.\n- Make stored-value commits atomic with the winning terminal outcome.\n- Buffer terminal results for later observation and cover\ntermination-before-commit behavior.\n\n## Why\n\nCompletion, termination, observation, and stored-value updates must\nagree on one linearized outcome under cancellation races.\n\n## Impact\n\nTerminal delivery becomes deterministic and terminated cells cannot\ncommit state after termination wins.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Focused terminal-state regression passed.\n- Stack-tip validation: `just test -p codex-code-mode -p\ncodex-code-mode-protocol` (70 passed).\n- Parent branch:\n`cconger/code-mode-runtime-compact-03b-session-runtime`.","verified_at":"2026-06-21T19:05:25Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f774455c3a831dfab2c6f37a1f624b8097f6f2c2","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f774455c3a831dfab2c6f37a1f624b8097f6f2c2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f774455c3a831dfab2c6f37a1f624b8097f6f2c2/comments","author":{"login":"cconger","id":200563,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMDU2Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/200563?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger","html_url":"https://github.com/cconger","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"63f009e9dad2e70454b7ed6434d8aa28dfb52b51","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/63f009e9dad2e70454b7ed6434d8aa28dfb52b51","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/63f009e9dad2e70454b7ed6434d8aa28dfb52b51"}]},{"sha":"63f009e9dad2e70454b7ed6434d8aa28dfb52b51","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDYzZjAwOWU5ZGFkMmU3MDQ1NGI3ZWQ2NDM0ZDhhYTI4ZGZiNTJiNTE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Channing Conger","email":"cconger@openai.com","date":"2026-06-21T18:18:36Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-21T18:18:36Z"},"message":"code-mode: move session ownership into runtime (#29285)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Move code-mode cell ownership and shared stored values from\n`CodeModeService` into `SessionRuntime`.\n- Keep the protocol-facing execute/wait behavior behind the existing\nservice adapter.\n- Add runtime-level ownership and isolation coverage.\n\n## Why\n\nThis establishes a transport-neutral session boundary before later\nlifecycle and create/observe changes.\n\n## Impact\n\nNo intended model-facing behavior change. This is an ownership and\nlayering refactor.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Stack-tip validation: `just test -p codex-code-mode -p\ncodex-code-mode-protocol` (70 passed).\n- Parent branch: `cconger/code-mode-runtime-compact-03a-runtime-types`.","tree":{"sha":"a2da0305cea37ebd949d4011bfc8a96592aa0dc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/a2da0305cea37ebd949d4011bfc8a96592aa0dc3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/63f009e9dad2e70454b7ed6434d8aa28dfb52b51","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOCr8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAM4gQAIxH9peSBgzpQErVMGkBgA8O\nKgGjHzYeZZH4LI6j2FWz2GXc0oCe4a84k4tLaefe+7MCqhcnMQSYOKg9/4Cg2/eE\nBJpuMNosXtjFDZ66ZWcRfcsCrBoEnociYH3E9tx9g7UYHMot2iCwf7PiylQBWbAb\ncMjR5FGIX21C8Ut+pS1ddE/85LYB0rIIgs7Oso+jR5DhG+dC0t7yrVee1JVVmXjO\nB2+k3gJ2lUWz3ECtQ7LdDV1lcbEoXsAd4cr0d9UJXDGqP1eOpZkVSCDz4k9JGXIW\nQ/g0U5mUVk3Y7Gd14Ek2rmDQLa1GkoZo6c4tZSwO7xJwL6x0GaEv0O/Nm3ai/WqY\nmDJcpVCiunIq2YHheQBp03+4WsA2iUmFrpAd0StrhM75dVZXJbvmiXoeUBdIpRhV\n3V9KGKddScauCele5cP4isqouiKUHSxbrWmaSbWbmyVQm1Xx6I5DwGY+F0M9tRq/\n5bd40AO8TnAtTZagVwRl/yg8f/YLETTnOPTvzTICuWM7U+2WQ6Jd4LvwSP/ttWbD\naaLjnjbNIyyrzyX6ahoTakr5SmFQeaey75E8+ems6y0lzKHZyykze3Pv2WEgJ9P7\n58j1UXrxJ2UiGBbkutezGVmHWbPqzVLQv7yTDwx/EW6EYC4q6ZELA9edt6AcbIsm\n5mYIypMfSmuCc2SUjBss\n=ainz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a2da0305cea37ebd949d4011bfc8a96592aa0dc3\nparent 6d993ca6464570993e9312096d77b964e64bfab5\nauthor Channing Conger <cconger@openai.com> 1782065916 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782065916 -0700\n\ncode-mode: move session ownership into runtime (#29285)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Move code-mode cell ownership and shared stored values from\n`CodeModeService` into `SessionRuntime`.\n- Keep the protocol-facing execute/wait behavior behind the existing\nservice adapter.\n- Add runtime-level ownership and isolation coverage.\n\n## Why\n\nThis establishes a transport-neutral session boundary before later\nlifecycle and create/observe changes.\n\n## Impact\n\nNo intended model-facing behavior change. This is an ownership and\nlayering refactor.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Stack-tip validation: `just test -p codex-code-mode -p\ncodex-code-mode-protocol` (70 passed).\n- Parent branch: `cconger/code-mode-runtime-compact-03a-runtime-types`.","verified_at":"2026-06-21T18:18:36Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/63f009e9dad2e70454b7ed6434d8aa28dfb52b51","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/63f009e9dad2e70454b7ed6434d8aa28dfb52b51","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/63f009e9dad2e70454b7ed6434d8aa28dfb52b51/comments","author":{"login":"cconger","id":200563,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMDU2Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/200563?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger","html_url":"https://github.com/cconger","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6d993ca6464570993e9312096d77b964e64bfab5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6d993ca6464570993e9312096d77b964e64bfab5","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6d993ca6464570993e9312096d77b964e64bfab5"}]},{"sha":"6d993ca6464570993e9312096d77b964e64bfab5","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDZkOTkzY2E2NDY0NTcwOTkzZTkzMTIwOTZkNzdiOTY0ZTY0YmZhYjU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Channing Conger","email":"cconger@openai.com","date":"2026-06-21T17:49:31Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-21T17:49:31Z"},"message":"code-mode: define transport-neutral runtime types (#29170)\n\n## Summary\n\n- introduce a private `session_runtime` boundary for cell creation\nrequests, observation modes, lifecycle events, output items, and tool\nmetadata\n- update the cell actor and in-process service to use those\ntransport-neutral types\n- keep cell ID allocation on the owning session side\n\n## Motivation\n\nCell lifecycle vocabulary currently lives inside the cell actor\nimplementation. That makes the service adapter and future session\nruntime depend on actor-specific types, increasing the size and\ncomplexity of the runtime ownership change.\n\nThis is the first reviewable slice of the session-runtime stack. It\nseparates the transport-neutral data model without moving lifecycle\nownership or changing behavior.\n\nLater slices will move session state behind this boundary, harden\nterminal and shutdown behavior, and split cell creation from\nobservation.\n\n## Behavior\n\nThere are no public API or user-visible behavior changes in this PR.\n\nIn particular:\n\n- `CodeModeSession::execute` and `wait` are unchanged\n- cell IDs remain allocated by the owning session\n- cell admission, observation, termination, and shutdown behavior are\nunchanged","tree":{"sha":"233a64e7946cb7241094b2924b3ff54a4b04d997","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/233a64e7946cb7241094b2924b3ff54a4b04d997"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/6d993ca6464570993e9312096d77b964e64bfab5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOCQrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAK44QAIu1jEl4vLo5ZR55nGEz9pCM\nRxeWrdgWQwuviFUrfiphIr6Ul5E8WbLDz0z5ASIcrNKFcZO7RLcGfl6EbJdDqVIT\njt4/OG6HY49RA4PlPqUtDMMCSVyxe5yqLWQjwsjOPspOCgqwbllZXSEuTXqECA58\nHlXBX/Cc+TQCmqEAbEBFMbKNCbrlRoUFbdzWlkdJzMmfhX/kkA/4UD9psOCsgxxw\n4nSwoIJdpoNcrKsimg+2NQ1iGm4jTEIxipxQCSAnHXSvzIkNFd46iQZa8Ds1zCWV\nEjR8lxh4lG3v3h9UZxOJ0942ZdmGSDiVe5k/yxOnuGC3db2z83cEFCnl/39HTOIf\nJuADqlwOdNoXc+LXvcLcZPrYvGcKQps+Dl7rlHUABMAYs5VvSr55Xxj/NKSdKL0/\niKAEXDTuA1fqm5gSOc9uFNzwLNnvsvdrJ4ZEmihu/J37EyLLQG7gccpUQ+2Eki8v\nbgpoSBXidBJUR1wfXsPc7ferYIY/2ND0gsYHn25FYlGiqI3mivinIldUoCVwE6LZ\n/OQFYYyeyPpl9lVRIuuxWNsrkL8HmsEb0DnQ51pTl1qtWnIDPgzx93uI55hvEqT/\nkP/sU3zkakIeaT7GfJ/VBuYlwI8qRy13t37oyh7nxvRJkkOHnlTQqurmuF4nNwAW\naDaunmqh9yoyqoxw1+Sy\n=PaBb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 233a64e7946cb7241094b2924b3ff54a4b04d997\nparent 6f5dd7b4226f3c77d4d253d8be1e10ac1686ccf9\nauthor Channing Conger <cconger@openai.com> 1782064171 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782064171 -0700\n\ncode-mode: define transport-neutral runtime types (#29170)\n\n## Summary\n\n- introduce a private `session_runtime` boundary for cell creation\nrequests, observation modes, lifecycle events, output items, and tool\nmetadata\n- update the cell actor and in-process service to use those\ntransport-neutral types\n- keep cell ID allocation on the owning session side\n\n## Motivation\n\nCell lifecycle vocabulary currently lives inside the cell actor\nimplementation. That makes the service adapter and future session\nruntime depend on actor-specific types, increasing the size and\ncomplexity of the runtime ownership change.\n\nThis is the first reviewable slice of the session-runtime stack. It\nseparates the transport-neutral data model without moving lifecycle\nownership or changing behavior.\n\nLater slices will move session state behind this boundary, harden\nterminal and shutdown behavior, and split cell creation from\nobservation.\n\n## Behavior\n\nThere are no public API or user-visible behavior changes in this PR.\n\nIn particular:\n\n- `CodeModeSession::execute` and `wait` are unchanged\n- cell IDs remain allocated by the owning session\n- cell admission, observation, termination, and shutdown behavior are\nunchanged","verified_at":"2026-06-21T17:49:32Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6d993ca6464570993e9312096d77b964e64bfab5","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6d993ca6464570993e9312096d77b964e64bfab5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6d993ca6464570993e9312096d77b964e64bfab5/comments","author":{"login":"cconger","id":200563,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMDU2Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/200563?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger","html_url":"https://github.com/cconger","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6f5dd7b4226f3c77d4d253d8be1e10ac1686ccf9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6f5dd7b4226f3c77d4d253d8be1e10ac1686ccf9","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6f5dd7b4226f3c77d4d253d8be1e10ac1686ccf9"}]},{"sha":"6f5dd7b4226f3c77d4d253d8be1e10ac1686ccf9","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDZmNWRkN2I0MjI2ZjNjNzdkNGQyNTNkOGJlMWUxMGFjMTY4NmNjZjk","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-21T12:53:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-21T12:53:16Z"},"message":"Use controlled time for remote initialization timeout test (#29329)\n\n## Summary\n\nThe remote-control initialization timeout test used a 50 ms wall-clock\ndeadline around a 10 ms transport timeout. A busy CI runner could miss\nthat outer deadline even when the rollback behavior was correct.\n\nPause Tokio time and advance it explicitly through the transport timeout\ninstead. The test still verifies that initialization fails and emits the\nmatching connection-closed event, without depending on scheduler speed.","tree":{"sha":"216b9ddc8c343d7769dc9e0efeeb670b47699e92","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/216b9ddc8c343d7769dc9e0efeeb670b47699e92"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/6f5dd7b4226f3c77d4d253d8be1e10ac1686ccf9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqN968CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASBsQABN7Q6ISNTEMbA2bRiI0wtyX\nT6ZtnvbC+zWK8Lq7jlvfogDp3dhYQIamOJNCnnHQdEOaakCHWXQHcJYBVn2utRgs\nBe2rKmeCVNfdx9h+pJz3IfTAocZTwuegVgauqdq58aNzo9/2efO2jlUglZkrxA9k\nxqiXrwHxw7rIubmYtnWpX+ri9NWuS8IQZYOMUdblNulMzTks90+nee+jmAkcoj8N\n10WgwBcP8jHuKp+XaKA3Q0L9I8Uju312g/My8V7dWSgqcGVu5Sc4Q7c7w2YRqE6a\nC4VPvGAYGXCWw+aV2DRjP/h2hygm77njCSsZXkYG/HL6qV0VdQpPsEiTUSl1sS+z\nFZ5bb7JUp9xfsCLQKmGuPqUI6NGjbQ28Sd3JeaJX6yMMRXiyxclk6OhQB1cscwuR\nBTNuktY6qPSPIlLbQNagZL2v2DESMBkFfeGSnpZ3VFR6FSWPQYaPvLjqs80/VIlm\npueLwDaiTmPa2A3ov8ZBbN2gkw6BE8IAhEUnb5DtrwlYfimpaT6iZVlZzSgoyjUg\nM95CBY1stCFpLKrVMLr3kAgfEc+3GdF8c7S0UVtuKvOLPByLl/5nQ/nfCjQWF8OM\naAfxjzBIZebl+lz0RPzrg6KZOFs8ISlnPRyYOZ2Th12AOyP3KIw9LjcOdMwPkevD\nWtL0yWjTkCZOOvc+Qz3G\n=XtqD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 216b9ddc8c343d7769dc9e0efeeb670b47699e92\nparent c2fbf4247abb9718a280c2647cedeab87db2e169\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782046396 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782046396 +0200\n\nUse controlled time for remote initialization timeout test (#29329)\n\n## Summary\n\nThe remote-control initialization timeout test used a 50 ms wall-clock\ndeadline around a 10 ms transport timeout. A busy CI runner could miss\nthat outer deadline even when the rollback behavior was correct.\n\nPause Tokio time and advance it explicitly through the transport timeout\ninstead. The test still verifies that initialization fails and emits the\nmatching connection-closed event, without depending on scheduler speed.","verified_at":"2026-06-21T12:53:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6f5dd7b4226f3c77d4d253d8be1e10ac1686ccf9","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6f5dd7b4226f3c77d4d253d8be1e10ac1686ccf9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6f5dd7b4226f3c77d4d253d8be1e10ac1686ccf9/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c2fbf4247abb9718a280c2647cedeab87db2e169","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c2fbf4247abb9718a280c2647cedeab87db2e169","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c2fbf4247abb9718a280c2647cedeab87db2e169"}]},{"sha":"c2fbf4247abb9718a280c2647cedeab87db2e169","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGMyZmJmNDI0N2FiYjk3MThhMjgwYzI2NDdjZWRlYWI4N2RiMmUxNjk","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-21T12:04:18Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-21T12:04:18Z"},"message":"Parallelize skill metadata stats (#29326)\n\n## Summary\n\nThis switches skill discovery to the simpler same-connection scalar\nrequest shape.\n\nAfter reading a skills directory, discovery now starts the existing\n`fs/getMetadata` calls for all visible entries in that directory before\nawaiting the results. There is no JSON-RPC batch frame and no new\nfilesystem API; remote filesystems use the existing request-id\nmultiplexing on the same exec-server connection.\n\nThis is the scoped alternative to the batch-frame approach in #29074 /\n#29075.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Collect visible directory entries before processing them.\n- Run their existing `fs.get_metadata(...)` calls with `join_all`.\n- Process the results in the original directory order, so skill\ndiscovery behavior stays the same.\n\n## Benchmarks\n\nFresh local benchmark against generated skill trees over a real\nexec-server remote filesystem. The benchmark calls the actual\n`load_skills_from_roots` path, so this includes directory reads,\nmetadata stats, `SKILL.md` reads, and parsing.\n\nTimes are p50 milliseconds from 5 samples after 1 warmup, using warmed\nruns.\n\n| Scenario | Legacy `main` | Batch frame stack (#29074 / #29075) |\nSame-connection scalar stack |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| 100 flat skills | 377.4 | 389.0 | 378.6 |\n| 500 flat skills | 1983.2 | 1856.6 | 1757.5 |\n\nTakeaway: for the actual skill discovery path, same-connection scalar is\ntied with legacy at 100 skills and best at 500 skills. The batch-frame\nstack does not show enough win here to justify the extra protocol/API\nsurface.\n\nBenchmark command:\n\n- `just test -p codex-exec-server benchmark_remote_skill_discovery\n--run-ignored ignored-only --no-capture`\n\nChecked locally with:\n\n- `just test -p codex-core-skills`\n- `just bazel-lock-update`\n- `just bazel-lock-check`","tree":{"sha":"b468d150a3317ab0019354a842728eb00678293a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/b468d150a3317ab0019354a842728eb00678293a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/c2fbf4247abb9718a280c2647cedeab87db2e169","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqN9NCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALd8QAI0T3yBUeGourKnUUcumW10i\nzoqiaH7oKay7F5GNLoAyBYBtT7nFnkhJRKuk9QE6GygIiyb1WhSQRayibW/v/PdU\nZIn+2RZprurqWQi+LIL9+wtrlaYPnjGdhI1gPnZZGMAslGOsA+XDFM6suMFsPBEL\nne1Ye/UqfaeCdPvmQvCAor4P2/LfHiYrHr1RWLSLndSMVKeoUayxkfrxgqaaHPFF\ntg/mWvGIvZnpUbCVsZK6hbrAfM3cbG53yM6tpq4CBpIAs3UEo/qYVgGTbgqzFCxp\n0CKmmkObjEf3Yli4KNMTgqQ+ec4kSTgFUg6uAPw2emZRTZ08TWK8Ei83wh31pqoh\nRagFOOQsk+QyIosf6w6xUWf07G3XfMcPCtZz7LyxgsojmvDJ0snI7B3jXM3eYIkI\nqvx7D9TlFZGBMGgcyTzptNhmw+WayTueKVqDRxQjzBpd+12LW7i+knORlRaf+5nx\nj/z+nqlxfVFfOPS3boOi1E3U5w4jnKbOn0g/VsILu9qh9EgsAvWcE1D98bfa7743\n2H9l6MppHH7nVLtH25IhSDCrUcMOF9Pg3U9U0d607JeChYUq5sJTocTUHFsyY+2J\nKo0CCF5e0miyeN0KgG8ZkzX4RmVOC3Z776Zn9rlbUFRqfS1C63Ii6xEq+o2jYYWx\niLluVyuXpCLsjmYxUzWz\n=mgUR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b468d150a3317ab0019354a842728eb00678293a\nparent 1088b30fda97c83b70b3b64e883d481ba40528ae\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782043458 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782043458 +0200\n\nParallelize skill metadata stats (#29326)\n\n## Summary\n\nThis switches skill discovery to the simpler same-connection scalar\nrequest shape.\n\nAfter reading a skills directory, discovery now starts the existing\n`fs/getMetadata` calls for all visible entries in that directory before\nawaiting the results. There is no JSON-RPC batch frame and no new\nfilesystem API; remote filesystems use the existing request-id\nmultiplexing on the same exec-server connection.\n\nThis is the scoped alternative to the batch-frame approach in #29074 /\n#29075.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Collect visible directory entries before processing them.\n- Run their existing `fs.get_metadata(...)` calls with `join_all`.\n- Process the results in the original directory order, so skill\ndiscovery behavior stays the same.\n\n## Benchmarks\n\nFresh local benchmark against generated skill trees over a real\nexec-server remote filesystem. The benchmark calls the actual\n`load_skills_from_roots` path, so this includes directory reads,\nmetadata stats, `SKILL.md` reads, and parsing.\n\nTimes are p50 milliseconds from 5 samples after 1 warmup, using warmed\nruns.\n\n| Scenario | Legacy `main` | Batch frame stack (#29074 / #29075) |\nSame-connection scalar stack |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| 100 flat skills | 377.4 | 389.0 | 378.6 |\n| 500 flat skills | 1983.2 | 1856.6 | 1757.5 |\n\nTakeaway: for the actual skill discovery path, same-connection scalar is\ntied with legacy at 100 skills and best at 500 skills. The batch-frame\nstack does not show enough win here to justify the extra protocol/API\nsurface.\n\nBenchmark command:\n\n- `just test -p codex-exec-server benchmark_remote_skill_discovery\n--run-ignored ignored-only --no-capture`\n\nChecked locally with:\n\n- `just test -p codex-core-skills`\n- `just bazel-lock-update`\n- `just bazel-lock-check`","verified_at":"2026-06-21T12:04:19Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c2fbf4247abb9718a280c2647cedeab87db2e169","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c2fbf4247abb9718a280c2647cedeab87db2e169","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c2fbf4247abb9718a280c2647cedeab87db2e169/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1088b30fda97c83b70b3b64e883d481ba40528ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1088b30fda97c83b70b3b64e883d481ba40528ae","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1088b30fda97c83b70b3b64e883d481ba40528ae"}]},{"sha":"1088b30fda97c83b70b3b64e883d481ba40528ae","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDEwODhiMzBmZGE5N2M4M2I3MGIzYjY0ZTg4M2Q0ODFiYTQwNTI4YWU","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-21T11:40:51Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-21T11:40:51Z"},"message":"Test pipelined scalar exec-server requests (#29325)\n\n## Summary\n\nThis adds focused coverage for the simpler same-connection scalar\nrequest path.\n\nThe exec-server connection already supports multiple in-flight JSON-RPC\nscalar requests on one connection. This test locks in that behavior by\nsending two normal requests before reading either response, without\nadding a batch frame or any new API surface.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added a processor-level test that initializes an exec-server\nconnection.\n- Sends two scalar `environment/info` requests back-to-back on the same\nconnection.\n- Verifies both responses come back on the same connection by request\nid.\n\nChecked locally with:\n\n- `just test -p codex-exec-server\nconnection_accepts_pipelined_scalar_requests`","tree":{"sha":"01760ed18c42b64595de0e8b5b24fee43bf74239","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/01760ed18c42b64595de0e8b5b24fee43bf74239"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/1088b30fda97c83b70b3b64e883d481ba40528ae","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqN83DCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAflQQACCwarZO5zdhmcgde0vg3Xdi\nDHUSxg6+iIsQmd5jKaITBlxrdL1KE93IskaS4WsnMYXvDATkbAoMfDqX5QkxfygQ\nCczxMav7c/DAIKAkSjubRY22QzsiQcY7Y4kaFsI1Ia5kWzjqOJbwTsXSSy+S0hXC\nOwm04YdAwDb6r6HRN8Ai3BAggrWPq62I8AmR76+YjOmOw0ECH92R53hXacFvkh3Y\n2JDaN2ccYn+7kUY2ngh+LvB8vy9eXsB+cAtgNn4/iEai3mVODZX+Tzm5TVZXUt4h\n436HEGjAezNGHTu92fN67zz48ZQigrXFIX0nVRAzNo7N1DHTD1+v911TIhS2AUoN\nD8VDRiZkkMltDlyITea3+ny1kEQsp5SojroFCNTYqyrWECwR5Drf3ggPZGq7t2os\nZZO16qzYZ7Rb4B+PMVxoPUDB9QIBy99swGGxaLoXuZzseINR1PvrINsFhZJyJLrZ\nI3FpjVKKOTOqxycKkIYDi9Buibc3i6G65APV2xUdNDBQ3B09EMRKx/1pubsCpGfd\nnbrO+T4cLHVdvdCTVgETShY9tzZl8zQl7d+WHmuKc+HU6Qo3kkU2Inr7xBqp6LJ+\neFlzn/Nt467UIoquk26xeTk23QOf0VL3Kxzzf27SqYAH3jumnwz65fna9FCPwxOg\nUqH9LPwmhYmo04NUqVCZ\n=men/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 01760ed18c42b64595de0e8b5b24fee43bf74239\nparent bd2968a4db3057657f6d242010bfd15f589124f3\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782042051 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782042051 +0200\n\nTest pipelined scalar exec-server requests (#29325)\n\n## Summary\n\nThis adds focused coverage for the simpler same-connection scalar\nrequest path.\n\nThe exec-server connection already supports multiple in-flight JSON-RPC\nscalar requests on one connection. This test locks in that behavior by\nsending two normal requests before reading either response, without\nadding a batch frame or any new API surface.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added a processor-level test that initializes an exec-server\nconnection.\n- Sends two scalar `environment/info` requests back-to-back on the same\nconnection.\n- Verifies both responses come back on the same connection by request\nid.\n\nChecked locally with:\n\n- `just test -p codex-exec-server\nconnection_accepts_pipelined_scalar_requests`","verified_at":"2026-06-21T11:40:51Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1088b30fda97c83b70b3b64e883d481ba40528ae","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1088b30fda97c83b70b3b64e883d481ba40528ae","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1088b30fda97c83b70b3b64e883d481ba40528ae/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"bd2968a4db3057657f6d242010bfd15f589124f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bd2968a4db3057657f6d242010bfd15f589124f3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/bd2968a4db3057657f6d242010bfd15f589124f3"}]},{"sha":"bd2968a4db3057657f6d242010bfd15f589124f3","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGJkMjk2OGE0ZGIzMDU3NjU3ZjZkMjQyMDEwYmZkMTVmNTg5MTI0ZjM","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-21T10:33:21Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-21T10:33:21Z"},"message":"Carry sandbox intent to remote exec servers (#29108)\n\n## What changed\n\nPR #29099 stopped sending the orchestrator's concrete sandbox wrapper to\na remote exec-server. Remote commands now arrive as plain native argv.\n\nThis PR adds the next piece: Codex also sends portable sandbox intent\nnext to that plain argv.\n\nFor a remote unified-exec command, the request can now include:\n\n- the canonical permission profile before local workspace-root\nmaterialization\n- the sandbox cwd and workspace roots as `PathUri` values\n- Windows sandbox settings\n- the legacy Landlock setting\n- whether managed networking must be enforced\n\nThe important part is that symbolic entries such as `:workspace_roots`\nstay symbolic while crossing the boundary. The executor can then bind\nthem to its own workspace-root paths instead of receiving\norchestrator-local absolute paths.\n\nThe data travels through `ExecRequest` into `ExecParams`. Older\nexec-servers can still deserialize requests because the new fields have\ndefaults.\n\n## Why\n\nThe orchestrator should not decide how another machine implements\nsandboxing.\n\nFor example:\n\n- a local macOS Codex would normally build a Seatbelt command\n- a remote Linux executor needs a Linux sandbox command instead\n\nThe orchestrator now sends the plain command plus the policy it intended\nto enforce. A later PR can let the exec-server choose and build the\ncorrect sandbox for its own operating system.\n\n## Important detail\n\nThis keeps the portable intent separate from the local `SandboxType`.\n\n`SandboxType::None` is ambiguous:\n\n- it can mean the command was explicitly approved to run without a\nsandbox\n- it can also mean the orchestrator host has no concrete sandbox\nimplementation available\n\nThose cases are different for remote execution. This PR adds\n`sandbox_requested` so an executor can still receive sandbox intent when\nthe orchestrator cannot build a local wrapper. Explicit unsandboxed\nretries still send no sandbox context.\n\n## Behavior today\n\nThis PR only transports the intent. The exec-server accepts the new\nfields but does not apply them yet.\n\nRemote commands therefore remain unsandboxed after this PR, just as they\nare after PR #29099.\n\n## Follow-up\n\nThe next PR will make exec-server read this portable intent, bind\nsymbolic workspace permissions to executor-native roots, choose the\nsandbox for its own operating system, build the wrapper locally, and\nthen spawn the command.","tree":{"sha":"c90934caedfceaec438744d022ed2ff085ded93e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/c90934caedfceaec438744d022ed2ff085ded93e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/bd2968a4db3057657f6d242010bfd15f589124f3","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqN73xCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABi4QAIGxgzaxxwooCZTdUDmuSjHw\n0Ic58MAlyXqTaiz84gPPvqZIgI85+TasEGUyHbMUOqLxJJ024eZYmf6TBa3y1b3q\nMLOdRHvL2DhiwrftppgKRp+2UKXN9W22NX+XgMoHIustxkweDHF7O3qOaD+pVi5k\nyPDR2wjyIp0rH7GzvcuS6w/zH4Kf6nYMi2XXlvs04pMCZd4T3F+5zQ7mSXZC8lWP\n4sJVZdeEMSxBrevV7vC87133bl5wlHv4gRkGGqAnFs3fdXkf5sMOeOye7itPkYk3\n0On9Lfigl77iviarSHTiY4nvt+2dd7aBtnadxbrSIpLj5d4Ytc3uEh1gIIJSF4jR\n91km7bafuwA8rGp+ZwaJQzyQBh5WfhV4jyz/WdIZaBjxG5n3P6ftE+N3qyj9fGf1\nXohVDstjtUQD32obVc2F9P8FnaV2wIdHdAv2hHJhiqoOBuPFXs1B82Lh53Zg6mCR\nzm4bJs/Wi/v4LMShXflDWZjvmuFwd1CWxP23qD9B/o+dQApKzYoK2DeX+zuxu5DS\ns9H448B/anjXD3BQhzozzDXBul6ooJMYwNrcE6UG95SNwy6ZQdq/JzuYFd8psNPB\n/LWyNQbB30yNt3/Yu5VmAFuXe3SevHjHii46b6Xa79R/P5iUbefhfLioRp0a2J3D\nO9rImT4TI4SPxQ/xt5X+\n=/g4H\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c90934caedfceaec438744d022ed2ff085ded93e\nparent aaf737fa59c4fc76984ec4cd705e8a7f07f0bd79\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782038001 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782038001 +0200\n\nCarry sandbox intent to remote exec servers (#29108)\n\n## What changed\n\nPR #29099 stopped sending the orchestrator's concrete sandbox wrapper to\na remote exec-server. Remote commands now arrive as plain native argv.\n\nThis PR adds the next piece: Codex also sends portable sandbox intent\nnext to that plain argv.\n\nFor a remote unified-exec command, the request can now include:\n\n- the canonical permission profile before local workspace-root\nmaterialization\n- the sandbox cwd and workspace roots as `PathUri` values\n- Windows sandbox settings\n- the legacy Landlock setting\n- whether managed networking must be enforced\n\nThe important part is that symbolic entries such as `:workspace_roots`\nstay symbolic while crossing the boundary. The executor can then bind\nthem to its own workspace-root paths instead of receiving\norchestrator-local absolute paths.\n\nThe data travels through `ExecRequest` into `ExecParams`. Older\nexec-servers can still deserialize requests because the new fields have\ndefaults.\n\n## Why\n\nThe orchestrator should not decide how another machine implements\nsandboxing.\n\nFor example:\n\n- a local macOS Codex would normally build a Seatbelt command\n- a remote Linux executor needs a Linux sandbox command instead\n\nThe orchestrator now sends the plain command plus the policy it intended\nto enforce. A later PR can let the exec-server choose and build the\ncorrect sandbox for its own operating system.\n\n## Important detail\n\nThis keeps the portable intent separate from the local `SandboxType`.\n\n`SandboxType::None` is ambiguous:\n\n- it can mean the command was explicitly approved to run without a\nsandbox\n- it can also mean the orchestrator host has no concrete sandbox\nimplementation available\n\nThose cases are different for remote execution. This PR adds\n`sandbox_requested` so an executor can still receive sandbox intent when\nthe orchestrator cannot build a local wrapper. Explicit unsandboxed\nretries still send no sandbox context.\n\n## Behavior today\n\nThis PR only transports the intent. The exec-server accepts the new\nfields but does not apply them yet.\n\nRemote commands therefore remain unsandboxed after this PR, just as they\nare after PR #29099.\n\n## Follow-up\n\nThe next PR will make exec-server read this portable intent, bind\nsymbolic workspace permissions to executor-native roots, choose the\nsandbox for its own operating system, build the wrapper locally, and\nthen spawn the command.","verified_at":"2026-06-21T10:33:22Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bd2968a4db3057657f6d242010bfd15f589124f3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/bd2968a4db3057657f6d242010bfd15f589124f3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bd2968a4db3057657f6d242010bfd15f589124f3/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"aaf737fa59c4fc76984ec4cd705e8a7f07f0bd79","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/aaf737fa59c4fc76984ec4cd705e8a7f07f0bd79","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/aaf737fa59c4fc76984ec4cd705e8a7f07f0bd79"}]},{"sha":"aaf737fa59c4fc76984ec4cd705e8a7f07f0bd79","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGFhZjczN2ZhNTljNGZjNzY5ODRlYzRjZDcwNWU4YTdmMDdmMGJkNzk","commit":{"author":{"name":"pakrym-oai","email":"pakrym@openai.com","date":"2026-06-21T04:50:09Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-21T04:50:09Z"},"message":"[codex] simplify token budget context (#29295)\n\n## Why\n\nThe token-budget feature currently adds remaining-token messages\nwhenever usage crosses the 25%, 50%, and 75% thresholds. Those periodic\ninserts create prompt churn without requiring action, while the\nnear-compaction reminder and explicit `get_context_remaining` tool\nalready cover actionable and on-demand budget information.\n\nThe context-window lineage block is also easier to scan as plain labeled\ntext than as a `<token_budget>`-wrapped fragment.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Stop recording automatic remaining-token messages at percentage\nthresholds.\n- Render context-window lineage in `First`, `Current`, `Previous` order\nwith colon-separated labels.\n- Omit the `Previous` line for the first context window.\n- Remove `<token_budget>` wrappers from newly rendered lineage,\nnear-compaction reminders, and `get_context_remaining` output.\n- Keep recognizing legacy wrapped fragments so existing rollouts remain\ncompatible.\n- Remove the post-sampling token snapshot that was only needed by the\nperiodic threshold path.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core token_budget` (11 tests passed)","tree":{"sha":"aa650b8498f3a1513a3136bb7243f5ec3997f22f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/aa650b8498f3a1513a3136bb7243f5ec3997f22f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/aaf737fa59c4fc76984ec4cd705e8a7f07f0bd79","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqN22BCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkQwQALCP7i4ggj5KQD2nwH2l99eG\nsOc0hzx7Fxc5N7Ehm9285SFFJPHZmHz6czDlnEtooxN9b1y5bHLHNuDHHVfMdrD+\nQa5XbZSUSC77M9aAPcWZRyby8ptA9FeTqlYuFq7KiHi6PzF5+Ku91Cl1rXtyNLkj\nwP2zjuE/KenO1+G9fFflFqIr+vtaCEuNtXk7LwzYsWnoW4C3JUxkHDvHfit6XZKI\nu0o6Nlx7gKTT18xW9iZoixtIz92dLY1uP8NP5S7FG9/xxgqYTMNOBRXIOVbwCNiA\n4khhtKDyBZdYvVe4vLLrdXiKf7C/DsdB09PPNygVBpFlwV11m48CKkBg5pCYnTpd\nPOcvFgWQZOCGmGOYXd/BK+reDWIQwrBjwQRyQtbhl6yxwx3FEhnlVI4YHos5Vmlq\nTfp2ZFFhZxwW3i5wckKBYWhBEIm1TqJWaS9iH8niqiaKU8eTse6z+fYcsow9dMll\nPu1m0LY5PwifPC6TFimrCMSb11ijLvSU9DVmOErTvqduKAwnfWleXfOmRc0k6sRQ\nJoXpoPZtYfIfoCK+pp5UGC+tOnxJGe3+Hog/sjcqSg1Nfh+K+ODtnw0wYuRxw9Kz\nR35qf1Eq+VMMr8I5gR0rnA1YVjwgXPt5wJmzSC7V0aZjDRfUy7Rji2ZZO1qD732Q\nZt0wYiyfYF0g5Sbnb6a5\n=JbTi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree aa650b8498f3a1513a3136bb7243f5ec3997f22f\nparent 6df037d47ff9359dbe1e471f5eb3f7e6ff1fe421\nauthor pakrym-oai <pakrym@openai.com> 1782017409 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782017409 -0700\n\n[codex] simplify token budget context (#29295)\n\n## Why\n\nThe token-budget feature currently adds remaining-token messages\nwhenever usage crosses the 25%, 50%, and 75% thresholds. Those periodic\ninserts create prompt churn without requiring action, while the\nnear-compaction reminder and explicit `get_context_remaining` tool\nalready cover actionable and on-demand budget information.\n\nThe context-window lineage block is also easier to scan as plain labeled\ntext than as a `<token_budget>`-wrapped fragment.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Stop recording automatic remaining-token messages at percentage\nthresholds.\n- Render context-window lineage in `First`, `Current`, `Previous` order\nwith colon-separated labels.\n- Omit the `Previous` line for the first context window.\n- Remove `<token_budget>` wrappers from newly rendered lineage,\nnear-compaction reminders, and `get_context_remaining` output.\n- Keep recognizing legacy wrapped fragments so existing rollouts remain\ncompatible.\n- Remove the post-sampling token snapshot that was only needed by the\nperiodic threshold path.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core token_budget` (11 tests passed)","verified_at":"2026-06-21T04:50:10Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/aaf737fa59c4fc76984ec4cd705e8a7f07f0bd79","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/aaf737fa59c4fc76984ec4cd705e8a7f07f0bd79","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/aaf737fa59c4fc76984ec4cd705e8a7f07f0bd79/comments","author":{"login":"pakrym-oai","id":204937752,"node_id":"U_kgDODDcaGA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204937752?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/pakrym-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6df037d47ff9359dbe1e471f5eb3f7e6ff1fe421","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6df037d47ff9359dbe1e471f5eb3f7e6ff1fe421","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6df037d47ff9359dbe1e471f5eb3f7e6ff1fe421"}]},{"sha":"6df037d47ff9359dbe1e471f5eb3f7e6ff1fe421","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDZkZjAzN2Q0N2ZmOTM1OWRiZTFlNDcxZjVlYjNmN2U2ZmYxZmU0MjE","commit":{"author":{"name":"pakrym-oai","email":"pakrym@openai.com","date":"2026-06-21T02:13:42Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-21T02:13:42Z"},"message":"[codex] add configurable token budget compaction reminder (#29255)\n\n## Why\n\nThe token-budget feature reports coarse remaining-context milestones,\nbut it does not give the model a configurable wrap-up prompt before\nautomatic compaction. A strict threshold-crossing check can also miss\nresumed or reconfigured windows that are already inside the threshold.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add structured `[features.token_budget]` configuration for an absolute\n`reminder_threshold_tokens` and bounded `reminder_message_template`;\n`{n_remaining}` is expanded when the reminder is delivered.\n- Compute remaining tokens against the next effective auto-compaction\nboundary, including scoped `body_after_prefix` accounting and the full\ncontext-window limit.\n- Make reminder delivery level-triggered before and after sampling, with\none-shot state owned by `AutoCompactWindow` and re-armed on compaction,\n`new_context`, restore, or history replacement.\n- Leave the existing initial full-window token-budget context, 25/50/75%\nnotices, and token-budget tools unchanged.\n- Persist the resolved feature configuration in the session config lock\nand regenerate the config schema.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-core token_budget`\n- `just test -p codex-core\ntoken_budget_reminder_emits_after_crossing_compaction_threshold`\n- `just test -p codex-core auto_compact_window`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nlock_contains_prompts_and_materializes_features`\n- `just test -p codex-features`\n- `just test -p codex-config`","tree":{"sha":"8e6472b7f1c1dbee3004f2378e185669ce0db11c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/8e6472b7f1c1dbee3004f2378e185669ce0db11c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/6df037d47ff9359dbe1e471f5eb3f7e6ff1fe421","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqN0jWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqCEQADNR123GLjiCtG5Td5HjA1gb\n2fiYUXtW1exlM+ck0PjlFy874kFoq+jjQpI77SRiTElQnropL/CvqK9ZQEhyjOdp\n7i4Stc9XUvKz4IxdWtC5Iu8hHgHwRSWSaLxJIYgc0Ly3+3QP6z5Aupg+GObSzVT6\nUHKMLvZ7QDRYZNgX1T934qbC1mwWvPd8EbtqqOXC+tGIP9w+CQu8DDnhTSlRKTAF\nkNK8fhJoAvUPAPFoJ+t+Ba3zzvASjnJSPPgNDyWRIyIS8BYCCu9+ViHB+BDkhBNY\ngTFvGfO5Bb0Tn9ZaSp6NOnZDEwdRxePY6fumnRp8gdECMdwxWMUhJinUI7QhpDdW\nhXrzyg6znPEleGLALOvq4qUAAYKmQ/v9KZaeZevYM+a+e3DNq+9Axfn42l6ZaBOC\nU5ZC/qzy+/QmuZjU3aC7FCn8W12hqzAePO9pQb9iCx1/GiPAUUIswTGqgd5G2uN1\n+oC5ZytXD1R5ylvklUet+DRODr8jIn6Bpl5w30gnxUDJskP4H7uxrSpth5gqHGbO\n2Dk8d6TdPMK0tQ02MB7kMl1v9nrl/4ZoAHcCmlx5xZ7Ex1Z3EmguJauZBlZqlLHJ\nybqZ4DgzkKQhf5vr4hRR/kUoX7Oae7SKkQiaKOUwHqAkZyR6qig7J/3TbTOHprk1\nwzYWZ0cN1lQnlvzsyRl1\n=GRg8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8e6472b7f1c1dbee3004f2378e185669ce0db11c\nparent b6d6be2a8474836856871e5c58af05653238278a\nauthor pakrym-oai <pakrym@openai.com> 1782008022 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782008022 -0700\n\n[codex] add configurable token budget compaction reminder (#29255)\n\n## Why\n\nThe token-budget feature reports coarse remaining-context milestones,\nbut it does not give the model a configurable wrap-up prompt before\nautomatic compaction. A strict threshold-crossing check can also miss\nresumed or reconfigured windows that are already inside the threshold.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add structured `[features.token_budget]` configuration for an absolute\n`reminder_threshold_tokens` and bounded `reminder_message_template`;\n`{n_remaining}` is expanded when the reminder is delivered.\n- Compute remaining tokens against the next effective auto-compaction\nboundary, including scoped `body_after_prefix` accounting and the full\ncontext-window limit.\n- Make reminder delivery level-triggered before and after sampling, with\none-shot state owned by `AutoCompactWindow` and re-armed on compaction,\n`new_context`, restore, or history replacement.\n- Leave the existing initial full-window token-budget context, 25/50/75%\nnotices, and token-budget tools unchanged.\n- Persist the resolved feature configuration in the session config lock\nand regenerate the config schema.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-core token_budget`\n- `just test -p codex-core\ntoken_budget_reminder_emits_after_crossing_compaction_threshold`\n- `just test -p codex-core auto_compact_window`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nlock_contains_prompts_and_materializes_features`\n- `just test -p codex-features`\n- `just test -p codex-config`","verified_at":"2026-06-21T02:13:43Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6df037d47ff9359dbe1e471f5eb3f7e6ff1fe421","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6df037d47ff9359dbe1e471f5eb3f7e6ff1fe421","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6df037d47ff9359dbe1e471f5eb3f7e6ff1fe421/comments","author":{"login":"pakrym-oai","id":204937752,"node_id":"U_kgDODDcaGA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204937752?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/pakrym-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b6d6be2a8474836856871e5c58af05653238278a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b6d6be2a8474836856871e5c58af05653238278a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b6d6be2a8474836856871e5c58af05653238278a"}]},{"sha":"b6d6be2a8474836856871e5c58af05653238278a","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGI2ZDZiZTJhODQ3NDgzNjg1Njg3MWU1YzU4YWYwNTY1MzIzODI3OGE","commit":{"author":{"name":"pakrym-oai","email":"pakrym@openai.com","date":"2026-06-21T01:02:02Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-21T01:02:02Z"},"message":"[codex] prototype mcp_history thread hint injection (#29259)\n\n## Why\n\nPrototype whether the harness can invoke the `mcp_history` MCP while\nconstructing full initial context and expose its thread hint to the\nmodel without requiring a model-issued tool call.\n\nThe prototype builds on the context-window lineage added by #29256 and\nis now based directly on `main`.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Call `mcp_history/thread_hint` with no arguments while building the\nfull `<token_budget>` context.\n- Pass the current `threadId` through MCP request metadata, matching the\nnormal MCP tool-call path.\n- Serialize only the unstructured `content` result and append it inside\n`<token_budget>` when the call succeeds.\n- Omit the additional context when the MCP call or content serialization\nfails.\n\n## Prototype limitations\n\n- The direct call bypasses the normal model-initiated MCP approval,\nlifecycle-event, telemetry, and result-sanitization path.\n- The call has no prototype-specific timeout, result-size cap, or\nper-window cache.\n- MCP latency is added to full-context construction, including\napplicable compaction paths.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-core token_budget`","tree":{"sha":"182e98c29215b267f0a4382e352287a9b566e0ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/182e98c29215b267f0a4382e352287a9b566e0ac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/b6d6be2a8474836856871e5c58af05653238278a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNzgKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANYAQACaFkl+LT/diWsHhjypxVVBY\nVrRIr4WoDIRBDhSCLucSamIbraRFmxZgLRzwzK7pEwuK94ksc4MtdkQk+QHixtza\n6b46dD3/43i/75obMf1CzfvQRvj02M0q2lUIWIRJLNlbcbOye4gmo4F0p9vNDZgv\nTvtbtZJvtOE4GV6k1a8PmlFU976iHwYKVlXWfJl5e4e6KGxxoKQcJnicdkjGvBk7\nSSrQEBWeBMhAiAcMKUgyibV7EpMVluerxvT4d3CwPOY0/JNPvoT8onoQG5VeqaNZ\nVp85eWjND1AjutcLXWyqY7Dqx3ah3QyqQymMqrhFOX4zzasKFSTXo2Vc4Qsg2qZS\nA8fwi1ddzKYbffjL4H6li2cLR/GksxgdW8HTVr9ovQ/PPfLTRXV2zdB1EsIXxQAx\nNySPiZsRSqFpVcu0/qFJk80y9jc7YKZh1AjujylL+CiXvdCSwPrnqoyhTc6Bt/Ha\nD08ppPeNGsqz2rYtOeSuC0iXy28bVWvnCpfbBmsfP3O5n5vrrcZrM8tz6BotUJ+o\n4RcGFyX9EUGZIDQkBCwLKviQXitxkEqh301MmZ03GRkCaEajo9vOJQx+LLxLOVA9\n4ffbTDACPW4q3eCbJ9AUF5MqnD2SeEgb5KD8p7SwAq/GJxCvQZ/4syL/g4MPsihA\nvgJ8SyK9L1+gvxDH2DoD\n=aelZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 182e98c29215b267f0a4382e352287a9b566e0ac\nparent d1209bddfce79e8f6cafd7f9212a2df6915aec5d\nauthor pakrym-oai <pakrym@openai.com> 1782003722 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782003722 -0700\n\n[codex] prototype mcp_history thread hint injection (#29259)\n\n## Why\n\nPrototype whether the harness can invoke the `mcp_history` MCP while\nconstructing full initial context and expose its thread hint to the\nmodel without requiring a model-issued tool call.\n\nThe prototype builds on the context-window lineage added by #29256 and\nis now based directly on `main`.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Call `mcp_history/thread_hint` with no arguments while building the\nfull `<token_budget>` context.\n- Pass the current `threadId` through MCP request metadata, matching the\nnormal MCP tool-call path.\n- Serialize only the unstructured `content` result and append it inside\n`<token_budget>` when the call succeeds.\n- Omit the additional context when the MCP call or content serialization\nfails.\n\n## Prototype limitations\n\n- The direct call bypasses the normal model-initiated MCP approval,\nlifecycle-event, telemetry, and result-sanitization path.\n- The call has no prototype-specific timeout, result-size cap, or\nper-window cache.\n- MCP latency is added to full-context construction, including\napplicable compaction paths.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-core token_budget`","verified_at":"2026-06-21T01:02:02Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b6d6be2a8474836856871e5c58af05653238278a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b6d6be2a8474836856871e5c58af05653238278a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b6d6be2a8474836856871e5c58af05653238278a/comments","author":{"login":"pakrym-oai","id":204937752,"node_id":"U_kgDODDcaGA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204937752?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/pakrym-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d1209bddfce79e8f6cafd7f9212a2df6915aec5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d1209bddfce79e8f6cafd7f9212a2df6915aec5d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d1209bddfce79e8f6cafd7f9212a2df6915aec5d"}]},{"sha":"d1209bddfce79e8f6cafd7f9212a2df6915aec5d","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGQxMjA5YmRkZmNlNzllOGY2Y2FmZDdmOTIxMmEyZGY2OTE1YWVjNWQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"pakrym-oai","email":"pakrym@openai.com","date":"2026-06-20T20:15:49Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-20T20:15:49Z"},"message":"core: add context window lineage IDs (#29256)\n\n## Why\n\nThe rendered `<token_budget>` fragment identifies the thread and current\ncontext window, but it does not expose enough lineage to identify the\nfirst window in the thread or the immediately preceding window. Those\nIDs also need to remain stable across compaction, resume, and rollback.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Track first, previous, and current UUIDv7 context-window IDs in\nauto-compaction state.\n- Render `thread_id`, `first_window_id`, `previous_window_id`, and the\ncurrent window ID in the full `<token_budget>` fragment.\n- Persist the first and previous window IDs in compacted rollout\ncheckpoints and restore them during rollout reconstruction.\n- Preserve compatibility with older compacted records that do not\ncontain the new optional fields.\n- Update focused state, rendering, reconstruction, rollback, and\nserialization coverage.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-core token_budget`\n- `just test -p codex-protocol compacted_item::tests`\n- `just test -p codex-core tracks_prefill_and_window_boundaries`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nreconstruct_history_uses_replacement_history_verbatim`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nthread_rollback_restores_cleared_reference_context_item_after_compaction`","tree":{"sha":"344f98bd5bf6b249ff438c99f15d1fcdeb17c53b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/344f98bd5bf6b249ff438c99f15d1fcdeb17c53b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/d1209bddfce79e8f6cafd7f9212a2df6915aec5d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNvT1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQ28QAJs/+MVfo75oaMditr/R5SPo\npqfU9EYEWvU0nZTuRlPsiJiVgs8SNeBcurM9C44niG7kc0//8GuJqzdGKRf+tmC+\nq18qM2Fd5cDg39FmF7JI31sBaTDG+Z2Z0d87Hw5mYP+N4fAUQc99dGr56aRkEzVU\nxqvspSq2sPH6euuSnFqkHcfSfc606B3an2fUO+RUmIMMfD9YaIkSNWx6obBBjwm/\nb+xcbnbbGRH5UQAuhcsOI+nZmC7hIsdXFl5ZFGT3CmxRlf81OkEkeJG01IaIBA9r\nJ7cKl1hIONMqKXXHcL+MUhjsQLA344twpIcG6U4FkmApzm3JivxQ1h5No98I5Gli\ngnAJE9+Ft5N9Hl8fpHKejmxgHc+9aY1Jmqidis0M7z40mjHKVe7zE2rU8zu6fmrT\nS9SM6y7XHbSwqEqTaTgd1eipmFybgg2U5TbFDvpWabG2AGyvUromGQwN4Umyczbe\nQiUKPqHWSWuLog59KAsA3Tuj0M/SPL1qG0XdnwVnKSvCTYZ0YVC87O0Utt1iIGsN\nQZGPVi6EBJC4FdAsS3jbm/9Tqk/qffCQjdVRv/UVD78r3Ouv7CzVoyVP8Fj8/xqN\n16dqlwygnQ74lYG0cPbjbl+t6BIwgcymRDyp678x0vprMpfBYExDR5W33BjrTESs\n1EU5hzkDNMtlGRleBs6l\n=yHEQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 344f98bd5bf6b249ff438c99f15d1fcdeb17c53b\nparent d66708232299bdbf373ec55b0d6b938c246cfa60\nauthor pakrym-oai <pakrym@openai.com> 1781986549 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781986549 -0700\n\ncore: add context window lineage IDs (#29256)\n\n## Why\n\nThe rendered `<token_budget>` fragment identifies the thread and current\ncontext window, but it does not expose enough lineage to identify the\nfirst window in the thread or the immediately preceding window. Those\nIDs also need to remain stable across compaction, resume, and rollback.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Track first, previous, and current UUIDv7 context-window IDs in\nauto-compaction state.\n- Render `thread_id`, `first_window_id`, `previous_window_id`, and the\ncurrent window ID in the full `<token_budget>` fragment.\n- Persist the first and previous window IDs in compacted rollout\ncheckpoints and restore them during rollout reconstruction.\n- Preserve compatibility with older compacted records that do not\ncontain the new optional fields.\n- Update focused state, rendering, reconstruction, rollback, and\nserialization coverage.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-core token_budget`\n- `just test -p codex-protocol compacted_item::tests`\n- `just test -p codex-core tracks_prefill_and_window_boundaries`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nreconstruct_history_uses_replacement_history_verbatim`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nthread_rollback_restores_cleared_reference_context_item_after_compaction`","verified_at":"2026-06-20T20:15:50Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d1209bddfce79e8f6cafd7f9212a2df6915aec5d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d1209bddfce79e8f6cafd7f9212a2df6915aec5d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d1209bddfce79e8f6cafd7f9212a2df6915aec5d/comments","author":{"login":"pakrym-oai","id":204937752,"node_id":"U_kgDODDcaGA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204937752?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/pakrym-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d66708232299bdbf373ec55b0d6b938c246cfa60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d66708232299bdbf373ec55b0d6b938c246cfa60","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d66708232299bdbf373ec55b0d6b938c246cfa60"}]},{"sha":"d66708232299bdbf373ec55b0d6b938c246cfa60","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGQ2NjcwODIzMjI5OWJkYmYzNzNlYzU1YjBkNmI5MzhjMjQ2Y2ZhNjA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Traut","email":"etraut@openai.com","date":"2026-06-20T04:37:01Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-20T04:37:01Z"},"message":"Allow resume and settings commands during tasks and MCP startup (#29154)\n\n## Why\n\nThe TUI treats both an active turn and MCP startup as a running task.\nThat currently blocks `/resume` and several settings commands even\nthough they do not compete with turn execution, which is especially\nfrustrating when MCP startup is slow.\n\nModel, permissions, personality, and service-tier selections already\nupdate thread settings independently of the running turn. Other clients\ncan send those updates mid-turn, while the current turn continues with\nits captured settings. Allowing the same updates from local slash\ncommands makes the TUI consistent with that existing behavior.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Allow `/resume` while a task is running.\n- Allow `/model`, `/permissions`, `/personality`, and service-tier\ncommands such as `/fast` while a task is running.\n- Keep the existing behavior where the active turn uses its captured\nsettings and updates apply to subsequent turns.\n- Exercise the commands under the busy state in the existing TUI tests\nand retain coverage for commands that should remain blocked.\n\n## Behavior note\n\nTurn settings such as model selection and reasoning effort are captured\nwhen a turn starts. Changing them during an active turn affects the next\nturn, not the turn already in progress. The status bar updates\nimmediately, so it may temporarily display the newly selected setting\nbefore that setting is actually in effect.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Focused `codex-tui` tests for resume dispatch, settings popups,\n`/fast`, and disabled-command behavior.\n\n## Related issues\n\nCloses #19015.\n\nAddresses the next-turn-safe model/reasoning switching portion of\n#14356; dedicated shortcuts and the proposed depth meter remain out of\nscope.","tree":{"sha":"5d200fa68583197cde0ed6459dc1705428613fef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/5d200fa68583197cde0ed6459dc1705428613fef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/d66708232299bdbf373ec55b0d6b938c246cfa60","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNhjtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2hwQAIi34dOVOya8Z/k1UWDM528q\nPkVbrVgpSaxwylZdLq5otX8hKq4TiSMrnUG4++7x5QuKP6enP2Fj8VOtRJkCZ1sF\nvjeMobtbDXKS7MFpHjmz2SvCUM2ZSsfQ395oFR5dub/C+7ee9XeAuzBjmO5Vqcfj\nLgUHpUbeswEGZWVEAyd7NXYx0ba9AtapsYNyQ7ZYJJ4fwKkXqa9sQ2yjRCzj+twx\nSHlE71UJuOor0bbhMqzeykvvfVVIiFzhz+r4eA1NV9Aeu4pXi0brlX1LsZ/EsVUu\nfIqgXsmo8u/W7sQCs+mhBwKG5p6+shLp76RZqxH8kC2wbUDqU3CoCfbCvv/nUoQ3\n6EwF/EkyBgt4ihS7lo5p+8WF5+mAfOhTx92uAcD9rWAD02m2QnVGiLOh4NapVkGg\nNq0FH2eeIPoGP8ZiNC/RNh3YNNHtv9mzsk+wux+oa5HOcXgRTR7j3adx7v6MH/rY\nNaqdcIsnJAGXKvJvjmuthICkvP4ckNxEjAfNoB518AhbJYBmrmarUcw/5bzaD5o9\nKJDE+oONZLODgdIiLPTqFIvsYaphjgRVYj163yQbgcAuVVMUqFINjUIhG8zLqplG\nWUTspe4Uewn4U7toeuyrwqWvx7rLfimgBfbxsBqU6T1kbVsfU4q0kQb5cM6JUHqg\nUjB2Oe6+y4fyEWSol3xT\n=Js8v\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5d200fa68583197cde0ed6459dc1705428613fef\nparent 64bdeed9f7adbe60c725153b3fb74ed044a36221\nauthor Eric Traut <etraut@openai.com> 1781930221 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781930221 -0700\n\nAllow resume and settings commands during tasks and MCP startup (#29154)\n\n## Why\n\nThe TUI treats both an active turn and MCP startup as a running task.\nThat currently blocks `/resume` and several settings commands even\nthough they do not compete with turn execution, which is especially\nfrustrating when MCP startup is slow.\n\nModel, permissions, personality, and service-tier selections already\nupdate thread settings independently of the running turn. Other clients\ncan send those updates mid-turn, while the current turn continues with\nits captured settings. Allowing the same updates from local slash\ncommands makes the TUI consistent with that existing behavior.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Allow `/resume` while a task is running.\n- Allow `/model`, `/permissions`, `/personality`, and service-tier\ncommands such as `/fast` while a task is running.\n- Keep the existing behavior where the active turn uses its captured\nsettings and updates apply to subsequent turns.\n- Exercise the commands under the busy state in the existing TUI tests\nand retain coverage for commands that should remain blocked.\n\n## Behavior note\n\nTurn settings such as model selection and reasoning effort are captured\nwhen a turn starts. Changing them during an active turn affects the next\nturn, not the turn already in progress. The status bar updates\nimmediately, so it may temporarily display the newly selected setting\nbefore that setting is actually in effect.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Focused `codex-tui` tests for resume dispatch, settings popups,\n`/fast`, and disabled-command behavior.\n\n## Related issues\n\nCloses #19015.\n\nAddresses the next-turn-safe model/reasoning switching portion of\n#14356; dedicated shortcuts and the proposed depth meter remain out of\nscope.","verified_at":"2026-06-20T04:37:02Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d66708232299bdbf373ec55b0d6b938c246cfa60","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d66708232299bdbf373ec55b0d6b938c246cfa60","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d66708232299bdbf373ec55b0d6b938c246cfa60/comments","author":{"login":"etraut-openai","id":223546144,"node_id":"U_kgDODVMLIA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/223546144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/etraut-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"64bdeed9f7adbe60c725153b3fb74ed044a36221","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/64bdeed9f7adbe60c725153b3fb74ed044a36221","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/64bdeed9f7adbe60c725153b3fb74ed044a36221"}]},{"sha":"64bdeed9f7adbe60c725153b3fb74ed044a36221","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDY0YmRlZWQ5ZjdhZGJlNjBjNzI1MTUzYjNmYjc0ZWQwNDRhMzYyMjE","commit":{"author":{"name":"charlesgong-openai","email":"charlesgong@openai.com","date":"2026-06-19T19:47:53Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-19T19:47:53Z"},"message":"[codex] Preserve skill descriptions outside model context (#29006)\n\n## Why\n\nSkill descriptions are used in model-visible lists: the default\navailable-skills catalog that supports implicit selection, and the\non-demand `skills.list` tool response used to discover orchestrator\nskills. A single overlong description should not consume a\ndisproportionate share of either list.\n\nEnforcing the 1024-character limit while loading or migrating skills is\nthe wrong boundary: it rejects otherwise-valid skills and discards\nmetadata that non-model consumers and full skill reads may need. Skill\nmetadata and `SKILL.md` content should remain intact; the cap belongs at\nmodel-visible list rendering boundaries.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Preserve full `description` and `metadata.short-description` values\nwhen loading skills.\n- Preserve full external-agent command descriptions during\n`source-command-*` migration instead of skipping commands solely because\ntheir descriptions exceed 1024 characters.\n- Preserve full normalized orchestrator descriptions in the underlying\nskills catalog.\n- Cap each description at 1024 Unicode characters when rendering the\ndefault available-skills context in `codex-core-skills` and\n`codex-skills-extension`.\n- Apply the same cap when serializing descriptions in the model-visible\n`skills.list` response.\n- Render truncated descriptions as 1021 original characters plus `...`.\n- Leave explicit `$skill` injection, `skills.read`, underlying metadata,\nand on-disk `SKILL.md` files unchanged and full-fidelity.\n\n## Implicit skill selection\n\nCodex injects a bounded catalog containing each implicitly allowed\nskill's name, description, and source locator, together with\ninstructions to use a skill when the task clearly matches its\ndescription. The model makes that semantic choice; after selecting a\nskill, it reads the full `SKILL.md` from its filesystem or provider\nresource. Explicit `$skill` mentions remain a separate path that injects\nthe full skill instructions. For orchestrator skills, `skills.list`\nprovides bounded discovery metadata before `skills.read` returns the\nfull selected resource.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just test -p codex-core-skills`\n- `just test -p codex-skills-extension`\n- `just test -p codex-external-agent-migration`\n\nThe focused regressions verify that overlong metadata is preserved at\nload and migration boundaries while default available-skills rendering\nand `skills.list` output produce the 1021-character prefix plus `...`.","tree":{"sha":"53a0b16bef4b9f22f70fa5f425e0c4d852a4d72e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/53a0b16bef4b9f22f70fa5f425e0c4d852a4d72e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/64bdeed9f7adbe60c725153b3fb74ed044a36221","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNZzpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAeoMQAGNMrwm7KJRPXuEitMIYpRW9\nsefebiLfkq56B5SRdFrBJASFbPtet3RItlw1tEaHZ9DzYGLOf/e9FOzZr+udK3eg\nU5/99/v5yZfR9H+Q8xTAlqiCPPqvptHCQDOZ73Jzok1q/VFoRkyljA0Jfngc7aBU\n8bOFX6nX19SjAVLDzFTDhm6dV9szZBHy7BBKVSy++xGhDd47ONlAzGwe9VNkFQrQ\n1P7JAJfUF/aVNJaaT5wLwPIK9yiav8GGQeJsRmZJQ8mTH5IfV5tb1It/81gDcEU3\nPQmq1z5WY4vsKEvtWS+P2DgKeqL1OqpcLmdT4Iiq4Z/BPiH1izB5y91FKt72QK4D\nkvybC9IEFRun3a6cwFS77nApcOH8xd0yNJuXFlxSnde6LknRYclbX5s1ewzZVkBW\nxRrgC1xNylwdBTOGegS4dm3ZiYwP1hZBXCCu9UFv09iKrntZajjT8iXn2ZH7UzQI\niHG/TIlcecE8DCvTFsr42KHpFKW+BS8QXb5L2/q1iCdVe3vLJh9xlgzA9QXdD91W\ndQxBE1vuI7v1KUScMhJJGE5b8rDIuXumykdFW7Gj14/JMZ8QpyfLnLKs6XVYFhD6\nI+FaoogGBAop9iMxakj17x+QIFpFQ2xdTjYtB5iVrPq5mn9VqDlZacKIKChrGCg4\nnp7k+cbfHT1WwUfCnBJT\n=DWLm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 53a0b16bef4b9f22f70fa5f425e0c4d852a4d72e\nparent abd901770e17b26b41b7371ec93b56fdcab61d7d\nauthor charlesgong-openai <charlesgong@openai.com> 1781898473 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781898473 -0700\n\n[codex] Preserve skill descriptions outside model context (#29006)\n\n## Why\n\nSkill descriptions are used in model-visible lists: the default\navailable-skills catalog that supports implicit selection, and the\non-demand `skills.list` tool response used to discover orchestrator\nskills. A single overlong description should not consume a\ndisproportionate share of either list.\n\nEnforcing the 1024-character limit while loading or migrating skills is\nthe wrong boundary: it rejects otherwise-valid skills and discards\nmetadata that non-model consumers and full skill reads may need. Skill\nmetadata and `SKILL.md` content should remain intact; the cap belongs at\nmodel-visible list rendering boundaries.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Preserve full `description` and `metadata.short-description` values\nwhen loading skills.\n- Preserve full external-agent command descriptions during\n`source-command-*` migration instead of skipping commands solely because\ntheir descriptions exceed 1024 characters.\n- Preserve full normalized orchestrator descriptions in the underlying\nskills catalog.\n- Cap each description at 1024 Unicode characters when rendering the\ndefault available-skills context in `codex-core-skills` and\n`codex-skills-extension`.\n- Apply the same cap when serializing descriptions in the model-visible\n`skills.list` response.\n- Render truncated descriptions as 1021 original characters plus `...`.\n- Leave explicit `$skill` injection, `skills.read`, underlying metadata,\nand on-disk `SKILL.md` files unchanged and full-fidelity.\n\n## Implicit skill selection\n\nCodex injects a bounded catalog containing each implicitly allowed\nskill's name, description, and source locator, together with\ninstructions to use a skill when the task clearly matches its\ndescription. The model makes that semantic choice; after selecting a\nskill, it reads the full `SKILL.md` from its filesystem or provider\nresource. Explicit `$skill` mentions remain a separate path that injects\nthe full skill instructions. For orchestrator skills, `skills.list`\nprovides bounded discovery metadata before `skills.read` returns the\nfull selected resource.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just test -p codex-core-skills`\n- `just test -p codex-skills-extension`\n- `just test -p codex-external-agent-migration`\n\nThe focused regressions verify that overlong metadata is preserved at\nload and migration boundaries while default available-skills rendering\nand `skills.list` output produce the 1021-character prefix plus `...`.","verified_at":"2026-06-19T19:47:53Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/64bdeed9f7adbe60c725153b3fb74ed044a36221","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/64bdeed9f7adbe60c725153b3fb74ed044a36221","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/64bdeed9f7adbe60c725153b3fb74ed044a36221/comments","author":{"login":"charlesgong-openai","id":200841148,"node_id":"U_kgDOC_iXvA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/200841148?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/charlesgong-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"abd901770e17b26b41b7371ec93b56fdcab61d7d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/abd901770e17b26b41b7371ec93b56fdcab61d7d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/abd901770e17b26b41b7371ec93b56fdcab61d7d"}]},{"sha":"abd901770e17b26b41b7371ec93b56fdcab61d7d","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGFiZDkwMTc3MGUxN2IyNmI0MWI3MzcxZWM5M2I1NmZkY2FiNjFkN2Q","commit":{"author":{"name":"Anton Panasenko","email":"apanasenko@openai.com","date":"2026-06-19T19:02:12Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-19T19:02:12Z"},"message":"chore(deps): advance tokio-tungstenite (#29132)\n\n## Why\n\nResponses websocket connections use `tokio-tungstenite`. When DNS\nreturns an unusable native IPv6 address before a working IPv4 address,\nsequential dialing can consume Codex's outer websocket timeout before\nreaching IPv4. The merged fork change adds Happy Eyeballs-style\nalternate-family racing so websocket dialing matches the recovery\nbehavior already present in the HTTP path.\n\n## What Changed\n\nAdvance the workspace `tokio-tungstenite` patch from `132f5b39` to\nmerged commit `e5e64b86`, and update the matching lockfile source. The\nnew revision comes from\n[openai-oss-forks/tokio-tungstenite#1](https://github.com/openai-oss-forks/tokio-tungstenite/pull/1).","tree":{"sha":"a1bfd3abbe895275b0ee68b14ed976d341816a91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/a1bfd3abbe895275b0ee68b14ed976d341816a91"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/abd901770e17b26b41b7371ec93b56fdcab61d7d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNZI0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfn8QAKMAHRyZwaSvDvxMwEg94w14\ncfJFqIZI8MgZnareg3E1Xsx55UIsz3oHUVMtokaijtBjkceU1/8PaL0Cm6tY7Au1\npTAHM2ZVvdHp34B+ubmMmo5GPihECkSqVPpjRXd4p0jHFq+1QxboxjCWXTd1uC6o\nnyox/n/hCXiyI27lWHQMxEhDgskDeC/R6Vfq/ioWwQhZAOCb8R3gp8LU4DYjQP93\nk1Vvd8moBmXZ8B0WsKLMXuHPF2Tc06y5kEbSxaSrvCfGKK68h2nvhhIXOh7hmvH4\nlFFgyWY39sC7wZ96Qm/2jLEHA0doyZMi8EoGwRnGKaypVzMmlKAZz14C0EB4oVYj\nKPYycp9tFZdmGm7YZDkMA8j1GCREQwFfUrMh+xjPBzP04SnbLYJb/RxaL67fTk28\nqfKuhEEbHq2nFN0Wg0OwBTyJssOv9DIFCGXuC8ipClyXaeTQHdlIc7rglTVizH0C\n+FdKamolAHIL5n8hwuMPjbg9pvp+cBt+FtPHm9OTW+2Sgzg3Ikml5LHSzFDa1QPA\nfLLRoQMrYZ09Hj6wPCcGtLZ8jSqx4sz+ClNQyA8Ol2I8oZP5BxLdzuBZEx+sZHnc\ntrvAp/RRqKwIl+U7T5mp9DfbIzXkJcBXKgwBbL0UCopYCehfoZ8y8FboTr4vQ82v\n3pXqCWF3BmBl+0pAMxj8\n=z5qI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a1bfd3abbe895275b0ee68b14ed976d341816a91\nparent a57b268d61ca7d4d20819587b999d8a15635440b\nauthor Anton Panasenko <apanasenko@openai.com> 1781895732 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781895732 -0700\n\nchore(deps): advance tokio-tungstenite (#29132)\n\n## Why\n\nResponses websocket connections use `tokio-tungstenite`. When DNS\nreturns an unusable native IPv6 address before a working IPv4 address,\nsequential dialing can consume Codex's outer websocket timeout before\nreaching IPv4. The merged fork change adds Happy Eyeballs-style\nalternate-family racing so websocket dialing matches the recovery\nbehavior already present in the HTTP path.\n\n## What Changed\n\nAdvance the workspace `tokio-tungstenite` patch from `132f5b39` to\nmerged commit `e5e64b86`, and update the matching lockfile source. The\nnew revision comes from\n[openai-oss-forks/tokio-tungstenite#1](https://github.com/openai-oss-forks/tokio-tungstenite/pull/1).","verified_at":"2026-06-19T19:02:13Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/abd901770e17b26b41b7371ec93b56fdcab61d7d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/abd901770e17b26b41b7371ec93b56fdcab61d7d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/abd901770e17b26b41b7371ec93b56fdcab61d7d/comments","author":{"login":"apanasenko-oai","id":228802911,"node_id":"U_kgDODaNBXw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228802911?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai","html_url":"https://git