rl":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c83618ab2098525d343df2160d98b2449dca6d5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c83618ab2098525d343df2160d98b2449dca6d5d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c83618ab2098525d343df2160d98b2449dca6d5d"}]},{"sha":"c83618ab2098525d343df2160d98b2449dca6d5d","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGM4MzYxOGFiMjA5ODUyNWQzNDNkZjIxNjBkOThiMjQ0OWRjYTZkNWQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Winston Howes","email":"winston@openai.com","date":"2026-06-19T16:00:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-19T16:00:44Z"},"message":"Use cached and live web access terminology (#29095)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Rename the string-valued external web access enum variants from\n`Offline` / `Online` to `Cached` / `Live`.\n- Align the transport names with the existing `web_search = \"cached\"` /\n`\"live\"` configuration vocabulary.\n\nExisting behavior is unchanged: `WebSearchMode::Cached` and\n`WebSearchMode::Live` continue to send the backward-compatible boolean\nvalues `false` and `true`; `Indexed` remains the only mode currently\nsent as a string.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-api` (127 passed)","tree":{"sha":"2c44b0e38d4bf548a9d3633174b29c28b1e7d8ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/2c44b0e38d4bf548a9d3633174b29c28b1e7d8ea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/c83618ab2098525d343df2160d98b2449dca6d5d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNWesCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAn08QAEXPav7UM/09QsLTULoo9a71\nus+uO25gMy4KtD8eVxbeLi/Aw6rE2saWvyC9lY4d9zl84folbh0bitpLNmgChZ9z\nB8sdywKOJ2s5Z25BIu8d2C5cOKHHBNHylP4dEFfSYUdlXkydLmCn7iTaK36a+hy5\nX108BVSLrKj+N0Fpf6SYB27Vin7LWUW+5mjD9TFPhkInR0vzHotwWair1n/eaOFk\n74O3zCAOc83GhaJYKeieWz0P2DVLZr1n8hBQwV7p3RZbtSj3kMBOWDEE/E68T2e5\n+nO13r6QFXQcdvdw2ke3/68XphQ9V1dpignFigcZhM/QeI+kmpu32vj7sUNfOFq0\nmsuE4nAnZE7znL21lIue1ZEQxEQKx5dZ67+CJjzfjkx6GkZ1olx/T501N2h/Earg\n647kGtoqHJ4Iq4UnZikJHJyKaVS4mj4ROwpaNvsKRYpdOIvzjnirPvYemyqDWMQf\n6dbdUJiirkGmSjXn4mcOBO5pjOhICk0edhckwKNylOGqy4vjhwWjXk8oUrMA26MM\ni6gbsUpzJ2Pw7/QvMKfLNdpEFg4dIDE/+XEmubm4GZfF/y4qcHcQnLf5+kc/hvmG\nfeBbvxsyZn7LpEZ4Y+SP/z59gBGtkDqYT1UskgJJFls+IGcO4lZ5vIEAkocX0C97\nIQa1+ImWmci5rYXVAWSm\n=0zxi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2c44b0e38d4bf548a9d3633174b29c28b1e7d8ea\nparent 04483f4ce5694d471e471583d4ca286908d7c8b7\nauthor Winston Howes <winston@openai.com> 1781884844 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781884844 -0700\n\nUse cached and live web access terminology (#29095)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Rename the string-valued external web access enum variants from\n`Offline` / `Online` to `Cached` / `Live`.\n- Align the transport names with the existing `web_search = \"cached\"` /\n`\"live\"` configuration vocabulary.\n\nExisting behavior is unchanged: `WebSearchMode::Cached` and\n`WebSearchMode::Live` continue to send the backward-compatible boolean\nvalues `false` and `true`; `Indexed` remains the only mode currently\nsent as a string.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-api` (127 passed)","verified_at":"2026-06-19T16:00:45Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c83618ab2098525d343df2160d98b2449dca6d5d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c83618ab2098525d343df2160d98b2449dca6d5d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c83618ab2098525d343df2160d98b2449dca6d5d/comments","author":{"login":"winston-openai","id":177672674,"node_id":"U_kgDOCpcR4g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177672674?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/winston-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"04483f4ce5694d471e471583d4ca286908d7c8b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/04483f4ce5694d471e471583d4ca286908d7c8b7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/04483f4ce5694d471e471583d4ca286908d7c8b7"}]},{"sha":"04483f4ce5694d471e471583d4ca286908d7c8b7","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDA0NDgzZjRjZTU2OTRkNDcxZTQ3MTU4M2Q0Y2EyODY5MDhkN2M4Yjc","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-19T15:05:51Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-19T15:05:51Z"},"message":"Keep remote exec commands native to the executor (#29099)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Remote unified-exec now sends the original command argv to exec-server\ninstead of materializing the orchestrator's sandbox wrapper first.\n- Local unified-exec keeps the existing sandbox path unchanged.\n- Add a focused regression test for a macOS-selected sandbox producing\nplain remote argv.\n\nBefore:\n\n    macOS orchestrator -> /usr/bin/sandbox-exec ... -> Linux exec-server\n\nAfter:\n\n    macOS orchestrator -> /bin/bash -lc pwd -> Linux exec-server\n\nThis is intentionally only the first cleanup step. Remote unified-exec\ncommands are sent without a process sandbox until the targeted\nfollow-ups below land. For the macOS-to-Linux path this is not a\npractical regression: the old sandboxed attempt failed before process\nlaunch because the Linux executor could not spawn macOS sandbox paths.\n\n## Targeted follow-ups\n\n1. Carry sandbox intent separately from argv.\n   - Add an optional sandbox field to exec-server process params.\n- Reuse FileSystemSandboxContext rather than introducing a new sandbox\nmodel.\n   - Carry managed-network enforcement as one explicit bit.\n   - Keep argv plain.\n\n2. Apply that intent inside exec-server.\n   - Add a small process-start adapter before LocalProcess::exec.\n- Reuse the existing codex-sandboxing SandboxManager and exec-server\nruntime paths.\n- Follow the same shape already used by exec-server filesystem\nsandboxing.\n   - Do not duplicate or move the sandbox implementations.\n\n3. Report the sandbox actually used.\n   - Return the executor-selected sandbox type from process/start.\n- Use that value in core for sandbox-denial detection and retry\nbehavior.\n\n## End state\n\nThe orchestrator sends plain commands plus portable sandbox intent. The\nexecutor chooses and applies its own native sandbox: Linux executors use\nLinux sandboxing, macOS executors use Seatbelt, and Windows executors\nuse Windows sandboxing. Concrete wrapper argv, helper paths, and sandbox\nenv markers never cross the executor boundary.","tree":{"sha":"98ee331d0efb7b5d880eb0af5bfc4f426f6cf070","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/98ee331d0efb7b5d880eb0af5bfc4f426f6cf070"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/04483f4ce5694d471e471583d4ca286908d7c8b7","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNVrPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQ0IQAKapVNTd/Eb31MS/J0ZcM8Eb\nDiwq2lXYOCUsLrJoEQgJvMQXMeQhW5k5FeL2Sg3cDUEBn4F9bzKG2VJwGYae9yog\nGh3mw4vS0ZK0U1tJ3bMYJCWrntn/pm8hDlm7cRw1kBR64aiQSlXUrFwi3R4rpxya\nuefjhh7lmH/znvS2mII91TcqoYKpk0GSN/HHTg2TVyJHQxSHsTDAP9fNWQbGCBSF\nvCDCEFFxnYoF4PQ7mgQv6BdVfJxnG/c6TArhypUpkLkJpEyW3cxtDI4uK6hRu4h8\ncXvnOf9S33y4D6W8+mQgUTAvgW4Wcdh6IYclwytQAg343NYZKerokQqPbhoEihX4\nexxBMI/5nkylRajTCLHaRN2KIVn3zbMNoWx4X3cJg0oXtN6Iw8l6TeVRwp2Xdvbi\n8z0Q8lE6FJuRhwExo050W4w0sXv+Q7oM8dxd+jnFX0tpBG8HpbTuZ6CLUUL8Baws\nekUdEmCNn/lKkUj03KUHoylFBM3YcqDAHS3AoF3kAsFzXgEGqsW4b5TJWsqwOjtI\n7yUmveYgdbZGai2CH3uJUoZh8xmrzNRXogBteUIgyD81N+KqSPMYAVV92da5aNNs\nWUz7l/kUX6qdX5R+6c5+CRNaenAL+jyS4X93kqhox6Kxtlu4ALqngyuw4dsVaNQ5\n3yaGOwoU0K/nbQboZQ7j\n=W+d8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 98ee331d0efb7b5d880eb0af5bfc4f426f6cf070\nparent 81b000421dc795062019f3737db6fac3fda16aa4\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1781881551 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781881551 +0200\n\nKeep remote exec commands native to the executor (#29099)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Remote unified-exec now sends the original command argv to exec-server\ninstead of materializing the orchestrator's sandbox wrapper first.\n- Local unified-exec keeps the existing sandbox path unchanged.\n- Add a focused regression test for a macOS-selected sandbox producing\nplain remote argv.\n\nBefore:\n\n    macOS orchestrator -> /usr/bin/sandbox-exec ... -> Linux exec-server\n\nAfter:\n\n    macOS orchestrator -> /bin/bash -lc pwd -> Linux exec-server\n\nThis is intentionally only the first cleanup step. Remote unified-exec\ncommands are sent without a process sandbox until the targeted\nfollow-ups below land. For the macOS-to-Linux path this is not a\npractical regression: the old sandboxed attempt failed before process\nlaunch because the Linux executor could not spawn macOS sandbox paths.\n\n## Targeted follow-ups\n\n1. Carry sandbox intent separately from argv.\n   - Add an optional sandbox field to exec-server process params.\n- Reuse FileSystemSandboxContext rather than introducing a new sandbox\nmodel.\n   - Carry managed-network enforcement as one explicit bit.\n   - Keep argv plain.\n\n2. Apply that intent inside exec-server.\n   - Add a small process-start adapter before LocalProcess::exec.\n- Reuse the existing codex-sandboxing SandboxManager and exec-server\nruntime paths.\n- Follow the same shape already used by exec-server filesystem\nsandboxing.\n   - Do not duplicate or move the sandbox implementations.\n\n3. Report the sandbox actually used.\n   - Return the executor-selected sandbox type from process/start.\n- Use that value in core for sandbox-denial detection and retry\nbehavior.\n\n## End state\n\nThe orchestrator sends plain commands plus portable sandbox intent. The\nexecutor chooses and applies its own native sandbox: Linux executors use\nLinux sandboxing, macOS executors use Seatbelt, and Windows executors\nuse Windows sandboxing. Concrete wrapper argv, helper paths, and sandbox\nenv markers never cross the executor boundary.","verified_at":"2026-06-19T15:05:52Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/04483f4ce5694d471e471583d4ca286908d7c8b7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/04483f4ce5694d471e471583d4ca286908d7c8b7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/04483f4ce5694d471e471583d4ca286908d7c8b7/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"81b000421dc795062019f3737db6fac3fda16aa4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/81b000421dc795062019f3737db6fac3fda16aa4","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/81b000421dc795062019f3737db6fac3fda16aa4"}]},{"sha":"81b000421dc795062019f3737db6fac3fda16aa4","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDgxYjAwMDQyMWRjNzk1MDYyMDE5ZjM3MzdkYjZmYWMzZmRhMTZhYTQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-19T12:42:26Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-19T12:42:26Z"},"message":"Add config toggles for orchestrator skills and MCP (#28942)\n\n## Why\n\nOrchestrator-provided skills and Codex Apps MCP tools add model-visible\ninstructions, resources, and tools beyond the local workspace. Hosts\nneed config-level switches to disable those orchestrator-owned surfaces\nindependently, without disabling regular skills or regular MCP servers.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Adds `[orchestrator.skills].enabled` and `[orchestrator.mcp].enabled`\nconfig entries, both defaulting to `true`.\n- Includes the new settings in `config.schema.json` and in the config\nlock so resolved thread configuration preserves the same orchestrator\nexposure decisions.\n- Threads `orchestrator.skills.enabled` through the app-server skills\nextension so disabled orchestrator skills do not expose the `skills`\nnamespace or inject orchestrator skill context.\n- Gates Codex Apps MCP exposure, app instructions, and app auth\neligibility on `orchestrator.mcp.enabled` while leaving non-Codex-Apps\nMCP tools available.\n- Updates the thread-manager sample config to disable both\norchestrator-owned surfaces.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Added config parsing, loading, defaulting, and schema coverage for the\nnew settings.\n- Added MCP exposure coverage that `orchestrator.mcp.enabled = false`\nremoves Codex Apps tools while preserving regular MCP tools.\n- Added app-server coverage that `orchestrator.skills.enabled = false`\nprevents orchestrator skill tools, prompts, and resource reads from\nreaching the model turn.","tree":{"sha":"b1395f5488dc9808469e4311acb31c4afa9e798c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/b1395f5488dc9808469e4311acb31c4afa9e798c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/81b000421dc795062019f3737db6fac3fda16aa4","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNTkyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4JMQAKwFJ8/UCNrKCxDAF4aWaIYG\nU7GVhQ+vrUpV0br5UM466g48R8jeWJcM9ZksG3P+1sLoyAw5HmuYdmvZVodCarBY\nsyCFLwFtnGpgJLMlKDCW1CWuehbywdx2EgdDcRwMKPABBst5e2qG836I0fq/qr3o\nrpa6EjidUix2t0uD/W+aQvu8mcvKdwYs1022S/4BJ2+QBUuccpl3K1hX0TlEQJJ7\nsfHmP8hRG15lFhOOY0LX+0BRLW8V2GbUYDHCo8DGeRVLznUl3v3unXur2sZ7WaIv\nV+5EK7S2nboQn9ZYosrVcWaDt9gzDCnbGYIVMxJm2f9xm3qIP/ddGcIr8hx9/GYC\nlORCYGB3me1OCLDROKSAdbN5n3TQ0G3hwPlzRretZam8C5oXpAbl0cMV0HpZKJWt\ncXm5aZrYshtOUEnGweIvk/LgDwgfmEOGWkWdu4HhfwzcrvA53sxtCakRLmcSKLu/\nLdOasc552lM9ahkSrlZjVcd7HbOJbtInEHbKkb1yAWKuzBmCcQcnbFUWyOVYgEOc\njIDQuevP40Pwc6tKtUvchvgCmjdPKzZrtU69qBa0APYJQzLnW5D+qnY6WG9sIlUJ\nIOArl7vEmTwlEYGyoz1aCnnv75/9vDb6QxaEPZWJ+ZwNJ0f2EBvHKFuoPFfLu3Pv\nQzxQO4bDmYFO4FP9TgEb\n=IF5/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b1395f5488dc9808469e4311acb31c4afa9e798c\nparent 3a2712ea141a5acb243689f803f26e48ff751771\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1781872946 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781872946 +0200\n\nAdd config toggles for orchestrator skills and MCP (#28942)\n\n## Why\n\nOrchestrator-provided skills and Codex Apps MCP tools add model-visible\ninstructions, resources, and tools beyond the local workspace. Hosts\nneed config-level switches to disable those orchestrator-owned surfaces\nindependently, without disabling regular skills or regular MCP servers.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Adds `[orchestrator.skills].enabled` and `[orchestrator.mcp].enabled`\nconfig entries, both defaulting to `true`.\n- Includes the new settings in `config.schema.json` and in the config\nlock so resolved thread configuration preserves the same orchestrator\nexposure decisions.\n- Threads `orchestrator.skills.enabled` through the app-server skills\nextension so disabled orchestrator skills do not expose the `skills`\nnamespace or inject orchestrator skill context.\n- Gates Codex Apps MCP exposure, app instructions, and app auth\neligibility on `orchestrator.mcp.enabled` while leaving non-Codex-Apps\nMCP tools available.\n- Updates the thread-manager sample config to disable both\norchestrator-owned surfaces.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Added config parsing, loading, defaulting, and schema coverage for the\nnew settings.\n- Added MCP exposure coverage that `orchestrator.mcp.enabled = false`\nremoves Codex Apps tools while preserving regular MCP tools.\n- Added app-server coverage that `orchestrator.skills.enabled = false`\nprevents orchestrator skill tools, prompts, and resource reads from\nreaching the model turn.","verified_at":"2026-06-19T12:42:27Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/81b000421dc795062019f3737db6fac3fda16aa4","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/81b000421dc795062019f3737db6fac3fda16aa4","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/81b000421dc795062019f3737db6fac3fda16aa4/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3a2712ea141a5acb243689f803f26e48ff751771","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3a2712ea141a5acb243689f803f26e48ff751771","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3a2712ea141a5acb243689f803f26e48ff751771"}]},{"sha":"3a2712ea141a5acb243689f803f26e48ff751771","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDNhMjcxMmVhMTQxYTVhY2IyNDM2ODlmODAzZjI2ZTQ4ZmY3NTE3NzE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Winston Howes","email":"winston@openai.com","date":"2026-06-19T12:35:57Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-19T12:35:57Z"},"message":"Add indexed web search mode (#28489)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Add `web_search = \"indexed\"` alongside `disabled`, `cached`, and\n`live`.\n- Use that same resolved mode for both hosted and standalone web search.\n- For hosted search, send `index_gated_web_access: true` with external\nweb access enabled only when `indexed` is selected.\n- For standalone search, preserve the existing boolean wire values for\nexisting modes (`cached` maps to `false` and `live` to `true`) and send\n`\"indexed\"` only for `indexed`; `disabled` keeps the tool unavailable.\n- Carry the mode through managed configuration requirements and\ngenerated schemas.\n\n## Why\n\nIndexed search provides a middle ground between cached-only search and\nunrestricted live page fetching. Search queries can remain live while\ndirect page fetches are limited to URLs admitted by the server.\n\nThe existing `web_search` setting remains the single source of truth, so\nhosted and standalone executors cannot drift into different access\nmodes. Without an explicit `indexed` selection, the existing\nmodel-visible tool and request shapes are unchanged.\n\n```toml\nweb_search = \"indexed\"\n\n[features]\nstandalone_web_search = true\n```\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-api` (`126 passed`)\n- `just test -p codex-web-search-extension` (`7 passed`)\n- `just test -p codex-core\ncode_mode_can_call_indexed_standalone_web_search` (`1 passed`)\n- Focused configuration, hosted request, standalone request, and\nmanaged-requirement coverage is included in the PR; remaining suites run\nin CI.\n\nThe full workspace test suite was not run locally.","tree":{"sha":"d4a5e4de120f2e7e00c26d2c33ce7d09bc9c5ded","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/d4a5e4de120f2e7e00c26d2c33ce7d09bc9c5ded"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/3a2712ea141a5acb243689f803f26e48ff751771","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNTetCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnagQAKwwCGGJeIK20hEZf4SuWiUF\nfuYaaWOdE6zSRMk9wYqhtJLHWKBY05ScTPKfum6m1TiIi2JsE2kGvChJBtiwpuFH\n6xRhKWt2w0872SewK6iSi5CXsiWDYMwyymUwxgiDcmc2XApf8ootK4CsofsQifnr\n60U/1/e6gucCDhmRHn378KrdxRjfhNFaz1T8gbv626kd9vhXBSzUQc3EDjYyYn/D\nr3m+VhmSEPfG1JjJiLyizKVTR9bs/cH+nDvbqhghBsx9ee1YUG/cbgYy+teJBx/h\nrKObHpHPzLL4Q4lA1WL0I2rSVOFdqaSkeopuFQQbFJb8qYqkWyMWWP4JRbH0ESJu\nk1G0AZZ6UQb00Aqzz+vNtww/HrnnyTFqgVdXubpAli/AHpgNs2ItYiJ59rWzSkYd\nYqUkL8bJN/bnz+L6p0IwQW7H+JISUupE19lpoLay/RkFeXejjfLdYbwuqDbf27RD\nhbIJYJHFnZNLNTLaIHf6Nh+tKTbJLgfNpgC9vmoX84B72jLGqh1GfLyKlwXxftCQ\nKGuNyh1tGd80iPQQUG6hEzLGeFzJAVQkpT7waj3MSjiHPpmAgM0KwmihZ9/kC4uu\nz0CIjrJM4vhJkHtIgOL5EHoORjFH0mUhp1Smx/kEFxCCVRlhwrqSKCDzYWWb6ycu\neulT69eFU4KR9GLa5QV7\n=hHIY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d4a5e4de120f2e7e00c26d2c33ce7d09bc9c5ded\nparent 7951397e4af9b52bac46a6cac90f1047c31b31a2\nauthor Winston Howes <winston@openai.com> 1781872557 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781872557 -0700\n\nAdd indexed web search mode (#28489)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Add `web_search = \"indexed\"` alongside `disabled`, `cached`, and\n`live`.\n- Use that same resolved mode for both hosted and standalone web search.\n- For hosted search, send `index_gated_web_access: true` with external\nweb access enabled only when `indexed` is selected.\n- For standalone search, preserve the existing boolean wire values for\nexisting modes (`cached` maps to `false` and `live` to `true`) and send\n`\"indexed\"` only for `indexed`; `disabled` keeps the tool unavailable.\n- Carry the mode through managed configuration requirements and\ngenerated schemas.\n\n## Why\n\nIndexed search provides a middle ground between cached-only search and\nunrestricted live page fetching. Search queries can remain live while\ndirect page fetches are limited to URLs admitted by the server.\n\nThe existing `web_search` setting remains the single source of truth, so\nhosted and standalone executors cannot drift into different access\nmodes. Without an explicit `indexed` selection, the existing\nmodel-visible tool and request shapes are unchanged.\n\n```toml\nweb_search = \"indexed\"\n\n[features]\nstandalone_web_search = true\n```\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-api` (`126 passed`)\n- `just test -p codex-web-search-extension` (`7 passed`)\n- `just test -p codex-core\ncode_mode_can_call_indexed_standalone_web_search` (`1 passed`)\n- Focused configuration, hosted request, standalone request, and\nmanaged-requirement coverage is included in the PR; remaining suites run\nin CI.\n\nThe full workspace test suite was not run locally.","verified_at":"2026-06-19T12:35:58Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3a2712ea141a5acb243689f803f26e48ff751771","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3a2712ea141a5acb243689f803f26e48ff751771","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3a2712ea141a5acb243689f803f26e48ff751771/comments","author":{"login":"winston-openai","id":177672674,"node_id":"U_kgDOCpcR4g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177672674?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/winston-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7951397e4af9b52bac46a6cac90f1047c31b31a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7951397e4af9b52bac46a6cac90f1047c31b31a2","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/7951397e4af9b52bac46a6cac90f1047c31b31a2"}]},{"sha":"7951397e4af9b52bac46a6cac90f1047c31b31a2","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDc5NTEzOTdlNGFmOWI1MmJhYzQ2YTZjYWM5MGYxMDQ3YzMxYjMxYTI","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-19T12:08:31Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-19T12:08:31Z"},"message":"Document raw response item compatibility (#29086)\n\nAdds a short AGENTS.md note asking reviewers to treat raw response item\nevents as compatibility-sensitive, even while they are experimental.\n\nThis keeps future app-server changes from accidentally breaking Codex\nCloud consumers of raw response item events.","tree":{"sha":"3ec830b39eca66716fb3917f16ea0f58f7a99a26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/3ec830b39eca66716fb3917f16ea0f58f7a99a26"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/7951397e4af9b52bac46a6cac90f1047c31b31a2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNTE/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFykQAJjozb+1/o1e3ePN5ai4V59X\nweHSImEUzHpPFLlWHn5egqeHHP0oXc6K1qlJ0cj5I0XvCO6RwjVt0EaemV5o7L4f\nLD47THDrP3r3RoUoK9Vy7ZW6O1mY01fZoXUQK5TNxEEypbh7qvdjh3d1hsWd/hB0\nW720USvZNJxdRiJE22gtEzHnmqJ0Gp3jIqW414QTUUulBpPCWNFvib33aCzuIj+/\nw97GUrIBpjh2wH5mEQoEJPJ9+ozAL3NdkP7tM0//CUgIvu7MN/CbS94oGVi7azZG\noQpBiHB42rDJOQY+x06SbRkmH5FFEUFS9LmsYbhDHDg+D0T8f5ID43xrkNO13h/X\nM6OLBBsAYSkVZvGO+fhyfZoQU/hp4DwE2LP4h0hYULc7D1cEBsRKrYh+p0mL+Nt7\nLbvHgFVAa/GtVH+yeqW93Z4xogi/UB0BRgtkOUb0JRWF6pVqo96Q6D5AvkQISebq\nK1lBOIVM+Anqf+kU5/OXz/rHiYf9WZhDfklUvLvmrDs9Akm0BFIucIcI31Zs4czH\nf3Su59WW2GjPct/sU3YM8mBUqKvGhLyOGq0GUrgAGumdUAzZBdhbuz0S/bNuQ2LJ\nRsuMeoeyiwpTwYE6Xj16eX3cssiXDChCUWyKTfjsE4+8l7kyvclloxXmyZRcKzXy\nF7XcW/r/rXHNkbyfuQ0h\n=XEl5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3ec830b39eca66716fb3917f16ea0f58f7a99a26\nparent bd5d31b250af454080c4b1baa89adbf2597f16b4\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1781870911 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781870911 +0200\n\nDocument raw response item compatibility (#29086)\n\nAdds a short AGENTS.md note asking reviewers to treat raw response item\nevents as compatibility-sensitive, even while they are experimental.\n\nThis keeps future app-server changes from accidentally breaking Codex\nCloud consumers of raw response item events.","verified_at":"2026-06-19T12:08:31Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7951397e4af9b52bac46a6cac90f1047c31b31a2","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/7951397e4af9b52bac46a6cac90f1047c31b31a2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7951397e4af9b52bac46a6cac90f1047c31b31a2/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"bd5d31b250af454080c4b1baa89adbf2597f16b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bd5d31b250af454080c4b1baa89adbf2597f16b4","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/bd5d31b250af454080c4b1baa89adbf2597f16b4"}]},{"sha":"bd5d31b250af454080c4b1baa89adbf2597f16b4","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGJkNWQzMWIyNTBhZjQ1NDA4MGM0YjFiYWE4OWFkYmYyNTk3ZjE2YjQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-19T11:49:45Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-19T11:49:45Z"},"message":"Scope network approvals by environment (#28899)\n\nStacked on #28766.\n\n## Why\n\nNetwork approvals are environment-scoped: allowing a host in one\nexecution environment should not allow the same host in another\nenvironment.\n\n#28766 adds the inert IDs and constructor plumbing. This PR applies the\nbehavior on top.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Route managed network traffic through per-environment HTTP and SOCKS\nproxy listeners.\n- Stamp HTTP, HTTPS CONNECT, SOCKS TCP, and SOCKS UDP policy requests\nwith the source environment at the proxy boundary.\n- Carry the selected execution environment through shell, unified exec,\nzsh-fork, and sandbox transform paths.\n- Include the environment in pending, approved-for-session, and\ndenied-for-session network approval cache keys.\n- Include the environment in approval IDs and approval prompts.\n- Preserve legacy fallback for unattributed requests, but deny when\nactive-call attribution is ambiguous.\n- Fail closed if an environment-specific proxy endpoint cannot be\nprepared.\n\n## Validation\n\n- just fmt\n- CI will run tests and clippy","tree":{"sha":"3e53326058e28e85bde0c97fe11e65362e8ba9b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/3e53326058e28e85bde0c97fe11e65362e8ba9b4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/bd5d31b250af454080c4b1baa89adbf2597f16b4","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNSzZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyBwQAK//5vuN3onHbQZWmr5fQgOp\nwzvw+peRtTOl4av1oPqfyh/HyO41VPyh71ekgs9Gck73/PlwtTyjji/XEkEbXkrp\nAl8LEexlEUTvOZc1DQix5I51gNXyDY0mRKaPyH6EdwwSLnpgkSGuKqhuXhM+rPeL\n4mokwFqgm/lyryBazZ/jw5vPnFKlPSZcx6MmGRrbfEKlQylEAkfs6Go4dsmCaWyW\nk/LKWbfcU+Z8Yjcd5jXKRuC542vHzKF4UpkrCCZse9eyWRZ5px8X/WIGs6PmZM8e\nssbmly8k/edMDARcrJtiGzfF8wiCLmakh1SlS4Cvi77HBI/nQdEdlYQjqG0H3b2d\nvZMo51wGNyqAt+uUZrJr5b+5Yj/xnDcZQfe8ZU+IvE2Rqgs69geppjD0BtfbneGq\n3ktzXTJbcQ48c6yqpLVtoYZvjJkfFwUDpoGdTrdEekNz9Ldz+IBz67/GMRhdhJOh\ndFUf0B0pY678ddr34NL69vlxPZ9zsUOv9JIf/Oftf/1PbaygqTwUxPeB7JcR3daj\nyRP6gEAGxV++RT3oRl0WHcmZkfeqP9c4uGIx6KVRbg8qbAJuUYwwbqbssb3N2pfj\n1/W6alOzfh5hQvlPXgIVyC80Tad/X4t/Wtyjig5W0Lwrqg98C6Y4X1NNf6+nj/M+\nTdTlvPnCGBBrZRWISkOq\n=Dr2R\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3e53326058e28e85bde0c97fe11e65362e8ba9b4\nparent dac588f41398e8b628d71838d5745dad430477f1\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1781869785 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781869785 +0200\n\nScope network approvals by environment (#28899)\n\nStacked on #28766.\n\n## Why\n\nNetwork approvals are environment-scoped: allowing a host in one\nexecution environment should not allow the same host in another\nenvironment.\n\n#28766 adds the inert IDs and constructor plumbing. This PR applies the\nbehavior on top.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Route managed network traffic through per-environment HTTP and SOCKS\nproxy listeners.\n- Stamp HTTP, HTTPS CONNECT, SOCKS TCP, and SOCKS UDP policy requests\nwith the source environment at the proxy boundary.\n- Carry the selected execution environment through shell, unified exec,\nzsh-fork, and sandbox transform paths.\n- Include the environment in pending, approved-for-session, and\ndenied-for-session network approval cache keys.\n- Include the environment in approval IDs and approval prompts.\n- Preserve legacy fallback for unattributed requests, but deny when\nactive-call attribution is ambiguous.\n- Fail closed if an environment-specific proxy endpoint cannot be\nprepared.\n\n## Validation\n\n- just fmt\n- CI will run tests and clippy","verified_at":"2026-06-19T11:49:46Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bd5d31b250af454080c4b1baa89adbf2597f16b4","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/bd5d31b250af454080c4b1baa89adbf2597f16b4","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bd5d31b250af454080c4b1baa89adbf2597f16b4/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"dac588f41398e8b628d71838d5745dad430477f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/dac588f41398e8b628d71838d5745dad430477f1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/dac588f41398e8b628d71838d5745dad430477f1"}]},{"sha":"dac588f41398e8b628d71838d5745dad430477f1","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGRhYzU4OGY0MTM5OGU4YjYyOGQ3MTgzOGQ1NzQ1ZGFkNDMwNDc3ZjE","commit":{"author":{"name":"rka-oai","email":"rka@openai.com","date":"2026-06-19T09:00:01Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-19T09:00:01Z"},"message":"[codex] abort turns when rollout budgets expire (token budget 3/3) (#28707)\n\n## Stack\n\nDepends on #28494.\n\n## Description\n\nThis PR propagates shared rollout-budget exhaustion through the existing\n`CodexErr::TurnAborted` task result.\n\nEach thread records its model usage against the same ledger. Once the\nledger is exhausted, that usage update and all later usage updates\nreturn `TurnAborted`. The task wrapper emits the normal aborted-turn\nevent and lifecycle instead of completing the turn.\n\nThis is intentionally a soft boundary: there is no cross-thread\n`Op::Interrupt` fanout. An in-flight thread can finish its current\nresponse before it observes the exhausted ledger, but every thread\naborts at its next usage-accounting boundary.\n\n## Tests\n\nThe integration coverage verifies that:\n\n- the response that exhausts the budget aborts its turn;\n- a later response also aborts because the shared ledger remains\nexhausted; and\n- sub-agent usage draws from the same shared ledger; and\n- local and remote-v2 compaction abort without retrying or emitting a\ngeneric error.\n\nLocal checks:\n\n- `just test -p codex-core\nexhausted_budget_aborts_current_and_later_turns`\n- `just test -p codex-core subagent_usage_draws_from_the_shared_budget`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nabort_regular_task_emits_marker_before_turn_aborted`\n- `just test -p codex-core\ncompaction_budget_exhaustion_aborts_without_error_or_retry`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n- `just fmt`\n- `git diff --check`\n\nThe full workspace test suite was not run locally.","tree":{"sha":"c717eea41441b7b86bb3ee2e3cb39676b6a96b9c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/c717eea41441b7b86bb3ee2e3cb39676b6a96b9c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/dac588f41398e8b628d71838d5745dad430477f1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNQURCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXowQABxTGCuExGthhgbVZiAYUq/g\n+SOH04EvfUlgzI3jk/xswxrzfFRk5QRXjznEkHPfGgCNFDatOy0lTbXV02Rh8+lU\n5LYeQX61kPLXm8/vtGr53auHmTHuQBn9Fkt4JLsyMr/SBKN1/ex6clGxHdLfTwOh\nVbNgPZSbSUAt/KTAE+ijlh+ese77f6TnoNXrl6ghYnk2IT+OLfSjZE9fz6VfsNGh\nGvDgRDnnRs0W0in6AUJprMPX4Too3IfLG+I4Avx3tZinRAR4GQlNVLiZGtVTfgxM\nk8s838Jof0gc3B9X/Njyr0g9WpbtC50LThxfBrptyecLMZNgqGGIVKyWqUkVixcp\ngOnHekHZB0mQ8Dt+bk4DNlcaAapuu7KWJKkf4khC7NSzxttVm5BmnshTd+x0It9r\nAsyoyVoy8atej5/CkQAMRNSO2Eud0D/fsFYjHVwqP2rpm88Om+SW2FvEmp7LX6aJ\nsPeDeYEusnAB9RjnHJbiY+pxxxuEf51Zrnf84zB4FgbjKGcPs9IDCgseErZP/s3t\nPrZSBXWQUvKRwFPMluxaqRSueE7Mc4fImu0eRHzOjw3BujHTw8BxPYOFEe0OPhju\nBgGt9ikuRjOS00RYQbrQlLqh2BfmrT3Q5NVBFW0voh3l2vHZXo85C5cs09WCX2JN\npnTa+/QRxlod8/vpPRAH\n=Rw+y\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c717eea41441b7b86bb3ee2e3cb39676b6a96b9c\nparent 7abfcf220bbb57029e2ff5d9914124aef7ef3d0f\nauthor rka-oai <rka@openai.com> 1781859601 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781859601 -0700\n\n[codex] abort turns when rollout budgets expire (token budget 3/3) (#28707)\n\n## Stack\n\nDepends on #28494.\n\n## Description\n\nThis PR propagates shared rollout-budget exhaustion through the existing\n`CodexErr::TurnAborted` task result.\n\nEach thread records its model usage against the same ledger. Once the\nledger is exhausted, that usage update and all later usage updates\nreturn `TurnAborted`. The task wrapper emits the normal aborted-turn\nevent and lifecycle instead of completing the turn.\n\nThis is intentionally a soft boundary: there is no cross-thread\n`Op::Interrupt` fanout. An in-flight thread can finish its current\nresponse before it observes the exhausted ledger, but every thread\naborts at its next usage-accounting boundary.\n\n## Tests\n\nThe integration coverage verifies that:\n\n- the response that exhausts the budget aborts its turn;\n- a later response also aborts because the shared ledger remains\nexhausted; and\n- sub-agent usage draws from the same shared ledger; and\n- local and remote-v2 compaction abort without retrying or emitting a\ngeneric error.\n\nLocal checks:\n\n- `just test -p codex-core\nexhausted_budget_aborts_current_and_later_turns`\n- `just test -p codex-core subagent_usage_draws_from_the_shared_budget`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nabort_regular_task_emits_marker_before_turn_aborted`\n- `just test -p codex-core\ncompaction_budget_exhaustion_aborts_without_error_or_retry`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n- `just fmt`\n- `git diff --check`\n\nThe full workspace test suite was not run locally.","verified_at":"2026-06-19T09:00:02Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/dac588f41398e8b628d71838d5745dad430477f1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/dac588f41398e8b628d71838d5745dad430477f1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/dac588f41398e8b628d71838d5745dad430477f1/comments","author":{"login":"rka-oai","id":240799229,"node_id":"U_kgDODlpN_Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/240799229?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/rka-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7abfcf220bbb57029e2ff5d9914124aef7ef3d0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7abfcf220bbb57029e2ff5d9914124aef7ef3d0f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/7abfcf220bbb57029e2ff5d9914124aef7ef3d0f"}]},{"sha":"7abfcf220bbb57029e2ff5d9914124aef7ef3d0f","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDdhYmZjZjIyMGJiYjU3MDI5ZTJmZjVkOTkxNDEyNGFlZjdlZjNkMGY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Shijie Rao","email":"shijie.rao@openai.com","date":"2026-06-19T08:50:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-19T08:50:44Z"},"message":"Expose thread-level multi-agent mode (#28792)\n\n## Why\n\nOnce multi-agent mode can be selected per turn, clients also need to\nchoose the initial selection when creating a thread and observe that\nselection through lifecycle and settings APIs.\n\nThe selected value is intentionally distinct from the effective\nmodel-visible value: no client selection is represented as `null`, even\nthough an eligible multi-agent v2 turn derives `explicitRequestOnly` as\nits effective default.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add the optional experimental `thread/start.multiAgentMode` parameter\nand pass it through thread creation.\n- Preserve an omitted initial value as an unset selection rather than\neagerly storing `explicitRequestOnly`.\n- Apply an explicit `thread/start` selection to the first turn through\nthe session configuration established at thread creation.\n- Restore the latest persisted effective mode as the selected baseline\non cold resume when rollout history contains one.\n- Inherit the optional selected mode from a loaded parent when creating\nrelated runtime threads.\n- Return the current selected `multiAgentMode` from `thread/start`,\n`thread/resume`, `thread/fork`, and thread settings, using `null` when\nno mode is selected.\n- Keep lifecycle reporting independent from model capability and feature\neligibility; core turn construction remains responsible for calculating\nand persisting the effective mode.\n\n## Not covered\n\n- Clearing an existing loaded-session selection back to unset through\n`turn/start`; omitted or `null` currently retains the session's\nselection.\n- A TUI control, slash command, or `config.toml` preference.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 just test -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 just test -p codex-app-server multi_agent_mode`\n\nThe focused app-server coverage verifies explicit `thread/start`\ninitialization, first-turn prompting, nullable reporting for an omitted\nselection, and retention of selections that are not currently\nruntime-eligible.\n\n## Stack\n\nStacked on #28685. This PR contains only the thread initialization and\nlifecycle/settings API layer.","tree":{"sha":"c4e86ca4b0a00058bf2e69ff653be9fb4060dbdd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/c4e86ca4b0a00058bf2e69ff653be9fb4060dbdd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/7abfcf220bbb57029e2ff5d9914124aef7ef3d0f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNQLkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAW0AQAJjrFRqrAiNZUwg0xbjaHwno\nbTgCfP8pcuGIA/0AF/FUR+DhsmL+FUYn0NEGi5LBsAYOTbllsP7J2ECxwSnQhljq\nvZgY8FbHuY54AJLRMdbVE+IFIjLvm8cMzEz5ytVdJ0F2ci1PuA6lU7E1yCQqkWxx\n+1tloS1quKwRFxc544lMsHMZG5BfyvBjPNecMiBDB+xO7K5ShxLxwLixPqDeuyLx\ne5vH4FBr68PajbeSUkIPSz49dGYGVIHXIs3Khit+guiDOBuD6OLKly71v/BRzZvr\nkv1wx3kIDm16ptcXg3CtJGJ1SHw5EGq34yjShp7GtYfSOF9tKcKSqZ1kFU1U6uRx\nwTRCN8tYc6kc3CWsQfTuf6AQUMgw+S01VH39kxCpPxHzcim2Mz4Bk2dGM6dRagBb\njK1tzeD8N5+JmuIqXdb+XYfLM9ecbeJuydvfo+WhGJcBJ/haSv3bUTgC1YTAMqAb\ne5c62bFUjL0WMRnR22mhF1b+8bxmw3NIUHDGj+1oE7XDHhK4v6ApEvJOd7WBGGrl\nLnqCf33Fnw725mWmdl1wj6N9jntXovpmoYjtbNRl1bAkNjJqXREzVbVPxqb9dkNM\nFcboNNIu8HRPJlVnMIju/RK7syOHWRkwP2rxqnekhZF2GBsu3InzqSn5/YltXVc2\nAm8FClhi8VzcWDqzPG9x\n=jaYa\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c4e86ca4b0a00058bf2e69ff653be9fb4060dbdd\nparent fc8c6b73841e279f95f53b08771a7969e953bdf4\nauthor Shijie Rao <shijie.rao@openai.com> 1781859044 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781859044 +0200\n\nExpose thread-level multi-agent mode (#28792)\n\n## Why\n\nOnce multi-agent mode can be selected per turn, clients also need to\nchoose the initial selection when creating a thread and observe that\nselection through lifecycle and settings APIs.\n\nThe selected value is intentionally distinct from the effective\nmodel-visible value: no client selection is represented as `null`, even\nthough an eligible multi-agent v2 turn derives `explicitRequestOnly` as\nits effective default.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add the optional experimental `thread/start.multiAgentMode` parameter\nand pass it through thread creation.\n- Preserve an omitted initial value as an unset selection rather than\neagerly storing `explicitRequestOnly`.\n- Apply an explicit `thread/start` selection to the first turn through\nthe session configuration established at thread creation.\n- Restore the latest persisted effective mode as the selected baseline\non cold resume when rollout history contains one.\n- Inherit the optional selected mode from a loaded parent when creating\nrelated runtime threads.\n- Return the current selected `multiAgentMode` from `thread/start`,\n`thread/resume`, `thread/fork`, and thread settings, using `null` when\nno mode is selected.\n- Keep lifecycle reporting independent from model capability and feature\neligibility; core turn construction remains responsible for calculating\nand persisting the effective mode.\n\n## Not covered\n\n- Clearing an existing loaded-session selection back to unset through\n`turn/start`; omitted or `null` currently retains the session's\nselection.\n- A TUI control, slash command, or `config.toml` preference.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 just test -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 just test -p codex-app-server multi_agent_mode`\n\nThe focused app-server coverage verifies explicit `thread/start`\ninitialization, first-turn prompting, nullable reporting for an omitted\nselection, and retention of selections that are not currently\nruntime-eligible.\n\n## Stack\n\nStacked on #28685. This PR contains only the thread initialization and\nlifecycle/settings API layer.","verified_at":"2026-06-19T08:50:45Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7abfcf220bbb57029e2ff5d9914124aef7ef3d0f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/7abfcf220bbb57029e2ff5d9914124aef7ef3d0f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7abfcf220bbb57029e2ff5d9914124aef7ef3d0f/comments","author":{"login":"shijie-oai","id":235382242,"node_id":"U_kgDODgel4g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/235382242?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/shijie-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"fc8c6b73841e279f95f53b08771a7969e953bdf4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/fc8c6b73841e279f95f53b08771a7969e953bdf4","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/fc8c6b73841e279f95f53b08771a7969e953bdf4"}]},{"sha":"fc8c6b73841e279f95f53b08771a7969e953bdf4","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGZjOGM2YjczODQxZTI3OWY5NWY1M2IwODc3MWE3OTY5ZTk1M2JkZjQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Shijie Rao","email":"shijie.rao@openai.com","date":"2026-06-19T05:47:51Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-19T05:47:51Z"},"message":"Add per-turn multi-agent mode (#28685)\n\n## Why\n\nMulti-agent v2 currently carries an explicit-request-only delegation\nrule in its static usage hint. That provides a safe default, but it\nprevents clients from selecting proactive delegation per turn without\nchanging static guidance or rewriting prior model context.\n\nThis change makes delegation mode a session selection that can be\nupdated through `turn/start`, while deriving the effective model-visible\nmode separately for each turn. Eligible multi-agent v2 turns remain\nexplicit-request-only unless proactive mode is both selected and\nenabled.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add the experimental `turn/start.multiAgentMode` parameter with\n`explicitRequestOnly` and `proactive` values. Omission retains the\nloaded session's current optional selection.\n- Add the default-off `features.multi_agent_mode` feature gate. Eligible\nmulti-agent v2 turns use the selected mode when enabled; an unset\nselection or disabled gate resolves to `explicitRequestOnly`.\n- Treat mode prompting as inapplicable for multi-agent v1 and other\nunsupported session configurations, producing no multi-agent mode\ndeveloper message rather than rejecting the turn.\n- Move the explicit-request-only rule out of the static v2 usage hint\nand into a bounded, tagged developer context fragment.\n- Emit the effective mode in initial context and only when that\neffective mode changes on later turns.\n- Persist the effective mode in `TurnContextItem` as the durable\nbaseline for resume and context-update comparisons.\n\nHistorical rollout items are not rewritten. Later mode developer\nmessages establish the current rule incrementally.\n\n## Not covered\n\n- Initial selection through `thread/start` and selected-mode reporting\nfrom thread lifecycle/settings APIs; those are isolated in the stacked\n#28792.\n- A TUI control or slash command for selecting the mode.\n- Persisting a preferred mode to `config.toml`; selection remains\nsession/turn scoped.\n- Changes to multi-agent concurrency limits, tool availability, or model\ncatalog capability declarations.\n- Rewriting historical rollout prompt items. Cold resume restores the\nlatest persisted effective mode when available while leaving historical\ndeveloper messages intact.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 just test -p codex-core multi_agent_mode`\n- Focused app-server coverage verifies that `turn/start.multiAgentMode`\nproduces proactive developer instructions for an eligible v2 turn.\n\n## Stack\n\nFollowed by #28792, which adds `thread/start` initialization and\nlifecycle/settings observability.","tree":{"sha":"0fbb31e502a0f3e7f81f9cb01c4a616c675a3aa5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/0fbb31e502a0f3e7f81f9cb01c4a616c675a3aa5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/fc8c6b73841e279f95f53b08771a7969e953bdf4","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNNgHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAo6sQAGL1/uX8WoSgFi/oLdOCTDgl\ndRrOknCusW0dmXt8DNZkppQJGI3LbdziAq9YepHhAn0o2ey2eE0ATJDng4qIMSJo\n0emPsJDqqRfjT4t2MH0/odD/g3gpBflgW0Ctg1UZA/SCp8sU3f0hlIqOdbKRebYv\n5IITxnheXZpl2ySrKULozVCKI9QX7s2TDsWboBX+G3uF1qo2nysypCbZCtPFcyQz\nFOBWYhGCd+GPLcOnAgPZ76yimrBMU1/us2w0XdK4ehvDCmHj3UH3EaL9YMoYRzT+\nojmiKa9yXluYFU28pVGaXAk5fwOpsLddQZiT67qaxnlQ6TUhxz8Sq63QpkgE7SrD\ngR4sm+9gxcIA2bDnjBZau64dcUMhLkya0i8l4BHSGOYaVGTc3w1Y1deOe/RA1KM8\nARA5aof6gVbh3hnuPan+MJUL3yNmvrGhJodDcOTPrhnTBc64tOwROO7U+q+r/Nj6\nLMyxgMoApWELkt/LyjhT9qbTCjn8joB+x2WTR57zpUOgij+WFy2EJVIH4S3pIcDh\nUu3yd+G75lYTe2wIjGseUh6Bhb9DI1SeAYJK/XQwNbzlEtF/1p1gAnWcCHgnbOBf\nAyLwi/4Qe35NWR3ln3g9LaE7xFn46LjI/h8uadkmp340ntTy8guevSu7xbMkGBsi\nXG8U1vDEYRIKQcLJ1+/I\n=UjFU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0fbb31e502a0f3e7f81f9cb01c4a616c675a3aa5\nparent f886e33e5a55fcb6637d1d05c0f44cab9fcb933f\nauthor Shijie Rao <shijie.rao@openai.com> 1781848071 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781848071 -0700\n\nAdd per-turn multi-agent mode (#28685)\n\n## Why\n\nMulti-agent v2 currently carries an explicit-request-only delegation\nrule in its static usage hint. That provides a safe default, but it\nprevents clients from selecting proactive delegation per turn without\nchanging static guidance or rewriting prior model context.\n\nThis change makes delegation mode a session selection that can be\nupdated through `turn/start`, while deriving the effective model-visible\nmode separately for each turn. Eligible multi-agent v2 turns remain\nexplicit-request-only unless proactive mode is both selected and\nenabled.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add the experimental `turn/start.multiAgentMode` parameter with\n`explicitRequestOnly` and `proactive` values. Omission retains the\nloaded session's current optional selection.\n- Add the default-off `features.multi_agent_mode` feature gate. Eligible\nmulti-agent v2 turns use the selected mode when enabled; an unset\nselection or disabled gate resolves to `explicitRequestOnly`.\n- Treat mode prompting as inapplicable for multi-agent v1 and other\nunsupported session configurations, producing no multi-agent mode\ndeveloper message rather than rejecting the turn.\n- Move the explicit-request-only rule out of the static v2 usage hint\nand into a bounded, tagged developer context fragment.\n- Emit the effective mode in initial context and only when that\neffective mode changes on later turns.\n- Persist the effective mode in `TurnContextItem` as the durable\nbaseline for resume and context-update comparisons.\n\nHistorical rollout items are not rewritten. Later mode developer\nmessages establish the current rule incrementally.\n\n## Not covered\n\n- Initial selection through `thread/start` and selected-mode reporting\nfrom thread lifecycle/settings APIs; those are isolated in the stacked\n#28792.\n- A TUI control or slash command for selecting the mode.\n- Persisting a preferred mode to `config.toml`; selection remains\nsession/turn scoped.\n- Changes to multi-agent concurrency limits, tool availability, or model\ncatalog capability declarations.\n- Rewriting historical rollout prompt items. Cold resume restores the\nlatest persisted effective mode when available while leaving historical\ndeveloper messages intact.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 just test -p codex-core multi_agent_mode`\n- Focused app-server coverage verifies that `turn/start.multiAgentMode`\nproduces proactive developer instructions for an eligible v2 turn.\n\n## Stack\n\nFollowed by #28792, which adds `thread/start` initialization and\nlifecycle/settings observability.","verified_at":"2026-06-19T05:47:52Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/fc8c6b73841e279f95f53b08771a7969e953bdf4","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/fc8c6b73841e279f95f53b08771a7969e953bdf4","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/fc8c6b73841e279f95f53b08771a7969e953bdf4/comments","author":{"login":"shijie-oai","id":235382242,"node_id":"U_kgDODgel4g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/235382242?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/shijie-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f886e33e5a55fcb6637d1d05c0f44cab9fcb933f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f886e33e5a55fcb6637d1d05c0f44cab9fcb933f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f886e33e5a55fcb6637d1d05c0f44cab9fcb933f"}]},{"sha":"f886e33e5a55fcb6637d1d05c0f44cab9fcb933f","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGY4ODZlMzNlNWE1NWZjYjY2MzdkMWQwNWMwZjQ0Y2FiOWZjYjkzM2Y","commit":{"author":{"name":"sayan-oai","email":"sayan@openai.com","date":"2026-06-19T05:27:45Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-19T05:27:45Z"},"message":"[3/3] app-server: configure environment connection timeout (#29025)\n\n## Why\n\nRemote environments registered through `environment/add` currently use\nthe fixed 10-second WebSocket connection timeout. Slow-starting\nexecutors need a caller-selected connection window, but this should not\nadd retry policy or couple exec-server behavior to Core’s\n`deferred_executor` feature.\n\nMake the timeout an optional part of the existing experimental request.\nExisting clients continue using the current default, while callers that\nknow an executor may take longer can request a larger window explicitly.\n\nDepends on #28683.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add optional `connectTimeoutMs` to `EnvironmentAddParams` and document\nit in the app-server README.\n- Pass the optional timeout through `EnvironmentRequestProcessor` into\none `EnvironmentManager::upsert_environment()` path; the manager applies\nthe existing default when it is omitted.\n- Preserve the existing single-attempt lifecycle. The configured value\ncontrols WebSocket connection and handshake time for both initial\nconnection and later reconnects; initialization retains its separate\ntimeout.\n- Add an app-server integration test that sends the real JSON-RPC\nrequest and verifies a stalled handshake observes the requested timeout.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `just test -p codex-exec-server`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nenvironment_add_applies_connect_timeout`\n\n## Rollout\n\nThis is additive and does not enable `deferred_executor`. Callers should\nsend a non-default timeout only after a compatible app-server is\ndeployed; omitted or `null` values retain the existing 10-second\ndefault.","tree":{"sha":"18b41002689874b634fae84a20ebc0cb7c507f4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/18b41002689874b634fae84a20ebc0cb7c507f4d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/f886e33e5a55fcb6637d1d05c0f44cab9fcb933f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNNNRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAeo0QABVrSIzeXhR1yo2jLRDpMVpk\nmPs/QXmSSW43mp6+/iuVCUvvi3mPpuMBN6R+HWc+SfMSuIJyeI71eaYss3IqNAQR\nRIsl/ERs4LQSRVYa62POLHLczBGXpTr2uysH84RBAVwq3dTw8GctWLB4ThWtVHPf\nAuCUpH9Y8Zo6pHFUgWuYTiMLB3kOsybmgcAcmzZ5Ed8Em5DZjjKn+ywKW8hPCb3j\nEqfdUSZQoJbaF+Rz5Omf73fkmRggFSWTrdelyWLmSbGXVRejRp55SPsFd3sFEG2s\njUonYtENSLeSVbGgvhLgSBMLPXysAuANt9OmmEeO9EisJ2IrRS+NmBHmIOrj3e/n\n2kpP74RfL/osQDeeajRBjko0DkzmzdwFagJJM+bHJkpUmqwu+7PQwcFDJVBsix8+\neCik9/rdht82VjBVKjyLrADYt6iglZRHCpLgfCOmhKNde85CYwwPXnbioAXOD/UO\ne3aDKxkQBbZsNEQmNI9HoF9uHs/lVhweEyO3PyaHgIqXXW3GB1zfv1jjV+VLAVV5\n8UNpPpGQQiBaJPB3hHbNJnAT0IoCgLNTq2Hj2zypvy/z1BFVnLtTMEgbNJTW3xj4\nCTe6k4MYga6XEKm7vC7BdZyxj6zf7vnTaYcZ/O/K8ZB2wWK1OUFWr7zQb7dskOKg\nxM78sPQ+VSGpXhOw7ROE\n=KIdT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 18b41002689874b634fae84a20ebc0cb7c507f4d\nparent 45a133bae0ec14584aba62919bc86307e9f10088\nauthor sayan-oai <sayan@openai.com> 1781846865 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781846865 +0000\n\n[3/3] app-server: configure environment connection timeout (#29025)\n\n## Why\n\nRemote environments registered through `environment/add` currently use\nthe fixed 10-second WebSocket connection timeout. Slow-starting\nexecutors need a caller-selected connection window, but this should not\nadd retry policy or couple exec-server behavior to Core’s\n`deferred_executor` feature.\n\nMake the timeout an optional part of the existing experimental request.\nExisting clients continue using the current default, while callers that\nknow an executor may take longer can request a larger window explicitly.\n\nDepends on #28683.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add optional `connectTimeoutMs` to `EnvironmentAddParams` and document\nit in the app-server README.\n- Pass the optional timeout through `EnvironmentRequestProcessor` into\none `EnvironmentManager::upsert_environment()` path; the manager applies\nthe existing default when it is omitted.\n- Preserve the existing single-attempt lifecycle. The configured value\ncontrols WebSocket connection and handshake time for both initial\nconnection and later reconnects; initialization retains its separate\ntimeout.\n- Add an app-server integration test that sends the real JSON-RPC\nrequest and verifies a stalled handshake observes the requested timeout.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `just test -p codex-exec-server`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nenvironment_add_applies_connect_timeout`\n\n## Rollout\n\nThis is additive and does not enable `deferred_executor`. Callers should\nsend a non-default timeout only after a compatible app-server is\ndeployed; omitted or `null` values retain the existing 10-second\ndefault.","verified_at":"2026-06-19T05:27:45Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f886e33e5a55fcb6637d1d05c0f44cab9fcb933f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f886e33e5a55fcb6637d1d05c0f44cab9fcb933f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f886e33e5a55fcb6637d1d05c0f44cab9fcb933f/comments","author":{"login":"sayan-oai","id":244841968,"node_id":"U_kgDODpf98A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/244841968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/sayan-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"45a133bae0ec14584aba62919bc86307e9f10088","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/45a133bae0ec14584aba62919bc86307e9f10088","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/45a133bae0ec14584aba62919bc86307e9f10088"}]},{"sha":"45a133bae0ec14584aba62919bc86307e9f10088","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDQ1YTEzM2JhZTBlYzE0NTg0YWJhNjI5MTliYzg2MzA3ZTlmMTAwODg","commit":{"author":{"name":"sayan-oai","email":"sayan@openai.com","date":"2026-06-19T05:06:34Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-19T05:06:34Z"},"message":"[2/3] core: track starting environments in snapshots (#28683)\n\n## Why\n\nRemote environments may still be resolving when Codex creates a session\nor turn. Waiting for the existing all-or-nothing environment snapshot\ncan hold startup until the selected environment is usable.\n\nBehind the default-off `deferred_executor` feature, let callers take a\nuseful snapshot immediately: completed environments remain available\nnormally, while unfinished environments are reported without blocking\nstartup. With the feature disabled, snapshots preserve the existing\nblocking behavior.\n\nDepends on #28674.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Store one ordered list of selected environments in\n`ThreadEnvironments`. Each selection owns one shared resolution that\nproduces its complete `TurnEnvironment`.\n- Start new resolutions in the background with `remote_handle()`,\nallowing snapshots and the future wait tool to share the same result\nwhile cancellation follows the retained handles.\n- Make `snapshot()` a read-only operation: nonblocking snapshots collect\ncompleted resolutions and retain handles for unfinished ones, while\nblocking snapshots await every resolution.\n- Replace completed failed resolutions from the current manager entry\nand log when failed environments are omitted.\n- Return attached and starting environments as a point-in-time view, and\ncount starting environments when deciding whether a snapshot is\nlocal-only.\n- Keep existing consumers attached-only. `to_selections()` derives from\nattached environments, so child threads do not inherit an environment\nthat is still starting.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just test -p codex-core environment_selection`\n- `just test -p codex-core\ndeferred_executor_reaches_model_before_remote_environment_is_ready`\n\n## Landing note\n\nKeep `deferred_executor` disabled for slow-starting executors until\nconfigurable `environment/add` connection timeouts and caller support\nland. When enabled, an environment that attaches after session startup\nmay remain absent from environment-derived model context, tools,\ninstructions, skills, and related state until follow-up refresh work\nlands.","tree":{"sha":"f82a532c3e09150b6b9a979c8f2a4eb571b06da6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/f82a532c3e09150b6b9a979c8f2a4eb571b06da6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/45a133bae0ec14584aba62919bc86307e9f10088","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNM5aCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAulIQADSfwt/vdcgdvRPyFViSJQcs\nv5DxidousNE7OphEM+dBZO9SKLE6cO9tRRxMtMdvY1GQ6qBR1VMuSyFdiACt8kfq\n4EXYFHCjoHX1pA3MOkR9hKIXU9dJwLPaNp3MOpB5pzc0Gytf59KeoFEHoxF8U9X1\nEaLBBrFs0oQGzNd91LgO6l/q64SUurckM80kGClUWagL+5lSa3ebOrhS8e4LUdD/\nOEh5/zzeNGoe2KwsXbwI/SzdA4x6c0dRuKn1xJT01sk8qYetvyOohqYRgQc3k9kK\n/lr1Rs2dLcTO3HoWzQCydliZ/Di+mCEvgHyU+fqYM6oDPTleXK7HE7IG4R0hrLK7\nidct56u9TIVVG6hgCz6XiRQ1JYS0MwfDIVgF0406B5GRByhRfqPgyY5LrZU6+aUN\nQfbYW1/t+oQ6tNT+kgbWGPbHgt5hjq88+PqRWjsQAMU0nFkGV4dd+WkWBJN51YJB\n+D63VWHuKkv7tg2iD6lzTUnzruAdG/GPwsuI61ICPhgJo3k+gjelTErmvvSJFZkR\nhozEsd7G8aeCJ9Z12QGnBPvXFdkm9FNcDa2lq+s0Lb+O0g818QNJS5z/7B2MhzzE\naihtB5fZMW5iBCi5Pk1T4JKm8XZKoxPlJvHmC68ff/WehKxN4HgxioizhJh/wi/T\nleoaOziCUR7YmYNPlfIT\n=bqBj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f82a532c3e09150b6b9a979c8f2a4eb571b06da6\nparent 41988e6a2442730639e71cf2a8b6e768737d1bb0\nauthor sayan-oai <sayan@openai.com> 1781845594 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781845594 +0000\n\n[2/3] core: track starting environments in snapshots (#28683)\n\n## Why\n\nRemote environments may still be resolving when Codex creates a session\nor turn. Waiting for the existing all-or-nothing environment snapshot\ncan hold startup until the selected environment is usable.\n\nBehind the default-off `deferred_executor` feature, let callers take a\nuseful snapshot immediately: completed environments remain available\nnormally, while unfinished environments are reported without blocking\nstartup. With the feature disabled, snapshots preserve the existing\nblocking behavior.\n\nDepends on #28674.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Store one ordered list of selected environments in\n`ThreadEnvironments`. Each selection owns one shared resolution that\nproduces its complete `TurnEnvironment`.\n- Start new resolutions in the background with `remote_handle()`,\nallowing snapshots and the future wait tool to share the same result\nwhile cancellation follows the retained handles.\n- Make `snapshot()` a read-only operation: nonblocking snapshots collect\ncompleted resolutions and retain handles for unfinished ones, while\nblocking snapshots await every resolution.\n- Replace completed failed resolutions from the current manager entry\nand log when failed environments are omitted.\n- Return attached and starting environments as a point-in-time view, and\ncount starting environments when deciding whether a snapshot is\nlocal-only.\n- Keep existing consumers attached-only. `to_selections()` derives from\nattached environments, so child threads do not inherit an environment\nthat is still starting.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just test -p codex-core environment_selection`\n- `just test -p codex-core\ndeferred_executor_reaches_model_before_remote_environment_is_ready`\n\n## Landing note\n\nKeep `deferred_executor` disabled for slow-starting executors until\nconfigurable `environment/add` connection timeouts and caller support\nland. When enabled, an environment that attaches after session startup\nmay remain absent from environment-derived model context, tools,\ninstructions, skills, and related state until follow-up refresh work\nlands.","verified_at":"2026-06-19T05:06:34Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/45a133bae0ec14584aba62919bc86307e9f10088","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/45a133bae0ec14584aba62919bc86307e9f10088","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/45a133bae0ec14584aba62919bc86307e9f10088/comments","author":{"login":"sayan-oai","id":244841968,"node_id":"U_kgDODpf98A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/244841968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/sayan-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"41988e6a2442730639e71cf2a8b6e768737d1bb0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/41988e6a2442730639e71cf2a8b6e768737d1bb0","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/41988e6a2442730639e71cf2a8b6e768737d1bb0"}]},{"sha":"41988e6a2442730639e71cf2a8b6e768737d1bb0","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDQxOTg4ZTZhMjQ0MjczMDYzOWU3MWNmMmE4YjZlNzY4NzM3ZDFiYjA","commit":{"author":{"name":"sayan-oai","email":"sayan@openai.com","date":"2026-06-19T04:50:15Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-19T04:50:15Z"},"message":"[1/3] core: add remote environment connection lifecycle (#28674)\n\n## Why\n\nRemote environments can be registered before their exec-server is first\nused. Starting the connection at registration time uses that startup\nwindow, while sharing one startup result prevents background work and\ncapability calls from opening competing connections.\n\nKeep initial startup simple: each environment makes one connection\nattempt using its configured transport timeout. A failed initial attempt\nis final for that environment, while an environment that disconnects\nafter connecting can still recover on a later operation.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Start URL and Noise environments in the background when they are added\nto `EnvironmentManager`. Provider snapshots are fully validated before\nconnection work begins.\n- Share one initial connection attempt and its saved result across\nmetadata, process, filesystem, and HTTP callers.\n- Keep configured stdio environments lazy until first use so\nregistration does not launch a process.\n- Tie background startup work to the environment lifetime so replacing\nor dropping an environment cancels unfinished work.\n- After an established client disconnects, share one fresh connection\nattempt across concurrent callers. A failed attempt fails the current\noperation without permanently preventing a later attempt.\n- Store the shared lazy client directly on `Environment` and expose\nsmall methods for starting, observing, and awaiting startup.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just test -p codex-exec-server`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nturn_start_resolves_sticky_thread_local_environment_and_turn_overrides`","tree":{"sha":"c87de920fa67a93f5f40592a3a3238ef09cefea3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/c87de920fa67a93f5f40592a3a3238ef09cefea3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/41988e6a2442730639e71cf2a8b6e768737d1bb0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNMqHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVjoQAG2hwx/em4/lU9QJhmgrbOrh\nX8t9d/CicfFJAbvSfz5mtZDPdetAR6J5aXnfYq2IrYIO25YIa6f2mdn2dQL8JXs+\n/ocYBC15SXtmFIG3lfjJ1471cqb5AC8M59ENZt23rJYvIKU14vG63EgxtUls0psZ\nrpM9KAeJacdv45m7I3AA6yCA3GryAyz018AyLKgMlwk+miqV/PS0O4s2qDqdhwkR\nTG2343rwXtaNXF4JpybtFHvmi8zKHCP6gi6LUUCzq+rR39kOtpjsgJi1fquyb8OG\nK4y7rCP2CEUbJpDaKWOBEW3Swoc/twbB6w/H2h8V0q333VOPebnGMMgvVUuuv4Gn\nRtDpHUScM3lr0ZJZsws6z1JkhD4J9A3S4+CeO0mA1oRqn3RNPNi1UhbsBHkwUW5j\no5U/pgMa7ZeMqv059H28cOH0AxSeLCED4vgOELhHhlNuCI5fPOnn/OFE5fLIMKvz\neIiTREq1NihUmdS6JP2G6lLudjjJYuo3FGWNT6ptt/VPNLhsEY+mP97ee6XlhPgu\nGRpunSohO2umj1GgrmIfF2slUMV4iduv9h3S9cqRPgQ97wieSarLV/b4nbBONJZQ\notDmZCHi+dQ8fTf+ZSCOTRTpARaKSaQ/IzJ41lTIiU64fMkEPTPEwCVYUht/mrpW\ntDChrY7MykCsrDoMFAog\n=nrck\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c87de920fa67a93f5f40592a3a3238ef09cefea3\nparent 4e6bc4226658b7bc2ba4e207506b51f8d6d3626f\nauthor sayan-oai <sayan@openai.com> 1781844615 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781844615 -0700\n\n[1/3] core: add remote environment connection lifecycle (#28674)\n\n## Why\n\nRemote environments can be registered before their exec-server is first\nused. Starting the connection at registration time uses that startup\nwindow, while sharing one startup result prevents background work and\ncapability calls from opening competing connections.\n\nKeep initial startup simple: each environment makes one connection\nattempt using its configured transport timeout. A failed initial attempt\nis final for that environment, while an environment that disconnects\nafter connecting can still recover on a later operation.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Start URL and Noise environments in the background when they are added\nto `EnvironmentManager`. Provider snapshots are fully validated before\nconnection work begins.\n- Share one initial connection attempt and its saved result across\nmetadata, process, filesystem, and HTTP callers.\n- Keep configured stdio environments lazy until first use so\nregistration does not launch a process.\n- Tie background startup work to the environment lifetime so replacing\nor dropping an environment cancels unfinished work.\n- After an established client disconnects, share one fresh connection\nattempt across concurrent callers. A failed attempt fails the current\noperation without permanently preventing a later attempt.\n- Store the shared lazy client directly on `Environment` and expose\nsmall methods for starting, observing, and awaiting startup.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just test -p codex-exec-server`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nturn_start_resolves_sticky_thread_local_environment_and_turn_overrides`","verified_at":"2026-06-19T04:50:16Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/41988e6a2442730639e71cf2a8b6e768737d1bb0","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/41988e6a2442730639e71cf2a8b6e768737d1bb0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/41988e6a2442730639e71cf2a8b6e768737d1bb0/comments","author":{"login":"sayan-oai","id":244841968,"node_id":"U_kgDODpf98A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/244841968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/sayan-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4e6bc4226658b7bc2ba4e207506b51f8d6d3626f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4e6bc4226658b7bc2ba4e207506b51f8d6d3626f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4e6bc4226658b7bc2ba4e207506b51f8d6d3626f"}]},{"sha":"4e6bc4226658b7bc2ba4e207506b51f8d6d3626f","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDRlNmJjNDIyNjY1OGI3YmMyYmE0ZTIwNzUwNmI1MWY4ZDZkMzYyNmY","commit":{"author":{"name":"xl-openai","email":"xl@openai.com","date":"2026-06-19T04:17:20Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-19T04:17:20Z"},"message":"[codex] Support protected resource OAuth discovery (#29022)\n\n## Why\n\nPlugin-install preflight and the actual OAuth login flow used different\ndiscovery implementations. Preflight had a Codex-specific implementation\nthat only queried authorization-server metadata on the MCP host, while\nlogin already used the upstream `rmcp` Rust MCP SDK. As a result,\nservers that advertise a separate authorization server through RFC 9728\nProtected Resource Metadata were classified as OAuth-unsupported during\nplugin installation, so login was skipped.\n\n## What changed\n\n- delegate plugin-install OAuth discovery to\n`rmcp::transport::AuthorizationManager`, the same implementation used by\nthe login flow\n- let `rmcp` follow Protected Resource Metadata first and perform direct\nRFC 8414 authorization-server discovery when protected-resource\ndiscovery does not yield usable metadata\n- retain Codex's existing HTTP headers, timeout, `no_proxy` behavior,\nand scope normalization around that discovery\n- add unit coverage and a pure-MCP plugin-install integration test that\nproves the protected-resource path reaches OAuth client registration\n\nThis only changes shared MCP OAuth discovery. App declarations and\n`appsNeedingAuth` behavior are unchanged.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-rmcp-client auth_status`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server plugin_install_starts_mcp_oauth`\n- real plugin-install smoke test with an isolated `CODEX_HOME`: both\nDigitalOcean MCP servers started OAuth callback listeners, while Linear\ncontinued to start its existing direct-discovery OAuth flow","tree":{"sha":"5b7c64bc8e0990db9369b6dcae72c9582f880bac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/5b7c64bc8e0990db9369b6dcae72c9582f880bac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/4e6bc4226658b7bc2ba4e207506b51f8d6d3626f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNMLQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANW8QAB15CbkxpA9gX3Kxb9W8TFI7\nl78owYap3VURL/VdImBNbq7EZ5GkY0Z5AdmS9orWDArtBNlD35LXM21bm0KFMPq+\nm4ntZKH4GS236GunzVsE+CowqrYzUbKD2CPusUN4jKVTSrao+Gtodd+wrqSTOrGj\nHXSW4AzfzgkvV4B6P17Wm671rsUP6ZL60n+XBEnZT7kmAejRlIlo20Kg0VD33IQo\nazKrQV61xFNvpWmWSt4iJz2OswIKBA3MW/ddB+38Osi+DvrHdVrCl/uvelPXnxhb\nCBZAaw+4/ui3BEDO54uyBMGWNkPOm4vGzcW3CD0iCbiYRcRY8mkHBkbmRdNuTWSI\n1j76MCMtSR5JBMaKxQl1RlsMNC+pui41fZC6z5ivVZDmJZFpVodSyIRGnQdoQmMW\nx652lGFYaILfpBlyvlKtPdBrAYCWVN9rJftyRdCfBVTo59n9AN3/gSMzNFRK7lHT\na6STL1WM494tw452c7EUq98pZa/9oDy3UVNJHOwxKuj6NL2WRs+qohlOEvGLdcvG\nHxPqVxO2NprwbiSZTQxbBxMcHLMPmepfHf87rx4/m9DLEWFL+e1muFMOGowvBjYM\n/EGEATueFqjzbBdocbyg5qu36BVEMIpIDwTyshAuS4lBo01yXcuuHrLqinNpOhU3\nPGCrRtZ1m70NoXUD9MU4\n=Ghbq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5b7c64bc8e0990db9369b6dcae72c9582f880bac\nparent 70a6aa2634adedaabf66a66f11c16e869c1c7d1e\nauthor xl-openai <xl@openai.com> 1781842640 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781842640 -0700\n\n[codex] Support protected resource OAuth discovery (#29022)\n\n## Why\n\nPlugin-install preflight and the actual OAuth login flow used different\ndiscovery implementations. Preflight had a Codex-specific implementation\nthat only queried authorization-server metadata on the MCP host, while\nlogin already used the upstream `rmcp` Rust MCP SDK. As a result,\nservers that advertise a separate authorization server through RFC 9728\nProtected Resource Metadata were classified as OAuth-unsupported during\nplugin installation, so login was skipped.\n\n## What changed\n\n- delegate plugin-install OAuth discovery to\n`rmcp::transport::AuthorizationManager`, the same implementation used by\nthe login flow\n- let `rmcp` follow Protected Resource Metadata first and perform direct\nRFC 8414 authorization-server discovery when protected-resource\ndiscovery does not yield usable metadata\n- retain Codex's existing HTTP headers, timeout, `no_proxy` behavior,\nand scope normalization around that discovery\n- add unit coverage and a pure-MCP plugin-install integration test that\nproves the protected-resource path reaches OAuth client registration\n\nThis only changes shared MCP OAuth discovery. App declarations and\n`appsNeedingAuth` behavior are unchanged.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-rmcp-client auth_status`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server plugin_install_starts_mcp_oauth`\n- real plugin-install smoke test with an isolated `CODEX_HOME`: both\nDigitalOcean MCP servers started OAuth callback listeners, while Linear\ncontinued to start its existing direct-discovery OAuth flow","verified_at":"2026-06-19T04:17:20Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4e6bc4226658b7bc2ba4e207506b51f8d6d3626f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4e6bc4226658b7bc2ba4e207506b51f8d6d3626f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4e6bc4226658b7bc2ba4e207506b51f8d6d3626f/comments","author":{"login":"xl-openai","id":184293535,"node_id":"U_kgDOCvwYnw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184293535?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/xl-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"70a6aa2634adedaabf66a66f11c16e869c1c7d1e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/70a6aa2634adedaabf66a66f11c16e869c1c7d1e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/70a6aa2634adedaabf66a66f11c16e869c1c7d1e"}]},{"sha":"70a6aa2634adedaabf66a66f11c16e869c1c7d1e","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDcwYTZhYTI2MzRhZGVkYWFiZjY2YTY2ZjExYzE2ZTg2OWMxYzdkMWU","commit":{"author":{"name":"pakrym-oai","email":"pakrym@openai.com","date":"2026-06-19T01:49:57Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-19T01:49:57Z"},"message":"core: assign item IDs to compacted replacement history (#29012)\n\n## Why\n\nRemote v2 compaction can return replacement-history items without IDs.\nBecause replacement history is installed directly, those items bypass\nnormal history preparation and remain ID-less in later Responses\nrequests even when the `item_ids` feature is enabled.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Pass the active `TurnContext` into `replace_compacted_history`.\n- When `item_ids` is enabled, assign missing IDs before installing and\npersisting replacement history.\n- Rebuild `CompactedItem` from the prepared history so live and\npersisted replacement histories match.\n- Add integration coverage requiring IDs on every ID-capable input item\nin the initial, remote v2 compaction, and post-compaction requests.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just test -p codex-core response_item_ids`\n- `just test -p codex-core websocket_v2_test_codex_shell_chain`\n- `just test -p codex-core remote_compaction_parity_pre_turn_auto`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nthread_inject_items_adds_raw_response_items_to_thread_history`","tree":{"sha":"742c225f1a55a1c2706d4f91b0b990073c123b45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/742c225f1a55a1c2706d4f91b0b990073c123b45"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/70a6aa2634adedaabf66a66f11c16e869c1c7d1e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNKBFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/JcQAA/Lll8nHLGWSfuUpzXcIfAB\nk+dgrKjJ6PoPDQZfo6WVwumWoqUUugxJJKuYh0TO9Bff0DdBbtETp8fnwsElmmUy\ncYvbGujskLGxzTRHvHd5FcE9635j/fihn5E9yjqVKssm8f+6sAH4UykkVv/F33fF\nv8hrB/qvYgpwtGS7eTrJcxDaZrl5f91OweuvL70jXul2PflGGuFUexD6RwbZTX6k\nG0rYTjpi2Ah9pYnnbewkIe5T39u3fmLn7pJzVilz4vUMoUk7XVzehWnI8NG5hTd9\npnAkOF8sYP8VDphO4XnD2+DpWHMsFOKMlKCl0TJhMYEWd+Xn4P2kZXKiXG0meWHO\nB8uSK0TJTWPAKx0TLT3DUOGt6g7nAFFecwV5auwJKFuiGBhrxl91FnkB9x+f99n1\nx7feEUK/c/acmqtjzlgovM162opwEcYzmZbsd183kaSnG6bHG6YlDMP5yWx/Fc4n\n/IOF8aQ8xXJoLg3bx49CKejCo4utI41pffZyd2gESdlQZG9KqgAQopBBdy+rLsOz\nD7kzhu6/OjM6uOoX9n33cF+2ji/NSAhCArvSqKrk/waoqwv5WNddCvmr+Cx6JbyE\nLNRrYrSFHZDdYmukv3LLacLurLeKCGVfjJ84vaqCe7WjW0WQWTIxo/zE5tqZQGEF\nf1/ejv9Z4O9YiDos/6Ht\n=LOKj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 742c225f1a55a1c2706d4f91b0b990073c123b45\nparent 73251b2f00b3d9bda142f622fc11bde5af793bdd\nauthor pakrym-oai <pakrym@openai.com> 1781833797 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781833797 -0700\n\ncore: assign item IDs to compacted replacement history (#29012)\n\n## Why\n\nRemote v2 compaction can return replacement-history items without IDs.\nBecause replacement history is installed directly, those items bypass\nnormal history preparation and remain ID-less in later Responses\nrequests even when the `item_ids` feature is enabled.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Pass the active `TurnContext` into `replace_compacted_history`.\n- When `item_ids` is enabled, assign missing IDs before installing and\npersisting replacement history.\n- Rebuild `CompactedItem` from the prepared history so live and\npersisted replacement histories match.\n- Add integration coverage requiring IDs on every ID-capable input item\nin the initial, remote v2 compaction, and post-compaction requests.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just test -p codex-core response_item_ids`\n- `just test -p codex-core websocket_v2_test_codex_shell_chain`\n- `just test -p codex-core remote_compaction_parity_pre_turn_auto`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nthread_inject_items_adds_raw_response_items_to_thread_history`","verified_at":"2026-06-19T01:49:58Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/70a6aa2634adedaabf66a66f11c16e869c1c7d1e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/70a6aa2634adedaabf66a66f11c16e869c1c7d1e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/70a6aa2634adedaabf66a66f11c16e869c1c7d1e/comments","author":{"login":"pakrym-oai","id":204937752,"node_id":"U_kgDODDcaGA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204937752?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/pakrym-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"73251b2f00b3d9bda142f622fc11bde5af793bdd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/73251b2f00b3d9bda142f622fc11bde5af793bdd","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/73251b2f00b3d9bda142f622fc11bde5af793bdd"}]},{"sha":"73251b2f00b3d9bda142f622fc11bde5af793bdd","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDczMjUxYjJmMDBiM2Q5YmRhMTQyZjYyMmZjMTFiZGU1YWY3OTNiZGQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"rka-oai","email":"rka@openai.com","date":"2026-06-19T01:46:57Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-19T01:46:57Z"},"message":"[codex] add clock current-time tool (#29011)\n\n## Summary\n- expose `clock.curr_time` when current-time reminders are enabled\n- query the session's configured time provider with the calling thread\nid\n- return the existing UTC reminder text for direct model calls\n- return `{ \"current_time\": \"YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS UTC\" }` in Code Mode\n\nClock lookup failures remain fatal, matching pre-inference reminder\nbehavior.\n\n## Testing\n- `just test -p codex-core current_time_tool_returns_the_latest_time`\n- `just test -p codex-core\ncode_mode_current_time_returns_structured_result`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`","tree":{"sha":"78a07b9672e00e43837a02610cc41704b8f7d385","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/78a07b9672e00e43837a02610cc41704b8f7d385"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/73251b2f00b3d9bda142f622fc11bde5af793bdd","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNJ+RCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAw8kQAG8loSPl/5eNcjWuAGwTxu/7\n6Ng1T7p5dPnsmC6jYv+AN5VInQHLEqQ44Wa4UArhOLd1kspDaoCI4p4eNIUcOGOS\n6midz6eMs4hXKVleyp9saLuopwB6uzBvYroAHiG/TVg+8NOyV1D3tge/F7RRZ80R\nAxw87pQFxK3C0HYP1QZJYvjZGJrwiTt36sBHO3Stzs43nyOfXXx1UMO72fUUgO4F\nXR/9sBnTzhZFqKO1Z6qlU7ViNjfJVXP2Sgfw+8Vu/GEUvgs8xY8JpcaUZRmGUl4R\nSenldPzLQx12gQqn5CspBMOvfPvp33Cy66QAHMbUKhUUZ2ibxIne4tecygM45K3W\nn7dY7f5UvIaKUmkAjYQF2uTa12r8HlBRWuij6B0oyxXm6gff0dZ1L/uvpjD6ES1B\nZpppZHEmh3ETagt3kotdeAdS42QYYxF+5bBltaQxTtdXjG4EjXgOzw6VBn+4P9+8\no+lvcnXYpfyi102qD4I0BUPT0wVCKfQJmevcuXjDgSbz5+ZoQiIFAuMFM0VfMPW2\nth85wJX8w80CZednolcWkk1kJZ6/tXn3Osoeh85a3cUHr0cLsk/PkHO0yRWcZhzP\nF0xbrOlJoti60TZ0jX9ybtmnRXS1IwtzyOLLl8gI9/5SAHvjTxggN7YmwRZov8Z7\nHOq8tdkgDTDP+HA68gGL\n=H9xR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 78a07b9672e00e43837a02610cc41704b8f7d385\nparent 38c96866f0213173f98cf102a8efbb5aad5f6543\nauthor rka-oai <rka@openai.com> 1781833617 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781833617 +0000\n\n[codex] add clock current-time tool (#29011)\n\n## Summary\n- expose `clock.curr_time` when current-time reminders are enabled\n- query the session's configured time provider with the calling thread\nid\n- return the existing UTC reminder text for direct model calls\n- return `{ \"current_time\": \"YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS UTC\" }` in Code Mode\n\nClock lookup failures remain fatal, matching pre-inference reminder\nbehavior.\n\n## Testing\n- `just test -p codex-core current_time_tool_returns_the_latest_time`\n- `just test -p codex-core\ncode_mode_current_time_returns_structured_result`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`","verified_at":"2026-06-19T01:46:58Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/73251b2f00b3d9bda142f622fc11bde5af793bdd","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/73251b2f00b3d9bda142f622fc11bde5af793bdd","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/73251b2f00b3d9bda142f622fc11bde5af793bdd/comments","author":{"login":"rka-oai","id":240799229,"node_id":"U_kgDODlpN_Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/240799229?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/rka-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"38c96866f0213173f98cf102a8efbb5aad5f6543","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/38c96866f0213173f98cf102a8efbb5aad5f6543","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/38c96866f0213173f98cf102a8efbb5aad5f6543"}]},{"sha":"38c96866f0213173f98cf102a8efbb5aad5f6543","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDM4Yzk2ODY2ZjAyMTMxNzNmOThjZjEwMmE4ZWZiYjVhYWQ1ZjY1NDM","commit":{"author":{"name":"xl-openai","email":"xl@openai.com","date":"2026-06-19T01:02:14Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-19T01:02:14Z"},"message":"[codex] Skip curated repo sync for remote plugins (#29005)\n\n## Summary\n\n- skip the legacy `openai-curated` startup repository sync when remote\nplugins are enabled and the current auth uses the Codex backend\n- keep the curated sync for API-key, Bedrock, and unauthenticated\nsessions that fall back to the local marketplace\n- preserve configured marketplace upgrades and all remote plugin startup\nwarmups\n\n## Why\n\nThe remote catalog owns plugin discovery and materialization only when\nit is usable for the current auth mode. Starting the legacy curated\nrepository sync in that case performs an unnecessary Git/HTTP/archive\ndownload and cache refresh. API-key and Bedrock sessions still require\nthe local curated marketplace, so they must continue syncing it.\n\n## User impact\n\nCodex startup no longer downloads or refreshes the local\n`openai-curated` snapshot when the remote catalog is active. Behavior is\nunchanged for auth modes that use the local curated marketplace.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `git diff --check`\n\nRust tests were not run per the repository's local verification policy\nfor this narrow conditional change.","tree":{"sha":"a79c50593d90d57675bb482ab697312329c08088","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/a79c50593d90d57675bb482ab697312329c08088"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/38c96866f0213173f98cf102a8efbb5aad5f6543","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNJUWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAg0oQAK/T4MgykCZIlk/SmDMEgINy\nwCP7ckEYpAbeMhFm+2qZSDJMUJ6RLQJvawEW0pAiHXs0GcBQV5emYtOpMwImTv5x\nTF0TBSa2v474wUF1t5K44/Lwjm5LRiD0zYuglPzmzSynwSZ7JieOiUIgmKlRDiQk\n01RXVdWtZxe+MnLK3Xd86xqPEhi4gajQOl3fKtpHL/mZaVTcjGRy310fVGR0ABQk\nfj1XVc51rkbKDa0NXpB02tidJzUGRSZdadD5dn/7rUeQaEQJfaaRRXk/SFhVL9ud\nZFJO1P8Q+KSosYobd6OWVqVAQQwrmcK/PvhTY9nt/U0L49qJxkqpvcsnBne3hveO\nYB5e9Mbj6lor31SJoj5z8nMq1WDqOx3iMpcTj04JS3aVX0Uxn7H7YBHZKFMkAmzJ\ne/TtG1UAT87r5qaeJ3fd1aAhv+/pkpKHIFtIBXlDs045b1TTbtEcSfizNqV93QOO\nL6rnyxXsz9TjLckDaH3UxyZWMf6AoqyOaRLdD6uYZNrfJ5I92Q+UicdpIj0twMXJ\nhrgqeHcaE/F85l07YD3qbSGcFm4oLdLWGfCOgLNRlBwpP6bT2drwRSeEPSkqjNJk\nY5epmfBNBJ0Q8bF4Bhrra1oIwk2rzEl3pIzwz406G59rnP4zqerSC4lGWRxjqsCE\nd/rCLy5nJnsXGm6cUFnf\n=NGNe\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a79c50593d90d57675bb482ab697312329c08088\nparent f00f93d8c0134c49e379af5a946f713f20649c3e\nauthor xl-openai <xl@openai.com> 1781830934 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781830934 -0700\n\n[codex] Skip curated repo sync for remote plugins (#29005)\n\n## Summary\n\n- skip the legacy `openai-curated` startup repository sync when remote\nplugins are enabled and the current auth uses the Codex backend\n- keep the curated sync for API-key, Bedrock, and unauthenticated\nsessions that fall back to the local marketplace\n- preserve configured marketplace upgrades and all remote plugin startup\nwarmups\n\n## Why\n\nThe remote catalog owns plugin discovery and materialization only when\nit is usable for the current auth mode. Starting the legacy curated\nrepository sync in that case performs an unnecessary Git/HTTP/archive\ndownload and cache refresh. API-key and Bedrock sessions still require\nthe local curated marketplace, so they must continue syncing it.\n\n## User impact\n\nCodex startup no longer downloads or refreshes the local\n`openai-curated` snapshot when the remote catalog is active. Behavior is\nunchanged for auth modes that use the local curated marketplace.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `git diff --check`\n\nRust tests were not run per the repository's local verification policy\nfor this narrow conditional change.","verified_at":"2026-06-19T01:02:15Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/38c96866f0213173f98cf102a8efbb5aad5f6543","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/38c96866f0213173f98cf102a8efbb5aad5f6543","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/38c96866f0213173f98cf102a8efbb5aad5f6543/comments","author":{"login":"xl-openai","id":184293535,"node_id":"U_kgDOCvwYnw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184293535?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/xl-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f00f93d8c0134c49e379af5a946f713f20649c3e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f00f93d8c0134c49e379af5a946f713f20649c3e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f00f93d8c0134c49e379af5a946f713f20649c3e"}]},{"sha":"f00f93d8c0134c49e379af5a946f713f20649c3e","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGYwMGY5M2Q4YzAxMzRjNDllMzc5YWY1YTk0NmY3MTNmMjA2NDljM2U","commit":{"author":{"name":"pakrym-oai","email":"pakrym@openai.com","date":"2026-06-19T00:30:55Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-19T00:30:55Z"},"message":"[codex] Assign response item IDs when recording history (#28814)\n\n## Why\n\nClient-created response items enter history without IDs, so their\nidentity is lost across rollout persistence and resume. IDs should be\nassigned once at the history-recording boundary, while IDs returned by\nthe server must remain unchanged.\n\nThe Responses API validates item IDs using type-specific prefixes.\nLocally generated IDs therefore use the matching prefix plus a\nhyphenated UUIDv7, keeping them valid while distinguishable from\nserver-generated IDs. Because this changes persisted history and\nprovider request shapes, the behavior is opt-in behind the\nunder-development `item_ids` feature. Compaction triggers remain request\ncontrols whose API shape does not accept an ID.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Register the disabled-by-default `item_ids` feature and expose it in\n`config.schema.json`.\n- Make supported optional `ResponseItem` IDs serializable and expose\nthem in the generated app-server schemas.\n- When `item_ids` is enabled, assign an ID during conversation-history\npreparation if an item has no ID.\n- Generate type-prefixed, hyphenated UUIDv7 IDs using the Responses API\nitem conventions.\n- Preserve existing server IDs without rewriting them.\n- Persist assigned IDs in rollouts and include them in subsequent\nResponses requests.\n- Remove the unsupported ID field from `CompactionTrigger` and document\nwhy it has no ID.\n- Add integration coverage for enabled ID persistence, preservation of\nserver IDs, and omission of generated IDs while the feature is disabled.\n\n`prepare_conversation_items_for_history` is the single response-item ID\nallocation boundary.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just test -p codex-features`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nresponse_item_ids_persist_across_resume_and_preserve_server_ids`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nnon_openai_responses_requests_omit_item_turn_metadata`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nresize_all_images_prepares_failures_before_history_insertion`\n- `just test -p codex-protocol`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `just test -p codex-api azure_default_store_attaches_ids_and_headers`","tree":{"sha":"f33173135990cc010e8647ee604d852bdfa9be98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/f33173135990cc010e8647ee604d852bdfa9be98"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/f00f93d8c0134c49e379af5a946f713f20649c3e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNI2/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADnsQAEVgK2hBCwaMpKajYO6Rd49o\npT4H/RP4+41+8ctLYZJhpziy0FLYCkSBOZ0008+UzbONSwqT5eVhxS3+cSSVNO6i\nM3PkrlFlfcislw5csux78Eq7u9rV9mGlkDK8c4t3WwByP00rB4yf79ClHiLrW/42\n/QphhsmKcssf/cdSeLmEHxSa7GlZf/lKA+7QynhiI5S878a1fJ9SOUsZaR9TSw3H\nC3JHjY6t+PikI2JEkCCcYoDTl8+CMdDlB/UCJQaSxyMfnM4HSjB6UOVPPdPk/xCr\nmkoM8l6sZmHBND1+EbL41ZotPbiw20uAXOoqcTOdny18RcRmwrEg0+e9dyPoBChl\n+WUz8ElQLujs5CS5bLt5F+RVNHkHZagYXo9kZYGdA9eu5FWw+FZeyXjqzavPcR1Y\n7rZaGOGydW6Z0cwE87SgvuIg+Pk9ODWwhz5Lrgvf2gaWEwrxIQo9qulrtAOk8aRM\n6G2YTRWvOCTxKhIf9Hn89NRHkY88oJ1YLybTJiwij3rAah/rDEpWCcqA7euW8oZC\nL1YkuuAlvKL1bz/qFHVODlYvfnHLiQZyyTf//bP69WwJzkupOYl/SQakDZB0fuxk\nEKIFUT5y4Po+XMiKYxSFHHottvhI2uVttYozsD5JgXRIAzQaxlbWCYW+vEnazlTH\n5FCGH3XpYL8xMWF+p4xl\n=8buY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f33173135990cc010e8647ee604d852bdfa9be98\nparent 8e7c213f8f520c65e65578e59f6a090437bcddaa\nauthor pakrym-oai <pakrym@openai.com> 1781829055 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781829055 -0700\n\n[codex] Assign response item IDs when recording history (#28814)\n\n## Why\n\nClient-created response items enter history without IDs, so their\nidentity is lost across rollout persistence and resume. IDs should be\nassigned once at the history-recording boundary, while IDs returned by\nthe server must remain unchanged.\n\nThe Responses API validates item IDs using type-specific prefixes.\nLocally generated IDs therefore use the matching prefix plus a\nhyphenated UUIDv7, keeping them valid while distinguishable from\nserver-generated IDs. Because this changes persisted history and\nprovider request shapes, the behavior is opt-in behind the\nunder-development `item_ids` feature. Compaction triggers remain request\ncontrols whose API shape does not accept an ID.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Register the disabled-by-default `item_ids` feature and expose it in\n`config.schema.json`.\n- Make supported optional `ResponseItem` IDs serializable and expose\nthem in the generated app-server schemas.\n- When `item_ids` is enabled, assign an ID during conversation-history\npreparation if an item has no ID.\n- Generate type-prefixed, hyphenated UUIDv7 IDs using the Responses API\nitem conventions.\n- Preserve existing server IDs without rewriting them.\n- Persist assigned IDs in rollouts and include them in subsequent\nResponses requests.\n- Remove the unsupported ID field from `CompactionTrigger` and document\nwhy it has no ID.\n- Add integration coverage for enabled ID persistence, preservation of\nserver IDs, and omission of generated IDs while the feature is disabled.\n\n`prepare_conversation_items_for_history` is the single response-item ID\nallocation boundary.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just test -p codex-features`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nresponse_item_ids_persist_across_resume_and_preserve_server_ids`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nnon_openai_responses_requests_omit_item_turn_metadata`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nresize_all_images_prepares_failures_before_history_insertion`\n- `just test -p codex-protocol`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `just test -p codex-api azure_default_store_attaches_ids_and_headers`","verified_at":"2026-06-19T00:30:56Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f00f93d8c0134c49e379af5a946f713f20649c3e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f00f93d8c0134c49e379af5a946f713f20649c3e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f00f93d8c0134c49e379af5a946f713f20649c3e/comments","author":{"login":"pakrym-oai","id":204937752,"node_id":"U_kgDODDcaGA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204937752?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/pakrym-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8e7c213f8f520c65e65578e59f6a090437bcddaa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8e7c213f8f520c65e65578e59f6a090437bcddaa","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8e7c213f8f520c65e65578e59f6a090437bcddaa"}]},{"sha":"8e7c213f8f520c65e65578e59f6a090437bcddaa","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDhlN2MyMTNmOGY1MjBjNjVlNjU1NzhlNTlmNmEwOTA0MzdiY2RkYWE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Peter Bakkum","email":"pbakkum@openai.com","date":"2026-06-19T00:11:21Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-19T00:11:21Z"},"message":"Always use AVAS for realtime WebRTC calls (#28856)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Remove the realtime `architecture` selector from core protocol,\napp-server protocol, config parsing, generated schemas, and callers.\n- Always create WebRTC realtime calls with the AVAS query params:\n`intent=quicksilver&architecture=avas`.\n- Keep direct websocket realtime behavior on the existing config/default\npath, while WebRTC starts without an explicit version now default to\nrealtime v1 because AVAS requires v1.\n\n## Notes\n\n- WebRTC realtime now means AVAS. If a caller explicitly asks to start\nWebRTC with realtime v2, Codex rejects that request because the AVAS\nWebRTC path only supports realtime v1. Websocket realtime is separate\nand can still use realtime v2.\n- The old `[realtime] architecture = \"realtimeapi\" | \"avas\"` config knob\nis removed. Local configs that still set it will need to delete that\nline.\n- Some app-server tests that were only trying to exercise realtime v2\nprotocol behavior now use websocket transport, because WebRTC is\nintentionally locked to AVAS/v1. Separate WebRTC tests cover the AVAS\nquery params, v1 startup, SDP flow, and sideband join.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Merged fresh `origin/main` at `83e6a786a2`.\n- `just fmt`\n- `just write-config-schema`\n- `just write-app-server-schema`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `just test -p codex-api -p codex-core -p codex-app-server-protocol -p\ncodex-app-server realtime` (176 passed)\n- `just test -p codex-protocol -p codex-config` (413 passed)","tree":{"sha":"d1ee2d4e966204c1e8ea26ed33e05b650804e227","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/d1ee2d4e966204c1e8ea26ed33e05b650804e227"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/8e7c213f8f520c65e65578e59f6a090437bcddaa","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNIkpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhboQAE1Mu4sXPIXQM+5c7qoDyhsr\nHQQtH2pazMavE6LvLY0FjGKjeFnqRxR9cgNw92JcXJcsrs08tupj0lbXFHcsramH\n2Stc0X5VSKmaSrEdfuNAx2a2qmnWyUILNZbvKlmNFOV0wy+/TzpOwUrACrr/eBDj\nrJ0apWgCHr8tqL0eBc+moVX338zqJhn0sJnFVeEJnFRGHWUhWOeorT1Ft2s3No9U\noL7XoPp8Ev3q0cFvL3BL1ku4YIOQHgmpQp9QU7Ik7YhsUJYT+0whQqo5PhXgAqRT\neln3oHFeh85hZ5BgY997sQa0OUIOwSe4wD3kZFn5pfEKr28QjuYde3zSAMlGRYxY\nZlLZL8IDLb70932OEQiwuhyzQqOke6K69oVvjvGOoHXNIf3y6GnTEDaCaYTz6cxC\ne3pAg1MCk3x3osFAnmPKhuM/InsUJhTDUV67td9e3qXInIHkggd2f8yF1sCLUNPx\nfQLlQzpPF/5nKTE+FtYUOaqCEoctGV4qLwYPoqMyUAbBklDJTjcqan0ASOdsNoh3\n7CuqGpx1Snx6i1FKQCY81DAk9WQtDUpAAm1WK7h8oP6A+jRhvt/5DMdKt9dcUpY/\nzewqHdwLcKEpaWtsBUfOBdX2EpoHwOUbnDTahAp7dqJI4V/XnxsWDZMDF3dtgNab\nYEhgmP3mMx+drpQNTGQu\n=c6ys\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d1ee2d4e966204c1e8ea26ed33e05b650804e227\nparent 7e37354a587920eaf65fbb3c3005f7b8e6c7c208\nauthor Peter Bakkum <pbakkum@openai.com> 1781827881 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781827881 -0500\n\nAlways use AVAS for realtime WebRTC calls (#28856)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Remove the realtime `architecture` selector from core protocol,\napp-server protocol, config parsing, generated schemas, and callers.\n- Always create WebRTC realtime calls with the AVAS query params:\n`intent=quicksilver&architecture=avas`.\n- Keep direct websocket realtime behavior on the existing config/default\npath, while WebRTC starts without an explicit version now default to\nrealtime v1 because AVAS requires v1.\n\n## Notes\n\n- WebRTC realtime now means AVAS. If a caller explicitly asks to start\nWebRTC with realtime v2, Codex rejects that request because the AVAS\nWebRTC path only supports realtime v1. Websocket realtime is separate\nand can still use realtime v2.\n- The old `[realtime] architecture = \"realtimeapi\" | \"avas\"` config knob\nis removed. Local configs that still set it will need to delete that\nline.\n- Some app-server tests that were only trying to exercise realtime v2\nprotocol behavior now use websocket transport, because WebRTC is\nintentionally locked to AVAS/v1. Separate WebRTC tests cover the AVAS\nquery params, v1 startup, SDP flow, and sideband join.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Merged fresh `origin/main` at `83e6a786a2`.\n- `just fmt`\n- `just write-config-schema`\n- `just write-app-server-schema`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `just test -p codex-api -p codex-core -p codex-app-server-protocol -p\ncodex-app-server realtime` (176 passed)\n- `just test -p codex-protocol -p codex-config` (413 passed)","verified_at":"2026-06-19T00:11:21Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8e7c213f8f520c65e65578e59f6a090437bcddaa","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8e7c213f8f520c65e65578e59f6a090437bcddaa","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8e7c213f8f520c65e65578e59f6a090437bcddaa/comments","author":{"login":"bakks","id":1172710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzI3MTA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1172710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bakks","html_url":"https://github.com/bakks","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bakks/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bakks/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bakks/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bakks/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bakks/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bakks/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bakks/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bakks/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bakks/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7e37354a587920eaf65fbb3c3005f7b8e6c7c208","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7e37354a587920eaf65fbb3c3005f7b8e6c7c208","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/7e37354a587920eaf65fbb3c3005f7b8e6c7c208"}]},{"sha":"7e37354a587920eaf65fbb3c3005f7b8e6c7c208","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDdlMzczNTRhNTg3OTIwZWFmNjVmYmIzYzMwMDVmN2I4ZTZjN2MyMDg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Alex Daley","email":"adaley@openai.com","date":"2026-06-19T00:08:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-19T00:08:04Z"},"message":"[plugins] Refresh plugin and tool caches after remote install (#28951)\n\nSummary\n- Refresh the installed remote-plugin snapshot and Codex Apps tools\nafter completing a remote JIT install.\n- Gate `completed: true` on every expected `app_connector_id` appearing\nafter the uncached `tools/list` refresh, while continuing to skip local\nbundle verification for server-side installs.\n- Keep the cached recommendations response and filter refreshed\ninstalled remote IDs locally, so this does not add another\nrecommendations fetch.\n- Add regression coverage for tools appearing after the hard refresh and\nremaining absent after the refresh. The resumed model request sees the\nrefreshed tool router when installation completes.\n\nRoot Cause\n- Remote suggestions from `openai-curated-remote` returned `true` before\ntaking the existing connector refresh path, leaving the resumed turn\nwith the pre-install Apps tool catalog.\n\nValidation\n- `just test -p codex-core request_plugin_install`\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins\nrecommended_plugin_candidates_filter_installed_and_disabled_plugins`\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins`\n- `just fix -p codex-core-plugins`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-core` was not fully clean locally: 2,729 passed,\n26 failed, and 16 skipped. The failures were dominated by local\nSeatbelt/network/timing issues, including plugin-install timeouts under\nfull-suite contention; the focused plugin-install runs pass.","tree":{"sha":"ac8a9d604f1ed065acd0cf19ed3f1e0909660807","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/ac8a9d604f1ed065acd0cf19ed3f1e0909660807"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/7e37354a587920eaf65fbb3c3005f7b8e6c7c208","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNIhkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAR50QADHTbXbndgQK4VfY877jiUX5\nhp7c8pyNavfZsNQ3U0+6LkwZ0JU5Cnpy5lBfAIeFrO3vcxagMLLax/cQe8cStMr4\nu1UBQ1k4xDeaCDGbKNSn3wsxkNHAe1/Poa018n6UWMTXHGyxiVwzqp2ACIb79EFd\n5Kf8H319xDJVzIbBgOxd4hhB1Wlibv4RmSd9Pf7sRLZ5E+GTcA+e33ghCsvjrMjU\nEH47ID/amMzHNrsjzTx/gkR181uDTRva591WwebcNgrww0N79vmhAXQWoUTBwpaH\nxqVY6feb+94rFFrpPO6nW/HRSXwFsqv+jJwCZY9n+raiyF7i1bjky+dUE2uXtVFo\nX6eG0nhJ9yjUTXZTCKxH7mrKvKJk4wisiyNmwPZJjU9e/70AWg5kzEmL3xd/3vt0\nVpwvXLX9Nkq/jJ0F0lvmUKxpBAiNYjgz5HahbyrVQLe5/kwP1+4C10F6hoKzhIuj\nY4Sf7O8Xm7tNguWAfC4p5sWUsEOY4WJUUhNWkKLYbDQeCjqGEA2Yf15QqBXbzMK9\n3mQUchRT7LlIQHUy9m/Rv+tvk90j8mFwP4FhHY78+HqGKuLxlEejjPrgkocC394G\npbMxHOjn3z3l4bB3vHX9pCjeIopHU4AioIrH3F6p1WZ85V9Yu+LRdMpUO3FJy/tK\ng9AsD8iRJq2ZbnS90JxF\n=PVsk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ac8a9d604f1ed065acd0cf19ed3f1e0909660807\nparent 5c12034e424f84af3c1e69f063203b19918fa374\nauthor Alex Daley <adaley@openai.com> 1781827684 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781827684 -0400\n\n[plugins] Refresh plugin and tool caches after remote install (#28951)\n\nSummary\n- Refresh the installed remote-plugin snapshot and Codex Apps tools\nafter completing a remote JIT install.\n- Gate `completed: true` on every expected `app_connector_id` appearing\nafter the uncached `tools/list` refresh, while continuing to skip local\nbundle verification for server-side installs.\n- Keep the cached recommendations response and filter refreshed\ninstalled remote IDs locally, so this does not add another\nrecommendations fetch.\n- Add regression coverage for tools appearing after the hard refresh and\nremaining absent after the refresh. The resumed model request sees the\nrefreshed tool router when installation completes.\n\nRoot Cause\n- Remote suggestions from `openai-curated-remote` returned `true` before\ntaking the existing connector refresh path, leaving the resumed turn\nwith the pre-install Apps tool catalog.\n\nValidation\n- `just test -p codex-core request_plugin_install`\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins\nrecommended_plugin_candidates_filter_installed_and_disabled_plugins`\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins`\n- `just fix -p codex-core-plugins`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-core` was not fully clean locally: 2,729 passed,\n26 failed, and 16 skipped. The failures were dominated by local\nSeatbelt/network/timing issues, including plugin-install timeouts under\nfull-suite contention; the focused plugin-install runs pass.","verified_at":"2026-06-19T00:08:04Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7e37354a587920eaf65fbb3c3005f7b8e6c7c208","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/7e37354a587920eaf65fbb3c3005f7b8e6c7c208","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7e37354a587920eaf65fbb3c3005f7b8e6c7c208/comments","author":{"login":"adaley-openai","id":192042180,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3JUxA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192042180?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adaley-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/adaley-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adaley-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adaley-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adaley-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adaley-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adaley-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adaley-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adaley-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adaley-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adaley-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5c12034e424f84af3c1e69f063203b19918fa374","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5c12034e424f84af3c1e69f063203b19918fa374","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/5c12034e424f84af3c1e69f063203b19918fa374"}]},{"sha":"5c12034e424f84af3c1e69f063203b19918fa374","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDVjMTIwMzRlNDI0Zjg0YWYzYzFlNjlmMDYzMjAzYjE5OTE4ZmEzNzQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"pakrym-oai","email":"pakrym@openai.com","date":"2026-06-19T00:00:49Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-19T00:00:49Z"},"message":"core: add UUIDv7 context window IDs (#28953)\n\n## Why\n\nThe token-budget context currently identifies a context window by its\nthread-local sequence number. A UUIDv7 gives the model a stable opaque\nidentity that remains fixed for a window and rotates when compaction or\n`new_context` starts the next one.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Preserve the existing monotonic value as `window_number` and add a\nUUIDv7 `window_id` to `CompactedItem`.\n- Generate and rotate the UUID with auto-compaction window state,\npersist it alongside the number, and reconstruct it on resume and\nrollback.\n- Accept legacy compacted rollout records where the numeric `window_id`\nrepresented the window number.\n- Use the UUID only in token-budget context; existing request headers\nand metadata continue using `thread_id:window_number`.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-protocol compacted_item::tests`\n- `just test -p codex-core token_budget`","tree":{"sha":"21a7bb329dd2c4f9b59c4b00d74026de3e24896d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/21a7bb329dd2c4f9b59c4b00d74026de3e24896d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/5c12034e424f84af3c1e69f063203b19918fa374","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNIaxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAw+oQAEVqlhbhSjGbnSb5Feo9QFQ4\nX5U7mo34OmgUiaknfj8j9ILfQjwpAEYk892mO0i1/OdnW7UAb8vwbM+4u/cs1hMn\n7EUuoEEhMjEdyzx1plMlN9eENkj3JwjBNb/WizQRr06TjHyX66Dk92HWKcRwlg7k\nwSl/b9asTQhHQ5c1UsBTg0RLofTswo2Py0oQYrHA8snWgmCKuPV4JnJ1Fiee3q6D\nmhVb4N+zTAwx680ovdfuLcNEWu7DO1qHzwZ4RSRsISzAW16HPpEN7hEsk1Zu6TOa\nxTBCWS9QV3qKg6VNYjE9zC+JcYVg4MaN/8+/oKSdLdCTNk1s7lLTanoJJxwUSFhw\nwU/qOmHbjRcjCd2eAkOMPN6SHkLFzNWQucOVb8E5KSoaMhqEavF5bxFL8ztBb2XU\nfEJSP8JGdsU4Ovgu9eYpQv9DnGoY52HS0rNl7wRmV5trRYHGfbMrUGqFE9586cZo\n6mdzfhd4ea4YamFOg0qbCn7iYnZnJ79gDqFg8TAhlJ+InkfHEeIx5ufvmLyZ8C7R\nyp4eXmoPpm3J/fsHekFUMa6OhI0Z5xu4fjmG4wkEcurckBHUfQ/LEPXnQiBcR3G4\n3rhCJ4+/2coVpKrslSsrbFJNP3jhRBvS99QUyyqdz6UCY9/YjWBGtXxjh8srhXb/\nacdWhCUDJ3cwwosp6Eo5\n=peTQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 21a7bb329dd2c4f9b59c4b00d74026de3e24896d\nparent e83b7841b0789d6f8b3252092d44e51a6e0e54ba\nauthor pakrym-oai <pakrym@openai.com> 1781827249 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781827249 -0700\n\ncore: add UUIDv7 context window IDs (#28953)\n\n## Why\n\nThe token-budget context currently identifies a context window by its\nthread-local sequence number. A UUIDv7 gives the model a stable opaque\nidentity that remains fixed for a window and rotates when compaction or\n`new_context` starts the next one.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Preserve the existing monotonic value as `window_number` and add a\nUUIDv7 `window_id` to `CompactedItem`.\n- Generate and rotate the UUID with auto-compaction window state,\npersist it alongside the number, and reconstruct it on resume and\nrollback.\n- Accept legacy compacted rollout records where the numeric `window_id`\nrepresented the window number.\n- Use the UUID only in token-budget context; existing request headers\nand metadata continue using `thread_id:window_number`.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-protocol compacted_item::tests`\n- `just test -p codex-core token_budget`","verified_at":"2026-06-19T00:00:50Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5c12034e424f84af3c1e69f063203b19918fa374","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/5c12034e424f84af3c1e69f063203b19918fa374","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5c12034e424f84af3c1e69f063203b19918fa374/comments","author":{"login":"pakrym-oai","id":204937752,"node_id":"U_kgDODDcaGA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204937752?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/pakrym-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e83b7841b0789d6f8b3252092d44e51a6e0e54ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e83b7841b0789d6f8b3252092d44e51a6e0e54ba","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e83b7841b0789d6f8b3252092d44e51a6e0e54ba"}]},{"sha":"e83b7841b0789d6f8b3252092d44e51a6e0e54ba","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGU4M2I3ODQxYjA3ODlkNmY4YjMyNTIwOTJkNDRlNTFhNmUwZTU0YmE","commit":{"author":{"name":"xl-openai","email":"xl@openai.com","date":"2026-06-18T23:45:58Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-18T23:45:58Z"},"message":"[codex] Reuse parsed plugin skills during session startup (#28844)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Preserve raw plugin skill-root snapshots in the matching loaded-plugin\ncache entry, keyed by the effective plugin root identity including\nnamespace.\n- Pass those snapshots through `SkillsLoadInput` as an optional preload,\nso session startup reuses plugin parsing while ordinary skill loads pass\n`None`.\n- Keep plugin skill loading cohesive: the existing loaders accept the\noptional snapshots directly, and uncached or marketplace-detail paths do\nnot create a cache.\n\n## Why\n\nPlugin discovery already parses plugin skills to determine available\ncapabilities. Cold session startup then scanned and parsed the same\nroots again while building the skills snapshot.\n\nThis solves the same duplicate-work problem as #28623 while keeping\nownership narrow: `PluginsManager` creates and owns\n`PluginSkillSnapshots` only for its loaded-plugin cache entry;\n`SkillsService` consumes an optional clone. Entry replacement or\nclearing naturally drops the snapshots, with no separate generation,\ncapacity policy, or watcher coupling.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `cargo clippy -p codex-core-skills --all-targets -- -D warnings`\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins\nskills_service_reuses_skills_parsed_during_plugin_load`\n- `just test -p codex-core-skills\nnamespaces_plugin_skills_using_provided_namespace`\n- `just fmt`","tree":{"sha":"0f3c6fe67566aed54b016c7885dc09bc58a9e9c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/0f3c6fe67566aed54b016c7885dc09bc58a9e9c1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/e83b7841b0789d6f8b3252092d44e51a6e0e54ba","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNIM2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXLIQAK7nINhrZUFU54PG5D2OogSV\n7TWOzfIhm1Va9PsMkgW8RUxr5zw4hC99ETDgBNHOv1OFw7exQQxts/KJXAiruKgV\nQ41qmvrGeTpvCCFydX+hYCIKYWHMwO1Me3Gdjr+gS9UnpMngNh7eQpdqCVDVAaY8\n7dggp2HCe6fOTYmAoCMXPqsZXvIOBFhSgvWm4Zzbq0XGRpNR3b9G9mR3R7oa6gR3\nkgAE4e8GoHPfNG+0e4VQeq+GxxvKfNQgIP4RoSASkk8H3yNPVkBWrLrPJSezJxT+\nStp9CEU5H1fTwTP97zCVBVf8qZ/aht8+H5fwA6NVmxorrcRYvApM9dFVPAOPLiJu\nCol2nm00fnCQom1eIVKxMMN/ArYFvDm8+AsSztBcIArjjVX94PA30cIdPtnIloy0\nZolbAHt3fGtZKW95u5NzT3ekDqIv0bWxF/ugHHivNo5NjI9AD/TenHPPRTCoLPBk\nGlS0NXeVKE4pqw5aYYMzaWlXc0TleZs96/WY8Kdww1hwfjU8pTEdz4nNPCf3Vu29\nEopJ+cSstDN2aoc4pQlUqpIRjwULD1bkV+LaV5qN+Lf8UZ/xW4/zN4pf8mUp7+dR\nK3lQ9LOOD1xuuTL6KduMREJgNzNuAxSzQrxMZ746G08gqzS/CvWsyLOJ9d4nfsRr\nDphrlwxXX29NLuzkBT2V\n=P6qP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0f3c6fe67566aed54b016c7885dc09bc58a9e9c1\nparent 346d2c163ff9191a37dc5f198ccd3cdd731430cc\nauthor xl-openai <xl@openai.com> 1781826358 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781826358 -0700\n\n[codex] Reuse parsed plugin skills during session startup (#28844)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Preserve raw plugin skill-root snapshots in the matching loaded-plugin\ncache entry, keyed by the effective plugin root identity including\nnamespace.\n- Pass those snapshots through `SkillsLoadInput` as an optional preload,\nso session startup reuses plugin parsing while ordinary skill loads pass\n`None`.\n- Keep plugin skill loading cohesive: the existing loaders accept the\noptional snapshots directly, and uncached or marketplace-detail paths do\nnot create a cache.\n\n## Why\n\nPlugin discovery already parses plugin skills to determine available\ncapabilities. Cold session startup then scanned and parsed the same\nroots again while building the skills snapshot.\n\nThis solves the same duplicate-work problem as #28623 while keeping\nownership narrow: `PluginsManager` creates and owns\n`PluginSkillSnapshots` only for its loaded-plugin cache entry;\n`SkillsService` consumes an optional clone. Entry replacement or\nclearing naturally drops the snapshots, with no separate generation,\ncapacity policy, or watcher coupling.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `cargo clippy -p codex-core-skills --all-targets -- -D warnings`\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins\nskills_service_reuses_skills_parsed_during_plugin_load`\n- `just test -p codex-core-skills\nnamespaces_plugin_skills_using_provided_namespace`\n- `just fmt`","verified_at":"2026-06-18T23:45:59Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e83b7841b0789d6f8b3252092d44e51a6e0e54ba","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e83b7841b0789d6f8b3252092d44e51a6e0e54ba","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e83b7841b0789d6f8b3252092d44e51a6e0e54ba/comments","author":{"login":"xl-openai","id":184293535,"node_id":"U_kgDOCvwYnw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184293535?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/xl-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"346d2c163ff9191a37dc5f198ccd3cdd731430cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/346d2c163ff9191a37dc5f198ccd3cdd731430cc","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/346d2c163ff9191a37dc5f198ccd3cdd731430cc"}]},{"sha":"346d2c163ff9191a37dc5f198ccd3cdd731430cc","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDM0NmQyYzE2M2ZmOTE5MWEzN2RjNWYxOThjY2QzY2RkNzMxNDMwY2M","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-18T23:39:21Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-18T23:39:21Z"},"message":"core: keep remote exec on reported shell (#28983)\n\n## Why\n\nWe need to avoid resolving shells on the app-server's host for remote\nenvironments. We might make it possible to do fancier shell resolution\nfrom remote envs but for now just require the model to produce a shell\nthat matches the environment's default.\n\nThis gets my e2e demo working for shell commands after #28854 moved\nshell resolution to PathUri and caused remote envs to hit the fallback\nshell when the shell wasn't available on the host.\n\n## What\n\nRemote `exec_command` calls now accept only the environment's reported\ndefault shell name or exact path, and execute with that reported path.\nOther explicit shells return a concise error. A Wine-backed integration\ntest covers explicit PowerShell execution in the Windows cwd.","tree":{"sha":"8f1fd7227f04f704baf6a9feb024964a42acb098","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/8f1fd7227f04f704baf6a9feb024964a42acb098"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/346d2c163ff9191a37dc5f198ccd3cdd731430cc","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNIGpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyuQQAER0/zQlFzVxe/9nwkmRZxaF\n+cPXvskRkYd+TGWQIYkZ/mwq7SGf6ZFNWXrj3qkDjcazvVyAK6QNXsPlvggt8JD1\nSBdMeUCc94LjwAhGl8QsYEyzNJWzDPdC+f6LxdlczPnUFTCIPvb3PBPWayBd4ikV\ngrvSdSSFBA0eHYOUnXWAfn9LglG5XTXeBYu186iKGEsCAlUXqSJYdRfo0Eg/CA/6\ntTBw2n5IHapnyZ7k9jYPDBfWlc3wdM5NuGVNdOq+6ymvLZkh82NLybXhCaT7guZF\naLLDREpFWaVwjJdxGfrhT1xAwu78TTuxD6w6Wjg21sBj6RHgSx6CpV+FHXT6JdPz\nDSMnNKOjZLLQ7t9Bt6izlUJyuzgcocGmbjVYxQUkosMuwgzJTpKwO98sA8gDOpk4\nz2tHWQTYyW+B8Zsv69WzguALVJ7YLZO900zzgZGDXU6B4aCZPcMv0dcCF8sA0ySB\nhTar4DXOdiKypjZEacOH5sHAXcR5WxibLaBGtYuX5HZFrXEQ9DB+Pg98291oPtvj\no7hVvuJteWVHvy6aLwtarSm5jPV7OMkWCn9ujyp55IpvSXgMc9uJU5tbuGoF4C6A\nMOlE1KjqNc3T1JTElMkJCKaHItna7MhSFHwiY5jmDNhPO2vd5V6ApjWpWazg/14J\nucB91qnaw9S7eVZGZke3\n=SGFM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8f1fd7227f04f704baf6a9feb024964a42acb098\nparent 195c936fa2cef6b5c88d74f90d5f83840058ca27\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1781825961 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781825961 +0000\n\ncore: keep remote exec on reported shell (#28983)\n\n## Why\n\nWe need to avoid resolving shells on the app-server's host for remote\nenvironments. We might make it possible to do fancier shell resolution\nfrom remote envs but for now just require the model to produce a shell\nthat matches the environment's default.\n\nThis gets my e2e demo working for shell commands after #28854 moved\nshell resolution to PathUri and caused remote envs to hit the fallback\nshell when the shell wasn't available on the host.\n\n## What\n\nRemote `exec_command` calls now accept only the environment's reported\ndefault shell name or exact path, and execute with that reported path.\nOther explicit shells return a concise error. A Wine-backed integration\ntest covers explicit PowerShell execution in the Windows cwd.","verified_at":"2026-06-18T23:39:21Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/346d2c163ff9191a37dc5f198ccd3cdd731430cc","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/346d2c163ff9191a37dc5f198ccd3cdd731430cc","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/346d2c163ff9191a37dc5f198ccd3cdd731430cc/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"195c936fa2cef6b5c88d74f90d5f83840058ca27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/195c936fa2cef6b5c88d74f90d5f83840058ca27","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/195c936fa2cef6b5c88d74f90d5f83840058ca27"}]},{"sha":"195c936fa2cef6b5c88d74f90d5f83840058ca27","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDE5NWM5MzZmYTJjZWY2YjVjODhkNzRmOTBkNWY4Mzg0MDA1OGNhMjc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-18T23:16:19Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-18T23:16:19Z"},"message":"core: log AGENTS.md paths as URIs (#28989)\n\n## Why\n\nNo need to do path contortions when it's for our own logs.\n\n## What\n\nFollow up on a previous PR's nit and update the path-types skill for\nfuture reference.","tree":{"sha":"4f316b30f3b832fc22aabf924ccc68a67db363c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/4f316b30f3b832fc22aabf924ccc68a67db363c0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/195c936fa2cef6b5c88d74f90d5f83840058ca27","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNHxDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMZcQAKRdt41DZ4sBzbZlj63UvSsI\nvAdwtnW4aZEme8cusO2P34goi/5JZQP/hmwxw9qemKGgDgG8yR6qKhY/QyNjVPbS\nhKwmwRuwtQOIBTBEvdvBsKXXKx4lBaHQ59UiuBj1jaGzbYYp8fUtHDSIc59dWL/N\nKcL0CQ6BL6Jn6isc9iJLFSHOZViF+HHnySaVQ4n1HwofS57CBFjqjR4oU5dzC1jr\ntODFgrTct1PQPGtFiC2Nz4Iw+rtYaxyiD4BrAee9ziFAltxRLvNOmGEhXMSZsVOi\nooDY/vICSNVZsuRSHOH6H8WI90l7oaIBvPSZtyHOzsQBE9gUU3BowL23aZJiz8mX\nRMy6LDq7g3GEYo8o8WjpCBvVpUmgXivVzDB1fl9d8JqQYgAfuM2