pe":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"bb72e151e50cfd4f6282ab86418188af3c83b5df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bb72e151e50cfd4f6282ab86418188af3c83b5df","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/bb72e151e50cfd4f6282ab86418188af3c83b5df"}]},{"sha":"bb72e151e50cfd4f6282ab86418188af3c83b5df","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGJiNzJlMTUxZTUwY2ZkNGY2MjgyYWI4NjQxODE4OGFmM2M4M2I1ZGY","commit":{"author":{"name":"pakrym-oai","email":"pakrym@openai.com","date":"2026-06-18T23:13:07Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-18T23:13:07Z"},"message":"[codex] Remove child AGENTS.md prompt experiment (#28993)\n\n## Why\n\n`child_agents_md` is a disabled, under-development experiment that adds\na second model-visible explanation of hierarchical `AGENTS.md` behavior.\nKeeping it leaves unused prompt, configuration, documentation, and test\nsurface.\n\n## What changed\n\n- remove the `ChildAgentsMd` feature and `child_agents_md` config schema\nentry\n- remove the hierarchical prompt asset, export, and instruction\ninjection\n- remove feature-specific tests and documentation\n- keep the generic unstable-feature warning coverage using\n`apply_patch_streaming_events`\n\nNormal project `AGENTS.md` discovery and composition are unchanged.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-features`\n- `just test -p codex-prompts`\n- `just test -p codex-core agents_md`\n- `just test -p codex-core unstable_features_warning`","tree":{"sha":"5edd9a07b35f827fe131aed3789160ba19355a83","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/5edd9a07b35f827fe131aed3789160ba19355a83"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/bb72e151e50cfd4f6282ab86418188af3c83b5df","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNHuDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArF4QAF3SDIH2EcoP4LHTq2CWmEXt\nTzF7RxPuG2GvTY8E0m+TcBQYLITqaxNDMrx0+glRRKQtgNtm41r5dIuAp36WB1Da\nXUhe1dAKcN4UXNGmSK8XaYuL0nm/Rpmy7RwBedqUyfmkpoTE3v56zqf7VCf+dOSo\nY7o93o2Iq6HTg4QLVMoQFKEODsqthzVlxm5aJ1038E2IbElye38sNPHOPI3yLKXW\neUs34azsG2EIkHwcQNGp+fDIAAf2NZud1A3qWQ6y20SYSlBlyr4NZB0Ib0Pjbvgl\nswEFpEPiiIu49GvHy1AJGVSe1IO+pKozqlE2QegRnC/VHDaPkCpS2GEVeiwr8TdV\nK/Peec2gEqvlVl6c3hxatkj4La1OncMjYuG4gqFGJcuUOO2jImJOl9wVy1QeuFEQ\nyy8V4ms/MEZ3XasE/emOiv9ro5WTtaARasMBYZtkiuZBSauVPwutIepKgjs1Buv1\nECaBLjpKAdgJrHW87QTI5I6wT6U76kspvqovexvY1wobLUU+vNUkdOC/B79oq2ic\nyMZGNALzyHZX4aO7mbW+eMuZp9eZW2iDBHswQtOog816mX3SecQ927BeNPdmKXsT\nL+5k2JKPeFin0bM0fMSd53TiKvrIBH8CljOxg+q2Mx8VwQkJzP8V9ORB8W8CoyvI\nkSj+YSIUviWNFWRMtXlP\n=8CWG\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5edd9a07b35f827fe131aed3789160ba19355a83\nparent 772c5c51952a8bd279dbeeedfea69a6feb837a1d\nauthor pakrym-oai <pakrym@openai.com> 1781824387 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781824387 -0700\n\n[codex] Remove child AGENTS.md prompt experiment (#28993)\n\n## Why\n\n`child_agents_md` is a disabled, under-development experiment that adds\na second model-visible explanation of hierarchical `AGENTS.md` behavior.\nKeeping it leaves unused prompt, configuration, documentation, and test\nsurface.\n\n## What changed\n\n- remove the `ChildAgentsMd` feature and `child_agents_md` config schema\nentry\n- remove the hierarchical prompt asset, export, and instruction\ninjection\n- remove feature-specific tests and documentation\n- keep the generic unstable-feature warning coverage using\n`apply_patch_streaming_events`\n\nNormal project `AGENTS.md` discovery and composition are unchanged.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-features`\n- `just test -p codex-prompts`\n- `just test -p codex-core agents_md`\n- `just test -p codex-core unstable_features_warning`","verified_at":"2026-06-18T23:13:08Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bb72e151e50cfd4f6282ab86418188af3c83b5df","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/bb72e151e50cfd4f6282ab86418188af3c83b5df","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bb72e151e50cfd4f6282ab86418188af3c83b5df/comments","author":{"login":"pakrym-oai","id":204937752,"node_id":"U_kgDODDcaGA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204937752?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/pakrym-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"772c5c51952a8bd279dbeeedfea69a6feb837a1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/772c5c51952a8bd279dbeeedfea69a6feb837a1d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/772c5c51952a8bd279dbeeedfea69a6feb837a1d"}]},{"sha":"772c5c51952a8bd279dbeeedfea69a6feb837a1d","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDc3MmM1YzUxOTUyYThiZDI3OWRiZWVlZGZlYTY5YTZmZWI4MzdhMWQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"charlesgong-openai","email":"charlesgong@openai.com","date":"2026-06-18T22:49:27Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-18T22:49:27Z"},"message":"[codex] Support marketplace plugin manifest fallback (#28789)\n\n## Summary\n\nSupport marketplace plugins whose source directory does not include a\ndiscoverable plugin manifest. Metadata-rich `marketplace.json` entries\nnow act as fallback plugin manifests for listing, local detail reads,\ninstall, and non-curated cache refresh.\n\nThe fallback preserves marketplace-entry plugin fields wholesale, then\nadds the small Codex-facing compatibility bridge for presentation\nmetadata. A real source `plugin.json` always wins when present.\n\n## Details\n\n- Capture flattened marketplace-entry fields into\n`MarketplacePluginManifestFallback`, preserving fields such as\n`version`, `description`, `skills`, `mcpServers`, `apps`, `hooks`,\n`agents`, `commands`, `strict`, `author`, and future manifest fields\nwithout a per-field translation list.\n- Bridge Claude-style top-level `displayName`, `author.name`,\n`homepage`, and marketplace `category` into Codex's nested `interface`\nfields only when the nested values are absent.\n- Treat fallback metadata as installable only when the marketplace entry\ncontributes metadata beyond bare `name` and `source`; existing\nmissing-manifest behavior remains for metadata-free entries.\n- Read local plugin details from the already parsed fallback manifest,\nincluding fallback-declared app and MCP paths, instead of rereading only\nan on-disk manifest.\n- Pass fallback contents into `PluginStore`, which validates them and\ninjects `.codex-plugin/plugin.json` into Store's existing atomic copy.\nLocal marketplace source directories are never mutated, and the fallback\npath no longer needs an additional staging directory.\n- Keep Git source materialization unchanged; Git clones still use the\nexisting marketplace source staging area before Store installation.","tree":{"sha":"b8d3394a42cfc240dec1fa1a5481934d966af6f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/b8d3394a42cfc240dec1fa1a5481934d966af6f6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/772c5c51952a8bd279dbeeedfea69a6feb837a1d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNHX3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIAEQAHV9kImhjo9l+NIljuvvshOO\n7XL+kFhcVE9Iex+WGsH6cEMFxFUEdI5O+10CE7ZmPVXQfzUKcyNyfiG/8zUi8aBf\n+4WIUzLkFqTSPh5x94TxmB+8xJjrZj7r7F8cVq7uPEoPIHo7qGdVM5htPgdU29kK\n+X3kVoSztOxh5zlK/eido4ch1B6QKeSHMjtViNGtsZjD2nBOiLBmMcslpoBh4c3R\nqSuIKXKc3qkJAmK8/tzJpZV2V9sLJmKmV4DqGQBqp6ZwN5EnFraNa8uz4ZFm7pr2\nOb/sTx63fU0zBpunRqqshTZonE5URH0E2A5F9Oc2Mb9AAkLHoQVGekFHg+nX+vBx\n+xdKVmu+nWeXo/L923avLmDfQb7P3HMjHnnLexZR1YtF4rU5M+CMboE9ML0Utll3\nV3KNrxg3khdcfzwoWvS0mEUncRSe/GN9+Gd8bSXW2HYolVhpvcgnzCjKuK5Ll/GA\nXbZRBh0SUENxq63GBjCp0MIppeVkYzhJO7DG3iqCbZdBwtyrCM1Hh0qKZj2NMJ7Z\nOSZwI4ZfelWzCz3mdER+kmSO0joOBEs5IpqIxCoLxgtCXOqjRkKO/cED57xgUjot\nhJxS9WOSZ1DYqhlsYs+waV8ixrgSf0lwdFwxVNRwLhtoOkSxEdSSXYgb9FugP7hG\nIHorz1tKuCVFZhMFuAtM\n=CNsA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b8d3394a42cfc240dec1fa1a5481934d966af6f6\nparent dce673905a191744138dbba19a7d3f8d85b10d6c\nauthor charlesgong-openai <charlesgong@openai.com> 1781822967 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781822967 -0700\n\n[codex] Support marketplace plugin manifest fallback (#28789)\n\n## Summary\n\nSupport marketplace plugins whose source directory does not include a\ndiscoverable plugin manifest. Metadata-rich `marketplace.json` entries\nnow act as fallback plugin manifests for listing, local detail reads,\ninstall, and non-curated cache refresh.\n\nThe fallback preserves marketplace-entry plugin fields wholesale, then\nadds the small Codex-facing compatibility bridge for presentation\nmetadata. A real source `plugin.json` always wins when present.\n\n## Details\n\n- Capture flattened marketplace-entry fields into\n`MarketplacePluginManifestFallback`, preserving fields such as\n`version`, `description`, `skills`, `mcpServers`, `apps`, `hooks`,\n`agents`, `commands`, `strict`, `author`, and future manifest fields\nwithout a per-field translation list.\n- Bridge Claude-style top-level `displayName`, `author.name`,\n`homepage`, and marketplace `category` into Codex's nested `interface`\nfields only when the nested values are absent.\n- Treat fallback metadata as installable only when the marketplace entry\ncontributes metadata beyond bare `name` and `source`; existing\nmissing-manifest behavior remains for metadata-free entries.\n- Read local plugin details from the already parsed fallback manifest,\nincluding fallback-declared app and MCP paths, instead of rereading only\nan on-disk manifest.\n- Pass fallback contents into `PluginStore`, which validates them and\ninjects `.codex-plugin/plugin.json` into Store's existing atomic copy.\nLocal marketplace source directories are never mutated, and the fallback\npath no longer needs an additional staging directory.\n- Keep Git source materialization unchanged; Git clones still use the\nexisting marketplace source staging area before Store installation.","verified_at":"2026-06-18T22:49:27Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/772c5c51952a8bd279dbeeedfea69a6feb837a1d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/772c5c51952a8bd279dbeeedfea69a6feb837a1d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/772c5c51952a8bd279dbeeedfea69a6feb837a1d/comments","author":{"login":"charlesgong-openai","id":200841148,"node_id":"U_kgDOC_iXvA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/200841148?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/charlesgong-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"dce673905a191744138dbba19a7d3f8d85b10d6c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/dce673905a191744138dbba19a7d3f8d85b10d6c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/dce673905a191744138dbba19a7d3f8d85b10d6c"}]},{"sha":"dce673905a191744138dbba19a7d3f8d85b10d6c","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGRjZTY3MzkwNWExOTE3NDQxMzhkYmJhMTlhN2QzZjhkODViMTBkNmM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-18T22:06:23Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-18T22:06:23Z"},"message":"core: load AGENTS.md from foreign environments (#28958)\n\n## Why\n\nMake it possible to load AGENTS.md from remote exec-servers whose OS is\ndifferent than app-server.\n\n## What\n\n- keep `AGENTS.md` discovery and provenance as `PathUri`, with\nroot-aware parent and ancestor traversal\n- expose lifecycle instruction sources as legacy app-server path strings\nin events while retaining `PathUri` internally\n- preserve and test mixed POSIX and Windows paths in model context and\nTUI status output\n- cover remote Windows loading end to end by seeding the Wine prefix\nthrough host filesystem APIs\n- fix bug in `PathUri`'s parent() implementation that would erase\nWindows drive letters","tree":{"sha":"7bee2b5fdb3fae9a496e1890a7284004c0bf7501","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/7bee2b5fdb3fae9a496e1890a7284004c0bf7501"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/dce673905a191744138dbba19a7d3f8d85b10d6c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNGvfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALPIQACo+CNCUWXnIaBssDVOCZRWm\nxS3K6UIZDPyv1goMarmxgBjaK1EXnBbuHz6ypK1u7/k+juIO9dy1T1sDWuWbZJVN\nXBs3qnqZUuoK60vgUcojf8DfB8WH7dCcgrSK8uVnJN3TJKRy92EtA4kDar0w2RKl\niwpXf3tYzENX9sBIZ/roQkFlg2lu0Lhl0sIf8xpxmQFwj+eo2EBAO0nijOCJxPbR\nPjPf+wUnFEXNdIACalAdlJuWJVPnHf8//prgdzlsmQdZYF/nxYjNzQzHQF4IcnJW\nf1qXoGuvWeGilpb7+bC+AgkMzIeCUOeaA3CrEkmkLjVE4ZhnaiIOe+xsPOMHXxjJ\nb3h+RDJ4fXe9/+eETLrFz+WRq6Db4Uc5i1loXtAEsKmVb0k4J7BetDZopKnohxcq\nPE2SFo8rSrbWL9bb4S7wxyCbO65qYYCygd1A/4qQ8F8Xc0QiWXRT8q4azI0kxNgf\nTXfIe4p6ESZp85h2Yn09bxr/3pO6shDI1wrao46pW4gCeqZATf90n1jt+4UL+f+I\nLhsajEJT3FQnbV4pYWTLIS0B77J4742nuBUvm12NlhLIwhZYaOCqgSFirKoFTFIe\n8RR/md1LdPakade6LK5p/qqfJ3tWkTMEsqUQG3Ewv0jHh/MSg25Dlpt1jCtyNzvU\ncbqhG+MU477ljy5Gj8QO\n=kPVF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7bee2b5fdb3fae9a496e1890a7284004c0bf7501\nparent 406062c3af8b27c8e1b4b83c485ebe1ae0df874c\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1781820383 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781820383 -0700\n\ncore: load AGENTS.md from foreign environments (#28958)\n\n## Why\n\nMake it possible to load AGENTS.md from remote exec-servers whose OS is\ndifferent than app-server.\n\n## What\n\n- keep `AGENTS.md` discovery and provenance as `PathUri`, with\nroot-aware parent and ancestor traversal\n- expose lifecycle instruction sources as legacy app-server path strings\nin events while retaining `PathUri` internally\n- preserve and test mixed POSIX and Windows paths in model context and\nTUI status output\n- cover remote Windows loading end to end by seeding the Wine prefix\nthrough host filesystem APIs\n- fix bug in `PathUri`'s parent() implementation that would erase\nWindows drive letters","verified_at":"2026-06-18T22:06:24Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/dce673905a191744138dbba19a7d3f8d85b10d6c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/dce673905a191744138dbba19a7d3f8d85b10d6c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/dce673905a191744138dbba19a7d3f8d85b10d6c/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"406062c3af8b27c8e1b4b83c485ebe1ae0df874c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/406062c3af8b27c8e1b4b83c485ebe1ae0df874c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/406062c3af8b27c8e1b4b83c485ebe1ae0df874c"}]},{"sha":"406062c3af8b27c8e1b4b83c485ebe1ae0df874c","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDQwNjA2MmMzYWY4YjI3YzhlMWI0YjgzYzQ4NWViZTFhZTBkZjg3NGM","commit":{"author":{"name":"xl-openai","email":"xl@openai.com","date":"2026-06-18T21:29:01Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-18T21:29:01Z"},"message":"[codex] Preserve remote plugin download status errors (#28863)\n\n## Summary\n\n- preserve the original HTTP status when a remote plugin bundle download\nreturns a non-success response\n- retain at most 8 KiB of the error response body and annotate\ntruncation or body-read failures\n- add regression coverage for an oversized error response\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe non-success response path reused the normal size-limited body\nreader. When an error response exceeded 8 KiB, that reader returned\n`DownloadTooLarge` before the code constructed `DownloadStatus`, masking\nthe upstream HTTP status and response context.\n\n## Impact\n\nRemote plugin installation failures now retain the actionable upstream\nHTTP status without allowing unbounded error bodies into logs.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nplugin_install_preserves_status_when_remote_bundle_error_body_is_too_large`\n- `just fmt`\n- `git diff --check`","tree":{"sha":"f07bfc548f9a277f872fe2ee1ec27d8f4012a885","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/f07bfc548f9a277f872fe2ee1ec27d8f4012a885"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/406062c3af8b27c8e1b4b83c485ebe1ae0df874c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNGMdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEi8QACnaWhXZmF0jJhiU8Tq1wOkV\nAWIvri5RIya+o8yKwPcO9FXl4/pMNpQyxSCS/XiYXcC1BW9DBMjMf7x1R+7rnD01\n3x58FArvMrBmAqy/nPTPneMat3LtVtFynyeZWVVpUTWkJ/U3L0LWfn7dSPUSB52B\nPYOaLvpWcKFjac9uApB4zhxoBDNX3PEV6tcp207cPYTdAk8pGzj7R/erbOonLmHq\nfLWVM48ihfTywKgf+QQM33l7CpTTjillw3mwzTXL+ZAXLgyn/bf3WsOiGIap+GQG\nCC1CUUPoc3ox4nwudItD9K4yauCsIbpnSk4CQ1U/DWXd2VivOMCsYtcfw/gyQUcC\nnOaBDbCi2AHK5yCHwec+cbwML/U5vF3mE46DtkDcmrz+ZAcBSmqTngiGtNpZoOvi\nSbwhqXSQ66rXWXKVzm7SrH5Oh6UBVw4FgQzC2AiZVBvCLIzQdEeyW123bkoPw3P9\nr0295sLMTVAi7ovsfpvNjydBaYzdSTEyUTSXtjCyXhvqPe/9Yhap0YHrG25UOifz\n5TkTvTfWbIIhcwdmXcA1Ias+s0JzFf7JfU0o0bjPPJbiXjqjvLUW1u+PljLsPCR0\n3SnRbu1dfEhe9h98iNu2oitwIFEOJ3ef0x2y1NCu38sFWj6m4pnap09kCWdRDmR6\nu3NJjEHjI/ILh/0Jecgr\n=zVa/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f07bfc548f9a277f872fe2ee1ec27d8f4012a885\nparent 4af7762f0129e903461a351cc1e6daa79cb0cea0\nauthor xl-openai <xl@openai.com> 1781818141 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781818141 -0700\n\n[codex] Preserve remote plugin download status errors (#28863)\n\n## Summary\n\n- preserve the original HTTP status when a remote plugin bundle download\nreturns a non-success response\n- retain at most 8 KiB of the error response body and annotate\ntruncation or body-read failures\n- add regression coverage for an oversized error response\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe non-success response path reused the normal size-limited body\nreader. When an error response exceeded 8 KiB, that reader returned\n`DownloadTooLarge` before the code constructed `DownloadStatus`, masking\nthe upstream HTTP status and response context.\n\n## Impact\n\nRemote plugin installation failures now retain the actionable upstream\nHTTP status without allowing unbounded error bodies into logs.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nplugin_install_preserves_status_when_remote_bundle_error_body_is_too_large`\n- `just fmt`\n- `git diff --check`","verified_at":"2026-06-18T21:29:02Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/406062c3af8b27c8e1b4b83c485ebe1ae0df874c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/406062c3af8b27c8e1b4b83c485ebe1ae0df874c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/406062c3af8b27c8e1b4b83c485ebe1ae0df874c/comments","author":{"login":"xl-openai","id":184293535,"node_id":"U_kgDOCvwYnw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184293535?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/xl-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4af7762f0129e903461a351cc1e6daa79cb0cea0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4af7762f0129e903461a351cc1e6daa79cb0cea0","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4af7762f0129e903461a351cc1e6daa79cb0cea0"}]},{"sha":"4af7762f0129e903461a351cc1e6daa79cb0cea0","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDRhZjc3NjJmMDEyOWU5MDM0NjFhMzUxY2MxZTZkYWE3OWNiMGNlYTA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Alex Daley","email":"adaley@openai.com","date":"2026-06-18T21:19:24Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-18T21:19:24Z"},"message":"[connectors] Ignore synthetic links for app accessibility (#28770)\n\nSummary\n- Stop treating Codex Apps MCP tools with\n`_meta._codex_apps.synthetic_link: true` as evidence that a connector is\naccessible in `app/list`.\n- Preserve synthetic tools in the agent-facing MCP connector set so they\nremain available for install/auth flows.\n- Keep the app-list accessibility cache limited to connectors backed by\nat least one non-synthetic tool.\n- Add focused regression coverage for both sides of the boundary.\n\nValidation\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nsynthetic_links_are_exposed_to_the_agent_but_not_accessible_in_app_list`\n- `git diff --check`\n- A crate-wide `just test -p codex-core` run completed with 2,699\npassing and 51 unrelated local sandbox/state failures, primarily state\nDB migration races (`UNIQUE constraint failed:\n_sqlx_migrations.version`).","tree":{"sha":"cde4052eca4b8c7898d8bdd83c1bfb51cb33c31f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/cde4052eca4b8c7898d8bdd83c1bfb51cb33c31f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/4af7762f0129e903461a351cc1e6daa79cb0cea0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNGDcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAh9kQAATB8HCpN5R8fnNPo5/CtF5q\nVLjAfKpYHOF893QTgiSfzH6yP/s9Cwxob5JtnSuEmj/KSnAos6JsRAwG77RTwUvr\n8cuY0G2bqgnoX/DbDuKDxRPmV8Ie78F/f1nXS6T96Ryb5Z0xD2dG4zNPOYOy50iK\nv7u6ut4Rtx07MAQ7Gq272lcLD1L5PX8TxhgvjduArdrXERjZF3D7R4UijKUrIzNQ\nGPFxzbeWQZkZtcCnpXEx7pnSU8XRWu1toBLo30VkDkm5ZX/1y1ivHZ7a5N+4XsBr\n9CaAyvodAZJsn6OrDUJ2eVroaId5V65YxSDoXFDA23iTObhF5Q6SmuinM9BIfCgj\n70soTnteLTmik9qN88sY8s0w6k3gaApE2PHGs2zoia2iU30A96hDCd1G1NRYfZQR\n39LXf/gnPvvySar8NPeEzvtuHWJXAVVlERj602nN5pEAOr0alBHc5yVNvxAi/2Ou\ne1ycU48NoNyfh8gekmnfDhqYsTsfBhZsw2mm8jByoTNgUDXWByKW1/hSHrwvl0C/\noiQRrYINU9z9h5f32ASIlvESxL1PmGa/+x4JiEcnfkBW6NXktGiJJ22kOk3piHID\nwr7ZlWJjSghf2LH6d7+A5gtiR5jaKf8sMXD2SW+1tmv39gRGasio3QBHy6ZNgNDg\n4JUx9ArawMftgOZm0z55\n=ibBs\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree cde4052eca4b8c7898d8bdd83c1bfb51cb33c31f\nparent ec848dde0e0b264ee6d703a43baeeae624bba98e\nauthor Alex Daley <adaley@openai.com> 1781817564 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781817564 -0400\n\n[connectors] Ignore synthetic links for app accessibility (#28770)\n\nSummary\n- Stop treating Codex Apps MCP tools with\n`_meta._codex_apps.synthetic_link: true` as evidence that a connector is\naccessible in `app/list`.\n- Preserve synthetic tools in the agent-facing MCP connector set so they\nremain available for install/auth flows.\n- Keep the app-list accessibility cache limited to connectors backed by\nat least one non-synthetic tool.\n- Add focused regression coverage for both sides of the boundary.\n\nValidation\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nsynthetic_links_are_exposed_to_the_agent_but_not_accessible_in_app_list`\n- `git diff --check`\n- A crate-wide `just test -p codex-core` run completed with 2,699\npassing and 51 unrelated local sandbox/state failures, primarily state\nDB migration races (`UNIQUE constraint failed:\n_sqlx_migrations.version`).","verified_at":"2026-06-18T21:19:25Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4af7762f0129e903461a351cc1e6daa79cb0cea0","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4af7762f0129e903461a351cc1e6daa79cb0cea0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4af7762f0129e903461a351cc1e6daa79cb0cea0/comments","author":{"login":"adaley-openai","id":192042180,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3JUxA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192042180?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adaley-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/adaley-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adaley-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adaley-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adaley-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adaley-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adaley-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adaley-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adaley-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adaley-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adaley-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ec848dde0e0b264ee6d703a43baeeae624bba98e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ec848dde0e0b264ee6d703a43baeeae624bba98e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ec848dde0e0b264ee6d703a43baeeae624bba98e"}]},{"sha":"ec848dde0e0b264ee6d703a43baeeae624bba98e","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGVjODQ4ZGRlMGUwYjI2NGVlNmQ3MDNhNDNiYWVlYWU2MjRiYmE5OGU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adrian","email":"145513011+adrian-openai@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-18T21:05:27Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-18T21:05:27Z"},"message":"feat: opt ChatGPT auth into agent identity (#19049)\n\n## Stack\n\nThis is PR 2 of the simplified HAI single-run-task stack:\n\n- [#19047](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/19047) Agent Identity\nassertion and task-registration primitives, including the shared\nrun-task helper used by existing Agent Identity JWT auth.\n- [#19049](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/19049)\nDisabled-by-default ChatGPT auth opt-in that provisions/reuses persisted\nAgent Identity runtime auth and its single run task.\n- [#19051](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/19051) Run-scoped\nprovider auth that uses one backend-owned task id for first-party\ninference and compaction requests.\n\n[#19054](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/19054) collapsed out of\nthe active stack because the simplified design no longer needs a\nseparate background/control-plane task helper.\n\n## Summary\n\nThis PR adds the disabled-by-default path for normal ChatGPT-login Codex\nsessions to obtain Agent Identity runtime auth through the Codex\nbackend. Existing Agent Identity JWT startup mode remains a separate\npath and does not require the feature flag.\n\nWhat changed:\n\n- adds the experimental `use_agent_identity` feature flag and config\nschema entry\n- adds an explicit `AgentIdentityAuthPolicy` so call sites choose\n`JwtOnly` or `ChatGptAuth` instead of passing a bare boolean\n- stores standalone Agent Identity JWT credentials separately from\nbackend-registered Agent Identity records\n- persists the registered Agent Identity record, private key, and single\nrun task id in `auth.json` so process restarts reuse the same identity\n- derives the agent/task registration base URL from ChatGPT/Codex auth\nconfig while keeping JWT JWKS lookup separate\n- provisions and caches ChatGPT-derived Agent Identity runtime auth when\n`use_agent_identity` is enabled\n- reuses the shared run-task registration helper from PR1 rather than\nadding a second task-registration path\n\nThis PR intentionally does not switch model inference over to\n`AgentAssertion` auth. The provider-auth integration lands in the next\nPR.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-login`","tree":{"sha":"a50378ea6f4e9f48f894ba21b7e5a2f9acfdb576","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/a50378ea6f4e9f48f894ba21b7e5a2f9acfdb576"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/ec848dde0e0b264ee6d703a43baeeae624bba98e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNF2XCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASMIQAAPk/rlUiYxAtIfDiXd0iqI1\nbEjusZheQc2XYnoZx3Nml3IJfp4nKw7AVyrsESNOC+avjr6FWx4vyMMOxZcusodh\nInvdOFNuQc0nZZs0KYd4wZmVBbWT/hZiY+Eo/AqujUUGocX0dbe8+ZGVOkFLYfaH\nVAPIgVPjslPRBe47m3Z+7gQJTs3w22YGMqQ+4+aeyl2srZ8IDFPkI7hJIH29yvM7\nsITqY5oR1LxdA+tmvC0gCyjf8a4YOzitYIe/sRzMptf4UFRUvoQDs01Rs6OTtx+t\ndjJRG+387JYbSlQuyb4ecb/uvnBtVDykk29REAw9D43HAERu6d8iqCjln08Cqp71\nf0GXNhZbWF0zAlNO8PEkXoxiHEt59v4V7RW7FU2ZwOEZoD3w7AqOAQZU5jJ3AO7Z\ny15Pd54O+j/yUI/Y8u66HF9S+6bWgGaNf0o8H7+E4c+bjxtLrCnKF0fKKFA3S/y2\nL5Ub84wqYkObR2XbRwBQLAw+2RlOFsfwInXAWasTHkCc3hqyNyO89vYFZhLdSBSm\nGudDU638POz1Qai/5BMCyl5HsJcEL8IJKRx17DTjKqSJFBOmekpKw6Cr8vxA0sxT\naKNLF5Lzgn7UdLCqOMNe/5sXUS8lRnjan2CwGN57k0jfYL/ArTzdl+ea1HDhsnrf\nf6NP051RLVbkda+z8Yqz\n=hjMk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a50378ea6f4e9f48f894ba21b7e5a2f9acfdb576\nparent 765309d5a611ea02be842ead0ab1a2828196fae9\nauthor Adrian <145513011+adrian-openai@users.noreply.github.com> 1781816727 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781816727 -0700\n\nfeat: opt ChatGPT auth into agent identity (#19049)\n\n## Stack\n\nThis is PR 2 of the simplified HAI single-run-task stack:\n\n- [#19047](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/19047) Agent Identity\nassertion and task-registration primitives, including the shared\nrun-task helper used by existing Agent Identity JWT auth.\n- [#19049](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/19049)\nDisabled-by-default ChatGPT auth opt-in that provisions/reuses persisted\nAgent Identity runtime auth and its single run task.\n- [#19051](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/19051) Run-scoped\nprovider auth that uses one backend-owned task id for first-party\ninference and compaction requests.\n\n[#19054](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/19054) collapsed out of\nthe active stack because the simplified design no longer needs a\nseparate background/control-plane task helper.\n\n## Summary\n\nThis PR adds the disabled-by-default path for normal ChatGPT-login Codex\nsessions to obtain Agent Identity runtime auth through the Codex\nbackend. Existing Agent Identity JWT startup mode remains a separate\npath and does not require the feature flag.\n\nWhat changed:\n\n- adds the experimental `use_agent_identity` feature flag and config\nschema entry\n- adds an explicit `AgentIdentityAuthPolicy` so call sites choose\n`JwtOnly` or `ChatGptAuth` instead of passing a bare boolean\n- stores standalone Agent Identity JWT credentials separately from\nbackend-registered Agent Identity records\n- persists the registered Agent Identity record, private key, and single\nrun task id in `auth.json` so process restarts reuse the same identity\n- derives the agent/task registration base URL from ChatGPT/Codex auth\nconfig while keeping JWT JWKS lookup separate\n- provisions and caches ChatGPT-derived Agent Identity runtime auth when\n`use_agent_identity` is enabled\n- reuses the shared run-task registration helper from PR1 rather than\nadding a second task-registration path\n\nThis PR intentionally does not switch model inference over to\n`AgentAssertion` auth. The provider-auth integration lands in the next\nPR.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-login`","verified_at":"2026-06-18T21:05:27Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ec848dde0e0b264ee6d703a43baeeae624bba98e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ec848dde0e0b264ee6d703a43baeeae624bba98e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ec848dde0e0b264ee6d703a43baeeae624bba98e/comments","author":{"login":"adrian-openai","id":145513011,"node_id":"U_kgDOCKxaMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/145513011?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrian-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/adrian-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrian-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrian-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrian-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrian-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrian-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrian-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrian-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrian-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrian-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"765309d5a611ea02be842ead0ab1a2828196fae9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/765309d5a611ea02be842ead0ab1a2828196fae9","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/765309d5a611ea02be842ead0ab1a2828196fae9"}]},{"sha":"765309d5a611ea02be842ead0ab1a2828196fae9","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDc2NTMwOWQ1YTYxMWVhMDJiZTg0MmVhZDBhYjFhMjgyODE5NmZhZTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"martinauyeung-oai","email":"martinauyeung@openai.com","date":"2026-06-18T21:02:54Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-18T21:02:54Z"},"message":"Emit Trusted MCP App Identity on Tool-Call Items (#27132)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Add optional `appContext` to app-server MCP tool-call items with\ntrusted `connectorId`, `linkId`, and `mcpAppResourceUri` metadata.\n- Preserve that context across tool-call events, persisted history,\nreconnects, and thread resume.\n- Keep the deprecated top-level `mcpAppResourceUri` temporarily for\nclient migration.\n\nThe consumer contract is `{ appContext: { connectorId, linkId,\nmcpAppResourceUri }, tool }`.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Full GitHub Actions suite passes, including CLA, Bazel tests, clippy,\nrelease builds, and argument-comment lint.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: martinauyeung-oai <280153141+martinauyeung-oai@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"a436ef1fb676048022739377ab17228ee371e54d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/a436ef1fb676048022739377ab17228ee371e54d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/765309d5a611ea02be842ead0ab1a2828196fae9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNFz+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAt3MQAKpEHVcyOKqm5uCKPKvQRb8o\n1otOiJ/cRwcIi6nv92mX9c4zTf0WnfdC9ipQVL+BZKFkMsxU4gEOw4ioPoZjn4n0\nn4GXE6tLbOudLdWeb8PtKizgn18YirI2xzLYxLd0S4hh/fOi9aXBXJkUrqYw9gJ3\nS+vAjNfyA/ikiUCnlawr/aaX1gZIzAEZJbYW6D/RduYIk8WI1bHdgwbNg7o5mSWt\njkPwP8CJxIilaPL7jinHs5i05zjLUJxq+kItJKHIOoZ8XkH3+5yT1A4CjM82Nq5T\nsX1+iZvtY9iUW43ui7pDGto561exLevoi7g6jc9YmVpgPU8XCrb2jQjs9XSbjKhV\n/uy15y2LOfV+dZBUwImGm96Hg9VWjvtySnXXPo1+gG2txGFG8RmC0hDOlO+6VllL\nRERd09/djCvjD9aczhIi5zSOMfIYV9jeXIEqq0PoTWH/kA7Mszw7BvEG4gWAHLgr\noikqnpSLM+sRY7h1YyjwZhqnlugs66hgwGI1HCU0ZZUtDJbeP/GNIzpxHIcjTpDA\n3OrboMx1xABneISlsJFQ1blPdisrYLQpQBhWwYZo4pMqTy5BsG9MLeaEh7SrH84u\nuRypd5X1TtVuzJO9v87iesVrYQmTfcIKncXjzK90eybeTjt4x2XQISggEuUrvsRf\nVJnCsf6n9u6uH0Pp6sHd\n=n+Fp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a436ef1fb676048022739377ab17228ee371e54d\nparent 9bcc09f9f7b529cb9547a1cf9f15d6288762e2e1\nauthor martinauyeung-oai <martinauyeung@openai.com> 1781816574 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781816574 -0700\n\nEmit Trusted MCP App Identity on Tool-Call Items (#27132)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Add optional `appContext` to app-server MCP tool-call items with\ntrusted `connectorId`, `linkId`, and `mcpAppResourceUri` metadata.\n- Preserve that context across tool-call events, persisted history,\nreconnects, and thread resume.\n- Keep the deprecated top-level `mcpAppResourceUri` temporarily for\nclient migration.\n\nThe consumer contract is `{ appContext: { connectorId, linkId,\nmcpAppResourceUri }, tool }`.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Full GitHub Actions suite passes, including CLA, Bazel tests, clippy,\nrelease builds, and argument-comment lint.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: martinauyeung-oai <280153141+martinauyeung-oai@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-18T21:02:55Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/765309d5a611ea02be842ead0ab1a2828196fae9","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/765309d5a611ea02be842ead0ab1a2828196fae9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/765309d5a611ea02be842ead0ab1a2828196fae9/comments","author":{"login":"martinauyeung-oai","id":280153141,"node_id":"U_kgDOELLMNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/280153141?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/martinauyeung-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/martinauyeung-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martinauyeung-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martinauyeung-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martinauyeung-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martinauyeung-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martinauyeung-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martinauyeung-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martinauyeung-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martinauyeung-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martinauyeung-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9bcc09f9f7b529cb9547a1cf9f15d6288762e2e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9bcc09f9f7b529cb9547a1cf9f15d6288762e2e1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9bcc09f9f7b529cb9547a1cf9f15d6288762e2e1"}]},{"sha":"9bcc09f9f7b529cb9547a1cf9f15d6288762e2e1","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDliY2MwOWY5ZjdiNTI5Y2I5NTQ3YTFjZjlmMTVkNjI4ODc2MmUyZTE","commit":{"author":{"name":"canvrno-oai","email":"kbond@openai.com","date":"2026-06-18T20:37:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-18T20:37:04Z"},"message":"TUI: improve unified mention selection visibility (#28959)\n\n## Summary\n\n[@milanglacier reported in\n#28653](https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/28653) that the active\nmention candidate is hard to distinguish. I suspect [@binbjz’s #28500\nreport](https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/28500) _(where arrow-key\nnavigation appeared not to work)_ may describe the same presentation\nproblem: the selection may have been changing, but the UI was not\nshowing the active row clearly in their terminal. This PR makes two\nsmall changes to the selection indication behavior:\n\n- Reserve a two-character gutter and mark the active candidate with `> `\nfor color-agnostic indicator coverage.\n- Apply the shared theme-aware accent to the entire selected row for\nextra emphasis.\n- Update the existing popup snapshot.\n\nReverse-video styling was considered, but avoided it because it is\noverly dependent on the user’s terminal palette.\n\n<img width=\"2046\" height=\"482\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b5eb62c3-fd24-4c09-906e-7bd66913b5c6\"\n/>\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-tui default_unified_mention_popup_snapshot`\n- `just clippy -p codex-tui`\n- `just fmt`\n- Compiled `codex-cli` and tested the unified mentions picker in the\nterminal.","tree":{"sha":"0f4e8f69726a4eacda2b3aebc2c89e3a574c9d4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/0f4e8f69726a4eacda2b3aebc2c89e3a574c9d4e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/9bcc09f9f7b529cb9547a1cf9f15d6288762e2e1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNFbwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFWMQACGMsNk3ErZctAYInmX1yHo6\nDC+Qg/TCi8gh5or0QtMWYZJY4XSYqaOifOi/DpCFNO3flk/Kk9xZmfa1OmHYEETG\nkVt1u4QZdSaxFEe5v4D+T32NPz22Ue6MhG2Q8J5dJlSEnCRCdgI3wFoN/ODrEx38\nCfP35+qIE7QJL1yk2j8b+NdAppMQx9lt0cJBcg9ceH7M5eWetyZZ3CudOrQAoyGO\nhkPKpZtRTRfmAN/MMxsAK3+RE+EzxCnQueHF9+8+emVYXRw1SQIczgwGiyGVzp1k\nxeD4iGqwtE6L/VMneDrKNVbUAJ+nvqxrbi+28gctv37nyFKxGxeIpu2u4gtwUAPm\ncfXojsKy38Y2dkqvoR7me1+Fct/T6PCr//LIANEEaA1AViLO9l8PEorF+HBJxmNt\nXLWXpcpYgpuJLdtp0ADnfrzEaLJJkoF6Gv6btAPGmpccWbownRq+hRTtw2kNEe2r\n6vX2StHZI6Lp4IZklNpuOSg7ef+V/dGnlTYYb+7LBtFR7KyddyknPk+QzQj9bopk\nISINSV61YxBmiICAlCXVWMWNaubvHDln5j0tv8eSFFOU3sj8QSzkIN5n90FJmwXX\n4GbFhAM9bBDWqhCLXw5Uv3+LxVhmVIXkXkDXQEpb8lBzoBvTr8HfaUwzEoMriwfz\neS6wtPgekPOQdfz4MvSF\n=IO9x\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0f4e8f69726a4eacda2b3aebc2c89e3a574c9d4e\nparent 29eb434bc5fd81f29540446f6989219736b09a80\nauthor canvrno-oai <kbond@openai.com> 1781815024 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781815024 -0700\n\nTUI: improve unified mention selection visibility (#28959)\n\n## Summary\n\n[@milanglacier reported in\n#28653](https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/28653) that the active\nmention candidate is hard to distinguish. I suspect [@binbjz’s #28500\nreport](https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/28500) _(where arrow-key\nnavigation appeared not to work)_ may describe the same presentation\nproblem: the selection may have been changing, but the UI was not\nshowing the active row clearly in their terminal. This PR makes two\nsmall changes to the selection indication behavior:\n\n- Reserve a two-character gutter and mark the active candidate with `> `\nfor color-agnostic indicator coverage.\n- Apply the shared theme-aware accent to the entire selected row for\nextra emphasis.\n- Update the existing popup snapshot.\n\nReverse-video styling was considered, but avoided it because it is\noverly dependent on the user’s terminal palette.\n\n<img width=\"2046\" height=\"482\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b5eb62c3-fd24-4c09-906e-7bd66913b5c6\"\n/>\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-tui default_unified_mention_popup_snapshot`\n- `just clippy -p codex-tui`\n- `just fmt`\n- Compiled `codex-cli` and tested the unified mentions picker in the\nterminal.","verified_at":"2026-06-18T20:37:05Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9bcc09f9f7b529cb9547a1cf9f15d6288762e2e1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9bcc09f9f7b529cb9547a1cf9f15d6288762e2e1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9bcc09f9f7b529cb9547a1cf9f15d6288762e2e1/comments","author":{"login":"canvrno-oai","id":257630656,"node_id":"U_kgDOD1shwA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257630656?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/canvrno-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"29eb434bc5fd81f29540446f6989219736b09a80","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/29eb434bc5fd81f29540446f6989219736b09a80","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/29eb434bc5fd81f29540446f6989219736b09a80"}]},{"sha":"29eb434bc5fd81f29540446f6989219736b09a80","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDI5ZWI0MzRiYzVmZDgxZjI5NTQwNDQ2ZjY5ODkyMTk3MzZiMDlhODA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Ning","email":"ericning@openai.com","date":"2026-06-18T20:29:01Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-18T20:29:01Z"},"message":"[codex] Remove hardcoded app ID filters (#28947)\n\n## Summary\n\n- remove the duplicated originator-specific connector ID denylists\n- stop filtering connector directory/accessibility results and\nlive/cached Codex Apps MCP tools by hardcoded connector ID\n- remove the now-unused `codex-login` dependency from\n`codex-utils-plugins`\n- update regression coverage so formerly blocked connector IDs are\npreserved\n\n## Why\n\nThe client-side policy was duplicated across crates, used opaque IDs\nwithout ownership or expiry information, and could drift between app\nlisting and MCP tool behavior. Server-provided visibility,\nauthorization, plugin discoverability, accessibility, enabled-state\nhandling, and consequential-tool approval templates remain unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just bazel-lock-update`\n- `just bazel-lock-check`\n- `git diff --check`\n- confirmed the final diff contains no hardcoded denylist symbols\n\nA targeted `codex-mcp` test build spent an unusually long time in local\ncompilation/linking. Its first attempt exposed a test-only `PartialEq`\nassertion issue, which was corrected. A follow-up non-linking `cargo\ncheck -p codex-mcp --tests` was still running when this draft was\nopened; CI should provide the complete Rust validation.","tree":{"sha":"f0748c887a92f13a77a8cad49deaf6395b1e69f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/f0748c887a92f13a77a8cad49deaf6395b1e69f6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/29eb434bc5fd81f29540446f6989219736b09a80","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNFUNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARHsQAFlta0wJbwbdLuJE4B+POSmZ\nGkRFEqIJv52H1Mh6h74HxfTrCFDu0RmYdIJdMa74DSQLEyczQaNz7jFWJf69NJvj\nPLOAbWdIXv+s8V3jufM8bsvWq5maEgjorGtMW/H7FPoDth5RyBjuDdWNMBG+tgEp\nlk7NQZJz5e0RoHee+KjA/TSD3KMU19eSOWsCJGbOqdm7ZqraMNyRB2vmN5fSuLq3\n6Pkw+UGy6aXnj6uH3iVTgmkNlopsWnbe96QpzYjlWvPVVyASP3FOCbWo+OcX1jK3\n0Nti2plQ3NhPoBG03LU1WFRrhlfh77o3moN2dMsqKH2jtNPfPqFmfYhBsVdZTzuW\nnSfQw5TkfV/JqViv7sVmv46jk0Q0kw67o3ZTAQ/GirvhcYNKK314AQz9v9tpeY1y\nO8hSJ8iV79Hn4pCwCSVKHuxasP+m+UHxQahczlJgnL3FBW6qF8yIbNvY/MF4bgcP\nwTFA+3GeMyhy3mfoKaBgtKBzDbCbZZ9aFSByYNGQF/A0C4Gp/XL457D7gubiJx/L\n+dgXxOmI+gRGTbnviv/qY4YJYGlD97ExIGMWro9CGroaczy14zLqo5qote42UfpP\nHt9qfLCNdnU6pt2YB/cvDYJ83xAIa01ifqAkxkozRd3xRe5DU9dz0hiTDtYNbX7x\nfXNBHsfqmao+nLaz8sc0\n=wb8x\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f0748c887a92f13a77a8cad49deaf6395b1e69f6\nparent d9dace8a593080572fdef4a8fbdad7f2c7fe226f\nauthor Eric Ning <ericning@openai.com> 1781814541 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781814541 +0000\n\n[codex] Remove hardcoded app ID filters (#28947)\n\n## Summary\n\n- remove the duplicated originator-specific connector ID denylists\n- stop filtering connector directory/accessibility results and\nlive/cached Codex Apps MCP tools by hardcoded connector ID\n- remove the now-unused `codex-login` dependency from\n`codex-utils-plugins`\n- update regression coverage so formerly blocked connector IDs are\npreserved\n\n## Why\n\nThe client-side policy was duplicated across crates, used opaque IDs\nwithout ownership or expiry information, and could drift between app\nlisting and MCP tool behavior. Server-provided visibility,\nauthorization, plugin discoverability, accessibility, enabled-state\nhandling, and consequential-tool approval templates remain unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just bazel-lock-update`\n- `just bazel-lock-check`\n- `git diff --check`\n- confirmed the final diff contains no hardcoded denylist symbols\n\nA targeted `codex-mcp` test build spent an unusually long time in local\ncompilation/linking. Its first attempt exposed a test-only `PartialEq`\nassertion issue, which was corrected. A follow-up non-linking `cargo\ncheck -p codex-mcp --tests` was still running when this draft was\nopened; CI should provide the complete Rust validation.","verified_at":"2026-06-18T20:29:01Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/29eb434bc5fd81f29540446f6989219736b09a80","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/29eb434bc5fd81f29540446f6989219736b09a80","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/29eb434bc5fd81f29540446f6989219736b09a80/comments","author":{"login":"ericning-o","id":182030612,"node_id":"U_kgDOCtmRFA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/182030612?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o","html_url":"https://github.com/ericning-o","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d9dace8a593080572fdef4a8fbdad7f2c7fe226f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d9dace8a593080572fdef4a8fbdad7f2c7fe226f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d9dace8a593080572fdef4a8fbdad7f2c7fe226f"}]},{"sha":"d9dace8a593080572fdef4a8fbdad7f2c7fe226f","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGQ5ZGFjZThhNTkzMDgwNTcyZmRlZjRhOGZiZGFkN2YyYzdmZTIyNmY","commit":{"author":{"name":"maja-openai","email":"163171781+maja-openai@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-18T20:16:14Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-18T20:16:14Z"},"message":"Make auto-review on-request prompt more proactive (#26496)\n\n## Why\n\n`on-request` approval policy text is currently tuned for user-reviewed\napprovals. For auto-reviewed productivity runs, likely sandbox blocks\nshould be escalated earlier so commands that need remote services,\nauthentication, or other out-of-sandbox access do not first fail or hang\ninside the sandbox.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Adds a separate `on_request_auto_review.md` permissions prompt\nselected for `AskForApproval::OnRequest` with\n`ApprovalsReviewer::AutoReview`.\n- Keeps the normal user-reviewed `on-request` wording unchanged.\n- Makes the `When to request escalation` bullets more explicit about\nlikely sandbox blocks, network access, remote\nauth/cluster/cloud/database access, out-of-sandbox environment access,\ngit operations that may write lock files, and short-timeout reruns after\nlikely sandbox-blocked attempts.\n- Omits approved command prefix and `prefix_rule` guidance for the\nauto-review on-request prompt.\n- Adds prompt tests covering the auto-review path, normal on-request\nwording, and inline permission request behavior.","tree":{"sha":"312ba88d1645e33fcdf05ed9dc5c1e657c2be603","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/312ba88d1645e33fcdf05ed9dc5c1e657c2be603"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/d9dace8a593080572fdef4a8fbdad7f2c7fe226f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNFIOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyJ0QAJkRoup0x5obbbrdnagWrZg1\nE6O0zLAAUVc2oOwWsIfdDLqYtSyKl0rqfBLCeFozQL6Nk567gxzoEQFdl9CGsgEv\nNbdaJgRtOKihyVElzyYZVB0jkFDOCf6NE1C2aiyLZKvMwoqNgkvTUKHmh19rL33n\ntJEEbWDmTRpzravpmSy+tjFebHxutCeNug/dH69IU5vOYdvOsKagVXHUckPCbL+U\nKZvQedmeUUhOihZd71DOJpxcqieZXBbWjgynVt5M2rgQdBruSXuBCwlMMcFoXl1o\nZ8xYActPD9BqZ+3aqy/Es8BItlZBwnxUILfnvQGPSXqLXv/OPlGS8D5TG+NqmO76\nd7CMJWr4/2W/yz8s6BOB92BF2skjoFcj/rSfyLTCBwVbDZY52vQYziolVcYhEHP9\nzKrQZDPOrdq163TzVJazV3uKs9jgphT8lYIlq/I6/lmK4SdNFIc9/h/LTSrBZbnR\nCCVa1dE3JL/QtjhvuK048i6HoIf5jVk9uqwxTkWPFAKwWIeG064c8dNTI5O3NxHg\niBIG5m1C0aIjRT+83X7uOE8F9gn0QGqECyC3SZgIvwGYVPVws4ByDLsr3ZpHU4VR\nBjhlOG0mxOz+jRf+TJuoDC4E77H6eZnnGRTDJt4O1c9Zvi6NurnOrAmlUdmvWCUU\niOx5BFAPVfFSB7nFkdh+\n=OaJh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 312ba88d1645e33fcdf05ed9dc5c1e657c2be603\nparent f4602b7516a28c09c89349300799ef347bbf7668\nauthor maja-openai <163171781+maja-openai@users.noreply.github.com> 1781813774 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781813774 -0700\n\nMake auto-review on-request prompt more proactive (#26496)\n\n## Why\n\n`on-request` approval policy text is currently tuned for user-reviewed\napprovals. For auto-reviewed productivity runs, likely sandbox blocks\nshould be escalated earlier so commands that need remote services,\nauthentication, or other out-of-sandbox access do not first fail or hang\ninside the sandbox.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Adds a separate `on_request_auto_review.md` permissions prompt\nselected for `AskForApproval::OnRequest` with\n`ApprovalsReviewer::AutoReview`.\n- Keeps the normal user-reviewed `on-request` wording unchanged.\n- Makes the `When to request escalation` bullets more explicit about\nlikely sandbox blocks, network access, remote\nauth/cluster/cloud/database access, out-of-sandbox environment access,\ngit operations that may write lock files, and short-timeout reruns after\nlikely sandbox-blocked attempts.\n- Omits approved command prefix and `prefix_rule` guidance for the\nauto-review on-request prompt.\n- Adds prompt tests covering the auto-review path, normal on-request\nwording, and inline permission request behavior.","verified_at":"2026-06-18T20:16:14Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d9dace8a593080572fdef4a8fbdad7f2c7fe226f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d9dace8a593080572fdef4a8fbdad7f2c7fe226f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d9dace8a593080572fdef4a8fbdad7f2c7fe226f/comments","author":{"login":"maja-openai","id":163171781,"node_id":"U_kgDOCbnNxQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/163171781?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maja-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/maja-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maja-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maja-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maja-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maja-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maja-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maja-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maja-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maja-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maja-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f4602b7516a28c09c89349300799ef347bbf7668","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f4602b7516a28c09c89349300799ef347bbf7668","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f4602b7516a28c09c89349300799ef347bbf7668"}]},{"sha":"f4602b7516a28c09c89349300799ef347bbf7668","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGY0NjAyYjc1MTZhMjhjMDljODkzNDkzMDA3OTllZjM0N2JiZjc2Njg","commit":{"author":{"name":"rka-oai","email":"rka@openai.com","date":"2026-06-18T20:12:11Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-18T20:12:11Z"},"message":"Add app-server current-time impl (varlatency 3/n) (#28835)\n\n## What\n\nServer should request:\n\n```\n{\n  \"id\": 42,\n  \"method\": \"currentTime/read\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"threadId\": \"11111111-1111-1111-1111-aaaaafdc2c11\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nClient should respond with something like:\n\n```rust\n{\n  \"id\": 42,\n  \"result\": {\n    \"currentTimeAt\": 1781717655\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Why\n\nSessions configured with `clock_source = \"external\"` need a\nthread-specific external time source before inference. The system clock\nremains the default production provider.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `cargo test -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `cargo test -p codex-app-server --test all\ncurrent_time_read_round_trip_adds_reminder_to_model_input`\n- `cargo test -p codex-app-server\nfirst_attestation_capable_connection_for_thread_only_uses_thread_subscribers`\n- `cargo test -p codex-analytics`\n- `just fix -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `just fix -p codex-app-server`\n\nStacked on #28824.","tree":{"sha":"04c322528a9a4488f30a2a0fe5264b285b772d4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/04c322528a9a4488f30a2a0fe5264b285b772d4c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/f4602b7516a28c09c89349300799ef347bbf7668","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNFEbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6TQQAGPQ5mMC5nEQGD1CsaT0V8mx\nDzjxmxZD1KuZ2XDAspaYA9XAVcx+ljIf4fTjP1ZxSodDPh1XDNDVC6imhb1qCWSK\nlei0VIBmb/aaqBXOpfadU7FBmrfhd2sCu27k/K/WKe4erxsNpP5UKfAIOdDL2LN9\nFsUaZOJxVUzaVdwICQULQUezNWASl/d5l+WFqkKApIiJJt6HDddVopWwzChuOjYG\ngNlqFMzS+OjTATQqG2KoyBiTRD3E7VH2jrEBK3Db8Nfda+OVVz7WQUgIUM/Zqbta\nbVM+u+M/I4h7g1exo5nHj3mmL1L8FJ5vWJ3F/PRSsK37o+bSoWAEopgNapKlRzjO\nAqqObzlI2ZIxlP0W0OhxA+lhx5oJMiCeE8642d/OB0f7I5gOcj4vhLaOTdYAkX2z\n7o9NwDixiZb34wls8h79B5hXbROOTCDLUL2mAyxSQmcub2G7Iys4qnmx3ZGVor8z\nkdphKqBXhQIm2+uSv/IuOlkh6qcqYDmT77XlpzdhIHIFvKh1oOwWSrUu9lGt+UrI\n7ZR2/bdaChxgJO8YA3GIfkkb3eOxYCN5uxsDSPXN466Blfl8so0SqV2/k0PI7TbR\nki5fWpQIyoHLD1FbGcdwODKSr/CGq0XIStpCEaV05C7avx/KADNhE6AQvy7nAGIa\nprqJtP0HDH+yqS8b6Bic\n=R5XX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 04c322528a9a4488f30a2a0fe5264b285b772d4c\nparent 0f89dd768c16549162f0005c4d77654e29f33f6e\nauthor rka-oai <rka@openai.com> 1781813531 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781813531 -0700\n\nAdd app-server current-time impl (varlatency 3/n) (#28835)\n\n## What\n\nServer should request:\n\n```\n{\n  \"id\": 42,\n  \"method\": \"currentTime/read\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"threadId\": \"11111111-1111-1111-1111-aaaaafdc2c11\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nClient should respond with something like:\n\n```rust\n{\n  \"id\": 42,\n  \"result\": {\n    \"currentTimeAt\": 1781717655\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Why\n\nSessions configured with `clock_source = \"external\"` need a\nthread-specific external time source before inference. The system clock\nremains the default production provider.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `cargo test -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `cargo test -p codex-app-server --test all\ncurrent_time_read_round_trip_adds_reminder_to_model_input`\n- `cargo test -p codex-app-server\nfirst_attestation_capable_connection_for_thread_only_uses_thread_subscribers`\n- `cargo test -p codex-analytics`\n- `just fix -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `just fix -p codex-app-server`\n\nStacked on #28824.","verified_at":"2026-06-18T20:12:11Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f4602b7516a28c09c89349300799ef347bbf7668","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f4602b7516a28c09c89349300799ef347bbf7668","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f4602b7516a28c09c89349300799ef347bbf7668/comments","author":{"login":"rka-oai","id":240799229,"node_id":"U_kgDODlpN_Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/240799229?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/rka-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0f89dd768c16549162f0005c4d77654e29f33f6e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0f89dd768c16549162f0005c4d77654e29f33f6e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/0f89dd768c16549162f0005c4d77654e29f33f6e"}]},{"sha":"0f89dd768c16549162f0005c4d77654e29f33f6e","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDBmODlkZDc2OGMxNjU0OTE2MmYwMDA1YzRkNzc2NTRlMjlmMzNmNmU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-18T19:31:19Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-18T19:31:19Z"},"message":"apply-patch: carry paths as PathUri (#28854)\n\n## Why\n\nAllows the model to edit files that are hosted on a different OS than\nwhere app-server is running.\n\n## What\n\n* Use `PathUri` for apply_patch-internal data structures\n* Limit `PathUri` -> `AbsolutePathBuf` conversion to cases where the\ninferred path convention matches the host OS, allows requiring valid\npaths to pass to perms check\n* Adds `PathConvention::path_segments()` for iterating over path\nsegments regardless of OS\n* Handle cross-platform relative paths in path filename parsing for\nsniffing a shell\n* Ensure we can apply patches in the wine e2e test","tree":{"sha":"342c6e02df06285781199a5e742bed615697c006","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/342c6e02df06285781199a5e742bed615697c006"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/0f89dd768c16549162f0005c4d77654e29f33f6e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNEeHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjVQQAJsX09cyId3hCDrEAlEZDNGj\nhvDPZ2tYGexM+CXcTISRGjrEmbXgNs9fGthqCssIhSYZI/H0AwrfKMSYQpgVb3ct\n/7et3YMNCom4OVfzuYejLLhFfR0bI3h3LUqIvRIgz9qyJwNslCoVSTIOO/0fk0xb\n25RdGksNldNqGqBpLpAhFDMWeTKUy/oryqDe+EXP9gDKsM7DLt2eKE4Cz1r+p9a0\nwm/txpglEB6lugj0TOB406eY3n4+RdRbC2le3J+DjtU8NdK8rfd5w4QjtON//DjT\niuwspivgjr21OOEfKauhgCeJ8Dj29p7XHoWsoOpjVlkPtLnBpkWMQTj/yH+EEFt2\nYvPwLiJi/3aGcJORwXZ0Y45kJFijDqK3j/McjYgLw5PbfLETZriGSiehNZwnVdNF\n1NzwaizQq6sj6uabtvRvpNyMRcTyHwZU6+/nY/qNqykBZh6jEgiDkZw0ceXVuE/4\n50BFxLxEOpjWt//SmwxZe0y0itMBmgSaNQe9NDok9p3OiAvGeel9ZAZU2xdKLCSN\ntJi1ghfqCflOk/T8Uqtb5gaI9rC9kpm6yqQuxD299l001fidm2NCyjiX2aqkpe2j\n1YWZfrKihy+20vZx365FHSh33Jzj+X6p5DGbxPJfkSXEUdtStiAfcPqdxDzfxbv4\nIBvzOp7oCu+fYS1761uZ\n=yJgu\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 342c6e02df06285781199a5e742bed615697c006\nparent a52a3b5197641a1c14949db88c4def5cf966f08c\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1781811079 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781811079 +0000\n\napply-patch: carry paths as PathUri (#28854)\n\n## Why\n\nAllows the model to edit files that are hosted on a different OS than\nwhere app-server is running.\n\n## What\n\n* Use `PathUri` for apply_patch-internal data structures\n* Limit `PathUri` -> `AbsolutePathBuf` conversion to cases where the\ninferred path convention matches the host OS, allows requiring valid\npaths to pass to perms check\n* Adds `PathConvention::path_segments()` for iterating over path\nsegments regardless of OS\n* Handle cross-platform relative paths in path filename parsing for\nsniffing a shell\n* Ensure we can apply patches in the wine e2e test","verified_at":"2026-06-18T19:31:19Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0f89dd768c16549162f0005c4d77654e29f33f6e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/0f89dd768c16549162f0005c4d77654e29f33f6e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0f89dd768c16549162f0005c4d77654e29f33f6e/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a52a3b5197641a1c14949db88c4def5cf966f08c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a52a3b5197641a1c14949db88c4def5cf966f08c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a52a3b5197641a1c14949db88c4def5cf966f08c"}]},{"sha":"a52a3b5197641a1c14949db88c4def5cf966f08c","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGE1MmEzYjUxOTc2NDFhMWMxNDk0OWRiODhjNGRlZjVjZjk2NmYwOGM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Matthew Zeng","email":"mzeng@openai.com","date":"2026-06-18T19:25:07Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-18T19:25:07Z"},"message":"[codex] Cache plugin metadata for tool suggestions (#27812)\n\n## Why\n\n`built_tools` runs for every sampling request, and local plugin\ndiscovery was repeatedly rereading plugin manifests, skills, MCP\nconfiguration, and app declarations to build the same tool-suggest\nmetadata.\n\nThat source-derived metadata is stable until the existing plugin manager\nreloads its cache. Runtime eligibility still needs to reflect the\ncurrent install, disable, policy, app-overlap, and authentication state.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add a bounded, in-memory tool-suggest metadata cache owned by\n`PluginsManager`.\n- Key cached metadata by plugin identity and source, while applying\nauthentication routing each time the metadata is projected.\n- Invalidate the metadata alongside the existing loaded-plugin cache,\nincluding its normal configuration, marketplace refresh, and\nremote-installed-plugin invalidation paths.\n- Guard against an in-flight load repopulating stale metadata after\ninvalidation.\n- Keep marketplace membership and all runtime eligibility filtering live\nrather than introducing a separate catalog or revision model.\n\n## Impact\n\nRepeated sampling requests reuse already-loaded plugin capability\nmetadata while retaining the existing plugin-manager lifecycle as the\nsingle freshness boundary.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins` — 252 passed\n- Added focused coverage for cache invalidation and authentication\nreprojection.","tree":{"sha":"6996f661932b1f1d0b4ff1c291c14ea8e938dd27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/6996f661932b1f1d0b4ff1c291c14ea8e938dd27"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/a52a3b5197641a1c14949db88c4def5cf966f08c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNEYTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuLIQAFRcVs0a/hi1aVLk2DgN3Ua0\n+jeYV6D4VaqvKtv0Z0eSIDu8gn2AFiK8946a77EZnSH3DG31vcaCt5wCR8Vrxr8e\nSsSRMfWEXCOis069fr8YsHjUjw6XoMhuyzTAx/RE7n2tQ7ZvNJPQV5h8k3tFBvJb\nptk7btL2zZ1hUcnbZPHuRrAqmEdkrGnBy+FJOYX1Zv1d/aq8RYtI1P+UoEDZyacc\nQYDilznclDECNcFVxQee7v/tDmUWq+3meWqTHxjMbbntc2DZVpWwKN0lnZuorQhu\nNMjjvmZ4IDXxQVAvlvmO9lSXOXR+14d4Gs38pe4WaPNzoYfc8Ph5HAsGpEU+LabA\na3oNwcoI8SnkNlPxe0epMM442KnjlB6TdzEW1BShBXTnzsBpaMPljjcexhW0zMFd\nd+Jahhl5e4T+AWjpV1Hkka18mLnnlenNMgm3rz+SRZju47riQnbOChzND4MhrWXR\nYbUL+TotrLv5UsTp7HhZFKLl2Tt5Oksj7RvuCU8rWYDIBy8d05OFgDgrL1vna+Ut\nMV27EV+F27F0hda7p2jf+jbMYNDt4Sw4tWHt79xuN6rHiPFMTMf4lPQFPAHa8EQC\nJeXgOv8h/k4FebJ1QZoYB2KLqHr23aSukCQGbMznh/LUzRnzfGWFWmIr5H/95GoT\n7DhdM61+bUTeLfNb1fub\n=pWrj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6996f661932b1f1d0b4ff1c291c14ea8e938dd27\nparent 752ed90d78ad9444dd449fbc8e71ad2121865be0\nauthor Matthew Zeng <mzeng@openai.com> 1781810707 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781810707 -0700\n\n[codex] Cache plugin metadata for tool suggestions (#27812)\n\n## Why\n\n`built_tools` runs for every sampling request, and local plugin\ndiscovery was repeatedly rereading plugin manifests, skills, MCP\nconfiguration, and app declarations to build the same tool-suggest\nmetadata.\n\nThat source-derived metadata is stable until the existing plugin manager\nreloads its cache. Runtime eligibility still needs to reflect the\ncurrent install, disable, policy, app-overlap, and authentication state.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add a bounded, in-memory tool-suggest metadata cache owned by\n`PluginsManager`.\n- Key cached metadata by plugin identity and source, while applying\nauthentication routing each time the metadata is projected.\n- Invalidate the metadata alongside the existing loaded-plugin cache,\nincluding its normal configuration, marketplace refresh, and\nremote-installed-plugin invalidation paths.\n- Guard against an in-flight load repopulating stale metadata after\ninvalidation.\n- Keep marketplace membership and all runtime eligibility filtering live\nrather than introducing a separate catalog or revision model.\n\n## Impact\n\nRepeated sampling requests reuse already-loaded plugin capability\nmetadata while retaining the existing plugin-manager lifecycle as the\nsingle freshness boundary.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins` — 252 passed\n- Added focused coverage for cache invalidation and authentication\nreprojection.","verified_at":"2026-06-18T19:25:07Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a52a3b5197641a1c14949db88c4def5cf966f08c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a52a3b5197641a1c14949db88c4def5cf966f08c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a52a3b5197641a1c14949db88c4def5cf966f08c/comments","author":{"login":"mzeng-openai","id":175741029,"node_id":"U_kgDOCnmYZQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/175741029?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mzeng-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/mzeng-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mzeng-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mzeng-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mzeng-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mzeng-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mzeng-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mzeng-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mzeng-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mzeng-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mzeng-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"752ed90d78ad9444dd449fbc8e71ad2121865be0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/752ed90d78ad9444dd449fbc8e71ad2121865be0","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/752ed90d78ad9444dd449fbc8e71ad2121865be0"}]},{"sha":"752ed90d78ad9444dd449fbc8e71ad2121865be0","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDc1MmVkOTBkNzhhZDk0NDRkZDQ0OWZiYzhlNzFhZDIxMjE4NjViZTA","commit":{"author":{"name":"rka-oai","email":"rka@openai.com","date":"2026-06-18T19:18:42Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-18T19:18:42Z"},"message":"current time reminders impl for system clock (varlatency 2/n) (#28824)\n\nStacked on #28822.\n\n## Summary\n\n- add a host-injectable current-time provider with a built-in system\nimplementation\n- record UTC developer reminders in history immediately before due model\nrequests\n- keep cadence state per session and force a refresh after compaction\n\nThis does NOT include the app server client <-> server clock logic. This\nPR is only for the reminder message & system clock that will be used in\nprod.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core varlatency_`\n- `just clippy -p codex-core -p codex-app-server -p codex-mcp-server -p\ncodex-thread-manager-sample`\n- `just fmt`","tree":{"sha":"2c65454dd4d88288478c5650bc5e59ed96082fc9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/2c65454dd4d88288478c5650bc5e59ed96082fc9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/752ed90d78ad9444dd449fbc8e71ad2121865be0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNESSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXvsQABrsVBz/pyQFvb7xmOAXbfdJ\n6g8g+qF32gw9SbLGRKUV2QoHpfcFQfq6tJc4HAJCbb/Qm63nSo04mPtC5KyFgoZH\nT9VpYBDBM2bwYtDuE+jkGi5VGWOpk8LTN5XwsxOJ9cHfb2io1g3zWpq9nzHDdjnu\nGAKnU0ABnvPHCBtYHznzNdufbLZPJtAxzheCY3HuzRDUEvM0kUQyX7nSvr75WLZz\n2Vn7Z4bGVbUS+zrxLPwyJ1I5UHaLyLcTS/nGE6o9GMLB7len2pHqyiEwU5pg05Xn\nA40K