eal/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"32a696dbacaa1383745455ea2a77d5477891ed0b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/32a696dbacaa1383745455ea2a77d5477891ed0b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/32a696dbacaa1383745455ea2a77d5477891ed0b"}]},{"sha":"32a696dbacaa1383745455ea2a77d5477891ed0b","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDMyYTY5NmRiYWNhYTEzODM3NDU0NTVlYTJhNzdkNTQ3Nzg5MWVkMGI","commit":{"author":{"name":"rka-oai","email":"rka@openai.com","date":"2026-06-18T18:52:19Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-18T18:52:19Z"},"message":"[codex] rollout budget implementation (varlength 2/N) (#28494)\n\n## Stack\n\nDepends on #28746. This PR implements shared rollout-budget accounting\nand model-visible reminders using the configuration defined in #28746.\n\n# Description / Main changes to Core:\n\n`AgentControl` will now be the area where \"rollout level\" features &\naccounting will have to live. It is incorrectly named for this\nresponsibility, but I think it can hold all the necessary shared state &\nfeatures (rollout token budget, mutliple thread interruption\nresponsibilitym etc)\n\nIn this PR, we have one \"token ledger\" that each thread will subtract\nfrom when sampling. The \"charge\" will occur when response.completed() is\ndone and the calculation will be done on the responses api usage\ncarrier. The calculation will weigh sampling and pre-fill tokens as\nspecified.\n\nEvery time the budget crosses the configured reminder threshold, a\ndeveloper message is appended before the thread's next request\n\nThis remaining budget will _always_ be restated/reminded after a\ncompaction event.\n\nExpiration and fan-out interruption will be in the stacked follow-up\n(and also live in Agent Control).\n\n## Reminders\n\n\"You have weighted {session_tokens_left} tokens left in the shared\nsession token budget.\"\n\nThe first request in each thread context receives the current remainder.\nLater reminders are emitted after aggregate weighted usage crosses a\nconfigured interval. If several intervals are crossed before a thread\nsends another request, Core inserts one reminder with the latest\nremainder.\n\nCompaction response usage is charged before the next context starts. The\nnext reminder is appended after the compaction summary, leaving the\ninitial context content stable.\n\n## Tests\n\nIntegration coverage verifies:\n\n- weighted output and non-cached input accounting\n- initial and periodic reminders\n- shared accounting between a root and sub-agent\n- post-compaction remainder and message placement\n\nLocal checks:\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-core rollout_budget`\n- `git diff --check`\n\nThe full workspace test suite was not run locally.","tree":{"sha":"de1bf3e60d5d294eb539c58ec742353e95538cce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/de1bf3e60d5d294eb539c58ec742353e95538cce"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/32a696dbacaa1383745455ea2a77d5477891ed0b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqND5jCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATHkQAH5Lgw8bCh1Z/ud34NfUfYRm\nRL0QE7BJtQ75VKFyxoahlZScowjeHMbiARM/Xu3Vial3jurzSVm9bZWqx9rmuNf+\nDTDvaQJqd7hfFKE6LJdiPmOp0YKFTUFmFjQnceLMDIIxWHloHWK9ilSKAzBE8Qlv\nlhblNO9bnco72cVwKUcGmqiWtuxjAPLvb0oqt0KRA14Bw58B0rGSsBGx689N1CII\nN/3LlF5FxHh5hppwHnZobfMDT01aPL2nU61apsEnxiesNr9mHHqHhL55VPbhX95r\n5e2BL0/axxneajqaNnhorqX8OgyqrRhKqiFuYK58BkOEhpCz0sgzLucDNft3yEnQ\n7Qvvm2pVhnro9U9+mDICuTkfpFj/skG5ijvI/PIHsC7c0LuJxoVESBj8ZbD3x6eG\nv0YKA6Pm+WMod/H03iSkmxJbdQqbPhStOKkLhXueUAFUhqb9IIxvemdBO1u1Zg5D\n0OQegLw8xTPmg9Bl9FjDOuEaNgpF+R2GcrbLuj6Egss6of6Su7wGqj8mxBvLKSNg\n8ZMrxTqTiYjkQHymsC0VJ3FwA3gm5vkkOD1QEvWL4gxZv56NgnRvRy+bkWUM362E\nV04KALyiovKQPIlQYPRiRWFuzw4A/VHPrcI3bxu2ehjNHLKxEEqL4QRM3h29wBta\n+7P4cWDhn6YUf+kNAbnY\n=wo+g\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree de1bf3e60d5d294eb539c58ec742353e95538cce\nparent df5f12285454ce0a6e78a1ce084b57b6860add41\nauthor rka-oai <rka@openai.com> 1781808739 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781808739 +0000\n\n[codex] rollout budget implementation (varlength 2/N) (#28494)\n\n## Stack\n\nDepends on #28746. This PR implements shared rollout-budget accounting\nand model-visible reminders using the configuration defined in #28746.\n\n# Description / Main changes to Core:\n\n`AgentControl` will now be the area where \"rollout level\" features &\naccounting will have to live. It is incorrectly named for this\nresponsibility, but I think it can hold all the necessary shared state &\nfeatures (rollout token budget, mutliple thread interruption\nresponsibilitym etc)\n\nIn this PR, we have one \"token ledger\" that each thread will subtract\nfrom when sampling. The \"charge\" will occur when response.completed() is\ndone and the calculation will be done on the responses api usage\ncarrier. The calculation will weigh sampling and pre-fill tokens as\nspecified.\n\nEvery time the budget crosses the configured reminder threshold, a\ndeveloper message is appended before the thread's next request\n\nThis remaining budget will _always_ be restated/reminded after a\ncompaction event.\n\nExpiration and fan-out interruption will be in the stacked follow-up\n(and also live in Agent Control).\n\n## Reminders\n\n\"You have weighted {session_tokens_left} tokens left in the shared\nsession token budget.\"\n\nThe first request in each thread context receives the current remainder.\nLater reminders are emitted after aggregate weighted usage crosses a\nconfigured interval. If several intervals are crossed before a thread\nsends another request, Core inserts one reminder with the latest\nremainder.\n\nCompaction response usage is charged before the next context starts. The\nnext reminder is appended after the compaction summary, leaving the\ninitial context content stable.\n\n## Tests\n\nIntegration coverage verifies:\n\n- weighted output and non-cached input accounting\n- initial and periodic reminders\n- shared accounting between a root and sub-agent\n- post-compaction remainder and message placement\n\nLocal checks:\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-core rollout_budget`\n- `git diff --check`\n\nThe full workspace test suite was not run locally.","verified_at":"2026-06-18T18:52:20Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/32a696dbacaa1383745455ea2a77d5477891ed0b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/32a696dbacaa1383745455ea2a77d5477891ed0b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/32a696dbacaa1383745455ea2a77d5477891ed0b/comments","author":{"login":"rka-oai","id":240799229,"node_id":"U_kgDODlpN_Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/240799229?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/rka-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"df5f12285454ce0a6e78a1ce084b57b6860add41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/df5f12285454ce0a6e78a1ce084b57b6860add41","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/df5f12285454ce0a6e78a1ce084b57b6860add41"}]},{"sha":"df5f12285454ce0a6e78a1ce084b57b6860add41","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGRmNWYxMjI4NTQ1NGNlMGE2ZTc4YTFjZTA4NGI1N2I2ODYwYWRkNDE","commit":{"author":{"name":"rka-oai","email":"rka@openai.com","date":"2026-06-18T18:39:02Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-18T18:39:02Z"},"message":"Add Config for Time Reminders (varlatency 1/n) (#28822)\n\n## Summary\n\nExample:\n\n> [features.current_time_reminder]\nenabled = true\nreminder_interval_model_requests = 1\nclock_source = \"system\"\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core varlatency`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nlock_contains_prompts_and_materializes_features`\n- `just fix -p codex-core -p codex-config -p codex-features`","tree":{"sha":"4ef45cee383570f5bcffb00ccb10e7224b86118e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/4ef45cee383570f5bcffb00ccb10e7224b86118e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/df5f12285454ce0a6e78a1ce084b57b6860add41","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNDtGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqxkQABggHDDfC3YdBKOMfGP0Col8\nYpXYNR75EcW8/zBkZ5G/SBNVjnW5k7wGXieT54n5EYQQHZUoeTK5LSfURfvrfxpE\nEukKGzxrOh2spscdzKbS9UxlBEjHZiiyqlxEHxk2d6XoZCxbeM4kqgnw9sYhNYqP\ngnHKxAZUlGrfpciWP8oLP68E93BtX5WX0RZdmOapJd47X5aCzUJVkGUW68RIZXbB\n0zPoC7F/au3VO5U0TR9BpOXF4l4QwRwGhP437ALGYUUKIeC0tRe5NL0fU56cB8xe\n/4Q9WyaLH5E6ZD5NjsH1Ea4ge+43BcNvZ4Z7t75Q4Hc8GrdSZND+SVh04YtNxVij\nfC/IiVwxXHOOk4n147BnVdYogtgBOEp5jJ6DFAE98qZFz+4WenXaOrvc9iWmzL/j\nCqG80P6b2K5IDcyYeCXUnHhWcWOa5tFM+VxscpTxk7usHIxVwhaCdsEW8FVtMOW3\n9oy7LsrYCZ9568+3IjxVOjfAWh7ezDBh+c0jTlJCD/nse6Y4eGzbXqxqcZ7L3PUW\nWx5ArfbnPO2M9K6+BdP1NB9ATZ25w6b7LI3jLcpqP2n/A3T1wrw6wjI898plKbVX\nYBU+LIsHT1sqkUWbjVla26t1Y0DVHqiaO9R6lUsWYpsybLU8r6yI5WGjDAJRhIhA\ncgN7rMpkBvNN0mpb+7ZJ\n=BF8H\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4ef45cee383570f5bcffb00ccb10e7224b86118e\nparent 636a2594c6f1ab691a79473388872487c8368ba8\nauthor rka-oai <rka@openai.com> 1781807942 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781807942 -0700\n\nAdd Config for Time Reminders (varlatency 1/n) (#28822)\n\n## Summary\n\nExample:\n\n> [features.current_time_reminder]\nenabled = true\nreminder_interval_model_requests = 1\nclock_source = \"system\"\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core varlatency`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nlock_contains_prompts_and_materializes_features`\n- `just fix -p codex-core -p codex-config -p codex-features`","verified_at":"2026-06-18T18:39:03Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/df5f12285454ce0a6e78a1ce084b57b6860add41","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/df5f12285454ce0a6e78a1ce084b57b6860add41","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/df5f12285454ce0a6e78a1ce084b57b6860add41/comments","author":{"login":"rka-oai","id":240799229,"node_id":"U_kgDODlpN_Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/240799229?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/rka-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"636a2594c6f1ab691a79473388872487c8368ba8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/636a2594c6f1ab691a79473388872487c8368ba8","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/636a2594c6f1ab691a79473388872487c8368ba8"}]},{"sha":"636a2594c6f1ab691a79473388872487c8368ba8","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDYzNmEyNTk0YzZmMWFiNjkxYTc5NDczMzg4ODcyNDg3YzgzNjhiYTg","commit":{"author":{"name":"rka-oai","email":"rka@openai.com","date":"2026-06-18T18:05:53Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-18T18:05:53Z"},"message":"Synchronize realtime notification test requests (#28946)\n\n## What\n\nDeliver the scripted realtime notification batch after the assistant\ntext append request instead of after the preceding developer text append\nrequest.\n\n## Why\n\nThe batch ends with an upstream error that closes the realtime\nconversation. When it is emitted after the developer append, it races\nthe subsequent assistant append: the app-server RPC can acknowledge the\nappend before its downstream WebSocket send completes, and the test\nintermittently observes three requests instead of four.\n\nMaking the fake server wait for the assistant append before emitting the\nterminal batch establishes the ordering the test asserts without sleeps\nor production-code changes.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `git diff --check`\n- CI (the failure is timing-dependent and most reproducible in the\nWindows Bazel shard)","tree":{"sha":"557ff7e357eaf021531e069015f2188107eca236","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/557ff7e357eaf021531e069015f2188107eca236"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/636a2594c6f1ab691a79473388872487c8368ba8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNDOBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8ZsQAEDbonaYIfFuXna5lLWlQIXN\n1UPm2TEM/gajXkikUZd9g3HB9g9PEcksH/5hN26PdgfMPYEZYNjihU6egd5b68FU\nSr45Wn25pj1JcG4vSzmqRGpH+w4uRSQ07un0RuxGGXnX6sbLEVua3vjR1LkN1kgf\niFrD4iuAQdVsRrkPlIuPyki4ddxekyg2B8RQsZr+4yu0f4+f0VZgfMRcXNCMxT9A\n7ExOriwJ6GSXFGjrzJoJLvZXzlMpFy/xC+jOkK3Hm63O0n9AXcAhiLWmv1BSwH25\n0793maQFly04V/0RsdP8N9Phg0arbd0yhpW5pMgOfyT2MRZ8bWDZAPfzZiaVUFWo\nF31LXYfJzCnN+dus58x0Bn+8wgv9+vOOnhB/roPZfGokPCwXt2DoJvzLBzomZxPh\nF4vAGKlrcZm1KwCAf81nkr4AIMBWx0O/eqcxRMLVLXMOaQtnQPAm4DqaP1siNBfq\nEkNDPqfvr4thHolVluvn3LyZMEvJNFJmb/sZenyM7/dBLwexP3msWwQOncTLCvXX\nV8GmkAwoTgtkRK7Q4etXV1qI+Xunm5YIJ7zMN9QCT6DG8FbBRSIhbXM07cKABO1m\nahynnpcJaUHolP+P8r+a77cflRgq5vcglpQrv7MAOnKGEHY7URCJ++1+yrY19kmp\nmoJgrx6850l0y9Ts5sPw\n=wN8Y\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 557ff7e357eaf021531e069015f2188107eca236\nparent afbb69a2fb52d7cb9b2f4fa1c50948dcb6d5a029\nauthor rka-oai <rka@openai.com> 1781805953 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781805953 +0000\n\nSynchronize realtime notification test requests (#28946)\n\n## What\n\nDeliver the scripted realtime notification batch after the assistant\ntext append request instead of after the preceding developer text append\nrequest.\n\n## Why\n\nThe batch ends with an upstream error that closes the realtime\nconversation. When it is emitted after the developer append, it races\nthe subsequent assistant append: the app-server RPC can acknowledge the\nappend before its downstream WebSocket send completes, and the test\nintermittently observes three requests instead of four.\n\nMaking the fake server wait for the assistant append before emitting the\nterminal batch establishes the ordering the test asserts without sleeps\nor production-code changes.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `git diff --check`\n- CI (the failure is timing-dependent and most reproducible in the\nWindows Bazel shard)","verified_at":"2026-06-18T18:05:54Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/636a2594c6f1ab691a79473388872487c8368ba8","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/636a2594c6f1ab691a79473388872487c8368ba8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/636a2594c6f1ab691a79473388872487c8368ba8/comments","author":{"login":"rka-oai","id":240799229,"node_id":"U_kgDODlpN_Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/240799229?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/rka-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"afbb69a2fb52d7cb9b2f4fa1c50948dcb6d5a029","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/afbb69a2fb52d7cb9b2f4fa1c50948dcb6d5a029","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/afbb69a2fb52d7cb9b2f4fa1c50948dcb6d5a029"}]},{"sha":"afbb69a2fb52d7cb9b2f4fa1c50948dcb6d5a029","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGFmYmI2OWEyZmI1MmQ3Y2I5YjJmNGZhMWM1MDk0OGRjYjZkNWEwMjk","commit":{"author":{"name":"iceweasel-oai","email":"iceweasel@openai.com","date":"2026-06-18T18:04:30Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-18T18:04:30Z"},"message":"[codex] Fix Windows sandbox runtime ACL refresh (#28943)\n\n## Why\n\nCodex Desktop repairs sandbox-user read/execute access for binaries\ncopied to `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\OpenAI\\Codex\\bin`, but Computer Use launches\nits bundled Node runtime from `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\OpenAI\\Codex\\runtimes`.\n\nOn fresh Windows installations, `CodexSandboxUsers` may therefore be\nunable to execute the bundled Node binary. The command runner starts,\nbut `CreateProcessAsUserW` fails with error 5 (`ACCESS_DENIED`), causing\nthe Node REPL to exit before Computer Use can discover applications.\n\nThis is a follow-up to #21564, which added the original runtime `bin`\nACL repair.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Expand the Codex Desktop runtime ACL roots from only `bin` to both\n`bin` and `runtimes`.\n- Apply the existing inherited read/execute ACL repair to each runtime\ndirectory when it exists.\n- Rename the setup helper to reflect that it now handles multiple\nruntime paths.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `cargo fmt -- --check`\n- `just test -p codex-windows-sandbox` was run: 113 tests passed and\nfive environment-dependent legacy execution tests failed because\n`CreateRestrictedToken` returned error 87.","tree":{"sha":"61bff818b361d15e49221c9ef81c5a0c0c010905","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/61bff818b361d15e49221c9ef81c5a0c0c010905"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/afbb69a2fb52d7cb9b2f4fa1c50948dcb6d5a029","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNDMuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAI4wQAEu42CKyN0Pp9vCOERtSwfKr\nXrkuScj+MdI5cQAILz9wyaVRfJpTJEY93SQtYdO7Pz3x686c68+k72D8JBGuBqyt\nXlzXkNyw94GH0v7fysma+vbZPkXyJ2OAvSYRDTqRV+16lAowI8iPEj5f2G72RH4b\ntJyGt+ZBO0vFd4AmkwLDj0YjBPEwjMJ6hiBz4RgckXYU+VR0ywUujvkLOkeu0UPr\nqKZbCTIXjWC7N1qstB/1JzOeMXH1z5bH6qOmnVnfENdmi4G1g7t9wK4+HNCluEu/\nXs7bQO4GNofEK8hjRtHcn4zNGaW6d1r3kf5RDTtJA743I4PKlJzkWB4SZXdC+t8l\ntxwAIVlFgjr18FeL/AMu8OMX68WbdVkkW4vXACzGnQWUPBJO6XSs7LLVCBwQKI/2\ncxQ5pbSlKcbnIcnN7YxRB7qakmDCqt8v385SrthwPG3Hs70kibqJFcGptnTwDyOE\nzKRv5wBRRwSEQ60PFjO8jemBQFKD7fgh74PVzMQ9fJb0JsQTBxdP7/H1ksI2toyW\nBBupyFbJQdvoKXvfnwbtFLaq9TGTP+mzVCE0lk5P/KC+8oNuPdPx21+c5z1vyw3l\nHEIaF3hQb2ckIqKIji1yRl9W8jyfj2vurV348SGntFgWh2OL81CNcXXcw9ba8u/X\nCRfGq+YjOIdIgCYpaNNR\n=onxC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 61bff818b361d15e49221c9ef81c5a0c0c010905\nparent 4c7228e423839fb6bd6e2f2a6abeb397ab3f2e28\nauthor iceweasel-oai <iceweasel@openai.com> 1781805870 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781805870 -0700\n\n[codex] Fix Windows sandbox runtime ACL refresh (#28943)\n\n## Why\n\nCodex Desktop repairs sandbox-user read/execute access for binaries\ncopied to `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\OpenAI\\Codex\\bin`, but Computer Use launches\nits bundled Node runtime from `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\OpenAI\\Codex\\runtimes`.\n\nOn fresh Windows installations, `CodexSandboxUsers` may therefore be\nunable to execute the bundled Node binary. The command runner starts,\nbut `CreateProcessAsUserW` fails with error 5 (`ACCESS_DENIED`), causing\nthe Node REPL to exit before Computer Use can discover applications.\n\nThis is a follow-up to #21564, which added the original runtime `bin`\nACL repair.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Expand the Codex Desktop runtime ACL roots from only `bin` to both\n`bin` and `runtimes`.\n- Apply the existing inherited read/execute ACL repair to each runtime\ndirectory when it exists.\n- Rename the setup helper to reflect that it now handles multiple\nruntime paths.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `cargo fmt -- --check`\n- `just test -p codex-windows-sandbox` was run: 113 tests passed and\nfive environment-dependent legacy execution tests failed because\n`CreateRestrictedToken` returned error 87.","verified_at":"2026-06-18T18:04:30Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/afbb69a2fb52d7cb9b2f4fa1c50948dcb6d5a029","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/afbb69a2fb52d7cb9b2f4fa1c50948dcb6d5a029","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/afbb69a2fb52d7cb9b2f4fa1c50948dcb6d5a029/comments","author":{"login":"iceweasel-oai","id":234057055,"node_id":"U_kgDODfNtXw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234057055?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/iceweasel-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4c7228e423839fb6bd6e2f2a6abeb397ab3f2e28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4c7228e423839fb6bd6e2f2a6abeb397ab3f2e28","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4c7228e423839fb6bd6e2f2a6abeb397ab3f2e28"}]},{"sha":"4c7228e423839fb6bd6e2f2a6abeb397ab3f2e28","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDRjNzIyOGU0MjM4MzlmYjZiZDZlMmYyYTZhYmViMzk3YWIzZjJlMjg","commit":{"author":{"name":"starr-openai","email":"starr@openai.com","date":"2026-06-18T18:03:42Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-18T18:03:42Z"},"message":"[codex] Initialize exec-server OpenTelemetry at startup (#25019)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Initialize stderr tracing and the configured OpenTelemetry provider\nfor local and remote `codex exec-server` startup.\n- Instrument the local and remote server entrypoints with a root runtime\nspan.\n- Keep raw Noise environment, registration, and stream identifiers out\nof exported spans while preserving them in local debug events.\n- Keep telemetry setup in a focused CLI module instead of growing the\ntop-level command entrypoint.\n\n## Stack\n\n- Previous: none (`#27058` has merged)\n- Next: #27466\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-exec-server --lib` (139 passed)\n- `just test -p codex-cli --test exec_server` (3 passed)\n- `just bazel-lock-check`\n- `just fix -p codex-exec-server -p codex-cli`\n- `just fmt`\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Richard Lee <richardlee@openai.com>","tree":{"sha":"96ab1bee6959579a58ea6eec61250c6d1c5bc1bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/96ab1bee6959579a58ea6eec61250c6d1c5bc1bb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/4c7228e423839fb6bd6e2f2a6abeb397ab3f2e28","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNDL+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyxUQAKVnnDUVV/CAdTbtKpt5ISf+\nkEVWdSLgLuJah+3VgvGQJSht3OHH4KPl3W9ZQk0FWMjrJI8tPs7umjjBSkP3rV85\nhjz92kBcRVLaHbP/Y60IrVcW2aQsVzeND5LXwKgGMU6amv8JN/QuySmnIja/tEmi\nybKXxje4v6Nr2+NZcI51S2du7J891VtKSVyQBjs4GkouVJEkp/kzsKJ2kfisy5Mg\nDuJdnyDSUOR45l5JeMHYXVLVIpP3QEFq8PZjHXy1HWmZ8Wl+sF0ILtfq+NAGpPbT\nD2eOYQ62hsuJSh4UjTwqTSnnwrU2sRTPCL+vItJNTjBcES8u8nNCO8Q64EVWNAPD\nfA6ivqD0ApcIh22XhOy21NjVIdYxHJywNJ1O52EIWpvedC+wHBrm7shhrsjcgprE\n1GR2CSzNr7xm3k7gFhb8NaL6O96ne+rsm/XZbP9v/jY3ql4LNnxAhrxZ3jkOefu8\n1qMFvlkcdyPmSMl/Zm9UiL1vhUAqCWXFMxEXQGdO7lB6Q3/R/uqAU257tn3g/yF0\nDAaLjdNjylcDc3fhwKEYWvcMfESBOceS+j9Kqek0mi4IcrWnskVKU8IzyvbelG3A\nttc//oEUg1sFoDU1lqWS4KQW9ZPlr+OiGTErKfWgCFtNSPzdGiMvkFz2zB5YKCy8\ng1ZuMt5GPwv4PWTVsoXo\n=LDco\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 96ab1bee6959579a58ea6eec61250c6d1c5bc1bb\nparent e8dd1b45cbfe241abf85c6696f7ab07e85a0c5d5\nauthor starr-openai <starr@openai.com> 1781805822 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781805822 -0700\n\n[codex] Initialize exec-server OpenTelemetry at startup (#25019)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Initialize stderr tracing and the configured OpenTelemetry provider\nfor local and remote `codex exec-server` startup.\n- Instrument the local and remote server entrypoints with a root runtime\nspan.\n- Keep raw Noise environment, registration, and stream identifiers out\nof exported spans while preserving them in local debug events.\n- Keep telemetry setup in a focused CLI module instead of growing the\ntop-level command entrypoint.\n\n## Stack\n\n- Previous: none (`#27058` has merged)\n- Next: #27466\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-exec-server --lib` (139 passed)\n- `just test -p codex-cli --test exec_server` (3 passed)\n- `just bazel-lock-check`\n- `just fix -p codex-exec-server -p codex-cli`\n- `just fmt`\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Richard Lee <richardlee@openai.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-18T18:03:42Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4c7228e423839fb6bd6e2f2a6abeb397ab3f2e28","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4c7228e423839fb6bd6e2f2a6abeb397ab3f2e28","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4c7228e423839fb6bd6e2f2a6abeb397ab3f2e28/comments","author":{"login":"starr-openai","id":176426273,"node_id":"U_kgDOCoQNIQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176426273?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/starr-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/starr-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starr-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starr-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starr-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starr-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starr-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starr-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starr-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starr-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starr-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e8dd1b45cbfe241abf85c6696f7ab07e85a0c5d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e8dd1b45cbfe241abf85c6696f7ab07e85a0c5d5","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e8dd1b45cbfe241abf85c6696f7ab07e85a0c5d5"}]}]